   "name": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "status": "disconfirmed",
   "status_label": "AUGUST 28 (Day 183): THE STRAIT THAT WAS DECLARED CLEARED WAS ATTACKED AGAIN, AND THE UNITED STATES ANSWERED BY BUILDING A COURT. UKMTO ISSUED WARNING 121-26 ON AUGUST 27 — A TANKER STRUCK BY AN UNKNOWN PROJECTILE IN THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ, FIRE EXTINGUISHED, CREW SAFE, NO ENVIRONMENTAL DAMAGE, THE SECOND VESSEL HIT THIS WEEK AND THIRTY-SIX HOURS AFTER TRUMP DECLARED EVERY MINE REMOVED UNDER A 'ZERO TOLERANCE' RULE. THE WEAPON WAS A PROJECTILE, NOT A MINE, WHICH LEAVES THE DEMINING CLAIM INTACT ON ITS OWN TERMS AND CONFIRMS AMBREY'S ASSESSMENT THAT MINES 'HAVE NEVER BEEN THE PRIMARY THREAT.' THE AMERICAN MOVE OF THE CYCLE WAS LEGAL: BLOOMBERG REPORTED ON AUGUST 26 THAT THE JUSTICE DEPARTMENT IS REVIVING MARITIME PRIZE COURTS — DORMANT SINCE THE SECOND WORLD WAR — TO CONDEMN SEIZED IRANIAN TANKERS AND CARGO AS US PROPERTY FOR SALE WITH PROCEEDS TO THE TREASURY, TO STRENGTHEN THE BLOCKADE AND OFFSET THE COST OF THE WAR; US ATTORNEY AARON REITZ CONFIRMED DOJ IS 'NOW REVIVING' AN 'ANCIENT BODY OF MARITIME LAW.' DIPLOMACY MOVED AND THEN CONTRADICTED ITSELF INSIDE ONE GOVERNMENT: QATAR'S PRIME MINISTER SHEIKH MOHAMMED BIN ABDULRAHMAN AL THANI SPENT AUGUST 27 IN TEHRAN MEETING ARAGHCHI, PEZESHKIAN, GHALIBAF AND SECURITY CHIEF MOHSEN REZAI — 'DIALOGUE AND DIPLOMATIC SOLUTIONS REMAIN THE OPTIMAL PATH' — WHILE A SENIOR IRANIAN SOURCE TOLD REUTERS THE AGREEMENT WITH OMAN 'HAS NOT BEEN FINALIZED,' A DAY AFTER THE IRGC SAID SHARES OF THE WATERWAY AND ITS REVENUES WERE SETTLED. REZAI RESTATED THE PRICE UNCHANGED FOR A THIRD MEDIATOR IN FOUR DAYS: LIFT THE BLOCKADE, UNFREEZE ASSETS, REMOVE OIL SANCTIONS. WASHINGTON CLOSED THE DOOR — THE WHITE HOUSE SAID THERE ARE 'NO TALKS OR CONVERSATIONS' UNDER WAY OR SCHEDULED, TRUMP SAID 'WE DON'T WANT TO SPEAK TO THEM,' LEAVITT SAID THE ADMINISTRATION IS 'CONTINUING TO PULL EVERY ECONOMIC LEVER' WITH 'THE NAVAL BLOCKADE... PROVEN HUGELY SUCCESSFUL,' AND REPORTING INDICATED THE ADMINISTRATION NO LONGER SEEKS TO REVIVE THE JUNE 17 MOU. THE TRAFFIC DATA LANDED AGAINST THE PRESIDENT'S OWN NUMBER: AL JAZEERA PUT TRANSITS AT ABOUT FIVE VESSELS A DAY FROM JULY 15 TO AUGUST 23 AGAINST A ~100/DAY BASELINE — NEARLY 95% DOWN — TWO DAYS AFTER TRUMP SAID TEN MILLION BARRELS MOVED THROUGH ON TUESDAY. GULF CRUDE EXPORTS ARE DOWN 47%; GIBSON SHIPBROKERS' RICHARD MATTHEWS: 'THERE IS NO ALTERNATIVE MARITIME ROUTE.' OIL PRINTS DIVERGED — BRENT $87-89.48, WTI $81-82 — ALL ATTRIBUTED TO DIPLOMACY RATHER THAN SUPPLY. INSIDE IRAN THE FUEL POSITION WAS DESCRIBED AS A RED ALERT WITH RESERVES POSSIBLY EXHAUSTED IN WEEKS, QUEUES IN TEHRAN AND MASHHAD, RATIONING SIGNALLED, AND THE RIAL AT ~2.06 MILLION. FORMER MOSSAD CHIEF BARNEA: 'NO CHOICE' BUT TO STRIKE 'UNTIL THE REGIME FALLS.' PENTAGON CASUALTIES HOLD AT 776. A TWENTY-SEVENTH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. STILL AIR, NAVAL, FINANCIAL AND NOW JUDICIAL — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. || AUGUST 27 (Day 182): A DOUBLE CYCLE, AND THE UNITED STATES SPENT IT MAKING THE STRAIT NAVIGABLE RATHER THAN TAKING IT. AXIOS REPORTED ON AUGUST 25, CITING US OFFICIALS, THAT SECRETARY OF STATE MARCO RUBIO HAS TOLD ALLIED FOREIGN MINISTERS THE UNITED STATES IS NOT EXPECTED TO LAUNCH NEW STRIKES ON IRAN 'FOR THE TIME BEING' AND WILL FOCUS ON SANCTIONS, THE NAVAL BLOCKADE AND 'MOVING EVER-INCREASING AMOUNTS OF OIL OUT OF THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ' — AND THAT A SECOND OFFICIAL EXPECTS THE POSTURE TO HOLD UNTIL AFTER THE MIDTERM ELECTIONS. IT IS THE FIRST TIME THE PAUSE HAS BEEN GIVEN A DURATION. ON AUGUST 25 TRUMP ANNOUNCED THAT THE US NAVY HAS CLEARED ALL MINES FROM THE STRAIT'S INTERNATIONAL WATERS, DECLARING 'ZERO TOLERANCE' — 'ANY SHIP OR BOAT PLACING NEW MINES WILL BE IMMEDIATELY AND SYSTEMATICALLY DESTROYED' — WITH SPACE FORCE SURVEILLANCE. US OFFICIALS SAID UNDERWATER DRONES HAD LOCATED MORE THAN 100 SUSPECTED MINES OVER RECENT MONTHS AND PRIVATE CONTRACTORS REMOVED OR DETONATED THEM, THE CENTCOM OPERATION HAVING BEGUN IN APRIL. GHARIBABADI CALLED THE CLAIM 'ONLY AIMED AT CALMING MARKETS' AND SAID 'NO ONE EXCEPT IRAN KNOWS THE LOCATION.' MARK HILBORNE OF KING'S COLLEGE LONDON GAVE THE CENTCOM CLAIM 'STRONG CONFIDENCE' FOR THE MAIN LANES WHILE WARNING OF RISKS BEYOND THEM; AMBREY'S ALEX ALMEIDA SAID MINES 'HAVE NEVER BEEN THE PRIMARY THREAT.' OMAN'S FOREIGN MINISTER BADR ALBUSAIDI MET ARAGHCHI IN TEHRAN ON AUGUST 25 AND THE TWO MINISTRIES ANNOUNCED A 'PHASED FRAMEWORK' FOR A JOINT TEMPORARY NAVIGATIONAL CORRIDOR AND A JOINT MINE-CLEARING PROJECT, WITH TALKS TO CONTINUE TOWARD A PERMANENT CORRIDOR AND 'THE FUTURE ADMINISTRATION OF THE STRAIT.' ON AUGUST 26 GHARIBABADI GAVE THE TERMS: SEVEN MILES WIDE, ENTRY BEGINNING IN IRANIAN TERRITORIAL WATERS WITH PART OF THE EXIT ALSO THROUGH THEM, IRANIAN PERMISSION AND SURVEILLANCE REQUIRED, MILITARY VESSELS BARRED, A PERMANENT ARRANGEMENT IN 30-60 DAYS — AND 'THE AGREED-UPON TRANSIT ROUTE WITH OMAN IS A TEMPORARY ROUTE.' FULL REOPENING IS CONDITIONED ON US COMPLIANCE WITH THE JUNE 17 MOU, SANCTIONS RELIEF, RELEASE OF FROZEN ASSETS, AN END TO THE WAR AND WAR-DAMAGE COMPENSATION. IRGC SPOKESMAN HOSSEIN MOHEBBI SAID THE TWO HAD AGREED 'EACH COUNTRY'S SHARE OF THE STRAIT'S WATERS AND IRAN AND OMAN'S SHARE OF ITS REVENUES' AND THAT 'THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ BELONGS TO IRAN AND THE SULTANATE OF OMAN.' THE ENFORCEMENT RECORD CUT AGAINST THE DIPLOMACY WITHIN A DAY: IRAN'S SHIPPING MONITORING AGENCY SAID THE INDIAN TANKER HAANA WAS WARNED TO STOP AND TURNED BACK ON THE SOUTHERN OMANI ROUTE AND THAT NO VESSEL TRAFFIC HAD BEEN OBSERVED THERE IN 24 HOURS — AGAINST THE KPLER FINDING OF >80% OF LIQUIDS TRANSITS ON THAT ROUTE. OIL FELL THREE SESSIONS RUNNING — BRENT TO ~$89 ON AUGUST 25 (A ONE-WEEK LOW) AND ~$86 ON AUGUST 26, WTI NEAR $80 — WITH BBH CALLING THE SANCTIONS 'MORE OF A WARNING SHOT THAN A DECISIVE BLOW.' TRUMP TOLD AL JAZEERA 'I HAVE NO TIME SCHEDULE, NONE. I'M NOT IN A HURRY,' TOLD GLENN BECK THE STRAIT IS 'A VERY FUNCTIONING STRAIT,' AND SAID MOJTABA KHAMENEI IS NOT DEAD BUT 'VERY SERIOUSLY WOUNDED.' INSIDE IRAN PETROL STATIONS RAN DRY UNDER A 20-LITRE LIMIT, THE EXECUTIVE VICE-PRESIDENT SAID 'WITH THE US NAVAL BLOCKADE, WE CANNOT IMPORT GASOLINE,' PEZESHKIAN CALLED THESE 'THE WORST CONDITIONS OF AN ECONOMIC WAR,' AND THE RIAL SET A RECORD 2.06 MILLION TO THE DOLLAR ON AUGUST 25. PENTAGON CASUALTIES MOVED TO 776 — 18 KILLED, 758 WOUNDED. QATAR'S PRIME MINISTER ARRIVES IN TEHRAN TODAY. A 25TH AND 26TH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. || AUGUST 25 (Day 180): THE FINANCIAL OFFENSIVE ARRIVED AND IT HAS A NAME. TREASURY SECRETARY SCOTT BESSENT HELD HIS 2 P.M. ET NEWS CONFERENCE ON AUGUST 24 AND UNVEILED 'OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST' — FIVE SECTORAL DETERMINATIONS AGAINST DIGITAL ASSETS, TECHNOLOGY, GOLD, AVIATION AND SHIPPING, WITH NEARLY 60 IRAN-LINKED PEOPLE, ENTITIES AND VESSELS DESIGNATED ACROSS THE UAE, HONG KONG, CHINA, SINGAPORE AND SWITZERLAND, EVERY COUNTRY GIVEN A DEFINED WIND-DOWN TIMELINE, MOST SECONDARY SANCTIONS DEFERRED BEHIND A 'CURE PERIOD,' AND A MAJOR FINANCIAL INSTITUTION SIGNALLED FOR DESIGNATION BY THE END OF THE WEEK. THE OBJECTIVE WAS STATED WITHOUT EUPHEMISM: 'IT IS GOING TO WORK IN IRAN, AND WE ARE GOING TO COLLAPSE THIS REGIME.' THE WHITE HOUSE POSITIONED THE OPERATION AS THE 'ENDGAME' PHASE SUCCEEDING OPERATION EPIC FURY — 'BEGINNING TODAY, THE ACTIONS OF TREASURY AND OTHER AGENCIES WILL TIGHTEN THE NOOSE AND BLOCK EVERY POTENTIAL SOURCE OF REVENUE THAT FUNDS THE IRGC.' REGIME COLLAPSE IS NOW A DECLARED WAR AIM AND THE DECLARED INSTRUMENT IS THE BANKING SYSTEM. THE CYCLE'S ONE COUNTER-INDICATOR IS LOGGED IN FULL: SECRETARY OF WAR PETE HEGSETH SAID THE SAME DAY THAT MILITARY FORCE IS NOT RULED OUT IN THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ 'OR ANYWHERE ELSE.' THE MARKET MARKED THE OFFENSIVE DOWN: BRENT FELL ON ANNOUNCEMENT DAY AFTER A WEEK OF MORE THAN 5% GAINS — REUTERS -1.4% TO ~$93, CNBC -2.5% TO $92.06, STRAITS.LIVE $92.10 AT -1.67% — ON PROFIT-TAKING. THE RIAL WENT THE OTHER WAY, HITTING A RECORD 2.02 MILLION TO THE DOLLAR ON THE OPEN MARKET AGAINST AN OFFICIAL RATE OF ~1.5 MILLION, WITH RICE UP ~60% AND BEEF UP >150% SINCE FEBRUARY. TEHRAN'S ANSWER WAS DISMISSAL PLUS A THREAT AGAINST HOST STATES: ARAGHCHI SAID WASHINGTON 'REPEATEDLY PUT FORWARD THE SAME OLD PLANS'; BAGHAEI SAID 'ANY ESCALATION OF THIS SITUATION WILL UNDOUBTEDLY BRING ABOUT CONSEQUENCES,' 'OUR HANDS ARE NOT TIED,' AND THAT IRAN HAS THE RIGHT TO TARGET ANY LOCATION USED TO LAUNCH ATTACKS AGAINST IT — WARNING COUNTRIES AGAINST PROVIDING TERRITORY OR FACILITIES TO THE UNITED STATES. TWO TANKERS WERE HIT IN TWENTY-FOUR HOURS: THE SAUDI VLCC AMZAN (BAHRI) BY HOUTHI BALLISTIC MISSILES AND DRONES ~63NM WEST OF YANBU IN THE RED SEA ON AUGUST 24, FIRE ON THE MAIN DECK AND CREW SAFE, DESCRIBED BY YAHYA SAREE AS A 'SIEGE FOR SIEGE' OPERATION AGAINST THE SAUDIS; AND AN UNNAMED TANKER DISABLED IN ITS ENGINE ROOM ~9NM NORTHEAST OF ASH SHISHAH, OMAN AT 0131 UTC ON AUGUST 25, UNCLAIMED. CENTCOM'S TALLY REACHED 71 REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED AS OF AUGUST 24 — AND DISCLOSED FOR THE FIRST TIME THAT MORE THAN 40 HUMANITARIAN AID VESSELS HAVE BEEN PERMITTED THROUGH. THE TRAFFIC PICTURE ACQUIRED ITS FIRST DIRECTIONAL DATASET: CNN BUSINESS, CITING KPLER, REPORTS MORE THAN 80% OF LIQUIDS TRANSITS OVER THE PRECEDING TWO WEEKS TOOK THE OMANI ROUTE OR WERE DARK TRANSITS THAT LIKELY DID, CONCLUDING IRAN HAS LOST SIGNIFICANT CONTROL; GULF NEWS PUTS SOUTHERN-CORRIDOR TRAFFIC UP ~400% OVER TWO WEEKS TO NEARLY 200 SHIPS WEEKLY; STRAITS.LIVE STILL CARRIES ONE TRANSIT AGAINST A 73-A-DAY BASELINE, 370 HULLS OFF BERTH, EIGHT OF NINE MAJOR CONTAINER CARRIERS ON THE CAPE ROUTE AND DECEMBER 31 REOPENING ODDS AT 34%. DIPLOMACY RAN THROUGH ISLAMABAD AND MUSCAT: FIELD MARSHAL ASIM MUNIR AND INTERIOR MINISTER MOHSIN NAQVI MET IRANIAN INTERIOR MINISTER ESKANDAR MOMENI IN TEHRAN ON AUGUST 24, WITH THE JUNE 17 ISLAMABAD MEMORANDUM'S 60-DAY WINDOW HAVING LAPSED IN MID-AUGUST WITHOUT EXTENSION; OMAN'S FOREIGN MINISTER SAYYID BADR ALBUSAIDI ARRIVES IN TEHRAN ON AUGUST 25 TO MEET ARAGHCHI. A TWENTY-FOURTH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. PENTAGON CASUALTIES HOLD AT 775 (18 KILLED, 757 WOUNDED), AND THE SERVICE SPLIT IS NEW AND POINTED: 580+ ARMY, 86 NAVY, 64 AIR FORCE AND 19 MARINES. PUMP $4.0991; DIESEL $5.6134 AT A FURTHER RECORD. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED FOR A 180TH DAY. || AUGUST 24 (Day 179): BOTH BELLIGERENTS SPENT THE CYCLE DRAFTING DOCUMENTS RATHER THAN MOVING FORCES. TREASURY SECRETARY SCOTT BESSENT PUBLISHED AN OP-ED IN THE FINANCIAL TIMES ON AUGUST 23 OPENING 'AT DAWN BEGINS AN ECONOMIC D-DAY — THE SINGLE GREATEST FINANCIAL OFFENSIVE EVER MARSHALLED AGAINST AN ADVERSARY,' with the detailing news conference set for 2 P.M. ET ON MONDAY AUGUST 24 and not yet held at cycle close; the declared targets are OIL SMUGGLING, SWAP LINES, CASH TRANSFERS, EXCHANGE HOUSES, SHIP REGISTRIES AND FRONT COMPANIES, and the declared mechanism is SECONDARY SANCTIONS on any state providing Iran 'any type of lifeline.' HOURS EARLIER IRAN'S PARLIAMENTARY NATIONAL SECURITY AND FOREIGN POLICY COMMISSION APPROVED ARTICLE 3 OF ITS 'STRATEGIC ACTION TO ENSURE THE SECURITY AND PROGRESS OF THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ' PLAN — service fees on 'AUTHORISED' transiting ships covering maritime, environmental, conditional fueling, insurance and safety services, payable 'IN RIALS OR ANY OTHER CURRENCY DESIRED BY THE ISLAMIC REPUBLIC OF IRAN,' with violators reported to face fines, detention or confiscation; the commission spokesman is named as HASSAN QASHQAVI by Middle East Eye and Al Jazeera and as EBRAHIM REZAEI by Reuters, and the measure still requires a full parliamentary vote and Guardian Council review. SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI ESCALATED FROM SELECTIVITY TO TOTALITY AND, FOR THE FIRST TIME, NAMED THE BYPASS ROUTES: via IRNA he warned Tehran 'WILL NOT ALLOW A SINGLE DROP OF OIL TO LEAVE THE PERSIAN GULF' if pressure escalates, said Iran would 'RETALIATE IN A SEISMIC MANNER,' said it would TARGET THE ALTERNATIVE OIL-SHIPPING ROUTES out of the Gulf, and CAUTIONED AGAINST ANY ADDITIONAL US MILITARY DEPLOYMENT to the region. AND THE MOST CONSEQUENTIAL IRANIAN STATEMENT OF THE CYCLE WAS NOT A THREAT: in two Tehran appearances on SUNDAY AUGUST 23 PRESIDENT MASOUD PEZESHKIAN SAID IRAN 'CANNOT CONTINUE WITH WAR FOREVER' and that 'ONE DAY, A DECISION MUST BE MADE TO SAVE THE COUNTRY FROM THE STATE OF NEITHER WAR NOR PEACE,' DEFENDING THE JUNE MOU against the purported misgivings of SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI — the first on-record elite split of the war on the Iranian side. A TWENTY-THIRD CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. CENTCOM'S BLOCKADE TALLY REACHED 70 REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED AS OF AUGUST 23, up from 68 on August 21. THE TRAFFIC PICTURE REMAINS IRRECONCILABLE FROM OPEN SOURCES: CNN puts transits at 20% OF THE PRE-WAR AVERAGE, straits.live carried ONE TRANSIT on its latest daily datapoint against a 73-A-DAY BASELINE, and a US official says American forces are facilitating 15-20 TRANSITS A NIGHT carrying ROUGHLY TEN MILLION BARRELS A DAY, adding 'THE IRGC CAN BE A NUISANCE, BUT THEY DON'T CONTROL THE STRAIT. WE DO.' EGYPTIAN FOREIGN MINISTER BADR ABDELATTY AND ABBAS ARAGHCHI SPOKE ON AUGUST 22 about de-escalation, the Oman track and implementation of the June 18 MOU, with Cairo stressing freedom of navigation. BRENT $94.39; PUMP $4.0986; DIESEL $5.6074 AT A RECORD AUGUST LEVEL; WAR RISK ~$10.0M PER VLCC AT 40× PRE-CRISIS WITH SIX P&I CLUBS WITHDRAWN; PENTAGON CASUALTIES HOLD AT 775 (18 KILLED, 757 WOUNDED). THE GROUND TRACKER CARRIES ONE CORRECTION — CARRIER PRESENCE IN CENTCOM IS TWO, NOT ONE — AND ONE BACKFILL: CNN REPORTED ON JUNE 12 THAT CJCS GEN. DAN CAINE FLEW FROM BRUSSELS TO CENTCOM HEADQUARTERS ON MAY 19 TO BE BRIEFED ON SENDING GROUND TROOPS INTO IRAN TO SEIZE ITS ENRICHED URANIUM, AND THAT TRUMP DECLINED IT ON CASUALTY GROUNDS BEFORE IRAN SEALED THE CACHE WITH COLLAPSED TUNNELS AND MINED ENTRANCES. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED FOR A 179TH DAY. || AUGUST 23 (Day 178): THE UNITED STATES CLAIMED THE WATER AND IRAN ALLOCATED THE TRAFFIC, ON THE SAME DAY, AND NEITHER CLAIM PRODUCED A LANDING. On AUGUST 22 Trump said 'I VIEW THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ AS AN AMERICAN TERRITORY RIGHT NOW' and re-posted the Truth Social map labelling the waterway 'NEW U.S. TERRITORY' he first published on August 18 — a sovereignty assertion over water, made with zero US ground forces on Iranian soil. Hours apart, IRNA announced that TEHRAN HAD GRANTED A NUMBER OF IRAQI OIL TANKERS PERMISSION TO TRANSIT after repeated Baghdad requests, the FIRST NAMED STATE-LEVEL EXEMPTION OF THE WAR. IRAN'S FOREIGN MINISTRY CALLED THE SANCTIONS DUE MONDAY A 'DECLARATION OF WAR ON ALL NATIONS' and an attempt 'TO EXERT EXTRATERRITORIAL SOVEREIGNTY OVER ALL INDEPENDENT UN MEMBER STATES,' warning of 'AN ABYSMAL RETURN TO FULL-SCALE CLASSIC COLONIALISM'; SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI SAID ANY COUNTRY JOINING THEM IS 'CONSIDERED AN ENEMY,' that Iran would 'HARM' its interests and disrupt GULF OIL SHIPMENTS, that 'THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ IS CLOSED AND WILL NOT REOPEN' absent a change in US behaviour, and that Iran would retaliate 'IN AN EARTHQUAKE-LIKE MANNER' — while conceding Iran had 'NOT YET ATTACKED ANY AMERICAN ECONOMIC INTERESTS.' A TWENTY-SECOND CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. CENTCOM'S BLOCKADE TALLY REACHED 68 REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED as of August 21, with more than 20 warships enforcing. AND THE TRAFFIC DATA NOW CUTS AGAINST THE AMERICAN CLAIM: Al Jazeera's August 20 analysis of August 1-19 found 236 hulls crossing — 83 OPENLY ON IRAN'S ROUTE, THREE OPENLY ON THE US-BACKED OMANI ROUTE, 148 DARK — and of 112 oil and gas vessels, 21 Iranian, two Omani and 89 dark, concluding that 'THE FEAR OF OFFENDING TEHRAN APPEARS TO OUTWEIGH TRUMP'S THREATS.' Named merchant casualties inside the Strait this month include the MINOAN PIONEER (third engineer missing, August 3), an ADNOC TANKER hit by missile (August 8), the NAVIG8 MESSI and TARIF hit by drones (August 13) and the MINOAN DIGNITY (chief engineer killed, August 17-18); ADNOC counts 16 vessels attacked since February 28, one killed and 20 injured. KHARG WAS RESTARTED, NOT TAKEN — an NITC VLCC loaded ~2m barrels at the Azarpad jetty on August 14 after a ~25-day halt. BRENT ~$94; PUMP $4.102; PENTAGON CASUALTIES 774-775. BESSENT'S SANCTIONS NEWS CONFERENCE IS SET FOR 2 P.M. ET MONDAY AUGUST 24. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED FOR A 178TH DAY. || AUGUST 22 (Day 177): THE WAR CHANGED CATEGORY RATHER THAN INTENSITY. THE PRESIDENT CANCELLED THE THREATENED MULTI-DAY ENERGY CAMPAIGN BY NAME LATE ON AUGUST 1 — citing progress toward a deal and requests from Iran and 'OTHER MIDDLE EASTERN COUNTRIES,' conditioned on the 'IMMEDIATE, COMPLETE, AND TOTAL OPENING OF THE HORMUZ STRAIT, AND AN END TO IRAN'S NUCLEAR THREAT' — after MBS and other regional leaders pressed for restraint; Tehran denied asking for anything and Trump then called Iranian leadership 'UNBELIEVABLY DUPLICITOUS.' NO US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN WAS CONFIRMED BY CENTCOM THROUGH AUGUST 19 — A TWENTIETH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT. THE 60-DAY MOU WINDOW EXPIRED AUGUST 17 WITH NOTHING SIGNED: Trump demanded Iran 'PUT UP THE WHITE FLAG OF SURRENDER,' said 'I HAVE NO TIME SCHEDULE,' threatened to 'BOMB THE S*** OUT OF' OMAN — the war's own mediator — and said he liked 'THE IDEA OF DECLARING [THE STRAIT] A TERRITORY,' calling the blockade a 'WALL OF STEEL.' ON AUGUST 20 THE ADMINISTRATION NAMED ITS NEXT PHASE AND IT IS FINANCIAL: VANCE declared a 'NEW PHASE' of economic pressure as 'THE BEST WAY TO ULTIMATELY ACCOMPLISH THE FINAL OBJECTIVE,' BESSENT promised 'THE TOUGHEST SANCTIONS IN HISTORY' and 'THE GREATEST COORDINATED ECONOMIC ISOLATION IN THE HISTORY OF THE WORLD' with details due MONDAY AUGUST 24 — and said the US LIKELY WOULD NOT RESTART LARGE-SCALE COMBAT. IRAN AND OMAN ANNOUNCED A HORMUZ ARRANGEMENT ON AUGUST 6-7 BARRING US AND ISRAELI VESSELS, FINING VIOLATORS UP TO 20% OF CARGO VALUE and denying passage to states deemed to have damaged Iran until compensated; WASHINGTON REJECTED IT. FORCE WAS USED AT SEA: a US Navy helicopter put TWO HELLFIRES INTO THE ENGINE ROOM OF THE CONTAINER SHIP VELA NOVA on AUGUST 11; CENTCOM's blockade tally reached 67 VESSELS REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED by AUGUST 20. THE UAE DETECTED TWO IRANIAN BALLISTIC MISSILES ON AUGUST 18 AND SUSPENDED ALL TRADE WITH IRAN ON AUGUST 19, cutting a partner supplying 30%+ OF IRANIAN IMPORTS. USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN LEFT AFTER 252 DAYS WITHOUT A PORT CALL and USS GEORGE WASHINGTON RELIEVED IT — A ROTATION, NOT A SURGE, CARRIER PRESENCE UNCHANGED AT ONE. KHARG WAS THROTTLED, NOT TAKEN: terminals idle with 16-17 TANKERS WAITING, one DARK VLCC LOADING AUGUST 12, the first since JULY 18. BRENT ~$93.40-$95.29 on AUGUST 21, a second weekly gain above 5%; HORMUZ TRANSITS 1-13 A DAY AGAINST A 73/DAY BASELINE; PENTAGON CASUALTIES 775 (18 KILLED, 757 WOUNDED) after a 60-WOUNDED BATCH UPDATE. PEZESHKIAN: 'IT IS BETTER THAT WE BRING THE WAR TO AN END NOW AS WE ARE IN A POSITION OF POWER AND DIGNITY.' STILL AIR, NAVAL AND NOW FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED. (Axios; NPR; Al Jazeera; CBS News; NBC News; CNBC; The Washington Post; Stars and Stripes; USNI News; CENTCOM; GlobalSecurity.org Day 173; straits.live; TradingEconomics, August 1-22, 2026.) || AUGUST 2 (Day 157): THE WEEKEND THE CAMPAIGN WAS TO BEGIN PASSED WITHOUT IT. Through the end of AUGUST 1 NO NEW US STRIKE WAVE on Iranian territory was reported, and the reporting verb reverted from 'has ordered' to 'is weighing': AL JAZEERA recorded that Trump 'HAD NOT YET AUTHORIZED THE POTENTIAL TWO-WEEK OPERATION TARGETING TEHRAN'S ELECTRICITY GRID,' and ABC NEWS reported that CENTCOM HAD PREPARED A TWO-WEEK AIR CAMPAIGN while some administration officials favoured 'A SHORTER, MORE SEVERE SALVO' to advance negotiations — an internal argument between two AIR options. THE CYCLE'S LARGEST NEW FACT IS A CEILING: CSIS puts remaining US stocks at FEWER THAN 827 PATRIOT INTERCEPTORS (from ~2,200 pre-war) and FEWER THAN 278 THAAD (from 452) — MORE THAN 60% EXPENDED — with THREE SOURCES TELLING CNN the estimates track internal government figures, production at 183 THAAD a year and ~3.5 years contract-to-delivery, THREE-PLUS YEARS TO REBUILD against $18.2BN allocated within a $67BN FY2026 emergency request, and GEN. DAN CAINE reported to have WARNED PRIVATELY about shortages, cited as a restraint on broader strikes. WASHINGTON MOVED PEOPLE INSTEAD OF MUNITIONS: US EMBASSIES IN AT LEAST TEN COUNTRIES (UAE, QATAR, OMAN, IRAQ, JORDAN, ISRAEL, KUWAIT, SAUDI ARABIA, BAHRAIN, EGYPT) told Americans to 'CONSIDER DEPARTING' or 'BE PREPARED TO DEPART,' citing 'THE POTENTIAL FOR UNFORESEEN ESCALATION.' UKMTO logged TWO TANKER INCIDENTS OFF OMAN — an explosion 21nm NE of KHASAB (no damage) and a projectile strike 11nm NE of LIMAH that damaged the ENGINE ROOM and left the vessel NOT UNDER COMMAND — both UNATTRIBUTED. HORMUZ TRANSITS FELL 77% IN A DAY (22 to 5); straits.live held 11% of normal, 371 STRANDED, 36 AIS-DARK, WAR-RISK INSURANCE 8.0× (~$2.5M/VLCC), 2% ODDS OF REOPENING BY AUG 15. IRAN DECLARED A 'COMPREHENSIVE PLAN' naming US ENERGY INFRASTRUCTURE IN THE REGION and ISRAELI CRITICAL INFRASTRUCTURE as targets (senior official via TASNIM), against a MARCH PRECEDENT that cost Gulf energy UP TO $58BN ACROSS 80+ FACILITIES. MAJ. GEN. ALI ABDOLLAHI: the US is 'RAPIDLY MOVING DOWN THE PATH OF ESCALATING TENSIONS' and states shielding America 'WILL BURN IN THE FIRE OF WAR.' THE SENATE REJECTED A WAR POWERS RESOLUTION 49-50 (Collins, Murkowski and Paul crossing over; Fetterman the lone Democrat blocking). US INTELLIGENCE ASSESSED IRAN LIKELY BEHIND CYBERATTACKS ON MUNICIPAL WATER SYSTEMS IN 7+ STATES, INCLUDING 30+ MINNESOTA SYSTEMS. BRENT SETTLED $87.93 (+1.21%), JULY +22.86% — revising down the $90.24 print logged the prior cycle. STILL AIR AND MARITIME ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO RELIEF ARG, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED. (Al Jazeera; ABC News; CBS News; CNN; CSIS; Military Times; EA WorldView; UKMTO via Gulf News and SCMP; Tasnim; TradingEconomics; straits.live, July 31 – August 1, 2026.) || AUGUST 1 (Day 156): THE UNITED STATES PICKS ITS INSTRUMENT — AND IT IS AIRPOWER AGAINST ENERGY, NOT MARINES AGAINST KHARG. THE WALL STREET JOURNAL reported that TRUMP HAS ORDERED ANOTHER WAVE OF STRIKES \"WITH THE AIM OF FORCING THE ISLAMIC REPUBLIC'S SURRENDER,\" expected to last SEVERAL DAYS and able to begin AS SOON AS THIS WEEKEND. CBS NEWS named the target classes: POWER PLANTS, REFINERIES, ELECTRICITY INFRASTRUCTURE ACROSS TEHRAN (under high-level discussion, no Friday decision) and BRIDGES OF DUAL MILITARY-CIVILIAN USE — with strikes possible throughout the weekend and discussion of CONCLUDING BEFORE MARKETS OPEN MONDAY. The plan was raised at TRUMP'S CAMP DAVID CABINET MEETING: \"WE'LL BE HITTING THEM VERY HARD. AT SOME POINT, THEY'RE GOING TO SAY, 'WE JUST CAN'T TAKE IT ANYMORE.'\" THE ORDER'S STATUS IS ITSELF CONTESTED: WSJ says ordered; CBS says TRUMP HAS NOT GIVEN FINAL AUTHORISATION; CNN's two officials say the strikes COULD BE CALLED OFF; an ISRAELI OFFICIAL says \"Israel is UNAWARE OF A DECISION to restart full military operations, nor has been requested of Israel to join any military actions against Iran\" against US sources saying Israel was notified and coordinating. White House political aides were \"STRONGLY OPPOSED.\" TRUMP: \"I'M LOSING FAITH IN THEM BECAUSE THEY DO LIE,\" while not ruling out a deal. IRAN ANSWERED BY DRONE ACROSS THE GULF: its army and the IRGC claimed ONE-WAY ATTACK DRONES against AHMAD AL-JABER and ALI AL-SALEM (Kuwait), SHEIKH ISA (Bahrain) — \"one of the most important US military installations in the Gulf region\" — and AL AZRAQ (Jordan), targeting AIRCRAFT SHELTERS, SATELLITE COMMUNICATIONS, POWER GENERATORS, NAVIGATION SYSTEMS and EQUIPMENT STORAGE, framed as revenge for an IRANIAN SU-24 PILOT killed in February; Iran claimed \"SIGNIFICANT DAMAGE\" and NO US OR BAHRAINI COMMENT FOLLOWED. US WOUNDED ROSE TO 685 (+32), KIA 18. CENTCOM CONFIRMED IT IS INVESTIGATING the Qeshm deaths of a TWO-YEAR-OLD AND THE CHILD'S PARENTS — spokesman: \"The U.S. military never targets civilians, unlike Iranian forces.\" ARAGHCHI DENIED DAMIETTA (\"Egypt is an important friend and partner\") and alleged an ISRAELI FALSE FLAG; EGYPT'S DIAA RASHWAN PUBLICLY REJECTED a WSJ report that Cairo blames Iran, with drone debris under forensic analysis. BRENT $90.24 (+3.87%), CLOSING JULY UP ~24% — ITS STRONGEST MONTH SINCE MARCH; DIESEL SET ANOTHER WAR HIGH AT $5.3530, regular $4.1060. HORMUZ TRANSITS HIT A TWO-WEEK HIGH OF 28 (JULY 29) AS LNG TRAFFIC RESUMED after a fortnight; straits.live still assesses 11% OF NORMAL THROUGHPUT, 1,364 STRANDED, 85 DARK TANKERS, WAR-RISK INSURANCE 8.0x PEACETIME. STILL AIR AND MARITIME ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO RELIEF ARG, NO DRAFT. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (The Wall Street Journal via The Times of Israel and Bloomberg; CBS News; CNN; Axios; Haaretz; ABC News; CNBC; Al Jazeera; Middle East Monitor; IranWire; Press TV; The Defense Post; Democracy Now!; TradingEconomics; straits.live; S&P Global; AAA, July 31, 2026.) || JULY 31 (Day 155): THE US GOES BACK TO BOMBING IRAN ITSELF. CENTCOM \"successfully completed a HEAVY WAVE of strikes against Iran,\" hitting \"DOZENS of Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) targets... including military command centers, missile and drone facilities, COASTAL SURVEILLANCE AND DEFENSE SITES, and MARITIME CAPABILITIES\" over roughly TWO HOURS — the FIRST STRIKE ON IRANIAN SOIL SINCE JULY 24 and, per a US official, \"ABOUT TWICE THE SIZE OF THE PREVIOUS\" bombardment. THE TARGET MAP IS A COASTLINE: Bandar Abbas, Qeshm, Kish, Abu Musa, three Bushehr cities, Kazerun, Farashband, Abadan and Ahvaz (7 sites, power out) — BUT NOT KHARG. IRNA: 3 KILLED, 2 WOUNDED ON QESHM, reported as a couple and their TWO-YEAR-OLD CHILD, with children aged 7 and 9 wounded; 3 IRGC personnel also reported killed. IRGC: \"the aggressor will be punished TODAY\"; states aiding the US will \"receive a harsh response\"; Iran retains \"FULL CONTROL\" of the Strait where \"a stranger who has come from thousands of kilometres away will not be allowed to interfere.\" IRGC CLAIMS THREE F-35s DESTROYED AT AL AZRAQ and US personnel killed; CENTCOM denies any aircraft destroyed or damaged and is SILENT ON THE CASUALTY CLAIM. THE WAR WIDENS TWICE: an Iranian strike killed a worker at a CHINESE COMPANY'S BUILDING in northern Kuwait (\"Iranian aggression\" — spokesman Saud Al-Atwan), and an UNCLAIMED DRONE hit the US-owned FSRU ENERGOS WINTER and the LNG carrier GASLOG SALEM at EGYPT'S DAMIETTA — the FIRST ATTACK ON EGYPTIAN SOIL of the war, on an IMPORT terminal; Egypt's cabinet confirmed a drone and named no one; Trump blamed Iran without evidence. SAUDI DEFENCE MINISTER PRINCE KHALID BIN SALMAN met Trump and Vance ONE DAY AFTER flying strikes in Iraq, carrying MBS's message: self-defence, but diplomacy is \"a more fruitful path\" and NETANYAHU IS PUSHING ESCALATION — while lobbying for F-35s. BAGHDAD called the July 28 strikes \"a flagrant violation of Iraq's sovereignty\" and summoned BOTH the US chargé d'affaires and the Iranian ambassador. BRENT eased below $90 ($89.45, −1.11%) after a 7.9% surge; DIESEL SET ANOTHER WAR HIGH at $5.339, regular $4.098. STRAIT METRICS SHOW AN APPARENT MEASUREMENT DISCONTINUITY (35 transits, 1,357 stranded, 9 dark vs 10-13/339/68 a day earlier) — recorded as printed and flagged. STILL AIR AND MARITIME ONLY — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no relief ARG, no draft. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (CENTCOM public release; Al Jazeera; CNBC; NBC News; The Hill; The Jerusalem Post; The Washington Times; Al Arabiya English; Business Recorder; The National; Seatrade Maritime; Euronews; Just Security; Semafor; Rudaw; straits.live; AAA, July 29-30, 2026.) || JULY 30 (Day 154): THE WAR RESUMES ON THREE RUNGS AND THE US RETALIATION LANDS IN IRAQ WITH SAUDI JETS. IRAN CLAIMS WHAT IT WOULD NOT CLAIM A DAY EARLIER: the IRGC said its air force targeted MUWAFFAQ SALTI AIR BASE and a CENTCOM centre in Jordan, where air defences intercepted FIVE missiles — 'As long as threats against the Islamic Republic of Iran continue and illegal and vicious actions by American forces against our interests continue, the resistance will continue.' THE IRGC THEN STRUCK AND STOPPED THREE TANKERS IN HORMUZ, its first claimed shipping strikes since the pause, saying they 'continued to move along an unsafe and illegal route, ignoring our warnings' — formally triggering Trump's July 22 one-bridge-or-power-plant doctrine, which was NOT invoked by the cycle close. TRUMP: Iran is 'GOING TO GET A BEATING'; 'WE'LL BE HITTING THEM HARD'; the US 'destroyed most of' Iran and will 'FINISH THE JOB.' BUT THE ACTUAL US KINETIC ACT WENT TO IRAQ: CENTCOM 'and the SAUDI ARABIAN ARMED FORCES conducted precision strikes in Iraq, July 28, against Iran-aligned terrorists that the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) directed to attack U.S. forces and Saudi energy infrastructure' — logistics hubs and weapons stores, after 30+ IRGC-directed drone attacks in 72 hours; RIYADH'S FIRST CLAIMED STRIKES INSIDE IRAQ OF THE WAR, under ARTICLE 51. PMF: 20 KILLED, 32 WOUNDED across Baghdad, Wasit, Nineveh, Basra, Kirkuk, Karbala and Diyala; the Iraqi presidency 'categorically rejected any attacks in Iraqi territory'; PM ALI AL-ZAIDI convened an emergency security meeting. IRAN REJECTS OMAN'S 50-50 PLAN and counterproposes ONE LANE ENTIRELY IN IRANIAN WATERS plus part of the other, with a reported $1M-PER-SHIP 'SERVICE FEE'; GHARIBABADI: 'If the Strait of Hormuz returns to its previous state, our success in this war is not complete,' 'there was no begging from the Iranian delegation,' and mine-clearing vessels 'WILL BE CONSIDERED LEGITIMATE TARGETS.' BRITAIN AND FRANCE REFUSE TO LEAD HEGSETH'S NAVAL COALITION absent an enduring ceasefire. REUTERS: CHINA TO SHIP UP TO 400 QW-12/FN-16 MANPADS TO IRAN WITHIN WEEKS, $60-70M via a Hong Kong intermediary (Beijing: 'completely groundless'; Pakistan: 'absolutely concocted and false'). BRENT JUMPS BACK ABOVE $90 (straits.live $90.40, +3.43%) after a July 28 close of $84.09; pump $4.091 regular, $5.329 diesel (war high). BACKLOG EASES A SECOND DAY: 339 stranded (from 405), 68 dark (from 77); PortWatch still 10 transits vs 88 baseline. PENTAGON: 'Operation Epic Fury has concluded,' no end date, total wounded 642. STILL AIR/MARITIME ONLY — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no relief ARG, and the DRAFT RULE WAS WITHDRAWN. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (CENTCOM public release; Al Jazeera; IranWire; Tasnim; Bloomberg; CNBC; CBS News; Democracy Now; Just Security; POLITICO/E&E News; Reuters via U.S. News; Muscat Daily; straits.live; AAA, July 28-29, 2026.) || JULY 29 (Day 153): THE PAUSE BREAKS — AND IT BREAKS FROM TEHRAN. At 5:45 p.m. ET July 28 CENTCOM said IRGC forces 'launched multiple ballistic missiles from Iran in an attempted surprise attack on U.S. forces' in the Middle East and that 'all Iranian missiles were successfully intercepted'; US forces 'remain vigilant and at a high state of readiness.' Initial estimates: no more than four missiles, trajectory reported toward a US base in JORDAN. No US casualties. Iran issued no claim or explanation. Hours earlier TRUMP HOSTED NETANYAHU — their first meeting since the war began — after publicly rebuffing his PICKAXE MOUNTAIN intelligence: 'I DON'T NEED BIBI TO TELL ME THAT... Bibi's telling me that because he WANTS ME TO STAY INVOLVED.' The closed-door session ran just over an hour with Vance, Rubio and Bessent present; Leavitt called it 'positive and productive,' a senior Israeli source 'excellent and comprehensive... first and foremost Iran' with an 'ironclad commitment' that Iran never get nuclear weapons, and Netanyahu 'one of the best we've ever had.' TZIPI HOTOVELY then said Pickaxe did not come up and that 'the idea that we have some intelligence here is a sort of FAKE NEWS that ran throughout the day' — while Trump said 'WE'LL HAVE TO TAKE OUT PICKAXE... we'll take it very easily' and 'IF THEY DON'T MAKE A DEAL THEN I GO BACK AND I FINISH THE JOB.' ON THE STRAIT: 'WE CONTROL THE STRAIT. Our navy is incredible. NOT ONE SHIP HAS GOTTEN TO IRAN during any blockade' — CENTCOM tally now 18 vessels stopped, 2 disabled, 2 boarded, 20+ warships. OMAN'S GULF-BACKED PLAN offers VOLUNTARY navigation-fund contributions on the Malacca model with NO MANDATORY TOLLS; Anna Kelly: 'Iran cannot toll the Strait, which is an international waterway'; Rubio: 'existing international law.' GHARIBABADI: Iran will take 'ANY ACTION' to keep control and has not requested US negotiations. MOHAJERANI claims 350+ government employees killed and Bushehr Airport destroyed, against Health Minister ZAFARGHANDI's 60 for the southern strikes — two tolls the same day. THE INTERCEPT: 8,000-9,000 Iranian drones/missiles since February, 9 US outposts struck since July 9, interceptor stocks 3+ years from recovery. BRENT slips a third session to ~$86.58 (−1.54%); pump $4.099 regular, $5.321 diesel (war high). BACKLOG EASES FOR THE FIRST TIME: 405 stranded (from 426), 77 dark (from 97), 13 tankers transiting. STILL AIR/MARITIME ONLY — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no relief ARG, no draft. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (CENTCOM via CBS/CNN/ABC/Fox News Digital; The Times of Israel; Ynetnews; Jewish Insider; AGBI; NBC News; IranWire; The Intercept; TradingEconomics; straits.live; AAA, July 28, 2026.) || JULY 28 (Day 152): THE PAUSE HOLDS A THIRD DAY AND THE PENTAGON'S 14TH-NIGHT STRIKE PLAN IS DECLINED — Trump did not authorise a 14th consecutive night of strikes, preferring to let negotiations run. TRUMP: 'I have a lot of patience. I have plenty of time. Plenty of time' — but 'If it doesn't [happen], we go back to doing what we were doing two days ago,' with strikes resuming at GREATER FORCE; to Axios, 'We are in very deep talks with Iran... Not much time. Either it goes fast or not at all,' and on stockpiles, 'We have plenty. We have a lot of ammunition.' A DIRECT FACTUAL SPLIT OPENS ON WHETHER TALKS EXIST: FM spokesman ESMAIL BAQAEI says Iran 'currently have no negotiations with the United States' and that the week's discussions were 'exclusively with Oman'; deputy FM KAZEM GHARIBABADI says the US made 'extreme demands' Iran rejected; the AP reports QATAR- and PAKISTAN-led mediators making significant progress. IRAN'S KHATAM AL-ANBIYA CENTRAL HEADQUARTERS warns the US naval blockade 'WILL BE REGARDED AS AN EXPANSION OF THE WAR IN THE REGION.' The US and UK convene a LONDON CONFERENCE this week on a multinational HORMUZ SHIPPING-PROTECTION COALITION (Hegseth and Gen. Caine may attend; allies to be asked for equipment and personnel) — a MARITIME rung, not a ground one. BRENT COLLAPSES A SECOND SESSION to the $85-90 range (TradingEconomics $90.28, -8.23%; UPI close $88.36); pump prices hold at $4.110 regular / $5.296 diesel. HORMUZ STILL SHUT: 426 vessels stranded, 97 tankers dark, 24 waiting off Kharg. REUTERS/IPSOS: ONE IN THREE Americans back the war — the lowest of the conflict — with 69% saying Trump has not explained its goals; approval 37%. NETANYAHU FLIES OUT SECRETLY from Nevatim amid a reported Iranian threat for a Tuesday 11 a.m. meeting. STILL AIR/MARITIME ONLY — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no relief ARG, no draft. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (Reuters/France24; CBS News; CNBC; Just Security; WANA; Axios; Reuters/Ipsos; TradingEconomics; straits.live; AAA; Times of Israel, July 27, 2026.) || JULY 27 (Day 151): THE PAUSE BECOMES TWO-SIDED AND TWO NIGHTS LONG — no US strikes overnight into July 26 (a Defense Department source: operations are 'ON A HOLD'), and Iran reciprocates publicly ('Since our strategy has essentially been retaliatory, we have also halted our retaliatory operations' — army spokesman Mohammad Akraminia); Bahrain, Jordan and Kuwait report no Iranian attacks. THE REPORTED RATIONALE IS CAPABILITY-SIDE: Axios says CENTCOM commander Gen. BRAD COOPER told the White House the strikes had 'significantly degraded' Iran's anti-shipping capability and the target set was 'MOSTLY EXHAUSTED,' while Gen. DAN CAINE warned on dwindling air-defence intercepts and VP VANCE cautioned against escalating. IRAN-OMAN DEPUTY-FM TALKS in Tehran report PROGRESS on 'shared principles and operational mechanisms' for safe passage 'respecting the sovereign rights of the two coastal states'; Amb. WALTZ says Trump is 'giving diplomacy some space' while 'there's more moving into theater.' BLOCKADE 'IN FULL EFFECT' (12 redirected / 2 disabled / 2 boarded; IRGC stopped 6 with warning shots; one tanker struck a mine). HORMUZ AT A NEAR-TOTAL STOP — ONE vessel and ZERO tankers in the 24 hours to July 25. BRENT PLUNGES >5% TO ~$91; pump $4.111 regular / $5.295 diesel. THE PENTAGON CUTS ITS OFFICIAL IRAN-WAR TOLL from 18 killed / 482 wounded to 14 / 420 by moving 4 deaths and 207 wounded into a new 'OVERSEAS OPERATIONS' category ('anomalies,' 'temporary data disruption'). UKRAINE STRIKES IRAN-LINKED CARGO VESSELS IN THE CASPIAN, killing a sailor. CBS/YouGov: 67% want the war ended, 35% approve of Trump's handling. NETANYAHU AT THE WHITE HOUSE TUESDAY. STILL AIR/MARITIME — and the amphibious rung FELL: the TRIPOLI ARG offloaded ~2,500 Marines of the 31st MEU at Okinawa July 22 with no relief announced. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (Al Jazeera; Fortune/AP; CBS News; CNN; Axios via MEMO; Washington Post; Fox News; Windward; TradingEconomics; AAA; Stars and Stripes; USNI News, July 22-26, 2026.) || JULY 26 (Day 150): THE 13-NIGHT AIR CAMPAIGN STOPS — Iran reports its FIRST NIGHT WITHOUT US STRIKES ('Iran had a peaceful night,' Health Ministry spokesman Hossein Kermanpour) and CENTCOM announces nothing and declines comment. Trump says the US is 'LOCKED AND LOADED' but the threatened 'massive' attack 'MAY BE UNNECESSARY,' calling Iranian negotiators 'by far the most serious that we've seen them' ('that doesn't mean we get there'); bottom line unchanged — 'They cannot have a nuclear weapon.' TWO MEDIATION CHANNELS OPEN: an Omani delegation in Tehran on 'appropriate mechanisms for managing ship traffic in the Strait of Hormuz,' and a Pakistan-led, China-encouraged push to restart US-Iran talks. THE KINETIC CENTRE MOVES TO THE RED SEA: Houthi ballistic/cruise missiles and drones hit Aramco at JIZAN (refinery ablaze) and YANBU in retaliation for Saudi strikes on Hodeidah/Kamaran; 'escalation for escalation.' WSJ reports BAHRAINI AND KUWAITI WARPLANES struck Iranian depots earlier in July with UAE targeting intelligence — KUWAIT calls it 'entirely false.' Blockade enforcement continues (M/T Lavine disabled, M/T Charminar boarded; 12 redirected / 2 disabled since re-imposition). Hormuz still functionally shut (15 transits July 19 vs 88 baseline; ~85 tankers dark). Brent ~$96-98 after the $100.69 July-23 settle; US pump average $4.111. STILL AIR/MARITIME — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; 50,000+ personnel. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (Fortune; Washington Post; Fox News; Al Jazeera; RFE/RL; WSJ; Arab Times, July 24-25, 2026.) || JULY 25 (Day 149): 13TH STRAIGHT NIGHT OF US STRIKES AS TRUMP WEIGHS A 'MASSIVE' ESCALATION 'BIGGER THAN OPERATION EPIC FURY' (no decision) AND IRAN REJECTS AN IRAQI-PM-BROKERED CEASEFIRE, refusing any temporary deal that leaves Hormuz control unresolved (Trump: talks continue, Tehran 'getting more serious' but 'need more of the same'). Oil RETREATED ~4% Friday to settle near $97 — biggest one-day drop since late June — after briefly topping $100 ($100.69 close July 23) on the Houthi attack on two Saudi tankers (Incilia, Layla), as crude kept traversing routes and Kazakhstan cut output. The Pentagon is reported readying OPTIONS for 'weeks' of limited ground operations (SpecOps/infantry raids on Kharg + coastal sites) pending Trump's approval; Iran's FM warns of 'repercussions' over Kharg and 'we never accept humiliation.' STILL AIR/MARITIME — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (NPR; CNN; Foreign Policy; Yahoo/CNBC; Fox News, July 24, 2026.) || JULY 24 (Day 148): THE AIR CAMPAIGN REACHES A 12TH STRAIGHT NIGHT AS OIL TOPS $100/BBL FOR THE FIRST TIME SINCE MAY (Brent ~$98.44, +4.6%; WTI ~$90.14) AND THE HOUTHIS MOVE FROM THREAT TO ATTACK, STRIKING SAUDI VESSELS IN THE RED SEA — a live second chokepoint atop the functionally shut Hormuz ('no way out'). Trump REFUSES a new ceasefire ('they need more of the same'), tells Axios Iran hasn't 'received enough pain yet' and is weighing a 'massive attack'; UN's Guterres warns the war is 'getting out of control... teetering on the edge of the unimaginable.' A new US service member killed (northern Iraq drone detonation); ~100 troops injured since July 7. STILL AIR/MARITIME — no landing, no Kharg seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel. Predicted US GROUND seizure remains DISCONFIRMED. (CNN; CNBC; UN News; Axios via Sinclair, July 23, 2026.) || JULY 23 (Day 147): THE AIR CAMPAIGN REACHES AN 11TH STRAIGHT NIGHT (~75 MIN) AS WASHINGTON COOLS ON DIPLOMACY. Rubio calls Tehran 'not serious' about talks; Trump dismisses ceasefire calls and vows to 'bomb and destroy ONE BRIDGE OR POWER PLANT' for every Hormuz ship attack, leaving the Qatar/Pakistan 10-day proposal hanging. Brent surges ~5% past $95/bbl (highest in ~6 weeks) as the Houthi Bab el-Mandeb blockade leaves oil 'no way out'; only 3 vessels cross Hormuz Tuesday. Pentagon identifies a 4th recently-killed service member (cumulative US KIA ~18); Hegseth puts the war's cost at ~$37.5B as Trump seeks ~$70B more. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged, with Trump saying 'we have other people that will do the ground campaign for us.' The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 21 (Day 145): THE AIR WAR REACHES A NINTH-TO-TENTH STRAIGHT NIGHT AND STRIKES A SECOND NUCLEAR-ADJACENT SITE (BUSHEHR). Iran immobilizes a SECOND tanker at Hormuz and claims four vessels intercepted; Kuwait's power-and-water plant burns a third day (cumulative 11 killed / 187 wounded), Bahrain takes fresh strikes (3 killed, 51 wounded). Brent crosses ~$90; only ~8 ships transit Hormuz. The Intercept reports US casualties (~446 killed/wounded) exceed the Pentagon's count. Trump vows to 'hit them very hard tonight... and tomorrow' and won't rule out taking Kharg ('I can't say... it would be foolish'). GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 20 (Day 144): THE WAR CROSSES A THRESHOLD — THE FIRST CONFIRMED US COMBAT DEATHS OF THE RESUMED (POST-MOU) PHASE. An Iranian ballistic-missile/drone strike on a US base in JORDAN (July 17) killed 2 US service members (1 missing, 4 wounded), and CENTCOM reported a further US service member killed in IRAQ (July 19); Al Jazeera cited a cumulative ~16 US KIA since late February (prior standing briefing count 15/13-combat; outlets differ). The US answered with an EIGHTH-night 'punishment' wave (~5.5 hrs from ~6pm ET) that widened into KHUZESTAN (Shadegan) and — a first for the war — struck an under-construction NUCLEAR plant (Darkhovin; IAEA: no nuclear material present, no radiological risk), alongside Sirik and Qeshm Island. Iran hit Kuwait's power-and-desalination complex for a SECOND straight day (fires, power disruption), fired at Jordan (Aqaba; 3 intercepted), Bahrain (nationwide sirens) and Qatar (a child wounded by intercept shrapnel), and declared the US-Iran MOU 'suspended'; the UAE condemned the Gulf strikes as a 'blatant violation of sovereignty.' Oil stayed elevated (Brent ~$88, July 17 close; no corroborated fresh July 19-20 settle) with Hormuz functionally shut. IRGC adviser Rezaei's 'full-scale offensive' ultimatum window (~July 19-20) lapsed without an Iranian ground offensive. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED EVEN THOUGH THE US-CASUALTY TRIPWIRE WAS CROSSED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. Trump was reported to 'float a ground campaign' (declared intent), but the US response was an intensified AIR/MARITIME campaign (eighth night, nuclear-plant strike), not a landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. (Al Jazeera; Fox News; The National; ABC News; Newsweek, July 18-19, 2026.) || JULY 19 (Day 143): THE AIR WAR DEEPENS INTO AN EIGHTH STRAIGHT NIGHT AND WIDENS INTO CENTRAL IRAN. The US uses MANNED FIGHTER JETS for the first time (~650 km inland to Yazd; Mehr says strikes fell outside the city, no casualties there; ~3 killed, 8 wounded in Hormozgan), re-strikes the disabled tanker Belma at Kharg, and SURGES DOZENS MORE AERIAL-REFUELING TANKERS to Israel as Trump weighs a 'broader campaign.' IRGC adviser Rezaei warns of 'full-scale offensive operations' if strikes continue ~2-3 more days (~July 19-20). Oil stays elevated at multi-week highs (Brent last reliably ~$88; an unverified ~$113 figure not corroborated); Hormuz functionally shut. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The US is widening the AIR/MARITIME campaign, not landing troops; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed.  || JULY 18 (Day 142): THE US-IRAN FIGHT ENTERS A SEVENTH STRAIGHT NIGHT. The US levels southern Iranian infrastructure (six Hormozgan bridges, an airport, rail, power; >=7 killed, 20 wounded) while Iran WIDENS its retaliation — hitting a Kuwaiti desalination-and-power plant (several Kuwaiti ground-forces members wounded), firing at Qatar and Jordan, and killing at least 8 US-backed Kurds (Komala) in Iraq. The Treasury's Iranian-oil sanctions waiver expires (July 17); Brent surges to ~$88 (WTI ~$82.49) and Hormuz falls below 5% of pre-war transits ('worst case scenario'). An IRGC commander warns of 'full-scale offensive operations.' GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged; Marines used only for at-sea boardings. The US asserts control of the Strait via blockade + air + maritime interdiction + sanctions snapback, still NOT a ground landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed.  || JULY 17 (Day 141): THE US-IRAN FIGHT ENTERS A SIXTH STRAIGHT DAY. The US WIDENS its strikes into NORTHERN Iran (command centers, missile sites) and, under the re-imposed blockade, DISABLES an unladen tanker HEADED FOR KHARG ISLAND that was trying to run the blockade — a Kharg-adjacent maritime interdiction, not a landing. Trump tells Fox the US will 'keep the Strait' and be its 'Guardian Angel' (and be 'reimbursed'); FM Araghchi retorts Iran is 'the GUARDIAN of the Strait and will remain so FOREVER.' Oil holds below $85 (Brent ~$84.95 July 15 settle; WTI >$80) with Hormuz traffic grinding back to/below pre-MOU pace (~21 transits Tuesday; running toll ~56 incidents, 17 seafarer deaths); talks stay in tatters. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The US asserts control of the Strait via blockade + air + maritime interdiction (now reaching Kharg-bound shipping), still NOT a ground landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 16 (Day 140): WITH THE NAVAL BLOCKADE BACK ON, THE US RUNS A FIFTH STRAIGHT NIGHT OF STRIKES and — in a US combat FIRST — hits the Bandar Abbas naval base with one-way attack SEA DRONES (three 'Corsair' USVs); within ~17 hours of restarting the blockade the US 'redirected' two commercial vessels and struck a tanker trying to skirt it. US strikes killed ≥7 Iranian troops at a Sistan-Baluchestan barracks (260+ wounded). Iran's IRGC threatened to halt ALL regional energy exports ('either for everyone or for no one'), warned it could block more seaways, and struck Jordan (3 missiles downed), Kuwait and Bahrain. Oil HELD its one-month high but did not spike further — Brent settled ~$84.95/bbl (+22c), WTI ~$79.60 — still >15% above pre-war; ~21 ships transited Hormuz (running toll ~56 incidents, 17 seafarer deaths); talks stalled. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The US now asserts control of the Strait via blockade + air + UNMANNED-MARITIME strike, still NOT a ground landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 15 (Day 139): THE US RE-IMPOSES ITS NAVAL BLOCKADE OF IRANIAN PORTS and Trump announces — then the SAME DAY reverses — a 20% 'toll' on Hormuz cargo, framing the US as the Strait's 'guardian'; Brent surges above $85/bbl (highest since June 15) as US CENTCOM runs a FOURTH straight night of strikes (Bushehr, Chah Bahar, Jask, Konarak, Abu Musa, Bandar Abbas) and Iran hits three more tankers (Stolt Magnesium; UAE-owned Mombasa B and Al Bahyah — 1 Indian crewman killed, ~8 wounded, 3 missing). This is the sharpest US coercion of the chokepoint yet — but the instruments are the NAVAL BLOCKADE (20+ warships, hundreds of aircraft) and AIR strikes, NOT a ground seizure: no US landing, port seizure, Kharg assault, new ARG/MEU order, or draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged; indirect talks (Qatar/Pakistan/Oman) continue. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed — even as the US moves closer to coercive control of the Strait, it does so from the sea and air, not with troops. NOTE: 'blockade lifted' streak ENDS — the US restarted the blockade July 14 (4pm ET). || Iran's IRGC Strait-of-Hormuz closure runs into a THIRD DAY (July 14 / Day 138) as Brent jumps above $78 (highest since June 22) and Washington floats an off-ramp: US officials say Tehran privately blamed the tanker strikes on an 'errant' hardliner faction and expect FM Araghchi to acknowledge, after Oman talks, that the strikes 'were a mistake' (analysts: 'implausible but convenient'); a further US-Iran round (Vance/Kushner/Witkoff/Rubio) is reported for Oman on Saturday. MOU BREACHED-NOT-CANCELLED / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 26. The US answer stayed AIR/stand-off strikes plus diplomacy; no US landing, port seizure, Kharg assault, new ARG/MEU order, or draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The coercion at the chokepoint is again Iran's, the US response air/diplomatic — the imminent-US-ground-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted. || Iran's IRGC Strait-of-Hormuz closure enters a SECOND DAY as Washington and Tehran publicly dispute whether it is open (US CENTCOM: the Strait 'is open... traffic is flowing'; Iran's Persian Gulf Strait Authority: passage 'is currently not possible'), with vessel-tracking at ~33-35% of pre-war; the IRGC's July 11 strike on the container ship M/V GFS Galaxy left one crewman missing, and Iran's July 12 multi-state retaliation hit up to five US-partner states (Bahrain, Kuwait, Jordan, Qatar, Oman; Qatar reported 3 wounded incl. a child) — July 13: DAY 137 / MOU BREACHED-NOT-CANCELLED / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 25. The US answer stayed AIR/stand-off strikes plus diplomacy (Qatar/Pakistan mediation; a further round reported possible next week, Switzerland floated); no US landing, port seizure, Kharg assault, new ARG/MEU order, or draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged; Brent held near $76/bbl. The coercion at the chokepoint is again Iran's, the US response air/diplomatic — the imminent-US-ground-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted. || Iran's IRGC unilaterally RE-CLOSES the Strait of Hormuz ('closed until further notice… until regional interference by the US ceases') after firing warning shots at a vessel on an 'unapproved route' — hours after Oman floats a two-corridor transit plan and Washington demands Tehran publicly declare the Strait open (US: Iran 'does not control' it) — July 12: DAY 136 / MOU BREACHED-NOT-CANCELLED / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 24. No major new US-Iran kinetic exchange was confirmed for July 11-12; the US held a 'strike-then-pause for diplomacy' posture while Pakistan/Qatar pressed mediation. Brent held above $76 (~5% weekly gain). The imminent-US-ground-seizure / Hormuz-and-Kharg thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — the force at the chokepoint is again IRAN's (a unilateral closure and warning shots), and the US answer is air and diplomacy, not a landing. || Breach-retaliation spike gives way to a DIPLOMACY-FORWARD PAUSE: after the July 7-9 two-sided regional exchange, US officials say Washington is 'striking then pausing to let diplomacy work,' Iran reportedly seeks a deal, and Pakistan/Qatar reconvene the parties — even as Trump posts the war's sharpest seizure threat ('we will be taking Kharg Island… and assume total control of their Oil and Gas Markets') — July 11: DAY 135 / MOU BREACHED-NOT-CANCELLED / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 23. No major new US-Iran kinetic exchange was confirmed for July 10-11; Kharg was struck only from the air (oil terminals spared), no landing or port seizure was ordered, no ARG/MEU order or draft followed, and ~50,000 US personnel were unchanged. Brent eased toward $77 and Hormuz tanker traffic was near a standstill (~2 transits July 9). The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — even at peak takeover rhetoric, it is Iran, not the US, that has used force at the chokepoint, and the US answered from the air. || Breach-retaliation cycle goes TWO-SIDED and REGIONAL: Iran retaliates across the Gulf (Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain, Jordan), US runs a ~90-target second-day wave, Trump says 'we attacked Kharg Island' and 'maybe we'll take over Kharg Island' — yet by July 10 mediators reconvene and the exchange still has not left the AIR/MARITIME rungs — July 10: DAY 134 / MOU BREACHED-NOT-CANCELLED / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 22. On July 9 Iran's IRGC hit four US-partner states (Patriot site in Kuwait, early-warning system in Qatar, fuel tanks in Bahrain, a US C2 node and Al-Azraq air base in Jordan; 10 ballistic missiles), mostly intercepted (one stable injury in Kuwait, debris-only damage in Jordan); the US answered with ~90 targets (~14 killed in Iran); Trump said US forces 'attacked Kharg Island' and 'maybe we'll take over Kharg Island' while deliberately sparing its oil terminals and doubting US 'stomach' for boots on the ground. Brent eased from $78.02 back toward $77. By July 10 Pakistan and Qatar were making fresh contacts to halt strikes and salvage the MOU (which Pakistan expected to hold), and Iran had reportedly sought a new deal; talks paused, not terminated. Every US ground indicator stayed at zero — no troops in Iran, no Kharg landing, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — Iran, not the US, is using force at the chokepoint, now also against the Gulf states. || Ceasefire declared 'OVER' by Trump, then walked back the same day; largest post-MOU strike wave stays AIR/MARITIME — ground rung unchanged — July 9: DAY 133 / CEASEFIRE 'OVER' (RHETORICALLY) / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 21. On July 8 US CENTCOM announced 'additional strikes' (aggregating to 80+ targets and 60+ IRGC small boats plus air-defense, C2, coastal-radar, surveillance and anti-ship-missile sites), and Trump, at the NATO Ankara summit, declared the ceasefire and MOU 'over' ('a waste of time'; Iran 'vicious, violent'; 'every time they hit us, we hit them 20') and threatened to bomb/blockade Iran again — then walked it back hours later ('I don't think it's going to start again'). Brent settled +5.2% at $78.02/bbl (eased on the walk-back). Even at this rhetorical peak the exchange stayed AIR and MARITIME — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 21). Khamenei was buried at Mashhad's Imam Reza shrine July 9, closing the state funeral; new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei still absent. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — Iran, not the US, is using force at the chokepoint. || Kinetic cycle RESUMES — Iran attacks three tankers, US answers with air strikes and an oil-waiver revocation; ground rung still unchanged — July 8: DAY 132 / CEASEFIRE DAY 92 (BREACHED) / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 20. The five-day off-the-kinetic streak broke on July 7: Iran's IRGC attacked three tankers near Hormuz (Qatari LNG carrier Al-Rekayyat, Saudi supertanker Wedyan, and a drone-hit tanker) to enforce its 'designated routes'; US CENTCOM launched 'a series of powerful strikes' (its largest post-MOU package) on air-defense, coastal, SAM, anti-ship-cruise-missile, drone and port sites near Bandar Abbas/Qeshm/Bandar Khamir/Sirik; and OFAC revoked Iran's oil-sales waiver (wind-down July 17). Iran called it a 'blatant violation' of the MOU and vowed 'decisive actions'; talks stay paused for the funeral week. Brent spiked ~5.5% to ~$76/bbl. The exchange stayed AIR and MARITIME — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 20). Khamenei's funeral crossed into Iraq (Najaf/Karbala July 8) ahead of burial at Mashhad July 9; new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei still absent. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — Iran, not the US, is using force at the chokepoint. || Funeral rites move to Qom; US talks stay paused; Hormuz governed by negotiation and Iranian toll claims — July 7: DAY 131 / CEASEFIRE DAY 91 / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 19. The war ran a fifth straight day off the kinetic track. After the July 6 main Tehran procession (projected up to 20 million mourners), the cortege for slain Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei reached Qom (Jamkaran mosque, Fatima Masoumeh shrine) on July 7, ahead of Najaf/Karbala July 8 and burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad July 9. New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (named March 9) still had not appeared publicly — reporting now ties his absence both to an Israeli assassination threat and to Feb 28 strike injuries (US officials earlier: 'wounded and likely disfigured') — keeping the who-runs-Iran question live. US-Iran talks stayed paused for the funeral week (Doha round: 'positive progress,' no breakthrough). On Hormuz, Iran maintained mid-August transit 'service fees' (US rejects) and the UK/France backed an Oman-led free-navigation effort. Brent held near pre-war ~$72/bbl (Saudi exports ~90% of pre-war, UAE >3.9M bpd, total Hormuz flows >10M bpd). No new strikes or shipping incidents reported. The ground rung stayed unchanged and de-escalatory — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 19). || Main funeral day; US talks stay paused; Hormuz governed by negotiation and Iranian toll claims — July 6: DAY 130 / CEASEFIRE DAY 90 / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 18. The war stayed off the kinetic track on the central and largest day of Khamenei's six-day state funeral (main Tehran procession Imam Hossein Sq. to Azadi Sq. at 6 a.m. local; Tehran's mayor projected up to 20 million mourners — potentially the city's largest-ever gathering; rites continue to Qom July 7, Najaf July 8, burial in Mashhad July 9). New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (named March 9) still had not appeared publicly, keeping the succession/who-runs-Iran question live. US-Iran talks stayed paused for the funeral week (to resume 'at the earliest possible time' per Qatar). On Hormuz, Iran's ambassador to China reaffirmed mid-August transit 'service fees' (with 'special treatment' for friendly nations; US rejects), Iran warned against a 'military display of extra-regional powers,' and the UK/France backed Oman on free navigation. OPEC+ agreed July 5 to raise August output by 188,000 bpd; oil markets reopened July 6 with Brent near pre-war ~$72/bbl (Saudi exports ~90% of pre-war, UAE >3.9M bpd, total Hormuz flows >10M bpd). The ground rung stayed unchanged and de-escalatory on the US side — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 18). Israel renewed a threat to kill Iran's new supreme leader. No new strikes or shipping incidents July 5-6. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted; live risks are deal durability (post-funeral round) and Hormuz governance (mid-August toll deadline). || Second funeral day; US talks stay paused; a succession question sharpens; Hormuz contest runs on — July 5: DAY 129 / CEASEFIRE DAY 89 / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 17. The war stayed off the kinetic track through a second day of Khamenei's six-day state funeral (Tehran lying-in-state; Qom procession July 5; 15-20 million mourners projected, the largest in Iranian history; delegations from 70+ countries incl. Russia's Medvedev, Pakistan's PM Sharif, Iraq's leaders, the Afghan Taliban FM, Hamas and Hezbollah — but no high-level GCC and no Western invitees). CNN reported the whereabouts of the new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (named March 9) remain unknown, sharpening a succession/who-runs-Iran question. US-Iran talks stayed paused for the funeral week; on Hormuz, Iran's deputy FM issued a 'serious warning' to France and the UK over their naval movements and reaffirmed mid-August 'service fees,' while the UK and France pledged to work with Oman on 'safe transit for ships of all nations.' Oil markets were closed (US Independence-Day weekend; last print Brent ~$72/bbl, July 3; Saudi/UAE exports ~90% of pre-war). The ground rung stayed de-escalatory on the US side — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 17). No new strikes or shipping incidents July 4-5. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted; live risks are deal durability (post-funeral round) and Hormuz governance (mid-August toll deadline). || War moves OFF the kinetic track and into a paused negotiation plus a state funeral — July 4: the two-day Doha round (indirect, via Qatar and Pakistan) concluded July 2 with 'positive progress' but NO breakthrough (a frozen-asset goods-purchase channel, a violations-deconfliction line, a Hormuz-passage focus), while the core disputes stayed open (US rejects any Iranian-led toll mechanism; Tehran asserts joint Iran-Oman sovereignty and plans tolls from mid-August; no frozen funds moved; Ghalibaf denied IAEA access to the bombed Fordow/Natanz/Isfahan sites). The US then agreed to halt talks for a week as Iran opened a SIX-DAY STATE FUNERAL for slain Supreme Leader Khamenei (July 4-9, Tehran→Qom→Najaf/Karbala→Mashhad; 15-20 million mourners expected — the largest in Iranian history; ~30 delegations incl. Russia's Medvedev and China) — DAY 128 / CEASEFIRE DAY 88 / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 16. Oil at a four-month low (Brent ~$71.5/bbl; Trump: 'they've come a long way'); Hormuz traffic recovering (258 vessels/week, up from 138). Iran, not the US, is asserting coercive Strait control (Tehran-designated tanker routes, a 'forceful response' threat, mid-August tolls) — the inverse of a US seizure. Still off the ground rung and de-escalatory on the US side: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU, no draft; USS Boxer ARG disaggregated. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted; the live risk is deal durability — now whether the post-funeral round convenes and whether the toll and inspection disputes are bridged. || Breach-retaliation cycle BREAKS into a stand-down — June 29: the US and Iran agree to halt mutual attacks and let vessels move freely through Hormuz, and Trump announces a fresh high-level meeting in Doha on Tuesday June 30 (Witkoff and Kushner attending; topic re-scoped to the Hormuz standoff), even as Iran's deputy FM Gharibabadi denies any technical talks were scheduled — DAY 124 / CEASEFIRE DAY 84 / BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 12. Iran-Oman open a first Strait-management meeting (demining/tolls disputed); Iran receives $6B of $12B in frozen assets; oil eases toward a four-month low (~$69.70/bbl). Still off the ground rung and de-escalatory on the US side: blockade lifted, USS Boxer ARG disaggregated, Strait reopening by negotiation. The imminent-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted; the live risk is deal durability — now whether the Doha meeting actually convenes.",
   "summary": "AUGUST 28 (Day 183): The Strait declared cleared was attacked again and the American answer was a court. UKMTO Warning 121-26 recorded a tanker hit by an unknown projectile on August 27, the second vessel struck this week, thirty-six hours after Trump declared all mines removed — a projectile, not a mine, confirming Ambrey's assessment that mines were never the primary threat. The Justice Department is reviving maritime prize courts, dormant since WWII, to condemn seized Iranian tankers and cargo as US property with proceeds to the Treasury, to strengthen the blockade and offset the war's cost. Qatar's PM spent August 27 in Tehran meeting Araghchi, Pezeshkian, Ghalibaf and Rezai — the third mediator in four days — while a senior Iranian source told Reuters the Oman agreement 'has not been finalized,' contradicting the IRGC a day earlier. Washington closed the door: 'no talks or conversations' scheduled, Trump 'we don't want to speak to them,' Leavitt on pulling 'every economic lever' behind a blockade 'proven hugely successful,' and the June 17 MOU reportedly abandoned. Al Jazeera put transits at ~5 vessels a day against a ~100/day baseline, nearly 95% down, against Trump's claim of ten million barrels on Tuesday. Oil prints diverged between $87 and $89.48 for Brent and $81-82 for WTI, all on diplomacy rather than supply. Iranian fuel reserves were described as at red alert with queues in Tehran and Mashhad and rationing signalled. Casualties hold at 776. Twenty-seventh consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iran. No landing, no Kharg seizure, no draft order. || AUGUST 27 (Day 182): The United States spent the cycle making the Strait navigable rather than taking it. Axios reported August 25 that Rubio told allied foreign ministers the US is not expected to launch new strikes 'for the time being,' with a second official expecting that posture to hold until after the midterms — the first duration ever attached to the pause. Trump announced all mines cleared from the Strait's international waters under a 'zero tolerance' rule, after underwater drones located 100+ suspected mines and private contractors removed them. Iran and Oman announced a phased framework for a joint temporary navigational corridor and joint mine-clearing, with Gharibabadi setting terms — seven miles wide, entry in Iranian territorial waters, Iranian permission and surveillance, military vessels barred, permanent arrangement in 30-60 days — while insisting the Strait is not reopened. Iranian forces then turned back the Indian tanker HAANA on that same southern route. Brent fell three sessions to ~$86; the rial set a record 2.06m; Tehran's petrol stations ran dry under a 20-litre limit. Pentagon casualties 776. A 25th and 26th night passed with no strike inside Iran. || AUGUST 24 (Day 179): THE SANCTIONS ARRIVED AND SO DID A FEE STATUTE — BOTH BELLIGERENTS SPENT THE CYCLE LEGISLATING AND WRITING RATHER THAN LANDING. Bessent published an FT op-ed on August 23 declaring 'at dawn begins an economic D-Day,' with the detailing news conference set for 2 p.m. ET Monday; hours earlier Iran's parliamentary National Security and Foreign Policy Commission approved Article 3 of its 'Strategic Action to Ensure the Security and Progress of the Strait of Hormuz' plan, imposing service fees on 'authorised' transiting ships payable in rials 'or any other currency desired by the Islamic Republic,' still requiring a full parliamentary vote and Guardian Council review. SNSC Secretary Mohsen Rezaei escalated from selectivity to totality — 'not a single drop of oil' would leave the Persian Gulf if pressure escalates, retaliation 'in a seismic manner' — and for the first time named the bypass routes as targets. President Pezeshkian broke publicly with the Supreme Leader's reported position, saying Iran 'cannot continue with war forever' and defending the June MOU: the first on-record Iranian elite split of the war. A twenty-third consecutive night passed without a confirmed strike inside Iran; CENTCOM reached 70 redirected, 3 disabled, 2 boarded; Brent held at $94.39 across a closed weekend; Pentagon casualties held at 775. The ground tracker carried a correction — carrier presence in CENTCOM is two, not one — and a backfill: CNN reported on June 12 that CJCS Gen. Dan Caine flew from Brussels to CENTCOM headquarters on May 19 to be briefed on sending ground troops into Iran to seize its enriched uranium, and that Trump declined it on casualty grounds before Iran sealed the cache. || AUGUST 23 (Day 178): TWO SOVEREIGNTY CLAIMS OVER THE SAME WATER, NEITHER BACKED BY A LANDING. On August 22 the President said he views the Strait of Hormuz as American territory and re-posted a map labelling it so; the same day Iran granted Iraqi oil tankers permission to transit, the first named state-level exemption of the war, after repeated requests from Baghdad including during parliament speaker Ghalibaf's visit. The strike pause held for a twenty-second night. Tehran's answer to the sanctions package due on Monday was aimed at third parties rather than at Washington: the foreign ministry called it a 'declaration of war on all nations' and SNSC secretary Mohsen Rezaei said any participating country is 'considered an enemy' whose interests will be harmed, naming Gulf oil shipments as the vector and stating that the Strait 'is closed and will not reopen.' The traffic data published this cycle is the strongest open-source evidence yet against the American claim of control: of 236 hulls crossing between August 1 and 19, eighty-three openly took Iran's route and three openly took the US-backed Omani route, with 148 going dark, and Al Jazeera concluded that fear of offending Tehran outweighs Trump's threats. CENTCOM's blockade tally moved to 68 redirected, 3 disabled and 2 boarded. The month's unrecorded human cost inside the chokepoint was entered into the ledger: the Minoan Pioneer's third engineer missing on August 3, an ADNOC tanker struck by missile on August 8, the Navig8 Messi and Tarif struck by drones on August 13, and the Minoan Dignity's chief engineer killed on August 17-18, against ADNOC's cumulative 16 vessels attacked, one killed and twenty injured since February 28. Kharg restarted rather than fell: an NITC VLCC loaded about two million barrels at the Azarpad jetty on August 14 after a roughly 25-day halt, with no US move against the island. Brent near $94, the US pump average $4.102, Pentagon casualties 774-775. The war's next scheduled event is a Treasury news conference. || AUGUST 22 (Day 177): THE LADDER WAS DISMANTLED FROM THE TOP, ON THE RECORD. The reported multi-day campaign against Iran's power plants, refineries and grid — the rung the corpus treats as immediately preceding a ground phase — was cancelled by the President late on August 1, and the cancellation held: no US or Israeli strike inside Iranian territory was confirmed by CENTCOM through August 19, a twentieth consecutive night, with no new Iranian civilian casualties from strikes across that span. The 60-day MOU negotiating window expired on August 17 with nothing signed; Trump demanded surrender, disclaimed any timetable, threatened to bomb Oman, and asserted control of the Strait 'with the blockade.' On August 20 the administration named its successor phase and it is financial — Vance's 'new phase' of economic pressure, Bessent's 'greatest coordinated economic isolation in the history of the world,' and Bessent's statement that large-scale combat likely would not restart. Iran answered with an announced Hormuz regime rather than a fleet: an Oman-brokered arrangement barring US and Israeli vessels and fining violators up to 20% of cargo value, which Washington rejected. The kinetic events of the cycle were maritime and small — Hellfires into the Vela Nova's engine room on August 11, a blockade tally of 67 redirected and 3 disabled, six killed aboard the Tihamah in the Bab al-Mandeb, a sanctioned Iranian shadow-fleet tanker hijacked by Somali pirates. The Gulf littoral moved toward Washington: the UAE detected two Iranian ballistic missiles on August 18 and suspended all trade with Iran on August 19. Naval posture was a relief rather than a reinforcement, with Lincoln out after 252 days without a port call and George Washington in. Kharg was throttled by blockade and insurance rather than seized, with Chinese purchases of Iranian crude falling from 823,000 to 534,000 bpd. Brent near $94; transits between one and thirteen a day against a 73/day baseline; US casualties 775. Iran's economy is the target now: −5.4% GDP projected, inflation near 70%, food inflation 128% point-to-point. Pezeshkian said publicly it is time to end the war 'in a position of power and dignity.' || AUGUST 1 (Day 156): THE COERCIVE PLAN IS STATED IN FULL AND IT HAS NO GROUND COMPONENT. Four outlets reported the same package on July 31: a multi-day bombing campaign against Iranian energy and civil infrastructure — power plants, refineries, Tehran's electricity grid, dual-use bridges — explicitly aimed at forcing surrender, able to begin as soon as the weekend. The WSJ reports it as ordered; CBS reports no final authorisation; an Israeli official says Israel is unaware of a decision. Kharg Island was not named and has never been seized; the March-era option of taking it with two MEUs and elements of the 82nd Airborne existed to supply exactly the leverage this air campaign now seeks. Iran's reply was one-way drones against US facilities at Ahmad al-Jaber, Ali al-Salem, Sheikh Isa and Al Azraq. US wounded reached 685 with 18 killed; CENTCOM is investigating the Qeshm deaths of a two-year-old and the child's parents. Tehran denied Damietta and Cairo rejected reporting that it blames Iran. Brent closed July at $90.24, up roughly 24% on the month; diesel set another war high. Hormuz transits reached a two-week high of 28 as LNG traffic resumed, against a throughput still assessed at 11% of pre-crisis norms. || JULY 31 (Day 155): THE UNITED STATES RESUMES STRIKING IRANIAN TERRITORY, AT ROUGHLY DOUBLE SCALE, ALONG THE COASTLINE. CENTCOM completed a \"heavy wave\" against \"dozens\" of IRGC targets over ~2 hours — the first munitions on Iranian soil since July 24 and about twice the size of the previous bombardment — declaring \"coastal surveillance and defense sites\" and \"maritime capabilities\" among its target categories and hitting Bandar Abbas, Qeshm, Kish, Abu Musa, Bushehr, Kazerun, Farashband, Abadan and Ahvaz. Kharg was not on the list. IRNA reported three killed on Qeshm, described as a couple and their two-year-old child. The IRGC vowed the aggressor \"will be punished today,\" threatened states aiding the US, claimed \"full control\" of the Strait, and asserted it had destroyed three F-35s at Al Azraq — which CENTCOM denied as to aircraft while saying nothing about the claimed US casualties. The war widened to two new places: a fatal Iranian strike on a Chinese company's building in Kuwait, and an unclaimed drone attack on two LNG vessels at Egypt's Damietta, the first attack on Egyptian soil and the first on an energy IMPORT terminal. Saudi Arabia flew strikes in Iraq on July 28 and argued for de-escalation in the Oval Office on July 29. Brent eased below $90 after a 7.9% surge; diesel set another war high at $5.339. Every ground-execution indicator stayed at zero for a 155th day, though the littoral target set is the first ambiguous shaping signal of the week. || JULY 27 (Day 152): THIRD DAY OF TWO-SIDED QUIET, AND THE ESCALATION OPTION THAT REACHED THE PRESIDENT WAS DECLINED. The Pentagon presented Trump a plan for a 14th consecutive night of strikes; he did not authorise it. Trump paired patience with an explicit air-resumption threat ('plenty of time'; 'we go back to doing what we were doing two days ago,' at greater force). Washington and Tehran now disagree on whether negotiations exist at all — Trump says 'very deep talks,' Baqaei says none with the US and 'exclusively with Oman' — while Qatar and Pakistan mediate. Iran's joint command declared the naval blockade 'an expansion of the war in the region.' The US and UK are assembling a multinational maritime coalition for Hormuz in London. Brent fell a second session to $85-90; the Strait stayed shut with 426 vessels stranded and 24 waiting off Kharg; pump prices held at wartime highs. Reuters/Ipsos put war support at one in three, the lowest of the conflict. Every ground-execution indicator stayed at zero for a 152nd day and the July 22 amphibious departure remains unreversed. || JULY 26 (Day 151): THE PAUSE HOLDS AND IRAN MATCHES IT. A second consecutive night without US strikes; a Defense Department source described operations as 'on a hold'; Iran's army spokesman said Tehran had also halted retaliatory operations, and Bahrain, Jordan and Kuwait logged no Iranian attacks. Axios reported CENTCOM commander Gen. Brad Cooper told the White House the target set was 'mostly exhausted' and Iran's anti-shipping capability 'significantly degraded'; Gen. Dan Caine warned on interceptor stocks. Iran-Oman deputy-FM talks in Tehran reported progress on Hormuz transit mechanisms while Baghaei said the Strait's status 'remains unchanged.' The blockade stayed in full effect (12 redirected / 2 disabled / 2 boarded) and traffic effectively stopped — one vessel and zero tankers in 24 hours. Brent fell more than 5% to ~$91; AAA pump prices hit $4.111 regular and $5.295 diesel. The Pentagon moved four July deaths and 207 wounded into a new 'Overseas Operations' category, cutting the official Iran-war toll to 14 killed and 420 wounded. Ukraine struck Iran-linked cargo vessels in the Caspian, killing a sailor and drawing an Iranian threat that it 'cannot go unanswered.' Every ground indicator held at zero and one fell: the Tripoli ARG offloaded ~2,500 Marines of the 31st MEU at Okinawa on July 22 with no relief ARG announced, leaving the Boxer ARG / 11th MEU as the theatre's sole amphibious group. || JULY 25 (Day 150): THE STRIKE STREAK BREAKS. After 13 consecutive nights, Iran reported no US strikes overnight and CENTCOM announced none. Trump paired 'locked and loaded' with the threatened 'massive' attack 'may be unnecessary,' calling Iranian negotiators the most serious he has seen. Mediation thickened on two channels — an Omani delegation in Tehran on Hormuz traffic mechanisms (a co-administration formula Washington rejects) and a Pakistan/China push to restart talks. The war's kinetic energy migrated to the Red Sea: Houthi strikes on Aramco at Jizan and Yanbu, Saudi strikes on Hodeidah and Kamaran, 'escalation for escalation.' WSJ reported the first direct Gulf Arab strikes on Iran (Bahraini and Kuwaiti warplanes, UAE targeting intelligence); Kuwait formally denies it. US blockade enforcement continued (M/T Lavine disabled; M/T Charminar boarded). Hormuz remains functionally shut at 15 transits versus an 88/day baseline; Brent ~$96-98; US pump average $4.111. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; 50,000+ personnel. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed (open-questions: kharg-seizure-total-control-threat-june-2026; gulf-states-direct-strikes-iran-july-2026). || JULY 23 (Day 147): THE AIR CAMPAIGN REACHES AN 11TH STRAIGHT NIGHT (~75 MIN) AS WASHINGTON COOLS ON DIPLOMACY. Rubio calls Tehran 'not serious' about talks; Trump dismisses ceasefire calls and vows to 'bomb and destroy ONE BRIDGE OR POWER PLANT' for every Hormuz ship attack, leaving the Qatar/Pakistan 10-day proposal hanging. Brent surges ~5% past $95/bbl (highest in ~6 weeks) as the Houthi Bab el-Mandeb blockade leaves oil 'no way out'; only 3 vessels cross Hormuz Tuesday. Pentagon identifies a 4th recently-killed service member (cumulative US KIA ~18); Hegseth puts the war's cost at ~$37.5B as Trump seeks ~$70B more. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged, with Trump saying 'we have other people that will do the ground campaign for us.' The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 22 (Day 146): THE WAR WIDENS ON THREE NEW NON-GROUND AXES. (1) Trump threatens to strike Iran's buried 'Pickaxe Mountain' enrichment site 'probably pretty soon... there's not a thing they can do about it' — a nuclear-site AIR-strike threat; Iran warns it would widen the war. (2) Iran-aligned Houthis declare a Bab el-Mandeb blockade, opening a SECOND chokepoint; two Saudi crude tankers U-turn from Yanbu. (3) Qatar and Pakistan (with Egypt/Oman) float a 10-day US-Iran ceasefire and a Hormuz 'middle corridor,' which Iran confirms receiving. The 10th straight night of US strikes (Sirik, Bandar Abbas, Qeshm, Shiraz, Isfahan) is done and an 11th is anticipated; Brent ~$91. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 21 (Day 145): The US-Iran air war reached a NINTH straight night (per CBS, ending ~10pm ET July 19) and a TENTH into July 20-21, and — for the second time in three days — struck a nuclear-adjacent site: US projectiles hit multiple locations in BUSHEHR, home to Iran's only civilian nuclear plant. Iran immobilized a SECOND oil tanker at Hormuz and said it intercepted four vessels over the weekend; Kuwait's power-and-water plant burned a third day (cumulative 11 killed / 187 wounded) and Bahrain took fresh strikes (3 killed, 51 wounded). Brent crossed ~$90/bbl (highest in over a month, ~+30% from early-July lows) and only ~8 ships transited Hormuz (lowest in three weeks). The Intercept reported US casualties (~446 killed/wounded) exceed the Pentagon's count. Trump vowed to 'hit them very hard tonight... and tomorrow' and would not rule out taking Kharg ('I can't say... it would be foolish'). GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The US widened the AIR/MARITIME campaign, not a landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. (CBS News; NPR; The Intercept; Newsweek, July 20, 2026.) || JULY 20 (Day 144): The war crossed a threshold — the first confirmed US COMBAT DEATHS of the resumed (post-MOU) phase. An Iranian ballistic-missile/drone strike on a US base in Jordan (July 17) killed two US service members (one missing, four wounded), and CENTCOM reported a further US service member killed in Iraq (July 19); Al Jazeera cited a cumulative ~16 US KIA since late February (the briefing's prior standing count was 15/13-combat; outlets differ on the exact tally). Framing the eighth-night wave as 'punishment' for the Jordan deaths, US CENTCOM struck for ~5.5 hours from ~6pm ET, widening into Khuzestan (Shadegan) and — for the first time in the war — hitting an under-construction nuclear plant (Darkhovin; the IAEA confirmed no nuclear material was present and no radiological risk), alongside Sirik and Qeshm Island. Iran struck Kuwait's power-and-desalination complex for a second straight day and fired at Jordan (Aqaba), Bahrain and Qatar (a child wounded by intercept debris), then declared the MOU 'suspended'; the UAE condemned the attacks as a 'blatant violation of sovereignty.' Oil held elevated (Brent ~$88 at the July 17 close, +~14% on the week) with Hormuz functionally shut, and Rezaei's 'full-scale offensive' ultimatum window (~July 19-20) lapsed without an Iranian ground offensive. Crucially, the ground rung stayed unchanged even though the US-casualty tripwire — reported as a condition Trump had set for authorizing a Kharg strike — was now crossed: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. Trump was reported to 'float a ground campaign,' but the actual US move was an intensified air/maritime campaign, not a landing — the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. (Al Jazeera; Fox News; The National; ABC News; Newsweek, July 18-19, 2026.) || JULY 18-19 (Day 142-143): The chokepoint war deepened on the AIR rung. The US ran a seventh and then an EIGHTH consecutive night of strikes, first leveling southern Iranian infrastructure (six Hormozgan bridges, an airport, rail, power) and then — for the first time — widening into CENTRAL Iran with MANNED FIGHTER JETS ~650 km inland to Yazd. Iran widened its retaliation (a Kuwaiti desalination-and-power plant; Qatar and Jordan; 8+ US-backed Kurds killed in Iraq), and the US surged dozens more aerial-refueling tankers to Israel as Trump weighed a broader campaign. The disabled tanker Belma was re-struck at Kharg. Oil stayed elevated at multi-week highs (Brent last reliably ~$88) with Hormuz functionally shut (<5% of pre-war transits). An IRGC adviser threatened 'full-scale offensive operations.' Still AIR/MARITIME coercion — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 17 (Day 141): The chokepoint contest ran into a sixth consecutive day, and the US both widened it geographically and tightened the blockade — still on the maritime/air rungs, not the ground one. US CENTCOM expanded strikes into NORTHERN Iran (beyond the southern Hormuz belt), and under the re-imposed blockade disabled an unladen tanker headed for Kharg Island that was trying to run it — a Kharg-adjacent interdiction, not a landing. Trump told Fox News the US would 'keep the Strait,' 'run it,' and be its 'Guardian Angel' (and be 'reimbursed'); FM Araghchi countered that Iran 'has always been the GUARDIAN of the Strait and will remain so FOREVER.' Brent held below $85 (WTI >$80) as Hormuz traffic ground back to/below the pre-MOU pace; the running war toll reached ~56 shipping incidents and 17 seafarer deaths. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero (no troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged); the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. || JULY 15 (Day 139): The chokepoint contest sharpened into the most active US coercion of the war — but still on the maritime/air rungs, not the ground one. On July 14 the US RESTARTED its naval blockade of Iranian ports (CENTCOM: 20+ US Navy warships and hundreds of military aircraft operating in the region), ending the ~27-day 'lifted' period that had run since the June 17 MOU. Trump announced a 20% 'toll' on cargo transiting Hormuz — casting the US as the Strait's 'guardian' and seeking reimbursement from Gulf beneficiaries (Saudi Arabia, UAE, Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait) — then reversed course the same day ('I don't think anybody should be able to charge a fee'), substituting Gulf-state investment deals. US CENTCOM ran a fourth consecutive night of strikes (Bushehr, Chah Bahar, Jask, Konarak, Abu Musa, Bandar Abbas) to 'continue degrading Iranian capabilities used to attack commercial shipping.' Iran answered with three more tanker attacks early July 14 — the chemical tanker Stolt Magnesium (projectile NE of Qalhat) and the UAE-owned oil tankers Mombasa B and Al Bahyah (cruise missiles), the IRGC claiming it hit 'offending supertankers' on a 'mined route' (one Indian crewman killed aboard Mombasa B, ~8 wounded incl. 6 Indians and 2 Ukrainians, 3 missing aboard Al Bahyah) — plus a missile/drone salvo at US assets in Kuwait and Bahrain (Kuwait intercepted 33 drones, 5 cruise missiles, 1 ballistic missile). The GFS Galaxy's missing crewman (from Pune, India) was confirmed dead July 14, his body recovered by the Omani Navy. Brent's September contract surged to ~$85.92/bbl as of 08:00 GMT July 14 (then above $86) — its highest since June 15, up ~19% from pre-conflict levels — as Hormuz crossings dropped by more than half (only 57 transits Fri-Sun). Indirect talks via Qatar, Pakistan and Oman continued (Oman's two-corridor draft pending). GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing/port seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The predicted imminent US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed — the US is asserting coercive control of the Strait via BLOCKADE and AIR power, not a landing. (Al Jazeera; CBS News; CNBC; NPR; CNN; en.wikipedia.org, July 13-14, 2026.) || JULY 14 (Day 138): Iran's July 12 IRGC 'closed until further notice' declaration ran into a third day while both sides signalled a diplomatic off-ramp. US officials briefed that Iran privately called the tanker strikes the work of an 'errant' hardliner faction and that Washington expected FM Araghchi to acknowledge after his Oman meetings that the strikes 'were a mistake' (analysts: 'implausible but convenient'); a further US-Iran round led by Vance, Kushner, Witkoff and Rubio was reported for Oman on Saturday, with Washington insisting talks 'can't progress until ships are assured safe passage.' Brent's September contract jumped >4% to ~$78.82/bbl (highest since June 22) as the sides kept trading strikes; vessel-tracking held transit near a third of pre-war. Firming detail put the M/V GFS Galaxy's crew at 11 Indian nationals (10 rescued, one missing) and reported Iranian navy Lt. Hamidreza Dehghani killed by a US strike at Jask. The US answer stayed air/stand-off strikes plus diplomacy, its naval blockade lifted (Day 26); no US landing, port seizure, Kharg assault, new ARG/MEU order, or draft. The imminent-US-ground-seizure-of-Hormuz/Kharg thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — the coercion at the chokepoint is Iran's. || JULY 12 (Day 136): The Hormuz contest sharpened on the Iranian side. Early July 12 (local) the IRGC Navy declared the Strait 'closed until further notice and until regional interference by the US ceases' after firing warning shots at a vessel on an 'unapproved route' — following Oman's July 11 two-corridor proposal (Southern Corridor in Omani waters, free pre-war navigation; Northern Corridor in Iranian waters, prior Iranian approval, no tolls) discussed by FM Araghchi and Omani FM Badr Albusaidi in Muscat. Washington demanded Iran publicly declare the Strait open and stop firing, insisting Iran 'does not control' it. No major new US-Iran kinetic exchange was confirmed for July 11-12; the US stayed 'strike-then-pause for diplomacy' while Pakistan/Qatar pressed mediation. Brent held above $76/bbl (~5% weekly gain); the naval blockade stayed lifted (Day 24) and ~50,000 US personnel were unchanged. The imminent-US-ground-seizure thesis stays disconfirmed-and-inverted — the coercion at the chokepoint is Iran's, and the US answer is air and diplomacy. || JULY 11 (Day 135): The sharpest breach-retaliation spike since the MOU cooled into a diplomacy-forward pause. After the July 7 tanker attacks, the US 80+-target and July 9 ~90-target waves, and Iran's July 9 retaliation against Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain and Jordan, US officials told CNN the administration was 'deliberately striking and then pausing to avoid escalation and let diplomacy work' and 'currently letting diplomacy take the lead,' with back-channel contacts and technical nuclear talks continuing; Pakistan and Qatar kept working to reconvene the parties, and Trump said Iran had contacted Washington seeking a new deal. Against that de-escalatory turn Trump posted the war's most explicit seizure threat — the US 'will be taking Kharg Island, and other oil infrastructure points, and assume total control of their Oil and Gas Markets' — which reporting noted would require boots on the ground. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 23) and ~50,000 personnel were unchanged. Brent eased toward $77/bbl and Hormuz tanker traffic was near a standstill (~2 transits July 9; ~40/day over two weeks vs a pre-war 125-140). The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg ground seizure stays disconfirmed and inverted — Kharg was struck only from the air, oil terminals were spared, and it is Iran, not the US, that has used force at the chokepoint. || JUNE 30 (Day 124): The three-day breach-retaliation cycle broke. On June 29 a US official said the US and Iran agreed to stand down and let vessels move freely through Hormuz, and Trump announced a fresh high-level meeting in Doha on Tuesday June 30 (Witkoff and Kushner attending; talks moved from Switzerland and re-scoped to the Hormuz standoff), while Iran's deputy FM Gharibabadi denied any technical talks had been scheduled. Iran and Oman held a first Strait-management meeting (demining and tolls disputed; Iran insists on demining alone and rejects a France-Oman initiative; Oman/GCC reject tolls as 'not acceptable'); Iran received $6B of $12B in frozen Qatari-held assets under the MOU (reportedly earmarked for US wheat and corn). Oil eased: Brent rose only slightly to ~$69.70/bbl off a four-month low. Hormuz traffic stayed thinned (29 vessels Sat, 12 Sun, down from 70 Wed) but container lines resumed Gulf services. The ground rung was unchanged and de-escalatory on the US side — the day's US move was diplomatic, not a ground operation; no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; blockade lifted (Day 12), USS Boxer ARG disaggregated. (NPR; CNBC; NBC News; CBS News; Euronews; The National; TradingEconomics, June 29, 2026.)",
