   "name": "Iran Casualties",
   "value": "AUGUST 27-28 — NO NEW IRANIAN CIVILIAN CASUALTIES FROM US OR ISRAELI STRIKES WERE REPORTED, across a twenty-seventh consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iranian territory since the August 1 cancellation of the energy campaign. Cumulative figures from the Iranian government remain 3,528 KILLED and 27,170 INJURED, alongside a WHO estimate of 37,181 total casualties including 3,375 deaths, and the divergence between the two series is carried rather than resolved. The harm recorded in this cycle is economic and civilian rather than kinetic: strategic fuel reserves described internally as at RED ALERT with stocks possibly exhausted within weeks, car queues blocking streets in Tehran and Mashhad, a rationing scheme and price increase signalled within weeks, the rial at a record ~2.06 million to the dollar against an official ~1.5 million, and inflation at almost 90% by Iran's own Statistical Center — against a White House figure of 'over 100%.' || AUGUST 25-27 — NO NEW IRANIAN CIVILIAN CASUALTIES FROM US OR ISRAELI STRIKES WERE REPORTED, across a twenty-fifth and twenty-sixth consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iranian territory since the August 1 cancellation. Cumulative figures from the Iranian government remain 3,528 KILLED AND 27,170 INJURED. A DIVERGENT INDEPENDENT FIGURE IS ENTERED THIS CYCLE: the WORLD HEALTH ORGANIZATION estimate carried in The Intercept's August 25 reporting is 37,181 TOTAL CASUALTIES INCLUDING 3,375 DEATHS — a higher injury count and a slightly lower death count than Tehran's own. The audit records both and adjudicates neither. Separately, the UN human rights chief has expressed alarm at a sharp rise in executions and death sentences in Iran since the bombing campaign began, with capital punishment used to intimidate the population; at least 56 executions on national-security charges had been recorded since March as of early August. (The Intercept, August 25, 2026; UN Human Rights Office statements, August 2026; NCRI and Iran International compilations, August 2026.) || AUGUST 24 — NO NEW IRANIAN CIVILIAN CASUALTIES FROM US OR ISRAELI STRIKES WERE REPORTED, a twenty-fourth consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iranian territory since the August 1 cancellation. Cumulative figures are unchanged: the Iranian government's published totals stand at 3,528 killed and 27,170 injured; HRANA's independently compiled baseline is 3,636 pending reconciliation — 1,221 military, 1,701 civilian and 714 unclassified as of August 23. Independent compilations place Iranian military KIA in a disputed 1,800-7,650 range (IRNA at the low end, Israeli military intelligence at the high end) and Iranian civilian deaths in a 1,701-3,636 range; 48-52 senior commanders and officials have been killed, including Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei. THE DAMAGE THIS CYCLE WAS MONETARY RATHER THAN PHYSICAL: the rial hit a RECORD 2.02 MILLION TO THE DOLLAR on the open market on August 24 against an official Central Bank rate of about 1.5 million, with rice reported up about 60% and beef up more than 150% since the war began. || AUGUST 23 — NO NEW IRANIAN CIVILIAN CASUALTIES FROM US OR ISRAELI STRIKES WERE REPORTED, a twenty-third consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iranian territory since the August 1 cancellation. Cumulative figures are unchanged: Iranian government figures of 3,528 killed and 27,170 injured, against an HRANA estimate of 3,684 killed (1,249 military, 1,721 civilian, 714 unclassified), pending reconciliation. (Wikipedia, '2026 Iran war,' retrieved August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera; HRANA.) || AUGUST 22 — NO NEW IRANIAN CIVILIAN CASUALTIES FROM US OR ISRAELI STRIKES WERE REPORTED, a twenty-second consecutive night without a confirmed strike inside Iranian territory since the August 1 cancellation. Compilation totals carried from the previous cycle stand at at least 3,527 killed and more than 27,000 wounded per Al Jazeera, with HRANA at 3,636 pending reconciliation. (GlobalSecurity.org daily updates; Al Jazeera compilation, August 2026.) || AUGUST 12-19 — THE TOLL IS STATIC BECAUSE THE STRIKES STOPPED. No new Iranian civilian casualties from strikes were reported as of AUGUST 19, consistent with the absence of US or Israeli operations over Iranian territory across TWENTY CONSECUTIVE NIGHTS since the August 1 cancellation. THE STANDING RANGES: HRANA records 3,636 DEATHS PENDING RECONCILIATION (1,221 military, 1,701 civilian, 714 unclassified); Iran's FOUNDATION OF MARTYRS counts 3,468 KILLED; AL JAZEERA'S AUGUST 12 COMPILATION gives AT LEAST 3,527 KILLED AND MORE THAN 27,000 WOUNDED; US AND ISRAELI ESTIMATES RUN TO 6,000 OR MORE TOTAL IRANIAN DEATHS. Among the Iranian dead are SEVEN INFANTS, 376 CHILDREN AND 496 WOMEN; more than 26,500 injured include at least 4,000 women and 1,621 children. CROSS-SOURCE TOTALS FOR THE WHOLE CONFLICT run from roughly 7,144 to 9,676+ KILLED with about 46,965 INJURED: Iran 3,468-6,000+; Lebanon 3,433 (Lebanese Health Ministry); United States 15-18; Israel 57; Iraq 119+; UAE 13; Kuwait 10, with smaller tolls in Bahrain, Saudi Arabia, Oman and Syria. The Qeshm deaths of a two-year-old and the child's parents remain under CENTCOM investigation. (militaryspend.org, 'Iran War Casualties'; iranwarlive.com; HRANA; Al Jazeera death-toll tracker, August 12, 2026; GlobalSecurity.org, 'Iran War 2026 — Day 173 Update,' August 19, 2026.) || AUGUST 1 — INDEPENDENT TRACKER RANGES, UNCHANGED THIS CYCLE. militaryspend.org (last updated July 30, 2026) gives Iranian military dead at 1,800-7,650 with 48-52 senior commanders killed, and Iranian civilian deaths at 1,701-3,636, noting that figures are contested across all categories and that independent verification inside Iran remains severely limited. Iranian official sources cited via Wikipedia give 3,528 killed and 27,170 injured cumulatively. The CFR Global Conflict Tracker's independent ledger records approximately 1,701 documented civilian deaths in Iran and up to 3.2 million displaced. No new Iranian casualty figure was published in this cycle; the July 30 Qeshm Island strike that killed a two-year-old and the child's parents remains under CENTCOM investigation. (militaryspend.org; CFR Global Conflict Tracker; Wikipedia '2026 Iran war', July 30 – August 1, 2026.) || JULY 31 — CENTCOM CONFIRMS AN INVESTIGATION INTO THE QESHM CIVILIAN DEATHS. US Central Command acknowledged it is investigating reports that an Iranian TWO-YEAR-OLD AND THE CHILD'S PARENTS were killed in the July 30 strike on Qeshm Island; a CENTCOM spokesman said 'The U.S. military never targets civilians, unlike Iranian forces.' Cumulative independent counts remain contested: HRANA has documented roughly 3,636 Iranian casualties and Iran's Foundation of Martyrs confirms 3,468, figures that combine military and civilian dead; cross-source counts across all fronts of the war put total deaths at roughly 7,144 to 9,676+ with about 46,965 injured as of July 20. No consolidated national toll was issued this cycle. (ABC News live updates; HRANA; Foundation of Martyrs, July 31, 2026.) || JULY 30 — THE US STRIKE WAVE KILLED CIVILIANS ON QESHM. Iran's official IRNA news agency said three people were killed and two wounded in a strike on the island of Qeshm; Al Jazeera reported the dead as a couple and their two-year-old child, with children aged seven and nine wounded and two further people trapped under rubble. Three IRGC personnel were separately reported killed. The strikes hit Bandar Abbas, Qeshm, Kish, Abu Musa, three Bushehr cities, Kazerun, Farashband, Abadan and Ahvaz — where seven locations were struck and power went out. No consolidated national toll was issued this cycle; the competing figures of the previous cycle stand unreconciled (government spokesperson Fatemeh Mohajerani's 350+ government employees killed in the line of duty against Health Minister Zafarghandi's 60 for the southern strikes). (IRNA via CNBC; Al Jazeera; The Jerusalem Post, July 30, 2026.) || JULY 29 — NO NEW STRIKE TOLL INSIDE IRAN; THE CUMULATIVE SPREAD WIDENS ON THE RECORD. The standing HRANA cumulative baseline is 3,636 deaths (1,221 military, 1,701 civilian, 714 unclassified) pending reconciliation, against Iran's Foundation of Martyrs' confirmed 3,468. US and Israeli estimates place total Iranian deaths at 6,000 or more, with injured estimates ranging from 15,000 (US/Israeli) to 26,500 (Iranian Health Ministry). The most recent reported deaths from strikes inside Iran remain the July 23 toll of four killed near Ahvaz and the July 22 Shalamcheh crossing toll of two killed and 11 wounded; Iranian authorities' July 18 figure of at least 50 killed and more than 500 wounded since the July resumption stands as the most recent cumulative official count for the July cycle. The two irreconcilable July 28 tolls — Mohajerani's 350+ government employees killed against Health Minister Zafarghandi's 60 for the southern strikes — remain unreconciled. Political executions since February 28 reached at least 50 with the July 28 public hangings in Isfahan, a toll distinct from war casualties. (HRANA; Iran Foundation of Martyrs; casualty trackers; IranWire, July 28-29, 2026.) || JULY 28 — IRAN ISSUED TWO IRRECONCILABLE TOLLS ON THE SAME DAY. Government spokesperson FATEMEH MOHAJERANI told a Tuesday press conference that more than 350 GOVERNMENT EMPLOYEES had been killed in the line of duty — telecommunications engineers, power-line workers, doctors, nurses and other service personnel — and that Bushehr Airport had been 'completely knocked out of service' with the aircraft there destroyed, while the Bushehr Meteorological Centre, 'which is completely of a civilian nature, has almost nothing left of it.' The same day Health Minister MOHAMMAD-REZA ZAFARGHANDI put the toll from recent US strikes in the southern provinces at 60. IranWire noted both figures were issued on the same day and cannot be reconciled from the public record. The cumulative Iranian toll remains above 3,400 since February 28. All figures are Iranian-sourced and not independently verified. (IranWire, 'Iran Gives Two Different Death Tolls for U.S. Strikes on Same Day'; Tehran Times; ABC News, July 28, 2026.) || JULY 27 — No new Iranian strike deaths reported on the third day without US strikes. Iran's health ministry's most recent figures remain 59 killed and 666 wounded from US strikes between June 27 and July 24, with the cumulative Iranian toll above 3,400 since February 28. Separately, one Iranian sailor was killed in Ukraine's July 25 Caspian Sea strike on an Iranian commercial vessel. (Iranian Health Ministry via Al Jazeera; CBS News, July 27, 2026.) || JULY 26 — Iran's health ministry reported 59 killed and 666 wounded from US strikes between June 27 and July 24, within a cumulative Iranian toll of more than 3,400 killed since the war began Feb 28, 2026. Figures are Iranian-sourced and not independently verified. No new Iranian strike deaths were reported on the second pause day. (CBS News; Fortune/AP, July 26, 2026.) || JULY 25 — Iran's Health Ministry reported more than 3,400 killed in Iran cumulatively since the war began Feb 28, 2026. For the resumed phase, Iranian officials put the July 8-25 period at more than 100 US air attacks across Iran, at least 50 killed and more than 500 wounded. No strikes and no new casualties were reported overnight into July 25 — spokesman Hossein Kermanpour said 'Iran had a peaceful night.' Iranian-sourced figures are not independently verified. (Fortune; Al Jazeera; The Washington Post, July 18-25, 2026.) || JULY 21 (Day 145) — At least 50 killed and 500+ wounded in Iran over the past three-plus weeks; US strikes on Bushehr (nuclear-plant city), southern infrastructure, bridges and coastal/military sites continued into a ninth-to-tenth straight night. (NPR; Al Jazeera; Casualties of the 2026 Iran war, July 20, 2026.) || JULY 19 — Iranian media reported at least 3 killed and 8 wounded across Hormozgan in the eighth night of US strikes (with additional deaths reported in bridge strikes near Bandar Khamir); Mehr said strikes that reached Yazd in central Iran fell 'outside the city limits' with no casualties there. Toll atop the 35+ killed and 300+ wounded reported over the prior week of the renewed campaign. (Al Jazeera; Mehr; Haaretz, July 18, 2026.) || JULY 18 — Iranian state media reported at least 7 killed and 20 wounded in the seventh night of US strikes on southern infrastructure (six Hormozgan bridges, an airport, railway stations, power sites), atop the ~35+ killed and 300+ wounded reported over the preceding days. (NPR; France 24; CBS News, July 17, 2026.)  || JULY 17 — No new confirmed nationwide toll beyond the Day-140 figures as the US ran a sixth day of strikes and expanded them into northern Iran; the last confirmed count was 7 Iranian troops killed at a Sistan-Baluchestan barracks with 260+ wounded across the country (Iran reporting 30+ deaths in recent days). (Fortune; Washington Times; Al Jazeera, July 15-16, 2026.) || JULY 15-16 — US strikes killed at least seven Iranian troops at an army barracks in Sistan and Baluchestan province, with more than 260 people wounded across the country; Iranian officials reported more than 30 deaths in recent days overall as the US ran a fifth consecutive round of strikes. (Fortune; Washington Times; Al Jazeera, July 15, 2026.) || JULY 9-10 — Iran's Health Ministry said the two days of US airstrikes (July 8-9) killed at least 14 and wounded ~78 in Iran, across several southern-coast cities. (NPR; Al Jazeera, July 10, 2026.) || JULY 9 — At least 14 killed and dozens wounded in Iran in the US second-day ~90-target strike wave (missile/drone storage, coastal logistics), per reporting on the renewed strikes. (Al Jazeera; The National, July 9, 2026.) ||  || Iran Forensics Chief Apr 24: nearly 3,400 killed (no new aggregate updates Apr 29-May 7) / HRANA: 3,636+ (Apr 18 figure) / Health Ministry: 2,076+ killed, 26,500+ injured / Iran International: 4,700+ security forces killed / Wikipedia/Britannica May 4 aggregation: '5,900+ confirmed civilian dead' across full conflict. 82,000+ structures damaged. MAY 7: US strikes on Iranian ports Bandar Abbas + Qeshm + Bandar Khamir + Sirik (Iran claims civilian areas hit; numbers not yet released). Iran rial 1.84M/USD open-market new all-time low — food inflation 104%/month; Iranians lost ~90% purchasing power; minimum wage ~$92/month equivalent. IMF 2026: -6.1% GDP, 68.9% inflation. Iran INTERNET SHUTDOWN DAY 68. Iran officials reportedly warned Pezeshkian rebuilding war-torn economy may take more than a decade.",
   "change": "AUGUST 27-28 — No new civilian casualties from strikes across a 27th quiet night. Iranian government totals hold at 3,528 killed / 27,170 injured; WHO estimate 37,181 casualties including 3,375 deaths. Cycle harm is economic: fuel reserves at internal 'red alert,' queues in Tehran and Mashhad, rationing signalled, rial ~2.06m, inflation ~90% (Iranian Statistical Center) against 'over 100%' (White House). || AUGUST 25-27 — No new civilian casualties from strikes across a 25th and 26th quiet night. Iranian government totals hold at 3,528 killed / 27,170 injured. NEW: WHO estimate of 37,181 total casualties including 3,375 deaths entered alongside, divergent from Tehran's own figures. UN rights chief records a sharp rise in executions since the campaign began. || AUGUST 24 — No new civilian casualties from strikes; totals unchanged at 3,528 killed and 27,170 injured (Iranian government), HRANA 3,636 pending reconciliation. The rial hit a record 2.02m/USD; rice +~60%, beef +>150% since February.",
