   "name": "Iranian Officials Assassinated",
   "value": "AUGUST 27-28 — No new assassinations were reported; no US or Israeli strike inside Iran has been confirmed since August 1, a twenty-seventh consecutive night. The succession question remains unresolved on the same terms: Trump said on August 26 that Mojtaba Khamenei is not dead but 'very seriously wounded' after roughly six months out of public view, and Iran continues to recognise him as Supreme Leader. THE ELIMINATION FRAME WAS RESTATED FROM OUTSIDE THE IRANIAN AND AMERICAN GOVERNMENTS: former Mossad chief BARNEA said on AUGUST 27 that there is 'NO CHOICE' but to keep striking Iran 'UNTIL THE REGIME FALLS — AND IT WILL FALL.' That is a statement of objective by a former official, not a targeting decision, and is logged at that weight alongside Treasury Secretary Bessent's August 24 declaration that 'we are going to collapse this regime.' || AUGUST 25-27 — No new assassinations reported; no US or Israeli strike inside Iran has been confirmed since August 1, a twenty-fifth and twenty-sixth consecutive night. The succession question moved rhetorically rather than factually: on AUGUST 26 President Trump told Glenn Beck that Supreme Leader MOJTABA KHAMENEI — absent from public view for about six months — is not dead but 'VERY SERIOUSLY WOUNDED,' describing injuries to 'the left side of his body, the arm, the leg, the whole thing,' and dismissing a contrary report in The Atlantic. Iran continues to recognise him officially as Supreme Leader. Cumulative senior Iranian command and official deaths across the war are unchanged. (CBS News live updates, August 26, 2026; Times of Israel, Business Standard and TASS reports of the Glenn Beck interview, August 26, 2026.) || AUGUST 24 — No new assassinations reported; no US or Israeli strike inside Iran has been confirmed since August 1, a twenty-fourth consecutive night. Cumulative senior Iranian command and official deaths across the war are placed at 48-52 in independent compilations, including Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei. || AUGUST 22 — No new assassinations reported; no US or Israeli strike inside Iran has been confirmed since August 1, a twenty-second consecutive night. || AUGUST 2026 — NO NEW ASSASSINATION OF AN IRANIAN OFFICIAL WAS REPORTED IN THIS CYCLE, consistent with the absence of any confirmed US or Israeli strike inside Iranian territory across twenty consecutive nights through August 19. The cumulative figure is unchanged. Iran's wartime command remains publicly active: Armed Forces chief ALI ABDOLLAHI warned of 'revolutionary, crushing, regret-inducing and devastating responses'; Army chief MAJ. GEN. AMIR HATAMI announced on AUGUST 16 a bounty of 5 BILLION TOMANS (~$30,000, DOUBLED TO ~$60,000 IF COLLECTED BY A WOMAN) for killing or capturing US service members, citing 'a large number of requests'; and Supreme Leader MOJTABA KHAMENEI has appointed a former IRGC commander to lead the Supreme National Security Council. (GlobalSecurity.org, 'Iran War 2026 — Day 173 Update,' August 19, 2026; Stars and Stripes, 'Iran offers up to $60K bounty on US troops,' August 17, 2026; The Jerusalem Post; Fox News live coverage, August 21, 2026.) || 10+ senior leaders/commanders killed",
   "change": "AUGUST 27-28 — No new assassinations; a 27th consecutive night with no confirmed strike inside Iran. Succession unresolved: Trump says Mojtaba Khamenei is 'very seriously wounded,' Iran still recognises him. Former Mossad chief Barnea, August 27: 'no choice' but to strike 'until the regime falls.' || AUGUST 25-27 — No new assassinations; a 25th and 26th consecutive night with no confirmed strike inside Iran. Trump said on August 26 that Mojtaba Khamenei is not dead but 'very seriously wounded' after about six months out of public view; Iran continues to recognise him as Supreme Leader. || AUGUST 24 — No new assassinations; no confirmed US or Israeli strike inside Iran since August 1, a twenty-fourth consecutive night. Cumulative senior deaths 48-52.",
