 "ground_invasion_tracker": {
  "last_updated": "2026-08-28",
  "status": "no_ground_troops",
  "status_note": "AUGUST 28, 2026 (Day 183): Status holds no_ground_troops for a 183rd consecutive day. THIS CYCLE PRODUCED NO EXECUTION INDICATOR, ONE FORCE-GENERATION DATAPOINT THAT IS THE STRONGEST STRUCTURAL EVIDENCE THE TRACKER HAS LOGGED SINCE THE APRIL THREE-CARRIER POSTURE, ONE INSTITUTIONAL DATAPOINT THAT IS NEW IN KIND, AND THREE COUNTER-INDICATORS. THE FORCE-GENERATION DATAPOINT IS A ROTATION, NOT A SURGE. The USS THEODORE ROOSEVELT CARRIER STRIKE GROUP will deploy from San Diego to the Middle East WITHIN WEEKS on a deployment expected to run AT LEAST SEVEN MONTHS, with crews told to plan for EIGHT, to RELIEVE the USS GEORGE WASHINGTON — which itself entered the Fifth Fleet area in the week of August 20 to relieve the USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN, departed CENTCOM on August 22 after more than 200 days. That is a one-for-one relief sequence sustaining a SINGLE carrier in theatre, against the TWO CENTCOM cited publicly in July and the THREE-CARRIER POSTURE this project logged in April as a candidate invasion-staging signature. Amphibious and ground-assault operations are preceded by CONCENTRATION; this is RELIEF-IN-PLACE. The eight-month planning horizon carries the posture into 2027, consistent with the previous cycle's Axios report that the non-kinetic posture is expected to hold until after the midterm elections. THE INSTITUTIONAL DATAPOINT IS A COURT. The Justice Department is reviving MARITIME PRIZE COURTS — dormant since the Second World War and of negligible use since 1898 — to condemn seized Iranian tankers and their cargo as United States property for sale, with proceeds to the Treasury, for the stated purposes of strengthening the blockade and offsetting the cost of the conflict. US Attorney AARON REITZ confirmed DOJ is 'now reviving' an 'ancient body of maritime law.' A state that expects to resolve a chokepoint by taking it does not rebuild nineteenth-century admiralty procedure in the interval; this is institutional investment in the maritime rung's longevity. THE WHITE HOUSE NAMED ITS OWN INSTRUMENTS AND A LANDING FORCE WAS NOT AMONG THEM: Press Secretary KAROLINE LEAVITT said on August 27 that the administration is 'CONTINUING TO PULL EVERY ECONOMIC LEVER' and that 'THE NAVAL BLOCKADE CONTINUES TO BE IN EFFECT AS WELL, WHICH HAS PROVEN HUGELY SUCCESSFUL.' THE COUNTER-INDICATORS ARE LOGGED WITHOUT DISCOUNT. (1) A THIRD carrier strike group is being generated for this theatre inside seven months, and the capability being sustained is a strike capability. (2) The BOXER AMPHIBIOUS READY GROUP with approximately 2,200 Marines of the 11th MEU remains in the Arabian Sea on its 59TH DAY with no publicly reported tasking — a preserved, not foreclosed, amphibious option. (3) Former Mossad chief BARNEA said publicly on August 27 that there is 'NO CHOICE' but to keep striking Iran 'UNTIL THE REGIME FALLS — AND IT WILL FALL,' alongside Treasury Secretary Bessent's standing declared objective of collapsing the regime; declared regime-collapse aims are the class of war aim that has historically preceded ground commitment when economic instruments fail. TWO STANDING INDICATORS RETURNED NEGATIVE AND ARE RECORDED EXPLICITLY: KHARG ISLAND was not seized, not targeted and not mentioned, and the USS TRIPOLI is IN PORT AT SASEBO, JAPAN — outside CENTCOM entirely. Every execution indicator remains at zero. || AUGUST 27, 2026 (Day 182): Status holds no_ground_troops for a 182nd consecutive day. This entry covers a DOUBLE CYCLE — the August 26 update was not run, so it consolidates August 25-27 — and it produced NO EXECUTION INDICATOR, ONE NEGATIVE DATAPOINT THAT IS THE MOST SPECIFIC THE TRACKER HAS EVER LOGGED, ONE STRUCTURAL DATAPOINT ABOUT INSTRUMENT CHOICE, AND TWO GENUINE COUNTER-INDICATORS. THE NEGATIVE DATAPOINT: on AUGUST 25 AXIOS reported, citing US officials, that Secretary of State MARCO RUBIO has told several allied foreign ministers in recent days that 'FOR THE TIME BEING' the United States is NOT EXPECTED TO LAUNCH NEW STRIKES against Iran and will instead focus on other means of pressure — without ruling out strikes if Iran attacks first. A SECOND OFFICIAL TOLD AXIOS THE POSTURE IS EXPECTED TO REMAIN IN PLACE UNTIL AFTER THE MIDTERM ELECTIONS, when another military campaign could again be considered. US officials described the priorities as SANCTIONS, THE NAVAL BLOCKADE, and 'MOVING EVER-INCREASING AMOUNTS OF OIL OUT OF THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ.' THREE INSTRUMENTS WERE NAMED AND NONE OF THEM IS A GROUND FORCE. This is the first time in 182 days that the pause has been given a duration, and the duration is measured in months. It is logged with its full qualification: two unnamed officials describing an unannounced future decision, not an order, and fully compatible with a campaign resuming in November. What it is not compatible with is an imminent landing. THE INSTRUMENT DATAPOINT: on AUGUST 25 the President announced that the US Navy has cleared ALL MINES from the international waters of the Strait of Hormuz, declaring a 'ZERO TOLERANCE' policy — 'ANY SHIP OR BOAT PLACING NEW MINES WILL BE IMMEDIATELY AND SYSTEMATICALLY DESTROYED' — with the Space Force 'watching every square inch.' US officials confirmed the method: US Navy UNDERWATER DRONES scanned the Traffic Separation Scheme over recent months and located MORE THAN 100 OBJECTS SUSPECTED TO BE MINES, and the military CONTRACTED WITH PRIVATE COMPANIES to remove or detonate them, the CENTCOM operation having begun in APRIL. Trump also said all 28 Iranian mine-laying boats had been destroyed. FOR A TRACKER WHOSE SUBJECT IS A PREDICTED AMPHIBIOUS SEIZURE, THE SIGNIFICANCE IS THE CHOICE OF TOOL: the United States removed the physical obstacle at the chokepoint with unmanned vehicles and commercial contractors, and addressed the future obstacle with a declaratory rule enforced from orbit. Neither is a step toward a lodgement; both are substitutes for one. THE COUNTER-INDICATORS, LOGGED WITHOUT DISCOUNT: Secretary of War PETE HEGSETH continued to say strikes remain 'ON THE TABLE' despite the economic focus, and Energy Secretary CHRIS WRIGHT said the United States could destroy Iranian nuclear facilities 'IF NECESSARY' and that 'IRAN HAS A NUCLEAR WEAPONS PROGRAM AND OUR GOAL IS TO STOP IT.' Both are air-and-missile formulations rather than ground ones, and neither forecloses anything. THE THIRD-PARTY PICTURE MOVED TOWARD A NEGOTIATED CHOKEPOINT RATHER THAN A SEIZED ONE: Iran and Oman announced a phased framework for a JOINT TEMPORARY NAVIGATIONAL CORRIDOR and a JOINT MINE-CLEARING PROJECT, with technical talks to continue toward a permanent corridor and 'THE FUTURE ADMINISTRATION OF THE STRAIT' — the first document of the war to address who governs the waterway afterwards, and it was signed by Tehran and Muscat, not Washington. NO NEW NAVAL DATA WAS PUBLISHED: USNI News publishes its Fleet and Marine Tracker on Mondays, the edition of record remains AUGUST 24, and the next falls on AUGUST 31. Carrier presence in CENTCOM stays at TWO after USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN departed for 7th Fleet. USS TRIPOLI remains in port at Sasebo, Japan. The BOXER ARG with the 11th MEU remains the only deployed ARG in theatre and has still received no tasking, no embarkation and no rehearsal. KHARG IS UNCHANGED — terminals idle under blockade, no targeting, no naval move. THE DRAFT RUNG IS UNCHANGED — automatic Selective Service registration still due by December 2026, no order, no call-up. FORCE LEVEL HOLDS ABOVE 50,000 WITH NONE OF IT INSIDE IRAN. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER.",
  "troop_count_in_theatre": "MORE THAN 50,000 US personnel in the Middle East, unchanged this cycle and unchanged since the Operation Epic Fury build-up. CENTCOM's last public figure, given in July, was more than 50,000 troops, around 200 combat aircraft and TWO AIRCRAFT CARRIERS. More than 330 US military aircraft are positioned in the region, principally across Al Udeid Air Base in Qatar, Muwaffaq Salti Air Base in Jordan and Prince Sultan Air Base in Saudi Arabia. CARRIER COUNT IS THE MOVING NUMBER AND IT IS MOVING SIDEWAYS: the USS Abraham Lincoln left CENTCOM on AUGUST 22 after a deployment of more than 200 days; the USS George Washington entered the Fifth Fleet area in the week of AUGUST 20 to relieve it; and the USS Theodore Roosevelt Carrier Strike Group will deploy from San Diego WITHIN WEEKS to relieve the George Washington in turn, on a deployment of at least seven months with crews told to plan for eight. The United States has maintained a continuous carrier presence in the Arabian Sea since the war opened in late February. The net effect of the sequence is ONE carrier sustained on station, not a concentration — down from two cited by CENTCOM in July and three in the April posture. NONE OF THE 50,000 IS INSIDE IRAN; no US ground force has entered Iranian territory at any point in the war.",
  "key_developments": [
   "AUGUST 27 — THE CARRIER FORCE IS BEING ROTATED, NOT MASSED, AND THE RELIEF SCHEDULE RUNS INTO 2027. The USS THEODORE ROOSEVELT CARRIER STRIKE GROUP will deploy from San Diego to the Middle East within weeks, on a deployment expected to last at least seven months with crews told to plan for eight, relieving the USS GEORGE WASHINGTON. The George Washington entered the Fifth Fleet area in the week of August 20 after deploying from Japan to relieve the USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN, which departed the CENTCOM area of responsibility on August 22 after more than 200 days. The United States has kept a continuous carrier presence in the Arabian Sea since late February. THE TRACKER READS THIS AS A NEGATIVE INDICATOR AND STATES THE REASONING: a one-for-one relief sequence sustains ONE carrier on station, against TWO cited by CENTCOM in July and THREE in the April posture logged by this project as a candidate staging signature. Massing precedes a landing; relief-in-place sustains a campaign. The eight-month planning horizon carries the posture past the midterm elections and into 2027. COUNTER-WEIGHT, LOGGED: a third strike group is being generated for one theatre inside seven months, and what is being sustained is a strike capability that a decision could redirect.",
   "AUGUST 26-27 — THE UNITED STATES IS BUILDING LEGAL MACHINERY FOR A LONG BLOCKADE. Bloomberg reported that the Justice Department is preparing to activate MARITIME PRIZE COURTS — dormant since the Second World War and of negligible use since the Spanish-American War of 1898 — to give federal prosecutors a faster route to condemn oil and other cargo taken from enemy or neutral vessels as UNITED STATES PROPERTY, to be sold with proceeds transferred to the Treasury. US Attorney AARON REITZ, whose Houston office is partnering with department headquarters, confirmed DOJ is 'NOW REVIVING' an 'ANCIENT BODY OF MARITIME LAW.' The stated purposes are to STRENGTHEN THE BLOCKADE and to OFFSET THE COST OF THE CONFLICT; the reported trigger is that the civil-forfeiture route used against a seized Venezuelan supertanker has bogged down under third-party interventions. Plans are described as unfinalised. FOR THE GROUND QUESTION THE SIGNIFICANCE IS STRUCTURAL: institutional investment of this kind is what a state does when it expects to be interdicting shipping for years, not when it expects to resolve the chokepoint by taking it.",
   "AUGUST 27 — THE WHITE HOUSE NAMED ITS INSTRUMENT SET IN AN OFFICIAL BRIEFING AND A GROUND FORCE WAS NOT IN IT. Press Secretary KAROLINE LEAVITT said the administration is 'CONTINUING TO PULL EVERY ECONOMIC LEVER' and that 'THE NAVAL BLOCKADE CONTINUES TO BE IN EFFECT AS WELL, WHICH HAS PROVEN HUGELY SUCCESSFUL.' She described Iranian conditions as 'inflation is over 100%. They can't pay their police. They can't pay their military,' and said 'no negotiations are happening right now, and this will continue until the president feels that maybe they come to the table in a meaningful way.' Two instruments named — economic levers and the naval blockade — and no reference to ground action of any kind.",
   "AUGUST 27 — COUNTER-INDICATOR, LOGGED AT FULL WEIGHT: A DECLARED REGIME-COLLAPSE OBJECTIVE WAS RESTATED BY A SENIOR ISRAELI FIGURE. Former Mossad chief BARNEA said there is 'NO CHOICE' but to keep striking Iran 'UNTIL THE REGIME FALLS — AND IT WILL FALL.' This stands alongside Treasury Secretary Bessent's August 24 statement that 'it is going to work in Iran, and we are going to collapse this regime.' ALI VAEZ of the International Crisis Group framed the resulting uncertainty on August 27, asking whether Washington is running 'a zero-sum campaign aimed at collapsing the regime, or leverage towards an agreement.' The tracker holds a declared collapse objective as the principal live pathway to a status change, because it is the class of war aim that historically produces ground commitment when economic instruments fail to deliver.",
   "AUGUST 27 — THE STRAIT WAS ATTACKED AGAIN AND THE AMERICAN RESPONSE WAS NOT KINETIC. UKMTO issued WARNING 121-26: a tanker in the Strait of Hormuz hit by an UNKNOWN PROJECTILE, fire since extinguished, crew safe, no environmental damage — the second vessel struck in the waterway this week, thirty-six hours after Trump declared all mines cleared under a 'zero tolerance' rule. No US strike, no boarding operation and no force movement was announced in response within the cycle. The weapon was a projectile rather than a mine, which leaves the demining claim intact on its own terms and confirms Ambrey's assessment that mines 'have never been the primary threat.'",
   "AUGUST 27 — STANDING NEGATIVE INDICATOR RECORDED EXPLICITLY: THE USS TRIPOLI IS NOT IN THEATRE. USNI's fleet tracking places USS TRIPOLI (LHA-7) IN PORT AT SASEBO, JAPAN. The second big-deck amphibious ship most often named in public invasion speculation is forward-deployed in the Western Pacific and is not in the CENTCOM area of responsibility at all.",
   "AUGUST 25 — THE NON-KINETIC POSTURE ACQUIRED A REPORTED DURATION, AND IT RUNS PAST THE MIDTERM ELECTIONS. Axios, citing US officials, reported that Secretary of State Marco Rubio has told several allied foreign ministers in recent days that 'for the time being' the United States is not expected to launch new strikes against Iran and will instead focus on other means of pressure; he did not rule out strikes if Iran attacks first. A second official said the posture is expected to remain in place until after the midterm elections, when another military campaign could again be considered. US officials named the priorities as sanctions, the naval blockade and 'moving ever-increasing amounts of oil out of the Strait of Hormuz.' This is the single most specific negative datapoint the tracker has logged, and it is qualified: two unnamed officials, an unannounced future decision, no order cited.",
   "AUGUST 25 — THE UNITED STATES CLEARED THE CHOKEPOINT INSTEAD OF TAKING IT, USING ROBOTS AND CONTRACTORS. President Trump announced that the US Navy has disposed of all mines in the international waters of the Strait of Hormuz and declared a 'zero tolerance' policy: 'Any ship or boat placing new mines will be immediately and systematically destroyed,' with the Space Force 'watching every square inch.' US officials confirmed that over recent months Navy underwater drones scanned the Traffic Separation Scheme and located more than 100 objects suspected to be mines, and that the military contracted with private companies to remove or detonate them; the CENTCOM operation began in April. Trump also said all 28 Iranian mine-laying boats had been destroyed. The capability applied to the chokepoint was unmanned and commercial, not amphibious.",
   "AUGUST 25-26 — THE FUTURE OF THE STRAIT WENT INTO A DOCUMENT SIGNED BY TEHRAN AND MUSCAT, NOT WASHINGTON. Oman's Foreign Minister Badr Albusaidi met Abbas Araghchi in Tehran and the two ministries announced a 'phased framework' comprising a joint temporary navigational corridor through the Strait and a joint mine-clearing project, with technical talks to continue toward a permanent corridor, 'the future administration of the Strait,' and mechanisms for information exchange, traffic management and maritime and security services. Deputy Foreign Minister Kazem Gharibabadi gave the terms on August 26: seven miles wide; entry beginning in Iranian territorial waters with part of the exit through them; Iranian permission and surveillance required; military vessels barred; permanent arrangement in 30-60 days. IRGC spokesman Brig. Gen. Hossein Mohebbi said the two had agreed 'each country's share of the strait's waters and Iran and Oman's share of its revenues.' For a tracker whose subject is a predicted US seizure, the governance question is being settled — provisionally and on paper — by two other states.",
   "AUGUST 26 — THE PRESIDENT REMOVED THE CLOCK. Trump told Al Jazeera: 'I have no time schedule, none. I'm not in a hurry. I have no time schedule at all,' adding 'We are winning very big' and that economic and military measures 'are both effective.' He told Glenn Beck the Strait is 'a very functioning strait.' An open-ended timeline is compatible with an eventual escalation, but it is not the language of an operation with an execution date.",
   "COUNTER-INDICATOR — SECRETARY OF WAR HEGSETH CONTINUED TO SAY STRIKES REMAIN 'ON THE TABLE' despite the shift to economic pressure. This is the same non-foreclosure formula the tracker has followed since April; it commits nothing and forecloses nothing, and it is recorded because a tracker that logs only de-escalatory evidence is not a tracker.",
   "COUNTER-INDICATOR — AUGUST 26: ENERGY SECRETARY CHRIS WRIGHT SAID THE UNITED STATES COULD DESTROY IRANIAN NUCLEAR FACILITIES 'IF NECESSARY' and that 'Iran has a nuclear weapons program and our goal is to stop it.' Atomic Energy Organisation head Mohammad Eslami said the same day that Iranian sites remain unsecured for inspection under wartime conditions. The nuclear file is the most plausible trigger for a renewed air campaign; it is not a ground trigger, and it is logged as an air-and-missile counter-indicator.",
   "NO NEW NAVAL DATA — USNI News publishes its Fleet and Marine Tracker on Mondays; the edition of record remains August 24 and the next is due August 31. That edition carries CENTCOM carrier presence at TWO after USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) left the Middle East for 7th Fleet, and USS Tripoli (LHA-7) in port at Sasebo, Japan — an amphibious assault ship in the wrong ocean for a Hormuz landing.",
   "AMPHIBIOUS RUNG UNCHANGED FOR A 58TH DAY IN THEATRE — the Boxer Amphibious Ready Group with the embarked 11th Marine Expeditionary Unit, about 2,200 Camp Pendleton Marines aboard USS Boxer (LHA-4), USS Portland (LPD-27) and USS Comstock (LSD-45), entered the region on June 30 and remains the only deployed ARG in the Middle East. No tasking order, no embarkation, no rehearsal, no announced amphibious exercise.",
   "KHARG UNCHANGED — loading terminals remain idle under the naval blockade with a tanker backlog offshore; no US targeting, no naval repositioning toward the island and no statement about it in this cycle. The Kharg option remains available, staffed, repeatedly reported and never taken, now for a fifth month.",
   "DRAFT RUNG UNCHANGED — automatic Selective Service registration of men aged 18-26 remains scheduled for implementation by December 2026 under the National Defense Authorization Act requirement. That is a database change, not a call-up: no draft order, no lottery, no induction authority, no change in statutory posture.",
   "CASUALTY COMPOSITION UNCHANGED IN SHAPE AND UPDATED IN TOTAL — the Pentagon's published toll now stands at 776 (18 killed, 758 wounded) after 60 wounded were added on August 21, with more than 90% of the newest additions Army soldiers. The service split of record remains more than 580 Army, 86 Navy, 64 Air Force and 19 Marines: across 182 days the service that would carry an opposed amphibious lodgement has absorbed roughly 2.5% of the wounded. That is the casualty signature of base defence and blockade enforcement, not of a force preparing for a beach.",
   "STRIKE PAUSE AT TWENTY-SIX NIGHTS — no confirmed US or Israeli strike inside Iranian territory since the President cancelled the planned multi-day energy campaign late on August 1."
  ],
  "kharg_island": {
   "status": "NOT SEIZED, NOT TARGETED, AND NOT MENTIONED IN THIS CYCLE — a 183rd consecutive day. Kharg Island's loading terminals remain largely idle under the US naval blockade, with tankers queued offshore. The one documented movement of the month remains partial and episodic: the WESTERN TERMINAL WAS REACTIVATED ON AUGUST 12 after a 25-day shutdown, with a VLCC berthed and loading for the first time since JULY 18, and no sustained export recovery has been confirmed since. The island concentrates roughly 90-95% of Iranian crude exports. No US strike on it has been reported since the March 14 strikes on mine and weapons storage that deliberately avoided the oil facilities, no US or Iranian statement about its status was made in this cycle, and no American force has landed on it or on any other Iranian territory.",
   "naval_activity": "US naval activity around the island and in the northern Gulf remains BLOCKADE ENFORCEMENT AND ESCORT, not assault preparation. CENTCOM's last published tally, as of AUGUST 24, is 71 COMMERCIAL VESSELS REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED and 2 BOARDED since the July 14 blockade resumption, plus more than 40 humanitarian vessels permitted through; no new tally was published in this cycle. The carrier presence supporting that enforcement is being ROTATED rather than reinforced: Lincoln out on August 22, George Washington in during the week of August 20, Theodore Roosevelt to sail from San Diego within weeks on a seven-to-eight month deployment. The BOXER AMPHIBIOUS READY GROUP remains in the ARABIAN SEA — outside the Gulf and outside any position from which a Kharg landing would be mounted without a further move — on its 59th day without publicly reported tasking. NEW THIS CYCLE: the Justice Department's revival of maritime prize courts would give the seizure campaign a standing legal disposal mechanism, which is investment in interdiction rather than in seizure of the island itself.",
   "notes": "The standing record on American consideration of taking the island is unchanged and is restated for calibration. In MARCH the Washington Post reported that the Pentagon was preparing for weeks of limited ground operations in Iran, potentially including raids on Kharg Island by special-operations and conventional infantry troops; on MARCH 30 Trump said publicly that the island 'lacks defences' and that the United States could capture it 'very easily'; on JUNE 11 he declared the United States 'will be taking Kharg Island' and assume 'total control,' then walked the threat back. Talk of a seizure subsided after the JUNE 17 memorandum of understanding and returned when Trump declined to rule it out in a Fox News interview. In JULY, Foreign Policy reported that former US military officials and outside experts do not see the United States moving toward a major ground operation in Iran. FIVE MONTHS OF AVAILABILITY, REPEATED PUBLIC CONSIDERATION, AND NO EXECUTION. The option is best characterised as prepared, publicly aired, and repeatedly declined."
  },
  "marine_movements": [
   "BOXER AMPHIBIOUS READY GROUP / 11th MARINE EXPEDITIONARY UNIT — IN THEATRE, UNTASKED, 59TH DAY. USS Boxer (LHD-4), USS Portland (LPD-27) and USS Comstock (LSD-45) with approximately 2,200 Camp Pendleton Marines of the 11th MEU are operating in the ARABIAN SEA, having entered the Middle East on JUNE 30, 2026 after deploying from San Diego roughly three weeks ahead of schedule in March. The ARG carries F-35B aircraft, MV-22 Ospreys, helicopters and surface connectors. USNI's fleet tracking continues to place the group in the Arabian Sea. NO TASKING, NO EXERCISE, NO REPOSITIONING INTO THE GULF AND NO LANDING HAS BEEN REPORTED IN 59 DAYS. The tracker records this as a PRESERVED OPTION rather than as a negative indicator: an untasked ARG in theatre is the capability a ground decision would use, and its continued presence is the strongest standing counter-indicator on this list.",
   "USS TRIPOLI (LHA-7) — NOT IN THEATRE. IN PORT AT SASEBO, JAPAN. The ship most frequently named in public speculation about an Iran amphibious operation, after Boxer, is forward-deployed in the Western Pacific and is outside the CENTCOM area of responsibility. Recorded explicitly because Tripoli is a standing item on this indicator list and its absence from the theatre is a datapoint, not an omission.",
   "CARRIER ROTATION — RELIEF, NOT REINFORCEMENT (AUGUST 20-27). USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN departed CENTCOM on AUGUST 22 after a deployment exceeding 200 days. USS GEORGE WASHINGTON entered the Fifth Fleet area in the week of AUGUST 20, having deployed from Japan to relieve it. USS THEODORE ROOSEVELT will deploy from SAN DIEGO WITHIN WEEKS to relieve the George Washington in turn, on a deployment of at least seven months with crews told to plan for eight. Net: one carrier sustained on station. This is force generation sized for endurance, not for assault.",
   "BOXER AMPHIBIOUS READY GROUP / 11th MARINE EXPEDITIONARY UNIT — IN THEATRE, UNTASKED, 58TH DAY. USS Boxer (LHA-4), USS Portland (LPD-27) and USS Comstock (LSD-45) with approximately 2,200 Camp Pendleton Marines entered the Middle East on June 30, 2026 after deploying from San Diego roughly three weeks ahead of schedule in March. The ARG carries F-35B aircraft, MV-22 Ospreys, helicopters and surface connectors in its well deck and is capable of supporting an amphibious landing. It remains the ONLY DEPLOYED ARG IN THE REGION. No tasking order, no embarkation, no rehearsal and no announced amphibious exercise has been reported in the 58 days since arrival.",
   "USS TRIPOLI (LHA-7) — IN PORT, SASEBO, JAPAN. USNI News's August 24 Fleet and Marine Tracker, the edition of record, places Tripoli pierside in Japan. The amphibious assault ship most frequently named in corpus predictions of a Hormuz landing is in the wrong ocean and alongside.",
   "31st MARINE EXPEDITIONARY UNIT — no return to theatre reported. The 31st MEU's ARG departed the Middle East in late July and has not been reported returning.",
   "82nd AIRBORNE DIVISION — approximately 2,000 soldiers with divisional headquarters in the region since late March 2026 in contingency and base-defence roles. No movement toward Iran, no forward staging, no change in mission reported in this cycle.",
   "NO NEW FLEET DATA THIS CYCLE — USNI News publishes its Fleet and Marine Tracker on Mondays. The August 24 edition is the current edition of record and the next is due August 31; no amphibious movement was reported by any other outlet in the interval."
  ],
  "draft_indicators": "NO CHANGE TO THE RUNG, AND ONE POINT OF NEW PRECISION ON THE DATE. Automatic Selective Service registration of male US citizens — and of most other males in the United States aged 18-26, including permanent residents, refugees, asylum seekers and undocumented men, with non-immigrant visa holders excepted — is now reported to take effect on DECEMBER 18, 2026, implementing the provision passed by Congress in the National Defense Authorization Act and signed into law. THAT IS A CHANGE IN HOW THE DRAFT POOL IS BUILT, NOT AN ACTIVATION OF THE DRAFT. Automatic registration orders nobody into service. There is no lottery, no induction authority, no call-up, no medical screening programme and no congressional measure seeking any of these. No member of Congress has introduced an induction bill and no administration official has raised conscription in connection with Iran at any point in the war. The Selective Service's JULY 23 withdrawal of its own automatic-registration rule remains logged as a contested-unresolved item, since the withdrawal of an agency rule against a statutory December deadline has been read both as procedural housekeeping and as implementation difficulty. NOTHING IN THIS CYCLE TOUCHED THE RUNG.",
  "assessment": "At Day 183 the tracker's strongest evidence is now about FORCE GENERATION rather than about rhetoric: the United States is rotating its carrier force one-for-one — Lincoln out August 22, George Washington in the week of August 20, Theodore Roosevelt to sail within weeks on a seven-to-eight month deployment — sustaining a single carrier on station against two in July and three in April, while the Justice Department rebuilds nineteenth-century prize-court machinery to dispose of seized tankers and the White House names economic levers and the naval blockade as its instruments. Concentration precedes a landing; relief-in-place and institution-building sustain a blockade, and the planning horizon now runs into 2027. Against that, three counter-indicators stand undiminished: a third carrier strike group is being generated for this theatre, the Boxer ARG with roughly 2,200 Marines has sat untasked in the Arabian Sea for 59 days, and a former Mossad chief has publicly demanded strikes 'until the regime falls' alongside a Treasury Secretary who has already declared regime collapse the objective. The status remains NO_GROUND_TROOPS with every execution indicator at zero, and the pathway most likely to change it remains the failure of the economic campaign to deliver a declared collapse objective rather than any force movement currently observable."
 },
 "daily_entries": [
  {
   "date": "2026-08-28",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Iran War",
   "headline": "DAY 183 — THE STRAIT THAT WAS DECLARED CLEARED WAS ATTACKED AGAIN, AND THE UNITED STATES ANSWERED BY BUILDING A COURT. THIRTY-SIX HOURS AFTER TRUMP DECLARED EVERY MINE REMOVED FROM THE STRAIT'S INTERNATIONAL WATERS UNDER A 'ZERO TOLERANCE' RULE, UKMTO ISSUED WARNING 121-26: A TANKER STRUCK BY AN UNKNOWN PROJECTILE IN THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ, FIRE SINCE EXTINGUISHED, CREW SAFE, NO ENVIRONMENTAL DAMAGE — THE SECOND VESSEL HIT IN THE WATERWAY THIS WEEK. THE WEAPON WAS A PROJECTILE, NOT A MINE, WHICH LEAVES THE DEMINING CLAIM INTACT ON ITS OWN TERMS AND CONFIRMS AMBREY'S ASSESSMENT THAT MINES 'HAVE NEVER BEEN THE PRIMARY THREAT.' THE AMERICAN MOVE OF THE CYCLE WAS LEGAL, NOT MILITARY: BLOOMBERG REPORTED THAT THE JUSTICE DEPARTMENT IS REVIVING MARITIME PRIZE COURTS — DORMANT SINCE THE SECOND WORLD WAR AND BARELY USED SINCE 1898 — TO CONDEMN SEIZED IRANIAN TANKERS AND THEIR CARGO AS UNITED STATES PROPERTY FOR SALE, WITH PROCEEDS TO THE TREASURY. US ATTORNEY AARON REITZ, WHOSE HOUSTON OFFICE IS PARTNERING WITH DEPARTMENT HEADQUARTERS, CONFIRMED DOJ IS 'NOW REVIVING' AN 'ANCIENT BODY OF MARITIME LAW.' THE STATED PURPOSES ARE TO STRENGTHEN THE BLOCKADE AND TO OFFSET THE COST OF THE WAR. DIPLOMACY MOVED AND THEN CONTRADICTED ITSELF INSIDE ONE GOVERNMENT: QATAR'S PRIME MINISTER SHEIKH MOHAMMED BIN ABDULRAHMAN AL THANI SPENT AUGUST 27 IN TEHRAN MEETING ARAGHCHI, PEZESHKIAN, GHALIBAF AND SECURITY CHIEF MOHSEN REZAI, SAYING 'DIALOGUE AND DIPLOMATIC SOLUTIONS REMAIN THE OPTIMAL PATH' — WHILE A SENIOR IRANIAN SOURCE TOLD REUTERS THAT THE AGREEMENT WITH OMAN OVER THE STRAIT 'HAS NOT BEEN FINALIZED,' A DAY AFTER THE IRGC SAID THE TWO STATES HAD SETTLED THEIR SHARES OF THE WATERWAY AND ITS REVENUES. WASHINGTON CLOSED THE DOOR IT HAD LEFT AJAR: THE WHITE HOUSE SAID THERE ARE 'NO TALKS OR CONVERSATIONS' UNDER WAY OR SCHEDULED, TRUMP SAID 'WE DON'T WANT TO SPEAK TO THEM. WE'RE NOT LOOKING TO MEET OR ANYTHING,' AND KAROLINE LEAVITT SAID THE ADMINISTRATION IS 'CONTINUING TO PULL EVERY ECONOMIC LEVER' WITH 'THE NAVAL BLOCKADE... PROVEN HUGELY SUCCESSFUL.' THE TRAFFIC DATA LANDED IN DIRECT CONTRADICTION OF THE PRESIDENT'S OWN NUMBER: AL JAZEERA PUT TRANSITS AT ABOUT FIVE VESSELS A DAY BETWEEN JULY 15 AND AUGUST 23 AGAINST A PRE-WAR BASELINE NEAR 100 — A DROP OF NEARLY 95% — TWO DAYS AFTER TRUMP SAID TEN MILLION BARRELS MOVED THROUGH THE STRAIT ON TUESDAY. STILL AIR, NAVAL, FINANCIAL AND NOW JUDICIAL — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER, A TWENTY-SEVENTH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT WITHOUT A CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN.",
