   "date": "2026-08-28",
   "theatre": "Russia-Ukraine War",
   "tag": "Russia-Ukraine",
   "headline": "RUSSIA-UKRAINE — THE AGENDA OF THE UNANNOUNCED MOSCOW VISIT WAS DISCLOSED, AND IT WAS A WARNING ABOUT THE BALTICS AND A REQUEST ABOUT IRAN. CIA DIRECTOR JOHN RATCLIFFE URGED RUSSIAN OFFICIALS NOT TO TAKE ACTIONS THAT COULD ESCALATE TENSIONS WITH ESTONIA, LATVIA AND LITHUANIA, AND USED THE SAME VISIT TO PRESS MOSCOW TO REDUCE ITS MILITARY AND ECONOMIC SUPPORT FOR IRAN. US INTELLIGENCE ASSESSMENTS UNDERLYING THE WARNING HOLD THAT RUSSIA MAY SEEK TO TEST NATO'S READINESS WITH A LIMITED MILITARY OPERATION OR A HYBRID ATTACK IN THE COMING YEARS, WITH THE BALTIC STATES AMONG THE MOST LIKELY TARGETS. PESKOV CONFIRMED THE MEETING WAS WITH RUSSIAN INTELLIGENCE REPRESENTATIVES AND NOT WITH PUTIN, WHO WAS BRIEFED AFTERWARDS; TRUMP CALLED THE TRIP 'SEMI-ROUTINE' AND SAID IT MIGHT BE LINKED TO EFFORTS TO END THE UKRAINE WAR; RATCLIFFE BRIEFED TRUMP AT THE WHITE HOUSE ON HIS RETURN. THE TWO WARS ARE NOW EXPLICITLY LINKED IN AMERICAN DIPLOMACY: THE SAME MEETING CARRIED A NATO DETERRENCE MESSAGE AND AN IRAN DECOUPLING REQUEST. THE FIGHTING DID NOT PAUSE FOR IT. RUSSIA STRUCK KYIV AND OTHER CITIES OVERNIGHT INTO AUGUST 27 WITH BALLISTIC MISSILES AND DRONES — SIX EXPLOSIONS IN THE CAPITAL INSIDE A MINUTE AROUND 3 A.M., AT LEAST SEVEN INJURED, TARGETS INCLUDING WAREHOUSES, PORTS AND ENERGY AND INDUSTRIAL FACILITIES PER FOREIGN MINISTER SYBIHA — WITH UKRAINE DOWNING SEVEN BALLISTIC MISSILES, ONE ANTI-SHIP CRUISE MISSILE AND ABOUT 90% OF THE DRONES. UKRAINE'S DEEP-STRIKE CAMPAIGN REACHED RUSSIA'S REFINING BASE: THE NORSI PLANT AT KSTOVO — RUSSIA'S FOURTH-LARGEST REFINERY AND SECOND-LARGEST GASOLINE PRODUCER — SUSPENDED CRUDE PROCESSING AFTER AN OVERNIGHT DRONE STRIKE, ITS FIFTH DRONE-RELATED SHUTDOWN IN UNDER FIVE MONTHS, AND UKRAINIAN DRONES ARE REPORTED TO HAVE SHUT ALL MAJOR LUKOIL REFINERIES. A UKRAINIAN STRIKE HIT A BUS IN RUSSIAN-CONTROLLED LUHANSK, KILLING NINE. NO NATO TROOP COMMITMENT.",
   "tags": [
