   "tag": "Iran War",
   "headline": "DAY 182 — A DOUBLE CYCLE, AND THE UNITED STATES SPENT IT MAKING THE STRAIT NAVIGABLE RATHER THAN TAKING IT. THE WEEK'S MOST CONSEQUENTIAL REPORT PUT A DURATION ON THE NON-KINETIC POSTURE FOR THE FIRST TIME: AXIOS SAID ON AUGUST 25 THAT SECRETARY OF STATE MARCO RUBIO HAS TOLD ALLIED FOREIGN MINISTERS THE UNITED STATES IS NOT EXPECTED TO LAUNCH NEW STRIKES ON IRAN 'FOR THE TIME BEING,' AND THAT A SECOND US OFFICIAL EXPECTS THE POSTURE TO HOLD UNTIL AFTER THE MIDTERM ELECTIONS, WHEN ANOTHER MILITARY CAMPAIGN COULD AGAIN BE CONSIDERED. ON AUGUST 25 TRUMP ANNOUNCED THAT THE US NAVY HAS CLEARED ALL MINES FROM THE STRAIT'S INTERNATIONAL WATERS AND DECLARED A 'ZERO TOLERANCE' POLICY — 'ANY SHIP OR BOAT PLACING NEW MINES WILL BE IMMEDIATELY AND SYSTEMATICALLY DESTROYED,' WITH THE SPACE FORCE 'WATCHING EVERY SQUARE INCH.' US OFFICIALS SAID UNDERWATER DRONES HAD IDENTIFIED MORE THAN 100 SUSPECTED MINES OVER RECENT MONTHS AND THAT PRIVATE CONTRACTORS DEALT WITH THEM. THE INSTRUMENT OF THE CYCLE WAS AN UNMANNED VEHICLE AND A CONTRACTOR, NOT A LANDING FORCE. THE GOVERNANCE OF THE WATERWAY MOVED ON PAPER TOWARD TEHRAN AND MUSCAT, NOT WASHINGTON. OMAN'S FOREIGN MINISTER BADR ALBUSAIDI MET ABBAS ARAGHCHI IN TEHRAN ON AUGUST 25 AND THE TWO MINISTRIES ANNOUNCED A 'PHASED FRAMEWORK' FOR A JOINT TEMPORARY NAVIGATIONAL CORRIDOR AND A JOINT MINE-CLEARING PROJECT. ON AUGUST 26 DEPUTY FOREIGN MINISTER KAZEM GHARIBABADI GAVE THE TERMS ON STATE TELEVISION: SEVEN MILES WIDE, ENTRY BEGINNING IN IRANIAN TERRITORIAL WATERS AND PART OF THE EXIT ALSO THROUGH THEM, IRANIAN PERMISSION AND SURVEILLANCE REQUIRED, MILITARY VESSELS BARRED, AND A PERMANENT ARRANGEMENT TO BE NEGOTIATED WITHIN 30 TO 60 DAYS. IRAN INSISTS THIS IS NOT A REOPENING — 'THE AGREED-UPON TRANSIT ROUTE WITH OMAN IS A TEMPORARY ROUTE' — AND CONDITIONS FULL OPENING ON US COMPLIANCE WITH THE JUNE 17 MOU, SANCTIONS RELIEF, RELEASE OF FROZEN ASSETS, AN END TO THE WAR AND WAR-DAMAGE COMPENSATION. THE ENFORCEMENT RECORD CONTRADICTED THE DIPLOMACY WITHIN A DAY: IRAN'S SHIPPING MONITORING AGENCY SAID THE INDIAN TANKER HAANA WAS WARNED TO STOP AND TURNED BACK ON THE SOUTHERN OMANI ROUTE, AND THAT NO VESSEL TRAFFIC HAD BEEN OBSERVED ON THAT ROUTE IN TWENTY-FOUR HOURS — AGAINST THE KPLER DATASET OF THE PREVIOUS CYCLE PUTTING MORE THAN 80% OF LIQUIDS TRANSITS ON IT. OIL FELL THREE SESSIONS RUNNING: BRENT TO ABOUT $89 ON AUGUST 25, A ONE-WEEK LOW, AND TO ABOUT $86 ON AUGUST 26, WITH WTI NEAR $80 — TRADERS CALLING THE SANCTIONS 'MORE OF A WARNING SHOT THAN A DECISIVE BLOW' AND PRICING THE OMAN CORRIDOR AS SUPPLY RELIEF. TRUMP TOLD AL JAZEERA: 'I HAVE NO TIME SCHEDULE, NONE. I'M NOT IN A HURRY.' HE TOLD GLENN BECK THE STRAIT IS 'A VERY FUNCTIONING STRAIT' AND THAT MOJTABA KHAMENEI IS NOT DEAD BUT 'VERY SERIOUSLY WOUNDED.' INSIDE IRAN THE PETROL STATIONS RAN DRY — TWENTY-LITRE LIMITS, CLOSURES AND QUEUES ACROSS TEHRAN, THE EXECUTIVE VICE-PRESIDENT SAYING 'WITH THE US NAVAL BLOCKADE, WE CANNOT IMPORT GASOLINE,' AND PEZESHKIAN CALLING THESE 'THE WORST CONDITIONS OF AN ECONOMIC WAR.' THE RIAL SET A RECORD 2.06 MILLION TO THE DOLLAR ON AUGUST 25. THE PENTAGON LEDGER MOVED TO 776 — 18 KILLED AND 758 WOUNDED. A TWENTY-FIFTH AND A TWENTY-SIXTH CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. THE PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED FOR A 182ND DAY.",
