   "source": "Axios, 'Rubio tells allies US not expected to launch new strikes on Iran,' August 25, 2026, and syndication (Reuters, TASS, Middle East Eye, DNA News, Times Kuwait); Axios, 'Trump announces all mines have been removed from the Strait of Hormuz,' August 25, 2026; Fox News Digital live updates, August 25, 2026 (Hegseth: strikes remain 'on the table'; Axios posture summary); Iran International live blog, entries of August 26-27, 2026 (Energy Secretary Chris Wright on Iranian nuclear facilities); The Intercept, 'Sixty More U.S. Soldiers Reported Injured in Iran War,' August 25, 2026; Stars and Stripes, 'Pentagon adds 60 wounded to Iran war casualty count,' August 21, 2026; USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, August 24, 2026 (most recent published edition; USNI publishes Mondays — no new edition in this cycle); Times of San Diego, 'USS Boxer amphibious group with Pendleton Marines arrives in Middle East,' July 5, 2026; USNI News, 'Boxer Amphibious Ready Group, 11th MEU Deploy from California,' March 20, 2026; Eurasia Business News, 'Iran's oil exports stall and Kharg Island idles under US blockade,' August 7, 2026; CNBC, 'Automatic U.S. military draft registration by December 2026 planned,' April 9, 2026; Friends Committee on National Legislation, 'Automatic Draft Registration: What Comes Next and Why it's a Problem,' May 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Trump tells Al Jazeera “not in a hurry” for Iran to return to talks,' August 26, 2026.",
   "summary": "STATUS: NO_GROUND_TROOPS, DAY 182, FOR A 182ND CONSECUTIVE DAY. THIS CYCLE COVERS TWO DAYS AND PRODUCED NO EXECUTION INDICATOR, ONE MAJOR NEGATIVE DATAPOINT, ONE STRUCTURAL DATAPOINT ABOUT INSTRUMENT CHOICE, AND TWO GENUINE COUNTER-INDICATORS.\n\nTHE NEGATIVE DATAPOINT, AND IT IS THE MOST SPECIFIC THE TRACKER HAS LOGGED. On AUGUST 25 AXIOS reported, citing US officials, that Secretary of State MARCO RUBIO has told several allied foreign ministers in recent days that 'FOR THE TIME BEING' the United States is not expected to launch new strikes against Iran and will instead focus on other means of pressure. He did not rule out strikes if Iran attacks first. A SECOND OFFICIAL said the posture is expected to remain in place UNTIL AFTER THE MIDTERM ELECTIONS, when another military campaign could again be considered. US officials described the priorities as sanctions, the naval blockade, and 'MOVING EVER-INCREASING AMOUNTS OF OIL OUT OF THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ.' THREE INSTRUMENTS WERE NAMED AND NONE OF THEM IS A GROUND FORCE. This tracker records the report with its full qualification: it rests on two unnamed officials describing an unannounced future decision, not on an order, and it is compatible with the campaign resuming in November. What it is not compatible with is an imminent landing.\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT DATAPOINT. On AUGUST 25 the President announced that the US Navy has cleared ALL MINES from the Strait's international waters, with a 'ZERO TOLERANCE' rule — 'any ship or boat placing new mines will be immediately and systematically destroyed' — and Space Force surveillance of the waterway. US officials confirmed the method: UNDERWATER DRONES scanned the Traffic Separation Scheme over recent months and located MORE THAN 100 SUSPECTED MINES, and PRIVATE CONTRACTORS removed or detonated them; the CENTCOM operation began in APRIL. FOR A TRACKER WHOSE SUBJECT IS A PREDICTED SEIZURE, THE SIGNIFICANCE IS THE CHOICE OF TOOL. The United States addressed the physical obstacle at the chokepoint with unmanned vehicles and commercial contractors, and addressed the future obstacle with a declaratory rule enforced from orbit. Neither is a step toward a lodgement; both are substitutes for one.\n\nTHE COUNTER-INDICATORS, RECORDED WITHOUT DISCOUNT. Secretary of War PETE HEGSETH continued to say that strikes remain 'ON THE TABLE' despite the economic focus. Energy Secretary CHRIS WRIGHT said the United States could destroy Iranian nuclear facilities 'IF NECESSARY' and that 'IRAN HAS A NUCLEAR WEAPONS PROGRAM AND OUR GOAL IS TO STOP IT.' Both are air-and-missile statements rather than ground statements, but both keep the military track alive and neither forecloses anything. A tracker that logs only de-escalatory evidence is not a tracker.\n\nTHE NAVAL PICTURE IS UNCHANGED AND NO NEW DATA WAS PUBLISHED. USNI News publishes its Fleet and Marine Tracker on Mondays; the edition of record remains AUGUST 24 and the next falls on AUGUST 31. That edition carries CENTCOM carrier presence at TWO after USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN (CVN-72) left the Middle East for 7th Fleet, with USS GEORGE H.W. BUSH (CVN-77) in the northern Arabian Sea and USS GEORGE WASHINGTON (CVN-73) on station since August 19. USS TRIPOLI (LHA-7) remains in port at Sasebo, Japan — an amphibious assault ship in the wrong ocean for a Hormuz landing. The BOXER AMPHIBIOUS READY GROUP with the embarked 11th MARINE EXPEDITIONARY UNIT, in theatre since June 30, remains the only deployed ARG in the region and has received NO TASKING, NO EMBARKATION ORDER AND NO REHEARSAL in the 58 days since it arrived.\n\nKHARG IS UNCHANGED. The island's loading terminals remain idle under the naval blockade with a tanker backlog offshore; there has been no US targeting, no naval repositioning toward it and no statement about it in this cycle. The Kharg option remains what it has been for four months: available, staffed, repeatedly reported, never taken.\n\nTHE DRAFT RUNG IS UNCHANGED. Automatic Selective Service registration of men aged 18-26 remains scheduled for implementation by DECEMBER 2026 under the National Defense Authorization Act requirement. That is a database change, not a call-up. No draft order, no lottery, no induction authority, no change in the statutory posture.\n\nTHE CASUALTY COMPOSITION STILL POINTS AWAY FROM A BEACH. The Pentagon's toll now stands at 776 — 18 killed and 758 wounded — with more than 90% of the newest additions Army soldiers, consistent with the service split entered in the previous cycle in which 19 of the wounded were Marines, roughly 2.5% of the total across 182 days. That is the casualty signature of base defence and blockade enforcement, not of a force fighting for or preparing for a landing.\n\nFORCE LEVEL HOLDS ABOVE 50,000 IN THE MIDDLE EAST, WITH APPROXIMATELY 2,000 SOLDIERS OF THE 82ND AIRBORNE DIVISION IN CONTINGENCY AND BASE-DEFENCE ROLES AND NONE OF IT INSIDE IRAN. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY.",
   "details": "EXECUTION INDICATORS THIS CYCLE: ZERO. No amphibious tasking order, no embarkation, no rehearsal, no forward staging of fuel/ammunition/medical, no evacuation of dependants, no draft order, no ground-force flow into theatre, no US personnel inside Iran. NEGATIVE DATAPOINT (August 25, Axios): Rubio told allied foreign ministers the US is not expected to launch new strikes 'for the time being' and will focus on other means of pressure; strikes not ruled out if Iran attacks first; a second official expects the posture to hold until after the midterm elections; stated priorities are sanctions, the naval blockade and 'moving ever-increasing amounts of oil out of the Strait of Hormuz.' Qualification logged: two unnamed officials, an unannounced future decision, no order cited. INSTRUMENT DATAPOINT (August 25): mine clearance completed in the international waters of the Strait by US Navy underwater drones (100+ suspected mines located over recent months) with removal/detonation by private contractors; CENTCOM operation began April; 'zero tolerance' declaratory rule with Space Force surveillance; Trump also claims all 28 Iranian mine-laying boats destroyed. COUNTER-INDICATORS: Hegseth — strikes remain 'on the table.' Energy Secretary Chris Wright — the US could destroy Iranian nuclear facilities 'if necessary'; 'Iran has a nuclear weapons program and our goal is to stop it.' Both non-ground in character; both logged. NAVAL: no new USNI Fleet and Marine Tracker this cycle (published Mondays; edition of record August 24, next August 31). Carrier presence in CENTCOM: TWO — USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77, in theatre since April 23) and USS George Washington (CVN-73, arrived August 19 with USS Robert Smalls and USS Shoup). USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) departed for 7th Fleet. USS Tripoli (LHA-7) in port Sasebo, Japan. 20+ warships supporting the blockade. AMPHIBIOUS: Boxer ARG (USS Boxer LHA-4, USS Portland LPD-27, USS Comstock LSD-45) with the 11th MEU, ~2,200 Camp Pendleton Marines, in theatre since June 30; the only deployed ARG in the region; no tasking, no embarkation, no rehearsal. KHARG: unchanged. Loading terminals idle under blockade with tanker backlog offshore; no US targeting, no naval repositioning, no statement this cycle. DRAFT: unchanged. Automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 due by December 2026 under the NDAA requirement; no draft order, no lottery, no induction authority. CASUALTY COMPOSITION: 776 total (18 killed, 758 wounded); >90% of the newest additions Army; the service split of record remains 580+ Army, 86 Navy, 64 Air Force, 19 Marines — Marines at ~2.5% across 182 days. FORCE LEVEL: more than 50,000 US personnel in the Middle East; ~200 combat aircraft and 330+ US military aircraft across Al Udeid, Muwaffaq Salti and Prince Sultan; Patriot and THAAD batteries; ~2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne Division in contingency and base-defence roles; none inside Iran.",
   "prediction_impact": "The corpus prediction that the United States would put troops ashore to seize the Strait of Hormuz or Kharg Island is DISCONFIRMED for a 182nd consecutive day, and this cycle moves the evidence from 'not yet' toward 'not on this timeline.' The Axios report gives the non-kinetic posture a reported horizon extending past the midterm elections — the first duration ever attached to it — while the instrument actually applied to the chokepoint was an unmanned underwater vehicle and a commercial contractor. Predictions that a mined Strait would force a physical American seizure to reopen it are DISCONFIRMED IN MECHANISM: the mines were cleared without a landing. Predictions of a US draft or mobilisation remain DISCONFIRMED; the only change in the Selective Service posture continues to be the administrative automation of registration due by December 2026. The counter-indicators are entered as UNTESTED: Hegseth's 'on the table' formula and Wright's statement that the United States could destroy Iranian nuclear facilities 'if necessary' both keep a military track open, and both describe air and missile action rather than ground action."
  },
