   "headline": "RUSSIA-UKRAINE — THE HIGHEST-LEVEL AMERICAN VISIT TO MOSCOW SINCE JANUARY HAPPENED WITHOUT ANNOUNCEMENT AND WITHOUT AN AGENDA MADE PUBLIC. CIA DIRECTOR JOHN RATCLIFFE FLEW TO MOSCOW ON AUGUST 25 ABOARD A US MILITARY TRANSPORT FROM JOINT BASE ANDREWS, TRACKED BY PUBLICLY AVAILABLE FLIGHT DATA. IT IS THE FIRST KNOWN VISIT TO THE RUSSIAN CAPITAL BY A US SPY CHIEF SINCE WILLIAM BURNS MET PUTIN IN NOVEMBER 2021. THE KREMLIN SAID RATCLIFFE MET RUSSIAN INTELLIGENCE COUNTERPARTS; PESKOV SAID PUTIN DID NOT PLAN TO MEET HIM, AND NOTHING OF WHAT WAS DISCUSSED HAS BEEN DISCLOSED. TRUMP ADMINISTRATION OFFICIALS HAD ASKED KYIV SEVERAL DAYS EARLIER TO PAUSE STRIKES ON MOSCOW AND OTHER RUSSIAN CITIES FROM MONDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY. ON THE SAME DAY PESKOV SAID THERE WERE NO PLANS FOR TALKS WITH WITKOFF OR KUSHNER THIS WEEK — 'NO, THERE ARE NO SUCH PLANS.' THE WAR ITSELF DID NOT PAUSE. RUSSIAN ATTACKS KILLED FOUR AND INJURED 95 ACROSS UKRAINE OVER AUGUST 25-26, WITH 163 DRONES LAUNCHED OVERNIGHT INTO AUGUST 26, 132 DOWNED AND STRIKES RECORDED AT 18 LOCATIONS. IN KRAMATORSK A RUSSIAN FPV DRONE CARRIED OUT A DOUBLE-TAP ATTACK ON RESCUE WORKERS CLEARING A STRUCK NINE-STOREY BLOCK, HITTING AN ARMOURED STATE EMERGENCY SERVICE AMBULANCE — THE SECOND ATTACK ON RESCUERS THAT WEEK. TWENTY-SIX WERE INJURED IN KRAMATORSK AND 37 HIGH-RISES DAMAGED. IN CHERNIHIV OBLAST A DRONE KILLED A 39-YEAR-OLD WOMAN AND HER FOUR-YEAR-OLD DAUGHTER. UKRAINE RESUMED DEEP STRIKES, HITTING A WILDBERRIES LOGISTICS HUB IN TAMBOV OBLAST WITH A 'MASSIVE DRONE ATTACK' THAT SET A FIRE ACROSS MORE THAN 100,000 SQUARE METRES. ISW REPORTS RUSSIA ESCALATING STRIKES ON UKRAINIAN-MOLDOVAN BORDER INFRASTRUCTURE ALONGSIDE ITS CAMPAIGN AGAINST PORTS, AND UKRAINIAN ADVANCES IN THE SLOVYANSK AND HULYAIPOLE DIRECTIONS AND WESTERN ZAPORIZHIA OBLAST. NO NATO TROOP COMMITMENT WAS ANNOUNCED.",
