   ],
   "source": "Venezuelanalysis, 'Venezuela: Rodríguez Announces Electricity Rationing Ahead of Heatwave, Drought Forecast,' August 2026; Venezuelanalysis, 'Venezuela: Rodríguez Calls for Electricity Rationing, US Chargé d'Affaires Visit Guri Dam,' August 2026; Cuba Headlines, 'Demonstrations Erupt in Aragua Against Delcy Rodríguez Amidst Venezuela's Worsening Blackouts,' August 2026; The Washington Times, 'As blackouts stretch for days, life in Cuba revolves around small bursts of electricity,' August 7, 2026; Wikipedia compilation '2024-2026 Cuba blackouts' (grid-collapse chronology); CNN Politics, 'Venezuela's Nicolás Maduro gets a June trial date,' July 22, 2026; PJ Media, 'Well, the New U.S.-Colombia Relationship Escalated Quickly,' August 8, 2026; Colombia One and Atlantic Council commentary on the de la Espriella transition, August 2026.",
   "summary": "THE HEMISPHERE'S TWO ENERGY EMERGENCIES CONVERGED THIS CYCLE, AND FOR THE FIRST TIME THE VENEZUELAN ONE PRODUCED SUSTAINED STREET PROTEST DIRECTED AT THE ACTING PRESIDENT.\n\nVENEZUELA. Pot-banging protests have MULTIPLIED IN RECENT DAYS in rejection of recurring blackouts and of appliance damage caused by electrical-service fluctuations. ARAGUA STATE, about 80 kilometres southeast of Caracas, is among the worst affected, with power cut FOUR TO FIVE HOURS EVERY DAY. In TURMERO residents took to the streets, BLOCKING ROADS AND SETTING TYRES ALIGHT against the outages and the government-imposed rationing. Acting President DELCY RODRÍGUEZ has called for ELECTRICITY AND WATER RATIONING amid rising social tension, announcing a package of immediate measures in early August to safeguard the National Electrical System and requesting activation of an ELECTRICITY AND WATER SAVINGS PLAN, attributing the crisis to the 'SUPER NIÑO' climate phenomenon and to disruption from a recent earthquake. The conservation measures — including instructions on air-conditioner settings — have been WIDELY REJECTED BY THE PUBLIC and have not relieved the outages. THE POLITICAL SIGNIFICANCE IS THAT THE GOVERNMENT NOW ABSORBING THE BLAME IS THE ONE THAT TOOK OFFICE AFTER THE US SEIZURE OF MADURO, NOT THE ONE THAT WAS REMOVED.\n\nTHE TRANSITION TRACK IS UNCHANGED. The Caracas government-opposition talks that opened on AUGUST 6 under JORGE RODRÍGUEZ and DINORAH FIGUERA continue with NO PUBLISHED ELECTORAL TIMETABLE. DELCY RODRÍGUEZ remains acting president, having been sworn in on JANUARY 5, 2026 as the first woman to exercise the powers of the Venezuelan presidency, with her 2018 US sanctions lifted in APRIL. NICOLÁS MADURO and CILIA FLORES remain in US custody with trial set for JUNE 1, 2027 before Judge Alvin Hellerstein in the Southern District of New York.\n\nCUBA. The cumulative figures are unchanged and are restated for continuity: the national electricity system has collapsed SIX TIMES IN 2026 — twice in March, three times within ten days in July and once on AUGUST 2-3 — with blackouts EXCEEDING TWENTY HOURS A DAY and some communities recorded at UP TO 105 CONSECUTIVE DAYS without steady electricity. What is newly documented is the response: in several municipalities, particularly in HAVANA, residents staged NEIGHBOURHOOD PROTESTS after blackouts lasting MORE THAN 48 HOURS, banging pots and pans and burning rubbish piled on street corners. The island lost its principal fuel supplier after the JANUARY 3 seizure of Maduro and the subsequent US oil blockade, with Mexican imports also halted under Washington's pressure; sanctions run under EXECUTIVE ORDER 14404, Visa and Mastercard processing has been lost, and the United Nations describes a humanitarian emergency. Foreign Minister BRUNO RODRÍGUEZ has said there has been 'NO PROGRESS' toward ending the impasse.\n\nCOLOMBIA. President ABELARDO DE LA ESPRIELLA, who took office on AUGUST 7 succeeding GUSTAVO PETRO, continues the programme he campaigned on: a hardline posture toward FARC dissidents, the ELN and the Clan del Golfo, mega-prison construction on the Bukele model, and the severance of relations with Cuba and Nicaragua — 'In my administration, there will be no ties with tyrannies' — alongside the closure of 14 embassies and 15 consulates. Reporting puts the membership of illegal armed groups at about 28,800, more than double the figure at the start of the Petro period.",
   "details": "VENEZUELA: pot-banging protests multiplying over recurring blackouts and appliance damage from voltage fluctuations; Aragua state (about 80 km southeast of Caracas) among the worst affected with 4-5 hour daily cuts; Turmero residents blocked roads and burned tyres. Delcy Rodríguez called for electricity and water rationing, announced immediate measures in early August to safeguard the National Electrical System and requested activation of an Electricity and Water Savings Plan, blaming the 'Super Niño' phenomenon and a recent earthquake; conservation measures including air-conditioner settings openly rejected by the public. Sworn in as acting president January 5, 2026; 2018 US sanctions lifted April 2026. TRANSITION: Caracas government-opposition talks opened August 6 under Jorge Rodríguez and Dinorah Figuera; no published electoral timetable. Maduro and Cilia Flores in US custody; trial set June 1, 2027 before Judge Alvin Hellerstein, SDNY. CUBA: six nationwide grid collapses in 2026 (two in March, three within ten days in July, one August 2-3); blackouts exceeding twenty hours a day; some communities up to 105 consecutive days without steady electricity; neighbourhood protests in Havana municipalities after outages exceeding 48 hours, residents banging pots and pans and burning rubbish. Fuel supply lost after the January 3 seizure of Maduro and the subsequent US oil blockade; Mexican imports halted under US pressure; Executive Order 14404 sanctions; Visa and Mastercard processing lost; UN describes a humanitarian emergency. Bruno Rodríguez: 'no progress.' COLOMBIA: President Abelardo de la Espriella in office since August 7, succeeding Gustavo Petro; hardline posture toward FARC dissidents, the ELN and the Clan del Golfo; mega-prison construction on the Bukele model; severance of ties with Cuba and Nicaragua ('In my administration, there will be no ties with tyrannies'); closure of 14 embassies and 15 consulates; membership of illegal armed groups reported at about 28,800.",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus predictions that removing Maduro would stabilise Venezuela are DISCONFIRMED AS TO OUTCOME SO FAR: the successor government is rationing electricity and water, is being blamed in the street for the outages, and has published no electoral timetable seven months after taking office. Predictions that US pressure on Venezuela would produce a secondary humanitarian crisis in Cuba are CONFIRMED and now include a public-order dimension — six nationwide grid collapses in 2026, blackouts past twenty hours a day, and neighbourhood protests in Havana after outages exceeding 48 hours. Predictions of a rightward realignment in the northern Andes are CONFIRMED: Colombia's de la Espriella government has severed ties with Cuba and Nicaragua and closed 14 embassies and 15 consulates."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-27",
   "theatre": "US-China Trade",
   "tag": "US-China",
   "headline": "US-CHINA — BEIJING ANSWERED THE DESIGNATIONS WITH A THREAT OF COUNTERMEASURES AND TEHRAN THANKED IT PUBLICLY. FOREIGN MINISTRY SPOKESMAN LIN JIAN SAID ON AUGUST 26 THAT 'CHINA WILL TAKE ALL NECESSARY MEASURES TO FIRMLY SAFEGUARD ITS OWN RIGHTS,' RESTATING THAT TRADE WITH IRAN 'SHOULD NOT BE DISRUPTED,' THAT IT 'COMPLIES WITH INTERNATIONAL LAW,' AND CONDEMNING THE MEASURES AS ECONOMIC WARFARE. IRAN'S PARLIAMENT SPEAKER MOHAMMAD BAGHER GHALIBAF THANKED CHINA FOR DECLINING TO COMPLY. AND THE VOLUME KEEPS FALLING WITHOUT ANY DESIGNATION HAVING BITTEN: KPLER DATA PUBLISHED AUGUST 26 PUTS CHINESE IMPORTS OF IRANIAN CRUDE THROUGH HORMUZ AT ABOUT 530,000 BARRELS A DAY — 48% BELOW PRE-WAR LEVELS AND 72% BELOW THE OCTOBER 2024 PEAK OF 1.9 MILLION — WITH THE RED SEA ROUTE AT ABOUT 1.02 MILLION BARRELS A DAY IN AUGUST AGAINST AN APRIL PEAK OF 2.62 MILLION. SHANDONG TEAPOTS ARE SUBSTITUTING: ONE BOUGHT BRAZIL'S LAPA CRUDE THIS WEEK AND OTHERS ARE LOOKING AT IRAQ'S BASRAH. FREIGHT VIA SUEZ NOW RUNS $10-11 A BARREL AGAINST ROUGHLY $5 VIA YANBU BEFORE THE HOUTHI CAMPAIGN, AND THE CAPE ROUTE TAKES ABOUT 50 DAYS AGAINST 25-27. THE SEPARATE TARIFF TRACK IS UNCHANGED AND STILL POINTED AT SEPTEMBER 24: A 7.5% SECTION 301 OVERCAPACITY TARIFF IS PREPARED AHEAD OF THE XI-TRUMP WASHINGTON SUMMIT, WHICH WOULD TAKE SECOND-TERM DUTIES TO ROUGHLY 20% — THE CEILING WASHINGTON COMMITTED TO ON JULY 27 — WITH THE CURRENT REPLACEMENT RATE AT 12.5% AND THE TRADE TRUCE EXPIRING NOVEMBER 10. TAIWAN IS QUIET BY THE NUMBERS: PLA SORTIE RATES HAVE REVERTED TO THE PRE-LAI BASELINE SINCE THE START OF 2026.",
   "tags": [
    "US-China",
    "Lin Jian",
    "All Necessary Measures",
    "Blocking Statute",
    "Economic Warfare",
    "Ghalibaf Thanks China",
