   "source": "CBS News live updates, August 26, 2026 (Lin Jian: 'China will take all necessary measures to firmly safeguard its own rights'; Ghalibaf thanks Beijing); The National, 'Chart of the week: China's Iranian oil imports nearly halve since war,' August 26, 2026 (Kpler data); Reuters via Yahoo Finance, 'Iranian oil offers to Chinese buyers fall as US blockade bites, sources say,' August 2026; RFE/RL via GlobalSecurity, 'Report: US Blockade Squeezes Iranian Oil Supplies To China,' August 21, 2026; Bloomberg, 'US Eyes China Overcapacity Tariffs of 7.5% Before Xi-Trump Talks,' August 24, 2026; Fortune, 'Trump readies a new tariff to punish China for its flood of cheap exports,' August 24, 2026; Taiwan Ministry of National Defense daily PLA activity releases, August 2026; American Enterprise Institute, 'China & Taiwan Update, August 7, 2026.'",
   "summary": "TWO DAYS AFTER CHINESE AND HONG KONG ENTITIES APPEARED ON THE FIRST OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST DESIGNATION LIST, BEIJING MOVED FROM OBJECTION TO A THREAT OF COUNTERMEASURES.\n\nTHE CHINESE POSITION HARDENED IN WORDING IF NOT IN SUBSTANCE. Foreign Ministry spokesman LIN JIAN said on AUGUST 26 that 'CHINA WILL TAKE ALL NECESSARY MEASURES TO FIRMLY SAFEGUARD ITS OWN RIGHTS,' restating that China's trade with Iran 'SHOULD NOT BE DISRUPTED' and 'COMPLIES WITH INTERNATIONAL LAW,' and characterising the American measures as ECONOMIC WARFARE that 'will only further intensify tensions.' The countermeasures already in place pre-date the designations: Beijing has instructed its companies to disregard US restrictions on independent refiners importing Iranian crude and has invoked its 2021 BLOCKING STATUTE prohibiting compliance with foreign sanctions it deems illegitimate. IRAN'S PARLIAMENT SPEAKER MOHAMMAD BAGHER GHALIBAF PUBLICLY THANKED CHINA for declining to comply — the first time in this war that Tehran has thanked Beijing by name for sanctions non-compliance.\n\nAND THE OPERATIVE FACT REMAINS THAT THE VOLUME COLLAPSED BEFORE ANY DESIGNATION TOOK EFFECT. Kpler data published on AUGUST 26 puts Chinese imports of Iranian crude moving through the STRAIT OF HORMUZ at about 530,000 BARRELS A DAY — 48% BELOW PRE-WAR LEVELS and 72% BELOW THE OCTOBER 2024 PEAK OF 1.9 MILLION barrels a day. The alternative RED SEA ROUTE, which peaked at 2.62 MILLION barrels a day in APRIL 2026 (a 228% increase on the preceding twenty-month average), fell to 940,000 in JULY and recovered only to about 1.02 MILLION in AUGUST — 61% below the April peak. China remains the world's largest crude importer at 12.4 MILLION barrels a day and takes about 90% of Iran's sanctioned oil exports, against a strategic reserve of 1-1.4 BILLION barrels.\n\nTHE SUBSTITUTION IS VISIBLE IN THE PURCHASE RECORD. Shandong's independent 'TEAPOT' refiners — about a fifth of Chinese refining capacity and the principal buyers of sanctioned crude — are moving off Iranian barrels: one bought BRAZIL'S LAPA CRUDE this week and others are examining IRAQ'S BASRAH, with buyers now looking beyond both Russia and Iran given thin Iranian availability under the blockade. Iranian oil offers to Chinese buyers have fallen as the blockade bites. THE ECONOMICS OF THE DETOUR ARE PART OF THE ANSWER: freight via SUEZ now costs roughly $10-11 A BARREL against about $5 via YANBU before the Houthi campaign, and the CAPE OF GOOD HOPE routing takes about 50 DAYS against 25-27 for the standard Red Sea passage.\n\nTHE TARIFF TRACK IS UNCHANGED AND STILL SCHEDULED. The United States is preparing a 7.5% SECTION 301 OVERCAPACITY TARIFF on Chinese goods ahead of a XI-TRUMP SUMMIT IN WASHINGTON ON SEPTEMBER 24. The rate would sit on top of the 10-12.5% announced the previous month and would take second-term duties to roughly 20% — precisely the ceiling Washington committed to on JULY 27 — with the current replacement rate at 12.5% and the bilateral trade truce expiring NOVEMBER 10. The design is explicitly calibrated to punish overcapacity without endangering either the truce or the summit.\n\nTAIWAN. The military picture is quieter than the trade picture. PLA incursion rates, which doubled to more than 300 a month after President Lai Ching-te's May 2024 inauguration, have REVERTED TO THE PRE-LAI BASELINE since the start of 2026 — assessed as an adjustment in Beijing's coercion strategy rather than seasonal variation. Taiwan's Ministry of National Defense tracked 21 PLA aircraft and nine to fourteen naval vessels on AUGUST 5, with 17 aircraft crossing the median line.",
   "details": "LIN JIAN (August 26): 'China will take all necessary measures to firmly safeguard its own rights'; trade with Iran 'should not be disrupted'; it 'complies with international law'; US measures condemned as economic warfare that 'will only further intensify tensions.' Pre-existing countermeasures: instruction to Chinese companies to disregard US restrictions on independent refiners importing Iranian crude; invocation of the 2021 blocking statute. Ghalibaf publicly thanked China for declining to comply. KPLER (published August 26): Chinese imports of Iranian crude via Hormuz ~530,000 bpd, 48% below pre-war and 72% below the October 2024 peak of 1.9m bpd. Red Sea route: April 2026 peak 2.62m bpd (+228% on the preceding 20-month average); July 940,000 bpd; August ~1.02m bpd (61% below the April peak). China imports 12.4m bpd of crude annually and takes ~90% of Iran's sanctioned exports; strategic reserve 1-1.4bn barrels. SUBSTITUTION: Shandong teapots (about a fifth of Chinese refining capacity, principal buyers of sanctioned crude) — one bought Brazil's Lapa crude this week; others examining Iraq's Basrah; buyers looking beyond both Russia and Iran. Iranian oil offers to Chinese buyers falling. FREIGHT: Suez route ~$10-11/bbl against ~$5 via Yanbu before the Houthi campaign; Cape of Good Hope routing ~50 days against 25-27 days for the standard Red Sea passage. TARIFFS: 7.5% Section 301 overcapacity tariff prepared ahead of the Xi-Trump Washington summit on September 24; would sit on top of 10-12.5% announced the previous month and take second-term duties to ~20%, the ceiling committed to on July 27; current replacement rate 12.5%; bilateral trade truce expires November 10. TAIWAN: PLA sortie rates reverted to the pre-Lai baseline since the start of 2026, assessed as a strategy adjustment rather than seasonal variation; August 5 — 21 PLA aircraft and 9-14 naval vessels tracked, 17 aircraft crossing the median line. US-Taiwan tariff deal of early 2026 stands at 15% against the 32% imposed in 2025, with Taiwan committed to about $85bn of US energy, aircraft and equipment purchases.",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus predictions that US secondary sanctions would force Chinese compliance are DISCONFIRMED SO FAR AS TO INTENT: Beijing has threatened 'all necessary measures,' invoked its blocking statute, and been publicly thanked by Tehran for non-compliance. Predictions that sanctions would be the instrument that cut Iran's oil revenue are DISCONFIRMED AS TO MECHANISM: the 48% year-on-year collapse in Chinese purchases through Hormuz was produced by naval interdiction and by freight economics — $10-11 a barrel via Suez against $5 via Yanbu — before any designation from the August 24 package took effect. Predictions of a US-China military confrontation over Taiwan in this period remain DISCONFIRMED: PLA sortie rates have fallen back to the pre-Lai baseline, and the operative bilateral instrument is a scheduled summit on September 24 with a tariff calibrated not to endanger it."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-27",
   "theatre": "East Asia — DPRK / Korean Peninsula",
   "tag": "North Korea",
   "headline": "NORTH KOREA — PYONGYANG HELD ITS MOST SIGNIFICANT POLITICAL MEETING SINCE THE EXERCISE CONCESSION AND DID NOT MENTION THE UNITED STATES AT ALL. KIM JONG UN PRESIDED ON AUGUST 25 OVER AN ENLARGED MEETING OF THE POLITICAL BUREAU OF THE WORKERS' PARTY CENTRAL COMMITTEE, REPORTED BY STATE MEDIA ON AUGUST 26, REVIEWING PROGRESS IN 'MAJOR ECONOMIC SECTORS' AND THE IMPLEMENTATION OF 2026 POLICY GOALS. THE REPORT CARRIED NO REFERENCE TO PRESIDENT TRUMP'S RENEWED OVERTURE OR TO A POSSIBLE SUMMIT. KIM CALLED FOR 'EXTRAORDINARY RESPONSIBILITY AND HIGH PRUDENCE' IN MAJOR STATE PROJECTS AND CITED 'A SERIES OF DEVIATIONS' CAUSED BY 'THE IMMATURE OPERATION AND LEADERSHIP OF THE ECONOMIC GUIDANCE ORGANS FAILING TO KEEP ABREAST OF OUR GREATER IDEALS AND PROGRESS.' TODAY, AUGUST 27, IS THE DATE ON WHICH ULCHI FREEDOM SHIELD'S COUNTEROFFENSIVE PHASE WAS ORIGINALLY SCHEDULED TO END. IT NEVER TOOK PLACE: THE ELEVEN-DAY, TWO-PHASE EXERCISE WAS CUT TO FIVE DAYS AS A GOODWILL GESTURE AND ENDED ON AUGUST 21, DELETING THE HALF PYONGYANG DENOUNCES AS AN INVASION REHEARSAL. NO FURTHER DPRK LAUNCH HAS BEEN REPORTED SINCE THE ROUGHLY TEN KN-25 SHORT-RANGE BALLISTIC MISSILES FIRED ON AUGUST 20, AND PYONGYANG HAS STILL NOT PUBLICISED THOSE LAUNCHES. NO DATE OR VENUE FOR A TRUMP-KIM MEETING HAS BEEN ANNOUNCED.",
   "tags": [
    "North Korea",
    "Kim Jong Un",
    "Politburo Enlarged Meeting",
    "Workers Party Central Committee",
    "Economy Focus",
    "No Mention Of Trump",
    "Extraordinary Responsibility",
    "Series Of Deviations",
    "Ulchi Freedom Shield",
    "Counteroffensive Phase Deleted",
    "August 27 Original End Date",
    "Exercise Curtailed",
    "KN-25",
    "August 20 Launches",
    "Silence On Launches",
    "No Summit Date",
    "Kim Yo Jong"
   ],
   "source": "The Korea Times, 'N. Korea's Kim presides over party meeting, with no mention of Trump's overture,' August 26, 2026; UPI, 'Kim Jong Un focuses on economy, silent on Trump overtures,' August 26, 2026; KCNA via Korea Times and UPI, report of the enlarged meeting of the Workers' Party Central Committee political bureau held August 25, 2026; Republic of Korea Joint Chiefs of Staff and Ministry of National Defense statements on the conclusion of Ulchi Freedom Shield, August 21, 2026.",
   "summary": "THE CONCESSION WAS MADE, THE ORDNANCE WAS FIRED, AND THIS CYCLE PYONGYANG ANSWERED WITH AN ECONOMIC AGENDA AND A SILENCE.\n\nTHE MEETING. On TUESDAY AUGUST 25 KIM JONG UN presided over an ENLARGED MEETING OF THE POLITICAL BUREAU of the ruling Workers' Party Central Committee, reported by state media on WEDNESDAY AUGUST 26. The meeting reviewed progress in the country's 'MAJOR ECONOMIC SECTORS' and discussed implementation of policy goals for 2026. Kim called for 'EXTRAORDINARY RESPONSIBILITY AND HIGH PRUDENCE' in carrying out major state projects and pointed to 'A SERIES OF DEVIATIONS,' which he attributed to 'THE IMMATURE OPERATION AND LEADERSHIP OF THE ECONOMIC GUIDANCE ORGANS FAILING TO KEEP ABREAST OF OUR GREATER IDEALS AND PROGRESS.'\n\nTHE ABSENCE IS THE DATAPOINT. The report of the most senior party gathering since the American exercise concession CARRIED NO MENTION OF PRESIDENT TRUMP'S RENEWED DIPLOMATIC OUTREACH, of the AUGUST 18-19 confirmation that he expects to meet Kim this year, or of any summit. Pyongyang has now received a unilateral American concession, answered it with a missile salvo it declined to publicise, and held a politburo meeting that does not acknowledge the offer. The audit records this as a non-response rather than a rejection — the DPRK has neither accepted nor refused, and KIM YO JONG's AUGUST 19 statement dismissing the exercise reduction as leaving the drills' 'provocative, aggressive nature' unchanged, and denying that any Trump-Kim contact occurred, remains the only substantive North Korean comment.\n\nTODAY IS THE DATE THE DELETED PHASE WOULD HAVE ENDED. ULCHI FREEDOM SHIELD was originally scheduled as an ELEVEN-DAY EVENT IN TWO PHASES — defensive operations to AUGUST 21 and COUNTEROFFENSIVE OPERATIONS TO AUGUST 27. It was curtailed to five days as a goodwill gesture and South Korea's military confirmed it ENDED ON FRIDAY AUGUST 21. THE COUNTEROFFENSIVE PHASE — the half Pyongyang denounces as an invasion rehearsal — DID NOT TAKE PLACE AT ALL, and the calendar reaches its scheduled end date today with nothing having been run.\n\nTHE SEQUENCE OF RECORD IS UNCHANGED: exercise reduction and Trump's confirmation that he expects to meet Kim this year on AUGUST 18-19; Kim Yo Jong's dismissal and her denial of any contact on AUGUST 19; about TEN KN-25 SHORT-RANGE BALLISTIC MISSILES fired roughly 300 kilometres seaward from the Pyongyang area on AUGUST 20; the drills terminated on AUGUST 21; and PYONGYANG STILL SILENT ON ITS OWN LAUNCHES, a departure from its usual practice of publicising tests. No further launch has been reported. NO DATE OR VENUE FOR A TRUMP-KIM MEETING HAS BEEN ANNOUNCED.",
   "details": "POLITBURO (held August 25, reported August 26): Kim Jong Un presided over an enlarged meeting of the political bureau of the Workers' Party Central Committee; reviewed progress in 'major economic sectors' and implementation of 2026 policy goals; called for 'extraordinary responsibility and high prudence' in major state projects; cited 'a series of deviations' attributed to 'the immature operation and leadership of the economic guidance organs failing to keep abreast of our greater ideals and progress.' No mention of Trump's renewed outreach or of a summit. ULCHI FREEDOM SHIELD: originally an eleven-day, two-phase exercise — defensive operations to August 21, counteroffensive operations to August 27; curtailed to five days as a goodwill gesture; ended Friday August 21; the counteroffensive phase never took place. August 27 is its original end date. SEQUENCE OF RECORD: August 18-19 exercise reduction and Trump's confirmation that he expects to meet Kim this year ('Yeah, I will be'; 'I get along with him great'), with Pyongyang's arsenal put at '57 very powerful nuclear weapons'; August 19 Kim Yo Jong dismisses the reduction as leaving the drills' 'provocative, aggressive nature' unchanged and denies any Trump-Kim contact; August 20 about ten KN-25 short-range ballistic missiles fired roughly 300 km seaward from the Pyongyang area; August 21 drills terminated. Pyongyang has not publicised its own launches. No further launch reported. No date or venue for a Trump-Kim meeting announced.",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus predictions of a fourth Trump-Kim summit remain UNTESTED: the offer stands, no date or venue exists, and the DPRK's most senior political gathering since the concession did not mention it. Predictions that unilateral exercise reductions would elicit reciprocal restraint are DISCONFIRMED for this instance — the concession was answered with a ten-missile salvo — while predictions that they would elicit escalation are also unsupported, since Pyongyang declined to publicise those launches and has fired nothing since. Predictions that the DPRK would exploit American distraction in the Middle East to raise its own tempo remain DISCONFIRMED at this point in the cycle: the observable North Korean agenda this week was economic management and an admission of 'a series of deviations' in it."
  },
