   "date": "2026-08-27",
   "theatre": "Global Economy — Hormuz-Dependent States",
   "tag": "Hormuz-Dependent Economies",
   "headline": "HORMUZ-DEPENDENT ECONOMIES — THE SIX-MONTH MARK IS BEING REACHED WITH RATIONING AS THE NORMAL CONDITION ACROSS SOUTH AND SOUTHEAST ASIA. PAKISTAN, BANGLADESH, THE PHILIPPINES, VIETNAM AND SRI LANKA HAVE IMPOSED FOUR-DAY WORKING WEEKS, WORK-FROM-HOME MANDATES OR SCHOOL CLOSURES TO CONSERVE FUEL. PAKISTAN IMPORTS ROUGHLY 85% OF ITS SUPPLY BY TANKER; BANGLADESH IMPORTS ABOUT 95% OF ITS PETROLEUM NEEDS. INDIA, WHICH TAKES 60% OF ITS LPG THROUGH THE STRAIT, IS SEEING BLACK-MARKETING OF DOMESTIC CYLINDERS AND RESTAURANT CLOSURES. IN NORTH ASIA THE EXPOSURE IS STRUCTURAL RATHER THAN IMMEDIATE: SOUTH KOREA DRAWS ABOUT 70% OF ITS CRUDE AND 18% OF ITS LNG THROUGH HORMUZ AND HOLDS ABOUT 206 DAYS OF RESERVES; JAPAN TAKES MORE THAN 90% OF ITS CRUDE FROM THE MIDDLE EAST, ABOUT 75% VIA HORMUZ, AND HOLDS ABOUT 146 DAYS. KOREAN PETROCHEMICALS ARE ALREADY IMPAIRED — LOTTE CHEMICAL, LG CHEM AND HANWHA SOLUTIONS HAVE ISSUED POTENTIAL FORCE MAJEURE NOTICES AND YEOCHUN NCC HAS DECLARED SUPPLY DISRUPTION. LNG CARRIER RATES ARE AROUND $300,000 A DAY, A 650% INCREASE, AND CRUDE TANKER RATES ARE AT HISTORIC HIGHS. IN THE UNITED STATES THE WAR IS NOW A PRICE INDEX: JULY PCE INFLATION HELD AT 3.7% YEAR-ON-YEAR, REPORTED AUGUST 26 AND WELL ABOVE THE FEDERAL RESERVE'S 2% TARGET, WITH THE AAA NATIONAL AVERAGE FOR REGULAR AT ABOUT $4.10 A GALLON AND AUGUST 2026 ON COURSE TO BE THE HIGHEST AUGUST ON RECORD AT A $4.06 MONTHLY AVERAGE, SURPASSING 2022'S $3.97.",
   "tags": [
    "Hormuz-Dependent Economies",
    "Pakistan",
    "Bangladesh",
    "Philippines",
