   ],
   "source": "The White House, 'Operation Economic Outcast: Total Isolation of the Iranian Regime,' August 24, 2026; NPR, 'Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent unveils new U.S. economic sanctions to isolate Iran,' August 24, 2026; PBS NewsHour, 'WATCH: Bessent announces new sanctions to block Iran's revenue streams,' August 24, 2026; CBS News, 'Bessent announces campaign to create \"economic onslaught\" against Iran and its partners,' August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'US launches “Operation Economic Outcast” to cut Iran's economic lifeline,' August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'US threatens toughest sanctions yet against Iran: What we know,' August 24, 2026; The Washington Post, 'Bessent unveils sweeping campaign of sanctions and pressure against Iran,' August 24, 2026; NBC News, 'Bessent threatens new Iran secondary sanctions, says Trump asking world leaders to cooperate,' August 24, 2026; Axios, 'Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent announces \"D-day\" sanctions against Iran,' August 24, 2026; Iran International live blog, 'US launches “Operation Economic Outcast” against Iran,' entries of August 24, 2026; U.S. Central Command via Iran International, blockade tally as of August 24, 2026; AP/ABC News, 'Iran's rial currency hits new record low as US prepares to announce more sanctions,' August 24, 2026; Gulf News, 'Iran currency plunges to record low as US dollar breaks 2 million rials on open market,' August 24, 2026; CNBC, 'Oil price today: WTI, Brent, U.S. sanctions, Iran,' August 24, 2026; Reuters via HDFC Sky, 'Oil Prices Dip on Profit Booking as US Sanctions Loom,' August 24, 2026; straits.live Strait of Hormuz status board, Day 177, 24 August 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Yemen's Houthis report attack on Saudi oil tanker in Red Sea,' August 24, 2026; gCaptain, 'Houthis Escalate Saudi Shipping Campaign With VLCC Strike,' August 24, 2026; UKMTO advisories via Arab News, 'Oil tanker struck by unidentified projectile off Oman,' August 25, 2026 (0131 UTC); UKMTO via Deccan Herald/Marine Link, 'Tanker hit by unknown projectile off Saudi Arabia's Yanbu, fire breaks out,' August 24, 2026; CNN Business, 'Iran has lost significant control of the Strait of Hormuz,' August 18-19, 2026 (Kpler data); Gulf News, 'US-Iran standoff: What UAE residents need to know today (Aug. 24, 2026)'; Press TV, 'Omani foreign minister to visit Iran to discuss Strait of Hormuz shipping,' August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Pakistan's army chief back in Iran: Can he break peace talks deadlock?', August 24, 2026; The Express Tribune, 'CDF Munir, Naqvi meet Iranian interior minister upon arrival in Tehran,' August 24, 2026; The Washington Post, 'More than 750 U.S. service members wounded in Iran war,' August 21, 2026; Stars and Stripes, 'Pentagon adds 60 wounded to Iran war casualty count,' August 21, 2026; AAA Fuel Prices national average, August 24, 2026.",
   "summary": "THE PENDING EVENT OF THE PREVIOUS CYCLE HAPPENED, AND IT HAPPENED ENTIRELY ON PAPER. Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent held his 2 p.m. ET news conference on Monday August 24 and gave the successor phase of the war a name: OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST. The audit had closed the previous cycle recording the announced shape rather than the announced content; the content is now on the record.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY ISSUED. Treasury made SECTORAL DETERMINATIONS against five parts of the Iranian economy — DIGITAL ASSETS, TECHNOLOGY, GOLD, AVIATION and SHIPPING — which is the legal architecture that makes whole industries sanctionable rather than named firms. Alongside it, nearly 60 Iran-linked people, entities and vessels were designated, located across the UNITED ARAB EMIRATES, HONG KONG, CHINA, SINGAPORE and SWITZERLAND. Bessent said every country would be given a DEFINED TIMELINE to wind down Iran-related business, that most secondary sanctions would NOT be immediate, and that a 'CURE PERIOD' would run before enforcement — 'We are giving everyone the opportunity to remedy bad behavior,' with the qualifier 'We do not have infinite patience here.' He indicated that the sanctioning of a major financial institution should be expected by the end of the week. The White House framing places the operation as the ENDGAME PHASE succeeding Operation Epic Fury: 'Beginning today, the actions of Treasury and other agencies will tighten the noose and block every potential source of revenue that funds the IRGC and the evil Iranian regime,' with Iran offered a choice between 'complete global isolation and a subsistence economy' and normalisation.\n\nTHE OBJECTIVE WAS STATED WITHOUT EUPHEMISM, AND THAT IS THE CYCLE'S MOST IMPORTANT SENTENCE. Bessent said of the campaign: 'It is going to work in Iran, and we are going to collapse this regime.' He also said 'we are launching an economic onslaught against Iran's financial connections around the globe'; 'our objective is to sever every economic lifeline that sustains this tyrannical regime until Tehran stands alone'; 'No one is above the reach of US sanctions'; and 'Let there be no ambiguity as to the position of the United States. An economic engagement of any kind with this murderous regime will expose those responsible to the full reach of American power.' REGIME COLLAPSE IS NOW AN OPENLY DECLARED WAR AIM AND THE DECLARED INSTRUMENT FOR ACHIEVING IT IS THE BANKING SYSTEM. For an audit whose central tracked prediction is a US ground seizure, the significance is that the administration has now stated both the maximalist objective and the non-military means in the same appearance.\n\nTHE ONE COUNTER-INDICATOR IS REAL AND IS RECORDED AS SUCH. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth said the same day that military force is NOT RULED OUT in the Strait of Hormuz 'or anywhere else.' This is the same non-foreclosure formula the audit has tracked since April; it forecloses nothing and commits nothing, and it is logged because a tracker that only records de-escalatory evidence is not a tracker.\n\nTHE MARKET MARKED THE OFFENSIVE DOWN. Brent FELL on the day of the announcement, after gaining more than 5% the previous week. Published figures diverge: Reuters carried Brent off 1.4% to about $93 and WTI off 1.6% to about $85.70; CNBC carried Brent off 2.5% to $92.06 and WTI off 2.5% to $84.89; the straits.live board carried $92.10, down 1.67% over 24 hours and about 27.9% above the ~$72 pre-crisis baseline. The explanation given across outlets is profit-taking after a two-week rally rather than a judgement on the sanctions. The audit records the direction and notes it plainly: the single greatest financial offensive ever marshalled against an adversary was announced, and the price of the commodity it targets went down.\n\nTHE RIAL WENT THE OTHER WAY. Iran's currency hit a record low of 2.02 MILLION TO THE DOLLAR on the open market as trading opened Monday, against an official Central Bank rate of about 1.5 million. Reporting puts rice up about 60% and beef up more than 150% since the war began. This is where the campaign is already landing, and it was landing before the designations were issued.\n\nTEHRAN'S ANSWER WAS DISMISSAL PLUS A TARGETING THREAT. Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said the campaign is bound to fail: 'They cannot think of any other solution in confronting the great Iranian people, so they repeatedly put forward the same old plans.' Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmail Baghaei said 'Any escalation of this situation will undoubtedly bring about consequences' and 'Our hands are not tied,' and — the operative line — said Iran has the RIGHT TO TARGET ANY LOCATION USED TO LAUNCH ATTACKS AGAINST IT, warning countries against providing territory or facilities to the United States. That is a threat against host states, delivered on the day the host states were asked to join a financial blockade.\n\nTWO TANKERS WERE HIT IN TWENTY-FOUR HOURS, IN TWO DIFFERENT SEAS. Yemen's Houthis struck the Saudi VLCC AMZAN, operated by the national shipping company Bahri, about 63 nautical miles west of YANBU in the Red Sea with ballistic missiles and drones on August 24; a fire broke out on the main deck, nearby vessels fled the area, all crew are safe and no environmental impact was reported. Houthi military spokesman Yahya Saree described the strike as part of a 'SIEGE FOR SIEGE' operation targeting the Saudis. Then at 0131 UTC on August 25 — inside this cycle — UKMTO reported a tanker struck by an unidentified projectile about NINE NAUTICAL MILES NORTHEAST OF ASH SHISHAH, OMAN, with the ENGINE ROOM DAMAGED and the vessel DISABLED; the crew were reported safe and no party has been identified as responsible.\n\nTHE BLOCKADE TIGHTENED BY ONE HULL AND DISCLOSED A NUMBER IT HAD NOT PUBLISHED BEFORE. CENTCOM said that as of August 24 US forces had redirected 71 commercial vessels, disabled three and boarded two since the July 14 resumption — up from 70 on August 23 — and, for the first time in this record, that MORE THAN 40 HUMANITARIAN AID VESSELS HAVE BEEN PERMITTED PASSAGE. A blockade that runs a humanitarian exception is a different instrument from a blockade that does not, and the audit logs the disclosure.\n\nAND THE TRAFFIC PICTURE ACQUIRED ITS FIRST DATASET THAT POINTS ONE WAY. CNN Business, working from Kpler ship-tracking data, reported that MORE THAN 80% OF LIQUIDS TRANSITS OVER THE PRECEDING TWO WEEKS TOOK THE OMANI ROUTE — the UN-authorised channel Iran opposes — or were dark transits that likely took it, concluding that Iran has LOST SIGNIFICANT CONTROL of the waterway. Gulf News separately reported southern-corridor traffic up roughly 400% over two weeks to nearly 200 ships weekly. Against that, the straits.live board still carries ONE transit on its latest daily datapoint against a 73-a-day baseline, 370 hulls holding position away from berth, eight of nine major container carriers routing via the Cape of Good Hope, and market odds of a December 31 reopening at 34%. The estimates remain irreconcilable, but the direction of the newest and best-sourced one has changed, and that is recorded.\n\nDIPLOMACY MOVED ON TWO TRACKS, BOTH THROUGH CAPITALS RATHER THAN CAPITALS' PATRONS. Pakistan's Chief of Defence Forces and Chief of Army Staff Field Marshal Asim Munir travelled to Tehran on August 24 with Interior Minister Mohsin Naqvi and met Iranian Interior Minister Eskandar Momeni, on a day-long visit aimed at a negotiated settlement. The 60-day window of the ISLAMABAD MEMORANDUM — signed by Pakistan, Iran and the United States on June 17 — LAPSED IN MID-AUGUST WITHOUT EXTENSION, and Islamabad's position is that the framework remains available as a template. Separately, Oman's Foreign Minister Sayyid Badr Albusaidi arrives in Tehran TODAY, August 25, to meet Araghchi on the Strait, following their August 21 telephone call and nearly three months of Iran-Oman negotiation over a safe shipping route.\n\nTHE LEDGER. The Pentagon's published toll held at 775 US casualties — 18 killed and 757 wounded — with no addition since August 21. The service breakdown published with that release is new to this record and is worth stating precisely: MORE THAN 580 OF THE WOUNDED ARE ARMY SOLDIERS, 86 ARE SAILORS, 64 ARE AIRMEN AND 19 ARE MARINES. Independent tallies counting casualties the Defense Casualty Analysis System omits put the true wounded total above 900. The AAA national average for regular gasoline was $4.0991 on August 24, effectively flat on the day and 95 cents above a year earlier; diesel reached $5.6134, a further record August level and $1.93 above last year. War-risk cover holds at about $10.0m per VLCC passage, forty times pre-crisis, with six P&I clubs withdrawn. No US or Israeli strike inside Iranian territory has been confirmed since August 1 — a twenty-fourth consecutive night.",
   "details": "OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST (announced 2 p.m. ET, August 24): five sectoral determinations — digital assets, technology, gold, aviation, shipping. Nearly 60 Iran-linked persons, entities and vessels designated across the UAE, Hong Kong, China, Singapore and Switzerland. Every country to receive a defined wind-down timeline; most secondary sanctions not immediate; a 'cure period' precedes enforcement; a major financial institution designation signalled for end of week. BESSENT QUOTES: 'It is going to work in Iran, and we are going to collapse this regime'; 'we are launching an economic onslaught against Iran's financial connections around the globe'; 'our objective is to sever every economic lifeline that sustains this tyrannical regime until Tehran stands alone'; 'No one is above the reach of US sanctions'; 'An economic engagement of any kind with this murderous regime will expose those responsible to the full reach of American power'; 'We are giving everyone the opportunity to remedy bad behavior'; 'We do not have infinite patience here'; 'This will not end until this regime stands alone'; it is 'no longer acceptable to operate in the gray spaces.' WHITE HOUSE: 'Beginning today, the actions of Treasury and other agencies will tighten the noose and block every potential source of revenue that funds the IRGC and the evil Iranian regime'; Iran's choice framed as 'complete global isolation and a subsistence economy' or normalisation; operation positioned as the endgame phase after Operation Epic Fury. CRITICISM: sanctions specialist Brett Erickson — 'This was not economic D-Day...It was something in the middle.' HEGSETH (August 24): military force not ruled out in the Strait of Hormuz 'or anywhere else.' IRAN: Araghchi — 'They cannot think of any other solution in confronting the great Iranian people, so they repeatedly put forward the same old plans'; Baghaei — 'Any escalation of this situation will undoubtedly bring about consequences,' 'Our hands are not tied,' and Iran has the right to target any location used to launch attacks against it, with a warning to countries against providing territory or facilities to the US. RIAL: record low 2.02m/USD on the open market August 24; official CBI rate ~1.5m; rice +~60%, beef +>150% since the war began. OIL: Brent -1.4% to ~$93 and WTI -1.6% to ~$85.70 (Reuters); Brent -2.5% to $92.06 and WTI -2.5% to $84.89 (CNBC); straits.live $92.10, -1.67% over 24h, +27.9% on the ~$72 baseline; move attributed to profit-taking after a >5% weekly gain. SHIPPING: Saudi VLCC AMZAN (Bahri) struck by Houthi ballistic missile and drones ~63nm west of Yanbu, Red Sea, August 24 — fire on main deck, nearby vessels fled, crew safe, no environmental impact; Houthi spokesman Yahya Saree called it a 'siege for siege' operation against the Saudis. UKMTO: tanker struck by unidentified projectile ~9nm NE of Ash Shishah, Oman, 0131 UTC August 25 — engine room damaged, vessel disabled, crew safe, no attribution. BLOCKADE: CENTCOM 71 redirected / 3 disabled / 2 boarded as of August 24 (70 on August 23; 68 on August 21; 67 on August 20; 64 on August 17; 44 on August 3; 35 on August 2), plus MORE THAN 40 HUMANITARIAN AID VESSELS PERMITTED PASSAGE — first disclosure of that figure. TRAFFIC: CNN Business/Kpler — >80% of liquids transits over the prior two weeks took the Omani route or were dark transits that likely did, 'Iran has lost significant control'; Gulf News — southern-corridor traffic up ~400% over two weeks to nearly 200 ships weekly; straits.live — 1 transit on the latest daily datapoint vs 73/day baseline, 370 hulls holding position, 8 of 9 major container carriers via the Cape of Good Hope, Dec 31 reopening odds 34%. DIPLOMACY: Field Marshal Asim Munir (CDF/COAS) and Interior Minister Mohsin Naqvi in Tehran August 24, meeting Interior Minister Eskandar Momeni; the Islamabad Memorandum of June 17 (Pakistan, Iran, US) lapsed in mid-August without extension; Oman FM Sayyid Badr Albusaidi arrives Tehran August 25 to meet Araghchi, after their August 21 call and ~3 months of route negotiation. US CASUALTIES: 775 total — 18 killed, 757 wounded; service split of the wounded: 580+ Army, 86 Navy, 64 Air Force, 19 Marines; independent tallies above 900. PUMP: AAA regular $4.0991 August 24 (yesterday $4.0986; week ago $4.0636; month ago $4.1054; year ago $3.1533). Diesel $5.6134 (yesterday $5.6074; week ago $5.4454; month ago $5.2401; year ago $3.6862). STRIKE PAUSE: no confirmed US or Israeli strike inside Iran since August 1 — a twenty-fourth consecutive night. WAR RISK: ~$10.0m per VLCC transit, 40x pre-crisis; six P&I clubs withdrawn.",
   "prediction_impact": "The predicted US ground seizure of the Strait of Hormuz or Kharg Island remains DISCONFIRMED at Day 180, and this cycle supplies the clearest evidence yet of what replaced it. Corpus predictions that the United States would pursue REGIME CHANGE in Iran are CONFIRMED as to objective — the Treasury Secretary said 'we are going to collapse this regime' on the record — and DISCONFIRMED as to instrument, because the declared means is a five-sector sanctions architecture with a cure period, not a landing force. Predictions that the war would end in a negotiated settlement are WEAKENED: the Islamabad Memorandum's 60-day window lapsed in mid-August without extension, and the mediating states are now working the problem through interior and foreign ministries rather than through a signed framework. Predictions that closing the Strait would give Iran durable leverage are now under direct empirical pressure: Kpler data showing more than 80% of liquids transits taking the Omani route, and a roughly 400% two-week rise in southern-corridor traffic, are the first datasets of the war pointing to Iranian loss of control rather than to a spread of estimates — though the straits.live and Kpler pictures remain irreconcilable and the audit does not resolve them. Predictions that oil would price the escalation upward are DISCONFIRMED for this instance: Brent fell on the day the offensive was announced. The Hegseth non-foreclosure is logged as a live counter-indicator and is UNTESTED. And the casualty composition is a quiet, hard datapoint against the ground thesis: after 180 days, 19 of 757 wounded are Marines — the service that would carry an amphibious lodgement has absorbed 2.5% of the wounded.",
   "alternate_readings": [
    {
     "reading": "Operation Economic Outcast is read as the decisive instrument that will bring the Iranian state down without a ground campaign — and, by the opposing reading, as a repackaging of sanctions that already existed, announced with D-Day rhetoric precisely because the kinetic campaign did not produce a settlement and there is no further military rung the administration is willing to climb.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Documented: Treasury issued five sectoral determinations (digital assets, technology, gold, aviation, shipping) and designated nearly 60 persons, entities and vessels across the UAE, Hong Kong, China, Singapore and Switzerland on August 24. Documented: Bessent said 'we are going to collapse this regime,' and separately on August 20 that maximum economic pressure means 'likely there will not be a large-scale kinetic restart.' Documented: most secondary sanctions are not immediate and a 'cure period' runs before enforcement. Documented: sanctions specialist Brett Erickson said 'This was not economic D-Day...It was something in the middle,' and Araghchi called the measures 'the same old plans.' Documented: Brent fell on the day of the announcement. Documented: the rial hit a record 2.02m to the dollar the same morning. Not documented: whether any third-country bank, refinery or registry will actually cease Iran-related business inside the timelines given, and whether the designations reach counterparties the existing dragnet did not.",
     "public_assertion_by": [
      "Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent and the White House, presenting the operation as the endgame phase that will isolate Iran completely",
      "Sanctions practitioners including Brett Erickson, who described the package as falling short of its billing",
      "Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi, characterising it as a repetition of failed policy",
      "Market participants, who sold crude on the announcement rather than bidding it up"
     ],
     "why_unresolvable": "A sanctions regime whose enforcement is deliberately deferred cannot be assessed on announcement day. The cure period means the first observable test — a designation against a major financial institution, or a third-country bank visibly exiting Iranian business — has not yet occurred. Resolution would require documented compliance or documented defiance by a named large counterparty in China, the UAE or Turkey, or a measurable further fall in Iranian export volumes attributable to designation rather than to the naval blockade.",
     "open_question_ref": "operation-economic-outcast-substance-august-2026"
    },
    {
     "reading": "Kpler's finding that more than 80% of recent liquids transits took the Omani route is read as proof that the US Navy has broken Iran's grip on the Strait — and, by the opposing reading, as a measure of how little traffic there is to allocate, since the same period carries straits.live at one transit against a 73-a-day baseline and 370 hulls sitting off berth.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Documented: CNN Business, citing Kpler, reported that more than 80% of liquids transits over the preceding two weeks took the Omani route or were dark transits that likely took it, and concluded Iran has lost significant control. Documented: Gulf News reported southern-corridor traffic up roughly 400% over two weeks to nearly 200 ships weekly. Documented: the straits.live board carries one transit on its latest daily datapoint against a 73-a-day pre-crisis baseline, 370 hulls holding position away from berth, and eight of nine major container carriers routing via the Cape of Good Hope. Documented: CENTCOM has redirected 71 vessels and permitted more than 40 humanitarian aid vessels through. Not documented: a single reconciled denominator. A route-share statistic and an absolute-volume statistic are not in conflict as arithmetic; they are in conflict as claims about who controls the waterway.",
     "public_assertion_by": [
      "CNN Business and Kpler, reporting Iranian loss of control by route share",
      "US officials asserting that American forces facilitate 15-20 transits nightly and that 'they don't control the strait. We do.'",
      "straits.live and war-risk underwriters, describing the waterway as closed to commercial shipping",
      "Iran's Supreme National Security Council, maintaining that the Strait 'is closed and will not reopen'"
     ],
     "why_unresolvable": "The dominant transit mode is dark by definition, and route attribution for dark hulls is inferred rather than observed. No party publishes a reconciled daily count with a stated methodology, and the two live datasets measure different things — share of a shrunken flow versus size of the flow. Resolution would require a single authority publishing daily transit counts with route attribution and a stated treatment of dark vessels, or insurers repricing on the basis of one of the figures.",
     "open_question_ref": "hormuz-transit-volume-dispute-august-2026"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-25",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Ground Invasion Tracker",
   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 180: STATUS HOLDS NO_GROUND_TROOPS, AND THIS CYCLE THE ADMINISTRATION PUT ITS THEORY OF VICTORY ON THE RECORD IN A SENTENCE. TREASURY SECRETARY BESSENT SAID OF OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST: 'IT IS GOING TO WORK IN IRAN, AND WE ARE GOING TO COLLAPSE THIS REGIME.' REGIME CHANGE IS NOW A DECLARED WAR AIM AND THE DECLARED INSTRUMENT IS FIVE SECTORAL SANCTIONS DETERMINATIONS WITH A CURE PERIOD, NOT A LANDING FORCE. THE WHITE HOUSE CALLS IT THE 'ENDGAME' PHASE SUCCEEDING OPERATION EPIC FURY. THE COUNTER-INDICATOR IS EQUALLY ON THE RECORD AND IS LOGGED: SECRETARY OF WAR HEGSETH SAID THE SAME DAY THAT MILITARY FORCE IS NOT RULED OUT IN THE STRAIT 'OR ANYWHERE ELSE.' A NEW STRUCTURAL DATAPOINT ARRIVED WITH THE PENTAGON CASUALTY BREAKDOWN: OF 757 WOUNDED, MORE THAN 580 ARE ARMY, 86 NAVY, 64 AIR FORCE AND 19 MARINES — THE SERVICE THAT WOULD CARRY AN OPPOSED LANDING HAS ABSORBED 2.5% OF THE WOUNDED ACROSS 180 DAYS. USNI'S AUGUST 24 TRACKER CONFIRMS USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN HAS LEFT CENTCOM AFTER ALMOST SEVEN MONTHS AND IS NOW IN 7TH FLEET, COMPLETING THE ROTATION THAT LEAVES CARRIER PRESENCE AT TWO. BOXER ARG WITH THE 11TH MEU REMAINS THE SOLE DEPLOYED ARG IN THEATRE AND HAS STILL RECEIVED NO TASKING, NO EMBARKATION AND NO REHEARSAL. KHARG UNCHANGED. DRAFT RUNG UNCHANGED. NO LANDING, NO SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER — DISCONFIRMED FOR A 180TH DAY.",
