   "source": "The White House, 'Operation Economic Outcast: Total Isolation of the Iranian Regime,' August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'US launches “Operation Economic Outcast” to cut Iran's economic lifeline,' August 24, 2026 (Hegseth non-foreclosure; Bessent quotes); Iran International live blog, entry of August 24, 2026, 20:36 GMT+1 (Hegseth: force not ruled out in the Strait 'or anywhere else'); CBS News, 'Bessent announces campaign to create \"economic onslaught\" against Iran and its partners,' August 24, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'US threatens toughest sanctions yet against Iran: What we know,' August 24, 2026 (Bessent: 'we are going to collapse this regime'); The Washington Post, 'More than 750 U.S. service members wounded in Iran war,' August 21, 2026; Stars and Stripes, 'Pentagon adds 60 wounded to Iran war casualty count,' August 21, 2026 (service breakdown: 580+ Army, 86 Navy, 64 Air Force, 19 Marines); The Intercept, 'The Pentagon Found a New Way to Undercount U.S. Casualties in Iran,' August 4, 2026; USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, August 24, 2026 (USS Abraham Lincoln departs CENTCOM for 7th Fleet); USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, August 17, 2026 (Boxer ARG in the Arabian Sea); The War Zone, 'Where Are The Aircraft Carriers: August 11, 2026' (one ARG deployed worldwide against a requirement of 'well north of three'); CNN, reporting of June 12, 2026 on the May 19 CJCS briefing on a ground mission to seize Iranian HEU and the President's decision against it; TankerTrackers reporting of August 14-16, 2026 on Kharg Island loadings; CNBC, 'Automatic U.S. military draft registration by December 2026 planned,' April 9, 2026; The Hill, 'Automatic registration for US military draft to begin in December,' 2026; U.S. Central Command via Iran International, blockade tally as of August 24, 2026.",
   "summary": "DAY 180 PRODUCED NO EXECUTION INDICATOR AND ONE DECLARATION OF INTENT THAT MATTERS MORE THAN MOST INDICATORS DO.\n\nTHE OBJECTIVE IS NOW STATED AND THE INSTRUMENT IS NOW NAMED, AND THEY DO NOT MATCH THE PREDICTION THIS TRACKER EXISTS TO TEST. At his August 24 news conference Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent said of Operation Economic Outcast: 'It is going to work in Iran, and we are going to collapse this regime.' That is regime change stated as a war aim by a cabinet secretary. The instrument he described in the same appearance is five sectoral determinations — digital assets, technology, gold, aviation, shipping — nearly 60 designations, defined wind-down timelines for third countries and a 'cure period' before secondary sanctions bite. The White House release positions the operation as the ENDGAME PHASE succeeding Operation Epic Fury. For a corpus prediction of a US ground seizure, this is the strongest single piece of evidence to date about how the administration intends to finish: the maximalist objective and the non-military means were announced in the same room, on the same afternoon.\n\nTHE COUNTER-INDICATOR IS REAL AND IS RECORDED WITHOUT DISCOUNT. Secretary of War Pete Hegseth said on August 24 that military force is NOT RULED OUT in the Strait of Hormuz 'or anywhere else.' This is the fourth month in which the non-foreclosure formula has been repeated, and it remains what it has always been: a statement that forecloses nothing, commits nothing and is compatible with both a landing and no landing. It is logged because the tracker's credibility depends on logging evidence that runs against its assessment.\n\nA NEW STRUCTURAL DATAPOINT ENTERED THE RECORD, AND IT IS QUIET BUT HARD. The Pentagon release that took the wounded count to 757 carries a service breakdown this tracker had not previously entered: MORE THAN 580 OF THE WOUNDED ARE ARMY SOLDIERS, 86 ARE SAILORS, 64 ARE AIRMEN AND 19 ARE MARINES. Across 180 days of war, the service that would carry an opposed amphibious lodgement has absorbed roughly 2.5% of the wounded. That is the casualty signature of a force protecting bases and enforcing a blockade, not of a force fighting for a beach or preparing to. Independent tallies counting casualties the Defense Casualty Analysis System omits put the true wounded total above 900, and the audit records that dispute alongside the official figure.\n\nNAVAL PICTURE — THE ROTATION COMPLETED AND THE COUNT IS CONFIRMED AT TWO. USNI News's fleet tracker of August 24 records that USS ABRAHAM LINCOLN (CVN-72) HAS LEFT THE MIDDLE EAST after almost seven months and is now in 7th Fleet. That closes the movement the previous cycle corrected: USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77) has been inside CENTCOM since April 23 and USS George Washington (CVN-73) arrived August 19, leaving net carrier presence at TWO — the same number CENTCOM published in July. A like-for-like rotation inside a static force level is not a build-up, and the completion of the relief confirms rather than changes that reading.\n\nAMPHIBIOUS PICTURE — UNCHANGED, AND THE STRUCTURAL CONSTRAINT IS UNCHANGED WITH IT. The Boxer Amphibious Ready Group — USS Boxer (LHD-4), USS Comstock (LSD-45), USS Portland (LPD-27) — with the embarked 11th Marine Expeditionary Unit remains the sole deployed ARG in the CENTCOM area, in the Arabian Sea, with no tasking, no embarkation, no landing rehearsal, no mine-countermeasures preparation and no repositioning toward Kharg reported at any point in the war. One ARG is deployed worldwide against combatant-commander requests for 'well north of three' ARG-MEU pairings; the Iwo Jima ARG with the 22nd MEU remains committed to SOUTHCOM counter-narcotics operations in the Caribbean.\n\nKHARG — NO CHANGE. No US amphibious, mine-countermeasures or ground activity against or near the island was reported in this cycle. Loading remains episodic following the mid-August restart after a roughly 25-day halt. The constraint on Iranian exports continues to be access, insurance and counterparty risk rather than infrastructure damage or occupation.\n\nDRAFT RUNG — NO CHANGE, AND THE TWO INSTRUMENTS REMAIN SEPARATE. Reporting continues to carry a start date of December 18, 2026 for automatic Selective Service registration of men aged 18 to 26 under the FY2026 National Defense Authorization Act, shifting registration from individuals to the agency via federal data integration. The Selective Service System's own automatic-registration rule was withdrawn in July 2026 and has not been re-proposed. Automatic registration builds the pool and inducts nobody: conscription requires Congress to amend the Military Selective Service Act and the President to authorise inductions, and neither step has occurred, been requested or been scheduled.\n\nFORCE LEVEL — UNCHANGED ABOVE 50,000, NONE OF IT INSIDE IRAN.",
   "details": "STATUS: no_ground_troops, Day 180, unchanged. DECLARED OBJECTIVE (NEW): Bessent, August 24 — 'It is going to work in Iran, and we are going to collapse this regime.' Instrument: Operation Economic Outcast — five sectoral determinations (digital assets, technology, gold, aviation, shipping), ~60 designations across the UAE, Hong Kong, China, Singapore and Switzerland, defined third-country wind-down timelines, cure period before enforcement. White House frames it as the endgame phase after Operation Epic Fury. COUNTER-INDICATOR (NEW, LOGGED): Hegseth, August 24 — military force not ruled out in the Strait of Hormuz 'or anywhere else.' CASUALTY COMPOSITION (NEW TO THIS TRACKER): of 757 wounded, 580+ Army, 86 Navy, 64 Air Force, 19 Marines; 18 killed; 775 total; independent tallies above 900. CARRIERS: USNI August 24 — USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) has left the Middle East after almost seven months and is in 7th Fleet; USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77) in CENTCOM since April 23; USS George Washington (CVN-73) since August 19. Net presence TWO, matching CENTCOM's July figure. AMPHIBIOUS: Boxer ARG (LHD-4, LSD-45, LPD-27) with 11th MEU in the Arabian Sea — sole deployed ARG in theatre, no tasking, no embarkation, no rehearsal, no MCM preparation, no movement toward Kharg. One ARG deployed worldwide against a stated requirement of 'well north of three'; Iwo Jima ARG / 22nd MEU committed to SOUTHCOM. GROUND COMPONENT: ~2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne Division with divisional headquarters in the region since late March 2026, contingency and base-defence roles, none inside Iran. KHARG: no US activity; loading episodic after the mid-August restart. DRAFT: December 18, 2026 automatic-registration date still reported under the FY2026 NDAA; SSS rule withdrawn July 2026 and not re-proposed; no draft order, no lottery, no induction authority, no IRR call-up. FORCE LEVEL: more than 50,000 US personnel in the Middle East, more than 330 aircraft, more than 20 warships enforcing the blockade (71 vessels redirected, 3 disabled, 2 boarded, plus more than 40 humanitarian aid vessels permitted through as of August 24). BACKFILL STANDING: CNN, June 12, 2026 — CJCS Gen. Dan Caine flew from Brussels to CENTCOM headquarters on May 19 to be briefed on sending ground troops into Iran to seize its highly enriched uranium; Trump declined on casualty grounds; Iran subsequently sealed the cache with collapsed tunnels and mined entrances.",
   "prediction_impact": "The predicted US ground seizure remains DISCONFIRMED for a 180th consecutive day, and this cycle sharpens the reason rather than merely extending the count. Corpus predictions of US-driven REGIME CHANGE in Iran move to CONFIRMED as to intent — the objective is now stated by name — while the specific predictions that regime change would be delivered by ground forces are DISCONFIRMED for this instance, because the instrument announced in the same appearance is a sanctions architecture with a deliberately deferred enforcement date. Predictions that the administration would preserve a military option indefinitely are SUPPORTED by Hegseth's non-foreclosure, which is logged as UNTESTED. The casualty composition is entered as new evidence against the ground thesis rather than as commentary: a force preparing an opposed landing generates Marine casualties, and after 180 days the Marine share of the wounded is 19 of 757. Predictions that a carrier build-up would presage a ground phase remain DISCONFIRMED — the Lincoln's departure completes a like-for-like relief that leaves the count at the same two carriers CENTCOM published in July. Predictions of a draft or mobilisation remain DISCONFIRMED: the only moving instrument is an administrative registration change that inducts nobody."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-25",
