   "tag": "Gulf States",
   "headline": "GULF STATES — THE SANCTIONS LANDED ON THE NEIGHBOURS AS MUCH AS ON TEHRAN, AND THE FIRST DESIGNATION LIST NAMES THE UAE. NEARLY 60 OF THE ENTITIES AND VESSELS DESIGNATED UNDER OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST SIT IN THE UNITED ARAB EMIRATES, HONG KONG, CHINA, SINGAPORE AND SWITZERLAND; ABU DHABI, WHICH SUSPENDED ALL TRADE, COMMERCIAL EXCHANGE AND FINANCIAL TRANSACTIONS WITH IRAN ON AUGUST 19, IS REPORTED TO BE PREPARING PHASED CARGO AND TRADE RESTRICTIONS IN PARALLEL WITH THE US MEASURES. THE GULF STATES THAT HAVE SPENT BILLIONS ON HORMUZ BYPASS PIPELINES HAVE NOT COMMENTED ON THE PACKAGE. IRAN'S FOREIGN MINISTRY SAID TEHRAN HAS THE RIGHT TO TARGET ANY LOCATION USED TO LAUNCH ATTACKS AGAINST IT AND WARNED COUNTRIES AGAINST PROVIDING TERRITORY OR FACILITIES TO THE UNITED STATES. THE HOUTHIS STRUCK THE SAUDI VLCC AMZAN OFF YANBU WITH BALLISTIC MISSILES AND DRONES IN WHAT THEIR SPOKESMAN CALLED A 'SIEGE FOR SIEGE' OPERATION AGAINST THE SAUDIS, AND A SECOND TANKER WAS DISABLED OFF OMAN'S ASH SHISHAH AT 0131Z TODAY. OMAN'S FOREIGN MINISTER ARRIVES IN TEHRAN TODAY. GULF AIR ROUTES REMAIN DISRUPTED.",
   "tags": [
    "Gulf States",
    "UAE",
    "Operation Economic Outcast",
    "UAE Designations",
