    "Six Blackouts 2026",
    "105 Days Without Power",
    "Bruno Rodriguez",
    "No Progress",
    "Executive Order 14404",
    "Fuel Blockade",
    "UN Humanitarian Emergency",
    "Venezuela",
    "Delcy Rodriguez",
    "Jorge Rodriguez",
    "Dinorah Figuera",
    "Maduro Trial June 2027",
    "Cilia Flores",
    "Colombia",
    "Petro"
   ],
   "source": "Al Jazeera, 'Cuba's power grid collapses again despite restoration efforts,' August 3, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Cuba suffers second island-wide blackout in a week amid Trump fuel blockade,' July 10, 2026; Wikipedia compilation '2024-2026 Cuba blackouts' (grid-collapse chronology); CNN Politics, 'Venezuela's Nicolás Maduro gets a June trial date,' July 22, 2026; Atlantic Council, 'Experts react: The US just captured Maduro. What's next for Venezuela and the region?'; Al Jazeera, 'Petro becomes first president to visit Venezuela since Maduro abduction,' April 24, 2026.",
   "summary": "NO MATERIAL DEVELOPMENT WAS REPORTED IN THIS THEATRE IN THE PAST TWENTY-FOUR HOURS, AND THE ENTRY IS LOGGED TO PRESERVE CONTINUITY AND TO CONSOLIDATE THE CUBAN FIGURES.\n\nCUBA. The national electricity system has now collapsed SIX TIMES IN 2026 — twice in March, three times within ten days in July, and once on AUGUST 2-3. Reporting describes blackouts EXCEEDING TWENTY HOURS A DAY, with some communities recorded at UP TO 105 CONSECUTIVE DAYS without steady electricity. The proximate cause is fuel: Cuba lost its principal supplier when Washington imposed an oil blockade following the January 3 seizure of Nicolás Maduro, and imports from Mexico have also been halted under US pressure. Sanctions run under EXECUTIVE ORDER 14404; Visa and Mastercard processing has been lost; the United Nations has described a humanitarian emergency endangering lives. Foreign Minister BRUNO RODRÍGUEZ said last week that there had been 'NO PROGRESS' toward ending the impasse. Industrial output and transport remain crippled.\n\nVENEZUELA. The government-opposition talks that opened in Caracas on August 6 under Jorge Rodríguez for the government and Dinorah Figuera for the opposition continue without a published electoral timetable. Delcy Rodríguez remains acting president; she has made significant changes to the armed forces, has met many of Washington's demands, and had her 2018 US sanctions lifted in April. Nicolás Maduro and Cilia Flores remain in US custody, with trial set for JUNE 1, 2027 before Judge Alvin Hellerstein in the Southern District of New York on four counts including narco-terrorism conspiracy and cocaine importation conspiracy.\n\nCOLOMBIA. No new development. The Petro government's April engagement with Caracas — the first presidential visit since Maduro's removal, which produced pledges of military cooperation against cross-border criminal networks — remains the operative state of the bilateral relationship.",
   "details": "CUBA: six nationwide grid collapses in 2026 (two in March, three within ten days in July, one August 2-3); blackouts >20 hours/day; some communities up to 105 consecutive days without steady electricity; fuel cut off since the January 3 seizure of Maduro and the subsequent US oil blockade; Mexican imports halted under US pressure; sanctions under Executive Order 14404; Visa and Mastercard processing lost; UN humanitarian emergency declared; FM Bruno Rodríguez: 'no progress' toward ending the impasse. VENEZUELA: Caracas talks opened August 6 under Jorge Rodríguez (government) and Dinorah Figuera (opposition), no published electoral timetable; Delcy Rodríguez acting president, US sanctions on her lifted April 2026; Maduro and Cilia Flores in US custody, trial June 1, 2027, Judge Alvin Hellerstein, SDNY, four counts. COLOMBIA: no new development; April 24 Petro-Rodríguez meeting and military-cooperation pledge remain operative.",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus predictions that removing Maduro would produce rapid Venezuelan democratisation remain UNRESOLVED and trending toward DISCONFIRMED: nineteen days after talks opened there is still no published electoral timetable, and the acting president is the outgoing government's vice-president. Predictions that the Venezuelan intervention would transmit into a Cuban collapse are PARTIALLY CONFIRMED and the transmission channel is exactly the one predicted — fuel — with six national grid failures in a single year and communities recorded at up to 105 days without steady power. Predictions of a US military move against Cuba remain DISCONFIRMED; the instrument is an oil blockade and a sanctions order, and this is the same substitution of economic for kinetic means recorded in the Iran theatre this cycle."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-25",
   "theatre": "US-China Trade",
   "tag": "US-China",
   "headline": "US-CHINA — THE ENFORCEMENT COLLISION ARRIVED AND WASHINGTON PUT CHINESE ENTITIES ON THE FIRST DESIGNATION LIST. OPERATION ECONOMIC OUTCAST NAMED PERSONS, ENTITIES AND VESSELS IN CHINA AND HONG KONG AMONG ITS ~60 DESIGNATIONS, AND THE ADMINISTRATION SIGNALLED THAT CHINA IS NOT EXEMPT FROM SECONDARY SANCTIONS. BEIJING'S ANSWER IS UNCHANGED AND EXPLICIT: SANCTIONS 'ARE NOT THE SOLUTION' AND DO NOT 'FIT THE INTEREST OF ANY PARTY'; CHINA HAS INVOKED ITS 2021 BLOCKING STATUTE AND HAS TOLD ITS COMPANIES TO IGNORE US RESTRICTIONS. AND ON THE SAME DAY A SEPARATE AND POSSIBLY LARGER COLLISION WAS REPORTED: THE UNITED STATES IS PREPARING A 7.5% SECTION 301 OVERCAPACITY TARIFF ON CHINESE GOODS AHEAD OF A XI-TRUMP SUMMIT IN WASHINGTON ON SEPTEMBER 24 — A RATE THAT WOULD TAKE SECOND-TERM DUTIES TO ROUGHLY 20%, EXACTLY THE CEILING WASHINGTON COMMITTED TO ON JULY 27, WITH THE CURRENT REPLACEMENT RATE AT 12.5% AND THE BILATERAL TRADE TRUCE EXPIRING NOVEMBER 10. CHINA'S IRANIAN CRUDE IMPORTS REMAIN AROUND 534,000 BARRELS A DAY IN AUGUST AGAINST ABOUT 1.4 MILLION A DAY LAST YEAR — A COLLAPSE PRODUCED BY THE BLOCKADE BEFORE ANY DESIGNATION WAS ISSUED.",
   "tags": [
    "US-China",
