   "date": "2026-08-24",
   "headline": "DAY 179 — THE SANCTIONS ARRIVE AND SO DOES A FEE STATUTE: BOTH SIDES SPENT THE CYCLE LEGISLATING AND WRITING RATHER THAN LANDING. BESSENT PUBLISHED AN FT OP-ED ON AUGUST 23 DECLARING 'AT DAWN BEGINS AN ECONOMIC D-DAY — THE SINGLE GREATEST FINANCIAL OFFENSIVE EVER MARSHALLED AGAINST AN ADVERSARY,' WITH HIS DETAILING NEWS CONFERENCE SET FOR 2 P.M. ET TODAY. HOURS EARLIER IRAN'S PARLIAMENTARY NATIONAL SECURITY AND FOREIGN POLICY COMMISSION APPROVED ARTICLE 3 OF ITS 'STRATEGIC ACTION TO ENSURE THE SECURITY AND PROGRESS OF THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ' PLAN — SERVICE FEES ON 'AUTHORISED' TRANSITING SHIPS, PAYABLE IN RIALS 'OR ANY OTHER CURRENCY DESIRED BY THE ISLAMIC REPUBLIC.' SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI ESCALATED FROM 'ENEMY' TO TOTALITY, WARNING VIA IRNA THAT TEHRAN 'WILL NOT ALLOW A SINGLE DROP OF OIL TO LEAVE THE PERSIAN GULF' IF PRESSURE ESCALATES, THAT IRAN WOULD 'RETALIATE IN A SEISMIC MANNER,' AND — NEW THIS CYCLE — THAT IT WOULD TARGET THE BYPASS ROUTES AROUND THE STRAIT. AND PRESIDENT PEZESHKIAN BROKE PUBLICLY WITH THE SUPREME LEADER: IRAN 'CANNOT CONTINUE WITH WAR FOREVER,' AND 'ONE DAY, A DECISION MUST BE MADE TO SAVE THE COUNTRY FROM THE STATE OF NEITHER WAR NOR PEACE.' A TWENTY-THIRD CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. CENTCOM'S BLOCKADE TALLY REACHED 70 REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED AS OF AUGUST 23. BRENT $94.39; PUMP $4.0986; DIESEL $5.6074; PENTAGON CASUALTIES HOLD AT 775. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED FOR A 179TH DAY.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Iran War",
   "tags": [
    "Iran War",
    "Strait of Hormuz",
