   ],
   "source": "USNI News, 'Carrier USS George Washington Now in the Middle East,' August 20, 2026; The War Zone, 'USS George Washington's Mideast Arrival Highlights Strain On Carrier Force,' August 2026; The War Zone, 'Where Are The Aircraft Carriers: August 11, 2026'; Stars and Stripes, 'USS George Washington arrives in Middle East to relieve USS Abraham Lincoln,' August 20, 2026; Army Recognition, 'U.S. Navy Deploys USS George H.W. Bush Aircraft Carrier to Indian Ocean in CENTCOM Area,' April 2026; USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, August 17, 2026; CNN Politics, 'Exclusive: US military rushed to prepare ground mission to capture Iran's uranium, but Trump paused it, sources say,' June 12, 2026; CNN Politics, 'Exclusive: Iran sealed uranium cache and placed mines amid fears of US operation to seize material,' June 13, 2026; New York Post via RT, 'Pentagon eyeing megaraid to steal Iran's nuclear stockpile,' July 26, 2026; Fox News opinion (Robert Maginnis), 'The Pentagon's plan to seize Iran's uranium isn't a raid. It's an invasion,' 2026; The Washington Post, 'Risky commando plan to seize Iran's uranium came at Trump's request,' April 1, 2026; The Washington Post/AP, 'Iran security chief threatens neighbors against economic measures,' August 22-23, 2026; Black Voice News, 'National Automatic Draft Registration Set to Begin in December 2026,' August 4, 2026; Military Times, 'Selective Service System wants to wargame the draft,' July 24, 2026; The Hill, 'Automatic registration for US military draft to begin in December,' 2026; TASS/CENTCOM blockade tally, August 23, 2026; CNBC, 'Bessent says U.S. likely won't restart large-scale Iran combat as it steps up economic pressure,' August 20, 2026.",
   "summary": "STATUS HOLDS AT no_ground_troops FOR A 179TH CONSECUTIVE DAY. This cycle produced no new execution indicator, one correction the audit owes its own record, and one backfill that is the most concrete ground-planning evidence in the war.\n\nTHE CORRECTION. The previous cycle recorded net carrier presence in CENTCOM as ONE following the August 19 relief of USS Abraham Lincoln by USS George Washington. That is wrong and is withdrawn. USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77) entered the CENTCOM area of responsibility on April 23 and has been operating in the northern Arabian Sea in support of the blockade throughout; USS George Washington (CVN-73), with USS Robert Smalls (CG-62) and USS Shoup (DDG-86), arrived on August 19 and relieved the Lincoln, which sailed for San Diego after roughly 200 consecutive days at sea without a liberty port call, a deployment length that drew official concern for crew mental and physical health. Net carrier presence in theatre is therefore TWO. The substantive judgment is unchanged and arguably strengthened: two carriers is exactly the number CENTCOM published in July, so the August movement is a like-for-like rotation inside a static force level, not a build-up. The War Zone's August 11 survey also records that no US carrier is currently positioned in the Western Pacific, which is a statement about the size of the force rather than about intent in the Gulf.\n\nTHE BACKFILL, AND IT CUTS BOTH WAYS. This tracker has carried the July 26 New York Post report of a Pentagon concept requiring 'thousands of ground troops' as the war's only genuine ground-planning indicator. That understated the record. CNN reported on June 12 that the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, Gen. Dan Caine, made a secret and rushed trip on May 19 from a meeting of senior NATO officials in Brussels back to CENTCOM headquarters in Tampa to be briefed on plans to send US ground troops into Iran to forcibly seize its stockpile of highly enriched uranium — and that the President declined to proceed after warnings that the operation could produce a large number of American casualties. On June 13 CNN reported that Iran had escalated efforts to seal the cache, deliberately collapsing tunnels and booby-trapping entrances with explosive mines, making access far more dangerous and time-consuming than a month earlier. The Washington Post had reported on April 1 that the commando concept was drawn up at Trump's own request. The audit enters this as the strongest evidence in the whole war that a ground operation was seriously prepared: a named four-star, a dated trip, a specific headquarters, a decision point. It is also, on the same evidence, the strongest documented instance of that operation being declined at the presidential level, and of the target being physically hardened against it in the weeks that followed. Both halves belong in the record.\n\nEVERY EXECUTION INDICATOR REMAINED AT ZERO. No landing, no embarkation, no MEU tasking, no airborne insertion, no relief ARG, no new deployment order, no mobilisation, no draft order, no medical or fuel prepositioning consistent with a lodgement, and no reported special-operations ground activity inside Iran. The amphibious rung should be read structurally rather than as a daily count: The War Zone's August 11 survey records ONE amphibious ready group deployed worldwide against combatant-commander requests for 'well north of three' ARG-MEU pairings, with three ARGs in maintenance and three in various training states. In theatre that one is the Boxer ARG — USS Boxer (LHD-4), USS Comstock (LSD-45), USS Portland (LPD-27) — with the 11th MEU, in the Arabian Sea as of the August 17 USNI tracker, never tasked and never repositioned toward Kharg. The Navy's other deployed ARG, Iwo Jima with the 22nd MEU, is committed to Caribbean counter-narcotics under SOUTHCOM; the 24th MEU is deployed without an ARG at all as 'Littoral Combat Force 24.' A force that cannot generate the pairings its own commanders ask for is not a force massing for an opposed landing.\n\nTHE ADMINISTRATION'S STATED PATH REMAINS FINANCIAL. Bessent's line from August 20 — that maximum economic pressure means 'likely there will not be a large-scale kinetic restart' — was not walked back in this cycle, and his FT op-ed of August 23 frames the next phase entirely in banking terms.\n\nIRAN'S OWN THREAT MODEL STILL EXPECTS FORCE FLOW THAT HAS NOT ARRIVED. Rezaei's August 23 remarks included a caution against any additional US military deployment to the region. That is a negative datapoint worth recording precisely because it is Iranian: the adversary is still warning against a build-up that the open force-flow record does not show.\n\nTHE DRAFT RUNG DID NOT MOVE. Reporting continues to carry a December 18, 2026 start for automatic Selective Service registration of men aged 18-26 under a Defense Authorization Act provision, covering citizens, green-card holders, refugees, asylum seekers and undocumented men in the same age band. Registration builds the pool and inducts nobody; conscription would still require Congress to amend the Military Selective Service Act and a presidential induction order, and neither exists. The Selective Service System's own 'readiness simulation' procurement produced no announced award.",
   "details": "STATUS: no_ground_troops, day 179. CARRIERS (CORRECTED): TWO in CENTCOM — USS George H.W. Bush (CVN-77), in theatre since April 23, northern Arabian Sea, blockade support; USS George Washington (CVN-73) with USS Robert Smalls (CG-62) and USS Shoup (DDG-86), arrived August 19, relieved USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72), which departed for San Diego after ~200 consecutive days at sea without a liberty port call. The prior cycle's 'net presence is one' is withdrawn. Two carriers matches CENTCOM's July public figure — rotation, not surge. No US carrier currently in the Western Pacific (TWZ, August 11). GROUND-PLANNING BACKFILL: CNN, June 12, 2026 — CJCS Gen. Dan Caine made a secret, rushed May 19 trip from a NATO meeting in Brussels to CENTCOM HQ, Tampa, to be briefed on plans to send ground troops into Iran to seize its highly enriched uranium; Trump decided against the operation after warnings of a large number of potential US casualties. CNN, June 13, 2026 — Iran collapsed tunnels and booby-trapped entrances with explosive mines to seal the cache. Washington Post, April 1, 2026 — the commando concept was drawn up at Trump's request. New York Post, July 26, 2026 — a later concept requiring 'thousands of ground troops' at Fordow, Natanz, Isfahan and Pickaxe Mountain with SEAL Team 6's Silver Squadron, the Army's 2nd Ranger Battalion and the 21st Ordnance Company; single-sourced, no decision reported. EXECUTION INDICATORS: all zero — no landing, no embarkation, no MEU tasking, no airborne insertion, no relief ARG, no new deployment order, no mobilisation, no draft order, no medical or fuel prepositioning consistent with a lodgement, no reported special-operations ground activity inside Iran. AMPHIBIOUS STRUCTURE: ONE ARG deployed worldwide (TWZ, August 11); combatant commanders request 'well north of three' ARG-MEU pairings; three ARGs in maintenance, three in training states. In theatre: Boxer ARG (LHD-4, LSD-45, LPD-27) with 11th MEU, Arabian Sea per USNI August 17, never tasked. Iwo Jima ARG with 22nd MEU committed to SOUTHCOM Caribbean counter-narcotics. 24th MEU deployed without an ARG as 'Littoral Combat Force 24.' USS Tripoli home at Sasebo/Okinawa since July 22. GROUND COMPONENT: ~2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne Division with divisional headquarters, in region since late March 2026, never committed to Iranian territory; ~2,200-2,500 Marines of the 11th MEU afloat. More than 50,000 US personnel in the Middle East, unchanged. More than 330 US military aircraft across Al Udeid, Muwaffaq Salti and Prince Sultan; more than 20 warships supporting the blockade. BLOCKADE: CENTCOM 70 redirected / 3 disabled / 2 boarded as of August 23. STATED PATH: Bessent, August 20 — maximum economic pressure means 'likely there will not be a large-scale kinetic restart'; FT op-ed August 23 frames the next phase in banking terms. IRANIAN SIGNAL: Rezaei, August 23 — cautioned against additional US military deployment to the region. DRAFT: December 18, 2026 automatic Selective Service registration for men 18-26 under a Defense Authorization Act provision (citizens, green-card holders, refugees, asylum seekers, undocumented men in band); no amendment to the Military Selective Service Act, no presidential induction order, no award announced under the 'readiness simulation' procurement. KHARG: no US amphibious, mine-countermeasures or ground activity against or near the island in this cycle.",
   "prediction_impact": "The predicted US ground invasion of Iran, and the predicted US ground seizure of Kharg Island or the Strait of Hormuz, remain DISCONFIRMED at Day 179. This cycle's backfill materially improves the audit's own evidence on both sides of the question and should be scored as such. Corpus predictions that the United States would prepare a ground operation against Iran's nuclear material are CONFIRMED as to preparation: a named Chairman of the Joint Chiefs flew from Brussels to Tampa on May 19 specifically to be briefed on sending ground troops into Iran. Corpus predictions that such an operation would be executed are DISCONFIRMED as to execution, by the same reporting: the President declined it on casualty grounds, and within weeks the target was physically sealed with collapsed tunnels and mined entrances, raising rather than lowering the cost of any later attempt. The audit's carrier-count correction does not change any prediction status: two carriers in CENTCOM is the same number CENTCOM published in July, so predictions of a naval surge preceding a landing remain DISCONFIRMED, and the correction removes an error that had made the negative case look marginally stronger than the evidence supports. Predictions that amphibious forces would mass are DISCONFIRMED and structurally so — one ARG deployed worldwide against a stated requirement of more than three is a force that cannot mass, irrespective of intent. Predictions of a return of conscription remain DISCONFIRMED in substance. And the administration's own declared theory of victory, restated in the Financial Times, runs through correspondent banking rather than through a beachhead."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-24",
   "headline": "GULF STATES — THE BYPASS BECOMES A TREATY ITEM AND IRAN THREATENS THE BYPASS. IN PARIS ON AUGUST 24 EMMANUEL MACRON AND CROWN PRINCE MOHAMMED BIN SALMAN CONVENE THE FRANCO-SAUDI STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP COUNCIL WITH HORMUZ ALTERNATIVES AS THE HEADLINE FILE — INCREASED TRADE THROUGH OMANI PORTS OUTSIDE THE GULF, EXPANDED AND POSSIBLY DOUBLED PIPELINE CAPACITY IN SAUDI ARABIA AND OTHER STATES, AND NEW REGIONAL RAIL LINKS — AND A STANDING FRANCE-SAUDI JOINT TASK FORCE ON ENERGY AND LOGISTICS BETWEEN THE MIDDLE EAST AND EUROPE MEETS AT MINISTERIAL LEVEL THE SAME DAY. ON AUGUST 23 SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI SAID IRAN WOULD TARGET PRECISELY THOSE ALTERNATIVE OIL-SHIPPING ROUTES OUT OF THE PERSIAN GULF IF NEIGHBOURS JOIN THE ECONOMIC WAR, AND WARNED VIA IRNA THAT TEHRAN 'WILL NOT ALLOW A SINGLE DROP OF OIL TO LEAVE THE PERSIAN GULF' IF PRESSURE ESCALATES. THE GULF'S ANSWER TO A CHOKEPOINT IS INFRASTRUCTURE; IRAN'S ANSWER TO INFRASTRUCTURE IS A THREAT TO STRIKE IT. NEITHER SIDE'S INSTRUMENT IS A GROUND FORCE.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Gulf States",
   "tags": [
    "Gulf States",
