   "source": "Institute for the Study of War, Russian Offensive Campaign Assessment, August 21-23, 2026; Ukrinform, war-update wire, August 23, 2026 (Izyum guided-bomb strike; Crimea radar and USV site struck; General Staff loss tally); Al Jazeera, 'Russia says ready for “new ideas” on Ukraine war that match Putin's goals,' August 21, 2026; The Moscow Times, 'Tear Down the Wall of Silence Around Negotiations To End Russia-Ukraine War,' August 20, 2026.",
   "summary": "THE FRONT DID NOT MOVE AND THE NEGOTIATING LANGUAGE MOVED SLIGHTLY, WHICH HAS BEEN THE SHAPE OF THIS THEATRE ALL SUMMER.\n\nThe kinetic record for August 23 is two-sided and unremarkable by the standards of this war. Russian forces launched guided bomb strikes on Izyum in Kharkiv oblast, wounding two people and damaging at least twenty buildings, vehicles and power lines. Overnight into August 23 Ukraine's Defence Forces struck a radar station and a site used by Russian forces to store and launch unmanned surface vessels in temporarily occupied Crimea — a continuation of the Ukrainian campaign against the Black Sea Fleet's remaining sensing and naval-drone infrastructure rather than a new axis. Ukraine's General Staff put cumulative Russian personnel losses since February 2022 at approximately 1,476,580 as of August 23; the figure is a Ukrainian claim and is recorded as such. Net Russian territorial gains for 2026 remain at 81.1 square kilometres.\n\nTHE DIPLOMATIC SIGNAL IS AN OPENING WITH A PRECONDITION BUILT INTO IT. Deputy Foreign Minister Sergey Ryabkov said on August 21 that Moscow is ready to listen to new ideas for ending the war provided they align with President Putin's position and are in line with 'realities on the ground.' The phrase does the work: 'realities on the ground' is the formula by which occupied territory is converted into a starting assumption rather than a subject of negotiation. Against that, President Zelensky said Ukraine, together with its partners in the United States and Europe, has developed a plan to end the war envisaging a ceasefire, the creation of a free economic zone and the withdrawal of troops. The two positions are not yet in the same document, and the second explicitly contemplates the withdrawal the first defines away.\n\nTHE IRAN WAR CONTINUES TO REACH THIS THEATRE THROUGH THE INTERCEPTOR MARKET. The pattern recorded in the previous cycle holds: Ukrainian forces are developing domestic technological solutions for targeting Russian ballistic launchers and jet-powered drones specifically in order to circumvent the need for foreign materiel amid global air-defence interceptor shortages. North Korean drone operators remain reported in Kursk oblast, a step up from the infantry deployments of earlier phases.",
   "details": "AUGUST 23 KINETIC: Russian guided bomb strikes on Izyum — two wounded, at least 20 buildings, cars and power lines damaged. Ukrainian strikes overnight into August 23 on a radar station and a storage/launch site for unmanned surface vessels in temporarily occupied Crimea. LOSSES: Ukrainian General Staff cumulative Russian personnel losses ~1,476,580 as of August 23 (Ukrainian claim). Net Russian territorial gains for 2026: 81.1 km²; line effectively static. DIPLOMACY: Ryabkov, August 21 — Moscow ready to listen to 'new ideas' provided they align with Putin's position and with 'realities on the ground.' Zelensky — plan developed with US and European partners envisaging a ceasefire, a free economic zone and a withdrawal of troops. SPILLOVER: Ukrainian development of domestic solutions for targeting Russian ballistic launchers and jet-powered drones to circumvent foreign materiel dependence amid global air-defence interceptor shortages; North Korean drone operators reported deployed to Kursk oblast (ISW).",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus predictions of a decisive Russian breakthrough in 2026 remain DISCONFIRMED: net gains of 81.1 square kilometres for the year describe a static line. Predictions that the Iran war would drain Western air-defence stocks and degrade Ukraine's position are PARTIALLY CONFIRMED, and the mechanism is now visible in Ukrainian procurement doctrine rather than only in supply figures. Predictions of a negotiated settlement in 2026 remain UNTESTED: Moscow's 'new ideas' formula preserves territorial facts as a precondition, and Kyiv's plan contemplates withdrawal, so the two tracks have not converged. Predictions of formal NATO troop commitments to Ukraine remain DISCONFIRMED."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-24",
   "headline": "LATIN AMERICA — NO MATERIAL CHANGE, AND THE THREE TRACKS ARE WHERE THEY WERE. THE CARACAS GOVERNMENT-OPPOSITION TALKS OPENED ON AUGUST 6 UNDER JORGE RODRÍGUEZ AND DINORAH FIGUERA CONTINUE WITHOUT A PUBLISHED ELECTORAL TIMETABLE, WITH DELCY RODRÍGUEZ AS ACTING PRESIDENT AND US SANCTIONS ON HER LIFTED IN APRIL. MADURO AND CILIA FLORES REMAIN IN US CUSTODY WITH TRIAL SET FOR JUNE 1, 2027 BEFORE JUDGE ALVIN HELLERSTEIN IN MANHATTAN ON FOUR COUNTS INCLUDING NARCO-TERRORISM CONSPIRACY. CUBA IS STILL RECOVERING FROM ITS SIXTH NATIONWIDE BLACKOUT OF 2026 ON AUGUST 2-3, CUT OFF FROM ITS MAIN FUEL SOURCE SINCE JANUARY WHEN THE ACTING VENEZUELAN GOVERNMENT STOPPED SHIPPING OIL. COLOMBIA'S ABELARDO DE LA ESPRIELLA HAS BEEN IN OFFICE SINCE AUGUST 7, SIGNALLING A FULL REACTIVATION OF THE HYDROCARBON SECTOR AND A CRACKDOWN ON ARMED GROUPS, WITH GUSTAVO PETRO STILL DISPUTING THE JUNE RESULT.",
   "theatre": "Latin America — Venezuela / Cuba / Colombia",
