   "date": "2026-08-24",
   "headline": "KOREAN PENINSULA — THE CONCESSION AND THE SUMMIT OFFER WERE BOTH ANSWERED WITH ORDNANCE, AND THIS BRIEFING OWES A BACKFILL. ON AUGUST 19 PRESIDENT TRUMP CONFIRMED HE EXPECTS TO MEET KIM JONG UN LATER THIS YEAR — 'YEAH, I WILL BE,' AND OF KIM, 'I GET ALONG WITH HIM GREAT' — WHILE PUTTING PYONGYANG'S ARSENAL AT '57 VERY POWERFUL NUCLEAR WEAPONS.' IT WOULD BE HIS FOURTH MEETING WITH KIM AND HIS FIRST SINCE RETURNING TO OFFICE; NO DATE OR VENUE WAS GIVEN. ULCHI FREEDOM SHIELD, WHICH BEGAN AUGUST 17, WAS CURTAILED FROM ELEVEN DAYS TO FIVE AS A GOODWILL GESTURE. PYONGYANG'S ANSWER ON AUGUST 20 WAS A BARRAGE OF ABOUT TEN 600MM KN-25 SHORT-RANGE BALLISTIC MISSILES FLYING ROUGHLY 300 KILOMETRES INTO THE EAST SEA — A SYSTEM NORTH KOREA HAS DESCRIBED AS ABLE TO DELIVER TACTICAL NUCLEAR WARHEADS — FOLLOWING LAUNCHES ON AUGUST 6 AND AUGUST 12. KIM YO JONG HAD ALREADY DISMISSED THE DRILL REDUCTION AND HAS DENIED ANY TRUMP-KIM CONTACT. SEOUL HELD AN EMERGENCY SECURITY MEETING.",
