   "date": "2026-08-24",
   "headline": "HORMUZ-DEPENDENT ECONOMIES — THE BYPASS MOVES FROM IMPROVISATION TO INSTITUTION, AND IRAN THREATENS IT. FRANCE AND SAUDI ARABIA HAVE STOOD UP A JOINT TASK FORCE ON MIDDLE EAST-EUROPE ENERGY AND LOGISTICS CONNECTIONS WHICH MEETS AT MINISTERIAL LEVEL ON AUGUST 24, ALONGSIDE THE MACRON-MBS SUMMIT ON OMANI PORTS, DOUBLED PIPELINE CAPACITY AND NEW REGIONAL RAIL. REZAEI SAID ON AUGUST 23 THAT IRAN WOULD TARGET EXACTLY THOSE ALTERNATIVE ROUTES. ASIAN ENERGY PRICES REMAIN ROUGHLY 50-100% ABOVE FEBRUARY LEVELS; RATIONING HAS HARDENED INTO STANDING POLICY FROM SEOUL TO DHAKA; INDIA HAS AVOIDED FORMAL FUEL RATIONING ENTIRELY, WITH RETAIL FUEL PRICES UP ABOUT 7% AGAINST A GLOBAL AVERAGE OF 25-30%. IN THE UNITED STATES THE PUMP AVERAGE IS $4.0986 AND DIESEL HAS REACHED $5.6074, A RECORD AUGUST LEVEL AND NEARLY TWO DOLLARS ABOVE A YEAR AGO — THE FREIGHT COST OF THE CHOKEPOINT, ARRIVING ON A LAG. AND THE CRISIS IS RESHAPING GENERATION POLICY: CSIS RECORDS A TAILWIND FOR NUCLEAR ENERGY ACROSS NORTHEAST ASIA.",
