   "headline": "DAY 178 — THE UNITED STATES CLAIMS THE WATER AND IRAN ALLOCATES THE TRAFFIC. ON AUGUST 22 TRUMP SAID 'I VIEW THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ AS AN AMERICAN TERRITORY RIGHT NOW' AND RE-POSTED A MAP LABELLING IT 'NEW U.S. TERRITORY' — AND ON THE SAME DAY TEHRAN GRANTED A NUMBER OF IRAQI OIL TANKERS PERMISSION TO TRANSIT, THE FIRST NAMED STATE-LEVEL EXEMPTION OF THE WAR. IRAN'S FOREIGN MINISTRY CALLED THE SANCTIONS DUE MONDAY A 'DECLARATION OF WAR ON ALL NATIONS' AND SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI SAID ANY COUNTRY JOINING THEM IS 'CONSIDERED AN ENEMY,' THAT THE STRAIT 'IS CLOSED AND WILL NOT REOPEN,' AND THAT IRAN WOULD RETALIATE 'IN AN EARTHQUAKE-LIKE MANNER.' A TWENTY-SECOND CONSECUTIVE NIGHT PASSED WITH NO CONFIRMED US OR ISRAELI STRIKE INSIDE IRAN. CENTCOM'S BLOCKADE TALLY REACHED 68 VESSELS REDIRECTED, 3 DISABLED, 2 BOARDED. AL JAZEERA'S ROUTE ANALYSIS FOUND THAT OF 236 HULLS CROSSING AUGUST 1-19, 83 OPENLY TOOK IRAN'S ROUTE AND 3 THE US-BACKED OMANI ROUTE — 'THE FEAR OF OFFENDING TEHRAN APPEARS TO OUTWEIGH TRUMP'S THREATS.' BRENT ~$94; PUMP $4.102; PENTAGON CASUALTIES 774-775. STILL AIR, NAVAL AND FINANCIAL ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO DRAFT ORDER. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED.",
