    "Basing Access Question",
    "82nd Airborne Uncommitted",
    "50,000 Personnel",
    "Kharg Not Taken",
    "Blockade Substitution",
    "Disconfirmed"
   ],
   "source": "U.S. Central Command via X, blockade tally as of August 21, 2026; USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, August 17, 2026; USNI News, 'Carrier USS George Washington Now in the Middle East,' August 20, 2026; Stars and Stripes, 'USS George Washington arrives in Middle East to relieve USS Abraham Lincoln,' August 20, 2026; Army Recognition, 'US Navy Iwo Jima Amphibious Ready Group Continues Caribbean Operations Targeting Drug Trafficking,' 2026; New York Post via RT, 'US weighs special forces raid to seize Iran’s enriched uranium,' July 26, 2026; Anadolu Agency, 'US weighs special forces operation to seize Iran’s enriched uranium stockpile: Report,' March 21, 2026; The Washington Post, 'Risky commando plan to seize Iran’s uranium came at Trump’s request,' April 1, 2026; Critical Threats / AEI-ISW, 'Iran Update Special Report, August 4, 2026'; Sputnik/CENTCOM, 'More Than 50,000 US Troops Deployed Across Middle East — US CENTCOM,' July 19, 2026; Stars and Stripes, '82nd Airborne ordered to Middle East as US weighs options on Iran,' March 25, 2026; Military Times, 'Selective Service System wants to wargame the draft,' July 24, 2026; The Hill, 'Automatic registration for US military draft to begin in December,' 2026; Military.com, 'Which Americans Will Be Automatically Registered for Military Draft, and When?', April 9, 2026; Black Voice News, 'National Automatic Draft Registration Set to Begin in December 2026,' August 4, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Türkiye, Saudi Arabia, Pakistan sign joint defence agreement: What’s in it?', August 7, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Trump hails Mecca pact: Can it replace the region’s US security umbrella?', August 17, 2026; Iran International live blog, August 22, 2026; Al-Monitor, 'Houthis claim new strikes on Saudi Arabia after IRGC warning: What to know,' August 2026; CNBC, 'Bessent says U.S. likely won’t restart large-scale Iran combat as it steps up economic pressure,' August 20, 2026.",
   "summary": "THE STATUS HOLDS AT no_ground_troops FOR A 178TH CONSECUTIVE DAY, AND THE CYCLE'S NOVELTY IS THAT THE AMERICAN CLAIM ON THE CHOKEPOINT MOVED FROM MILITARY TO LEGAL WITHOUT MOVING TO LAND. On August 22 the President said 'I view the Strait of Hormuz as an American territory right now' and re-posted the Truth Social map labelling the waterway 'NEW U.S. TERRITORY' that he first published on August 18. For a ground-invasion tracker this is the important distinction of the cycle: a sovereignty assertion over water carries no manpower requirement and generates no observable ground signature. Nothing about the claim requires or produces a landing, and none occurred.\n\nEVERY EXECUTION INDICATOR REMAINED AT ZERO. No landing, no embarkation, no MEU tasking, no airborne insertion, no relief amphibious ready group, no new deployment order, no mobilisation, no draft order, no medical or fuel prepositioning consistent with a lodgement, and no reported special-operations ground activity inside Iran. The only force-flow event of the last week was the like-for-like carrier relief already logged: USS Abraham Lincoln out after 252 days without a port call, USS George Washington in on August 19 with USS Robert Smalls (CG-62) and USS Shoup (DDG-86).\n\nTHE AMPHIBIOUS PICTURE DESERVES TO BE STATED STRUCTURALLY RATHER THAN INCREMENTALLY, BECAUSE THE STRUCTURE IS THE FINDING. The Boxer Amphibious Ready Group — USS Boxer (LHD-4), USS Comstock (LSD-45), USS Portland (LPD-27) — with the embarked 11th MEU of roughly 2,200-2,500 Marines remains the sole ARG in CENTCOM. The Navy's other deployed ARG, Iwo Jima with the 22nd MEU, is committed to Caribbean counter-narcotics operations under SOUTHCOM and is not available to CENTCOM without a redeployment order that has not been given. The 24th MEU is deployed without an ARG at all, operating as 'Littoral Combat Force 24' and spread throughout its region — a deliberately distributed construct that is the operational opposite of the concentration an opposed landing requires. USS Tripoli concluded its deployment on July 22, putting roughly 2,500 Marines of the 31st MEU ashore at Okinawa, and no relief ARG has been announced in the month since. One ARG, one MEU, no relief, no concentration.\n\nTHE ONE GENUINE GROUND-PLANNING INDICATOR IN THE OPEN RECORD IS OLDER THAN THIS CYCLE AND HAS NOT ADVANCED, AND THIS TRACKER RECORDS IT RATHER THAN OMIT IT. On July 26 the New York Post reported that the Pentagon is weighing an operation to seize Iran's enriched-uranium stockpile that would 'send thousands of ground troops to storm heavily fortified nuclear sites,' with retrieval performed by a small element drawn from SEAL Team 6's Silver Squadron, the Army's 2nd Ranger Battalion and the 21st Ordnance Company, supported by regular troops holding a perimeter and warplanes controlling an air corridor; the named targets are Fordow, Natanz, Isfahan and Pickaxe Mountain, with roughly 200 kg of an estimated 440-450 kg of 60%-enriched material believed to sit in deep tunnels near Isfahan. The report rests on a single unnamed source 'familiar with the matter'; CSIS's Joseph Rodgers, quoted in it, called the concept potentially 'the most sophisticated operation in military history.' Critical Threats' August 4 special report recorded that a ground option to secure the uranium had 're-emerged' in US planning as an alternative to airstrikes alone. The tracker weighs this at its true value: it is planning, it is unconfirmed by any official, no decision has been reported, and it is the same concept the President publicly declined in June when he said such a mission would have needed 'at least two weeks' on the ground and the airlift of 'massive equipment,' called the material 'entombed' and said there was 'no reason to.' Planning documents are not force flow. The distinction this audit has maintained since March — between options prepared and options executed — continues to hold.\n\nTHE DRAFT RUNG MOVED ON PAPER, AND THE MOVEMENT IS ADMINISTRATIVE RATHER THAN MOBILISING. Reporting continues to carry a start date of December 18, 2026 for automatic Selective Service registration of men aged 18 to 26 under a Defense Authorization Act provision that integrates federal databases, and a Black Voice News report of August 4 restates that date. This sits alongside — and is a distinct instrument from — the Selective Service System's own automatic-registration rule, which was withdrawn in July and has not been re-proposed; the audit flags the statute and the rule as separate tracks and does not treat the December date as evidence the withdrawn rule has returned. Whichever instrument prevails, automatic registration builds the pool and inducts nobody: conscription still requires Congress to amend the Military Selective Service Act and a presidential induction order, and neither has occurred. The Selective Service 'Readiness Simulation' vendor window closed in August with no award announced.\n\nTHE LARGEST STRUCTURAL FACT BEARING ON ANY FUTURE GROUND OPTION IS AN ALLIANCE FACT, AND THIS BRIEFING HAD NOT RECORDED IT. On August 7 Saudi Arabia, Türkiye and Pakistan signed the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement, declaring that an armed attack on any one of the three would be regarded as an attack on all. Turkish Foreign Minister Hakan Fidan described a structure resembling NATO's, with a ministers' committee, political and military committees and a permanent secretariat. These are the three states whose territory, airspace, basing, overflight and logistics a US ground campaign against Iran would most need: Saudi Arabia hosts Prince Sultan Air Base, Türkiye is a NATO member controlling the northern approaches, and Pakistan borders Iran and is the Muslim world's only nuclear-armed state. A mutual-defence pact among them, presented by its signatories as 'defensive in nature and not directed at any specific actor' and open to others, does not forbid US access — but it changes who must be consulted before a lodgement, and it was signed while Washington was pressing those same governments over Iran. Trump welcomed it on August 16-17 as a 'big, bold, and important first step,' saying he was 'very happy to see' it. Rezaei read it on August 22 as a signal that 'the US was leaving the region.'\n\nTHE SUBSTITUTION REMAINS INTACT AT KHARG. Loading resumed at the island in the August 12-14 window after a roughly 25-day halt — a National Iranian Tanker Company VLCC took on about two million barrels at the Azarpad jetty on August 14 per TankerTrackers — without any US naval move against the island and without any change to its status. The throttling instrument is blockade, insurance and secondary designation, not occupation, and the administration has now named that instrument as its forward strategy.\n\nONE ADJACENT GROUND OPTION IS BEING REPORTED, AND IT IS NOT AMERICAN AND NOT IN IRAN. Saudi Arabia is reported to be preparing for a possible escalation in Yemen that could include a ground offensive, following Houthi drone attacks on Najran airport and Aramco facilities on August 18-20 and Yemeni government fighting with Houthi forces northwest and south of Marib on August 22. The tracker logs this because a Saudi ground commitment in Yemen would consume the coalition manpower any US Iranian option would draw on — but it is a Saudi operation directed at Yemen, not a US operation directed at Iran, and it points away from rather than toward the predicted event.",
   "details": "STATUS: no_ground_troops, Day 178. EXECUTION INDICATORS AT ZERO: landing, embarkation, MEU tasking, airborne insertion, relief ARG, new deployment order, mobilisation, draft order, prepositioning for lodgement, reported special-operations ground activity inside Iran. AMPHIBIOUS: Boxer ARG (LHD-4, LSD-45, LPD-27) with 11th MEU sole ARG in CENTCOM; Iwo Jima ARG with 22nd MEU committed to the Caribbean under SOUTHCOM; 24th MEU deployed without an ARG as Littoral Combat Force 24; Tripoli concluded deployment July 22 with ~2,500 Marines of the 31st MEU ashore at Okinawa and no relief announced. CARRIERS: net one on station after the August 19 Lincoln/George Washington relief; CENTCOM's last public figure in July was 50,000+ personnel, ~200 combat aircraft and two carriers. GROUND COMPONENT: ~2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne Division with divisional headquarters in region since late March 2026, never committed; Maj. Gen. Brandon Tegtmeier commanding the deployed element per March reporting. AIR: 330+ aircraft across Al Udeid, Muwaffaq Salti and Prince Sultan via roughly 310 logistics flights since early January, plus Patriot and THAAD batteries. PLANNING (NOT EXECUTION): New York Post July 26 report of a uranium-seizure operation requiring thousands of ground troops, retrieval by SEAL Team 6 Silver Squadron / 2nd Ranger Battalion / 21st Ordnance Company, targets Fordow, Natanz, Isfahan, Pickaxe Mountain, ~200 kg of 440-450 kg of 60% HEU believed near Isfahan; single unnamed source, no official confirmation, no decision reported; Critical Threats August 4 notes the option 're-emerged.' DRAFT: reported December 18, 2026 start for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 under a Defense Authorization Act provision; separate SSS automatic-registration rule withdrawn in July and not re-proposed; 'Readiness Simulation' vendor window closed in August with no award announced; no amendment to the Military Selective Service Act and no induction order. ALLIANCE: Mecca Joint Defence Agreement signed August 7 by Saudi Arabia, Türkiye and Pakistan — attack on one treated as attack on all, ministers' committee, political and military committees, permanent secretariat; Trump called it a 'big, bold, and important first step.' ADJACENT: Saudi Arabia reported preparing for possible ground escalation in Yemen; Yemeni government forces engaged Houthis near Marib on August 22.",
   "prediction_impact": "The predicted US ground invasion of Iran, and the predicted US ground seizure of Kharg Island or the Strait of Hormuz, remain DISCONFIRMED at Day 178. This cycle supplies an unusually clean test of the corpus's reasoning, because the President made the strongest sovereignty claim of the war — 'I view the Strait of Hormuz as an American territory right now' — and it produced no ground signature whatsoever. Models that treat annexationist rhetoric as a leading indicator of occupation are DISCONFIRMED for this instance: the claim was verbal and cartographic, the enforcement is naval, and the manpower requirement is zero. Predictions that amphibious forces would mass ahead of a landing are DISCONFIRMED and now structurally so: one ARG in theatre, the Navy's other deployed ARG committed to the Western Hemisphere, and the 24th MEU deliberately deployed without an ARG in a distributed construct. Predictions that an American ground operation would follow the failure of air power are UNSUPPORTED by force flow but are NOT vacuous — the July 26 uranium-seizure report describes exactly the kind of thousands-strong ground operation the corpus anticipated, and the audit records it as live planning rather than dismissing it; it remains unconfirmed, undecided and previously declined by the President himself, so it moves nothing from disconfirmed to confirmed. Predictions of a return of conscription remain DISCONFIRMED in substance: the December 18 automatic-registration date builds a database, not an army, and induction authority has not been sought. And corpus predictions that a long war would erode the American alliance system gain their strongest support of the war from the Mecca Joint Defence Agreement — the three states most necessary to a US ground campaign against Iran have bound themselves to each other, with Washington's public blessing.",
   "alternate_readings": [
    {
     "reading": "The Mecca Joint Defence Agreement is read as a hedge against an unreliable United States — evidence the US-led Gulf security order is ending — and, by the opposing reading, as a burden-sharing supplement that Washington actively welcomes and that leaves American basing, overflight and command relationships untouched.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Documented: Saudi Arabia, Türkiye and Pakistan signed the pact in Mecca on August 7, declaring an armed attack on one an attack on all, with Turkish FM Hakan Fidan describing a NATO-like structure of a ministers' committee, political and military committees and a permanent secretariat. Documented: a Turkish official told Reuters the pact is 'defensive in nature and not directed at any specific actor' and is open to other regional states. Documented: Trump welcomed it on August 16-17 as a 'big, bold, and important first step.' Documented: Saudi Arabia has absorbed repeated Iranian and Houthi missile and drone strikes since February 28 and pressed Washington for restraint on August 1. Documented: Iran's Mohsen Rezaei said on August 22 that the agreement signalled the US was leaving the region. Not documented: any change to US basing agreements, overflight rights or command arrangements; any text of the pact addressing third-party access; any instance of the pact being invoked.",
     "public_assertion_by": [
      "The Council on Foreign Relations, in 'The U.S.-Led Middle East Order Is Over. The Mecca Agreement Proves It.'",
      "The signatory governments and a Turkish official quoted by Reuters, presenting it as defensive, complementary and open to others",
      "President Trump, welcoming it as a 'big, bold, and important first step' toward regional self-defence",
      "The Middle East Council on Global Affairs and the Arab Center, arguing it is diversification without substitution",
      "OSW, characterising it as 'a loose alliance' rather than a bloc",
      "Iran's Supreme National Security Council secretary Mohsen Rezaei, reading it as evidence of American withdrawal"
     ],
     "why_unresolvable": "A hedge and a supplement produce the same treaty text and the same welcoming statements until the pact is tested. Nothing in the open record shows whether the signatories would grant or withhold basing and overflight for a US operation against Iran, and no party has an incentive to say so in advance. Resolution would require an actual invocation, a documented refusal of US access, or publication of the pact's operative annexes.",
     "open_question_ref": "mecca-pact-substitute-or-supplement-august-2026"
    },
    {
     "reading": "The reported December 18, 2026 start for automatic Selective Service registration is read as the draft rung advancing by statute despite July's rule withdrawal — and, by the opposing reading, as a long-scheduled administrative modernisation with no connection to the Iran war whose start date predates the current escalation.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Documented: multiple outlets from April through August 2026 report a Defense Authorization Act provision automating Selective Service registration for men aged 18-26 by integrating federal databases, with a start date of December 18, 2026. Documented: the Selective Service System's own automatic-registration rule was withdrawn in July 2026 and has not been re-proposed. Documented: the SSS solicited vendors for a 'Readiness Simulation' of the new registration process with an August deadline; no award has been announced. Documented: reinstating conscription requires Congress to amend the Military Selective Service Act and a presidential induction order, neither of which has occurred. Not documented: whether the December date survives the rule withdrawal, whether the statute and the rule are being implemented on one track or two, and any statement linking either instrument to Iran contingency planning.",
     "public_assertion_by": [
      "The Hill, Time, CNBC, Military.com and Black Voice News, all reporting the December 2026 automatic-registration start date",
      "Military Times, reporting the Selective Service System's request to wargame the draft process",
      "Fact-checking outlets and the Selective Service System itself, stressing that no draft is being reinstated and that registration is not induction"
     ],
     "why_unresolvable": "A statutory implementation date and a withdrawn agency rule can coexist, supersede one another or quietly lapse, and the public record does not say which is happening. The absence of an award announcement is equally consistent with a paused programme and with an unannounced one. Resolution would require an SSS implementation notice, a re-proposed rule, or a Federal Register entry for the December date.",
     "open_question_ref": "selective-service-rule-withdrawal-july-2026"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-23",
   "headline": "GULF STATES — TEHRAN NAMES THE NEIGHBOURS AS TARGETS AND PARIS BECOMES THE VENUE FOR ROUTING AROUND THE STRAIT. ON AUGUST 22 SNSC SECRETARY MOHSEN REZAEI SAID ANY COUNTRY JOINING THE US SANCTIONS IS 'CONSIDERED AN ENEMY' AND THAT IRAN WOULD HARM ITS INTERESTS AND DISRUPT GULF OIL SHIPMENTS — A THREAT AIMED AT THE LITTORAL, NOT AT WASHINGTON. SAUDI CROWN PRINCE MOHAMMED BIN SALMAN TRAVELLED TO PARIS FOR AN AUGUST 24 FRANCO-SAUDI STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP COUNCIL WITH MACRON DEVOTED TO HORMUZ ALTERNATIVES — MARITIME DIVERSIFICATION, PIPELINES AND REGIONAL RAIL — HIS FIRST FRANCE VISIT SINCE 2023. THE AUGUST 7 MECCA JOINT DEFENCE AGREEMENT BETWEEN SAUDI ARABIA, TÜRKIYE AND PAKISTAN, WHICH THIS BRIEFING HAD NOT RECORDED, TREATS AN ATTACK ON ONE AS AN ATTACK ON ALL AND WAS WELCOMED BY TRUMP AS A 'BIG, BOLD, AND IMPORTANT FIRST STEP.' ADNOC HAS NOW HAD 16 VESSELS ATTACKED SINCE FEBRUARY 28, ONE CREW MEMBER KILLED AND 20 INJURED. QATAR IS PROJECTED TO CONTRACT 14.7% IN 2026 AND GULF ENERGY-FACILITY REPAIRS ARE ESTIMATED AT $58 BILLION.",
