   "date": "2026-08-22",
   "headline": "GULF STATES — THE LITTORAL BREAKS TOWARD WASHINGTON WHILE ITS ECONOMIES BREAK DOWN. THE UAE DETECTED TWO IRANIAN BALLISTIC MISSILES ON AUGUST 18 AND ON AUGUST 19 SUSPENDED ALL TRADE, COMMERCIAL EXCHANGE AND FINANCIAL TRANSACTIONS WITH IRAN UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE — CUTTING OFF A PARTNER THAT SUPPLIED MORE THAN 30% OF IRANIAN IMPORTS. THE WORLD BANK HAS CUT ITS 2026 GCC GROWTH FORECAST FROM 4.4% TO 1.3%, WITH KUWAIT AND QATAR EXPECTED TO CONTRACT AND OXFORD ECONOMICS SEEING RECESSION IN SOME GULF ECONOMIES IN THE SECOND HALF. QATAR HAS LOST ROUGHLY 17% OF ITS LNG EXPORT CAPACITY TO THE MARCH RAS LAFFAN STRIKE; SOME 80 ENERGY FACILITIES HAVE BEEN HIT FOR AN ESTIMATED $58 BILLION IN DAMAGE. AND THE ALLIANCE IS UNDER STRAIN FROM THE OTHER DIRECTION: TRUMP SAID ON AUGUST 17 THAT IF OMAN — THE WAR'S PRINCIPAL MEDIATOR — 'GETS IN THE WAY, WE'LL BOMB THE S*** OUT OF THEM,' ADDING THAT MUSCAT HAD NOT 'BEHAVED VERY WELL.' HOUTHI FORCES, WHO DECLARED A RED SEA BLOCKADE OF SAUDI ARABIA ON JULY 20, KILLED SIX ABOARD THE TIHAMAH IN THE BAB AL-MANDEB AND CLAIMED DRONE ATTACKS ON NAJRAN AIRPORT AND AN ARAMCO FACILITY ON AUGUST 20.",
