   "date": "2026-08-02",
   "headline": "DAY 157 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops, AND THIS IS THE CYCLE IN WHICH A PHYSICAL CONSTRAINT ON THE GROUND OPTION BECAME MEASURABLE. (1) THE REPORTED WEEKEND CAMPAIGN DID NOT BEGIN — NO STRIKE WAVE, NO LANDING, NO EMBARKATION, NO MEU TASKING. (2) THE MUNITIONS CEILING IS NOW QUANTIFIED: CSIS PUTS REMAINING STOCKS UNDER 827 PATRIOT (FROM ~2,200) AND UNDER 278 THAAD (FROM 452), MORE THAN 60% EXPENDED, THREE-PLUS YEARS TO REBUILD, WITH GEN. DAN CAINE REPORTEDLY WARNING PRIVATELY ABOUT SHORTAGES — AND A KHARG LODGEMENT WOULD HAVE TO BE COVERED BY EXACTLY THAT INVENTORY FOR AS LONG AS IT WAS HELD. (3) THE PEOPLE MOVED THE WRONG WAY FOR AN INVASION: TEN COUNTRIES' WORTH OF AMERICANS WERE TOLD TO DEPART, NOT A FORCE FLOW TOLD TO ARRIVE. (4) THE DRAFT RUNG SPLIT FOR THE FIRST TIME — THE WITHDRAWN AUTOMATIC-REGISTRATION RULE HAS STILL NOT BEEN RE-PROPOSED, BUT THE SELECTIVE SERVICE SYSTEM HAS PUT OUT A CONTRACTING REQUEST FOR A 'READINESS SIMULATION' TO WARGAME MOBILISATION SCENARIOS, WITH VENDOR SUBMISSIONS DUE AUGUST 14. (5) AMPHIBIOUS PICTURE UNCHANGED FOR AN ELEVENTH DAY: USS BOXER (LHD-4) WITH COMSTOCK, PORTLAND, THE 11TH MEU AND USS MIGUEL KEITH IN THE ARABIAN SEA, STILL THE SOLE DEPLOYED ARG FLEET-WIDE. EVERY EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO FOR A 157TH CONSECUTIVE DAY.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Ground Invasion Tracker",
   "tags": [
    "Ground Invasion Tracker",
