   "date": "2026-08-02",
   "headline": "DAY 157 GULF STATES — THE REGION IS TOLD TO EMPTY OUT. US EMBASSIES IN AT LEAST TEN COUNTRIES — THE UAE, QATAR, OMAN, IRAQ, JORDAN, ISRAEL, KUWAIT, SAUDI ARABIA, BAHRAIN AND EGYPT — ISSUED NEAR-SIMULTANEOUS AUGUST 1 SECURITY ALERTS TELLING AMERICANS TO 'CONSIDER DEPARTING' OR 'BE PREPARED TO DEPART,' CITING 'THE POTENTIAL FOR UNFORESEEN ESCALATION,' FLIGHT CANCELLATIONS AND PERIODIC AIRSPACE CLOSURES. KUWAIT'S AIR DEFENCES INTERCEPTED AND DESTROYED IRANIAN DRONES EARLY SATURDAY, WITH IRAN'S ARMY CALLING THE STRIKES RETALIATION FOR THE QESHM ISLAND ATTACK ON A RESIDENTIAL HOME. TWO TANKERS WERE HIT OR NEAR-MISSED IN OMANI WATERS. THE HOUTHI RED SEA BLOCKADE BEGAN TO BITE ON SAUDI EXPORTS — EIGHT TANKERS CLAIMED TURNED, WITH THE VLCC XIN LONG YANG AND THE TANKER RODOS ABANDONING BAB AL-MANDEB FOR SUEZ AFTER LOADING AT YANBU. IRAN NAMED REGIONAL US ENERGY INFRASTRUCTURE AS A RETALIATION TARGET, AGAINST A MARCH PRECEDENT THAT COST GULF ENERGY UP TO $58 BILLION ACROSS 80-PLUS FACILITIES. ISRAEL RAN LARGE DEMOLITIONS ACROSS SOUTHERN LEBANON FOUR DAYS BEFORE THE ROME TALKS.",
   "theatre": "Gulf States",
