   "headline": "DAY 157 RUSSIA-UKRAINE — THE INTERCEPTOR GAP BECOMES THE WAR'S CENTRAL FACT, AND IT LINKS TO IRAN. RUSSIA'S OVERNIGHT BARRAGE INTO AUGUST 1 KILLED AT LEAST NINE AND WOUNDED THIRTY IN KYIV AND SURROUNDING REGIONS, FOUR OF THE DEAD OR INJURED CHILDREN — AND ONLY ONE OF TWENTY-SEVEN BALLISTIC MISSILES WAS SHOT DOWN. ZELENSKY SAID UKRAINE HAS RUN OUT OF INTERCEPTORS AND WARNED THAT ITS AIR DEFENCES ARE BEING OVERWHELMED, THE SECOND MAJOR AERIAL ASSAULT IN TWO DAYS AND THE SECOND BALLISTIC ATTACK ON KYIV IN A WEEK. THE MISSING WEAPON IS PATRIOT — AND CSIS PUT REMAINING US PATRIOT STOCKS AT FEWER THAN 827 FROM ROUGHLY 2,200 PRE-WAR, MORE THAN 60% EXPENDED IN THE IRAN WAR, WITH THREE-PLUS YEARS TO REBUILD. UKRAINE ANSWERED ASYMMETRICALLY, SINKING A RUSSIAN CONTAINER SHIP IN THE BLACK SEA. ISW ASSESSED ON JULY 31 THAT RUSSIA'S NORTHERN GROUPING IS LIKELY LYING TO THE KREMLIN ABOUT GAINS IN NORTHERN SUMY AND KHARKIV, WITH BATTLEFIELD EVIDENCE NOT CORROBORATING THE CLAIMS AND UKRAINIAN FORCES COUNTERATTACKING. POLAND FORMALLY PROTESTED TO THE RUSSIAN AMBASSADOR OVER THE KH-101 INCURSION.",
