   "date": "2026-08-02",
   "headline": "DAY 157 MULTI-THEATRE — VENEZUELA'S NINTH DIALOGUE IN TWELVE YEARS OPENED ON AUGUST 1 WITH JORGE RODRÍGUEZ AND DINORAH FIGUERA ANNOUNCING A JOINT WORKING AGENDA TO 'STRENGTHEN DEMOCRACY,' FIGUERA SEEKING A TRUSTWORTHY CNE AND A WHOLLY RECONSTITUTED SUPREME COURT, AND VENEZUELANS WATCHING WITH 'CAUTIOUS OPTIMISM' AFTER TWELVE YEARS OF BROKEN ACCORDS — MACHADO STILL OUTSIDE BY CHOICE. IN COLOMBIA A TRUCK BOMB DETONATED BESIDE A POLICE STATION IN CÚCUTA ON THE VENEZUELAN BORDER, INJURING ELEVEN — EIGHT POLICE OFFICERS AND THREE CIVILIANS — SIX DAYS BEFORE ABELARDO DE LA ESPRIELLA'S AUGUST 7 INAUGURATION IN CALI; DEFENCE MINISTER PEDRO SÁNCHEZ BLAMED ELN 'NARCOTERRORISTS' AND OFFERED A REWARD ABOVE $64,000, WHILE PRESIDENT PETRO SPENT HIS LAST DAYS IN OFFICE IN HAVANA DISCUSSING THE US 'POLICY OF STRANGULATION' WITH DÍAZ-CANEL AND DID NOT COMMENT. CUBA'S ENERGY MINISTRY REPORTS FUEL RESERVES EXHAUSTED WITH BLACKOUTS OF 20-22 HOURS A DAY. QATAR CANNOT MEET ITS LONG-TERM ASIAN LNG DELIVERY SCHEDULES, RIPPLING FROM SEOUL TO SINGAPORE. NORTH KOREA REJECTED DENUCLEARISATION AND PREPARES 30,000 MORE TROOPS FOR RUSSIA.",
   "theatre": "Multi-theatre",
   "tag": "Multi-theatre",
