   "source": "Internal monthly scoring run, August 1, 2026. External verification: Council on Foreign Relations Global Conflict Tracker; Library of Congress Global Legal Monitor (January 28, 2026); Bundesregierung; euobserver; Euronews; CNN Politics; Task & Purpose; National Security Journal; Foreign Policy; Reuters/Ipsos; Kyiv Independent; UK Defence Journal; Newsweek; Al Jazeera; Manila Times; MercoPress; CP24; Latin America Reports; Times of Israel; Israel National News; American Enterprise Institute China & Taiwan Update (July 2, 24, 31, 2026); NK News; The Washington Post; Military.com; War Resisters' International; Kurdistan24; CSIS; NPR; CBS News; Congress.gov CRS; SDNY reporting.",
   "summary": "Full monthly re-evaluation of the corpus: 170 analysis files, 983 predictions and claims, meta.last_scoring_date advanced to 2026-08-01, next scoring date 2026-09-01. Currency web-verified across US-Iran, Russia-Ukraine, NATO-Russia, China-Taiwan, DPRK, Venezuela, Israel-Lebanon and US-China trade. Eight predictions changed status; 83 status_notes were rewritten, 61 of them ground-invasion entries brought forward from stale May 1 (Day 63) and June 1 (Day 95) framings to the Day 156 record. Four missing verdict.steelman fields were written (civilization-59, geo-strategy-update-4, geo-strategy-update-6, secret-history-10) and eight predictions missing the schema-required 'type' field were repaired (geo-strategy-end, secret-history-22).",
   "details": "STATUS CHANGES (8). CONFIRMED (1): game-theory-19[4] — 'German males aged 17-45 are not allowed to leave the country for more than 3 months without army permission, as a prelude to a national draft.' Germany's Wehrdienstmodernisierungsgesetz entered into force January 1, 2026: males aged 17+ must obtain the consent of the competent Bundeswehr career centre to leave Germany for more than three months, the obligation running to age 45 and applying even absent a declared state of emergency. Service remains formally voluntary, but men born 2008 or later face a mandatory fitness-and-willingness questionnaire and medical evaluation, and the Bundestag is to decide on 'needs-based conscription' if growth targets are missed, with the Defence Ministry assessing cohort drafts possible from July 2027. Age band, duration threshold, permission requirement, absence of an emergency trigger and the prelude-to-conscription framing all match. DISCONFIRMED (3): interview-x-QCALiCZb[10] — 'most military analysts expect an amphibious assault to control Hormuz'; Foreign Policy's July 27 survey of former commanders found the US 'does not appear to be moving toward a major ground operation in Iran,' the specialist literature emphasises that holding Kharg is harder than taking it, and the 31st MEU offloaded at Okinawa on July 26 with no relief ARG. interview-x-YEJgDBgb[1] — first strike as consent-manufacture for a draft and ground invasion; all three legs failed: Reuters/Ipsos support at one in three (lowest of the war), Selective Service withdrew the automatic-registration rulemaking on July 23, and there are zero US ground troops in Iran at Day 156. game-theory-18[9] — 'America will invade Cuba very soon' (aired April 2, 2026); four months elapsed with no invasion and no force generation, while the administration's one active hemispheric regime-change track opened on August 1 as negotiated Venezuelan transition talks. PARTIALLY CONFIRMED (4): game-theory-21[3] — automatic draft registration of 18-26s from December 2026 matches the December 2025 NDAA statutory mandate (December 19, 2026) exactly, but no full national draft followed and the implementing rulemaking was withdrawn July 23. interview-x-obQsUn0G[3] — Iran has kept Hormuz closed for five months (throughput ~11% of normal) but Brent peaked at $144.42 on April 7 and sits at $90.24; $200/bbl was never approached. interview-x-voQEteh6[2] and [3] — scored against the channel's own upload record: the Secret History series (28 episodes, August 22 – December 18, 2025) delivered a condensed civilizational course of nearly the predicted length and timing but framed as a new series rather than a condensation; the Game Theory series (22 episodes, January 6 – April 28, 2026) delivered the predicted geopolitics semester about a month early. GROUND-INVASION SWEEP: 61 ground-related status_notes refreshed to Day 156. No status reversals were warranted — unbounded 'eventually' predictions stay untested, conditionals stay untested because the antecedent has not obtained, and time-bounded predictions stay disconfirmed — but the evidentiary basis moved. Net movement this cycle was DOWNWARD on execution: the amphibious rung fell (31st MEU offloaded at Okinawa July 26, USS Boxer the sole deployed ARG fleet-wide), the draft rung fell (rulemaking withdrawn July 23), and the July 31 capitulation package reassigns the Kharg mission to airpower against energy infrastructure with no ground element in any of four independent accounts. Countervailing planning signals are logged: the July 24 report of Pentagon options for weeks of limited Kharg and coastal-raid operations pending approval, and the July 30 ambiguous shaping signal. CONTESTED_UNRESOLVED (10) reviewed, none reassigned: no new open-source evidence resolved the Kirk assassination framing, the Islamabad bad-faith claim, the Bitcoin/NSA origin claim, the COVID bioweapon claim, the Ford laundry-fire interpretation, the Kushner/Vance/Gabbard scapegoat framing, the JCPOA efficacy dispute, the Ugolino crux, or the 'world sides with Russia' realignment claim.",
   "prediction_impact": "Corpus totals after the run: 983 predictions and claims — 329 untested, 245 unfalsifiable, 190 partially_confirmed, 134 disconfirmed, 75 confirmed, 10 contested_unresolved. Net movement from untested: -8. The corpus's single most repeated forecast — a US ground invasion or ground seizure in Iran — remains DISCONFIRMED at Day 156, and this cycle strengthened it on evidence rather than on elapsed time: the Kharg option has now been available, staffed and repeatedly reported for four months without being taken, while the coercive mission it was designed to serve has been publicly reassigned to airpower. Independent third-party confirmation arrived this cycle from CFR's Global Conflict Tracker, which records that 'no significant US ground force commitment is documented' and that operations have 'remained primarily aerial and naval.' The most interesting result of the run is that the month's one outright CONFIRMATION was a European conscription-infrastructure claim, not an Iran claim — the corpus is more accurate about the machinery of mobilisation in Germany than about the use of American ground forces in the Gulf.",
   "alternate_readings": "A charitable reading of the untested ground predictions: none is time-bounded, the war is ongoing at Day 156, the Pentagon was reported on July 24 to be readying limited ground options pending approval, and roughly 2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne with divisional headquarters remain in theatre. On that reading the forecasts are early rather than wrong, and a single presidential decision would move them. The counter-reading, which this run adopts for the evidentiary note rather than for any status change: the instrument has now been chosen in public and it is not ground forces; the amphibious and draft rungs both fell during July; and a prediction that survives only because its window is unbounded is being sustained by its own vagueness rather than by the evidence. Both readings are recorded so that a future reversal — a landing, an embarkation order, a relief ARG, a re-proposed registration rule — is scored as new information and not as vindication of a claim that was never falsifiable in the first place."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-01",
   "headline": "DAY 156 — TRUMP ORDERS A MULTI-DAY BOMBING CAMPAIGN AGAINST IRAN'S ENERGY AND INFRASTRUCTURE 'WITH THE AIM OF FORCING SURRENDER,' REPORTEDLY ABLE TO BEGIN AS SOON AS THIS WEEKEND — POWER PLANTS, REFINERIES, TEHRAN'S ELECTRICITY GRID AND DUAL-USE BRIDGES ARE THE REPORTED TARGET CLASSES, AND THE PLAN WAS RAISED AT A CAMP DAVID CABINET MEETING WHERE TRUMP SAID 'WE'LL BE HITTING THEM VERY HARD... AT SOME POINT, THEY'RE GOING TO SAY, WE JUST CAN'T TAKE IT ANYMORE.' THE ORDER'S STATUS IS ITSELF CONTESTED: THE WSJ SAYS TRUMP HAS ORDERED IT, CBS SAYS HE HAS NOT GIVEN FINAL AUTHORISATION, AND AN ISRAELI OFFICIAL SAYS ISRAEL IS 'UNAWARE OF A DECISION.' MEANWHILE IRAN ANSWERED THE JULY 30 'HEAVY WAVE' BY DRONE ACROSS THE GULF: ITS ARMY AND THE IRGC CLAIMED ONE-WAY ATTACK DRONES AGAINST AHMAD AL-JABER AND ALI AL-SALEM IN KUWAIT, SHEIKH ISA IN BAHRAIN AND AL AZRAQ IN JORDAN, TARGETING AIRCRAFT SHELTERS, SATELLITE COMMUNICATIONS, POWER GENERATORS AND NAVIGATION SYSTEMS. US WOUNDED ROSE TO 685 (18 KIA). CENTCOM CONFIRMED IT IS INVESTIGATING THE QESHM DEATHS OF A TWO-YEAR-OLD AND THE CHILD'S PARENTS. ARAGHCHI DENIED THE DAMIETTA ATTACK AND CALLED IT A POSSIBLE ISRAELI FALSE FLAG; EGYPT PUBLICLY REJECTED REPORTING THAT CAIRO BLAMES IRAN. BRENT ROSE 3.87% TO $90.24, CLOSING JULY UP ~24%, ITS STRONGEST MONTH SINCE MARCH; DIESEL SET ANOTHER WAR HIGH AT $5.3530. STILL AIR AND MARITIME ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO RELIEF ARG, NO DRAFT. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED.",
