  {
   "date": "2026-08-01",
   "headline": "DAY 156 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops, AND THIS IS THE CYCLE IN WHICH THE REPORTED PLAN FOR FORCING IRANIAN CAPITULATION WAS STATED IN FULL AND CONTAINED NO GROUND COMPONENT. (1) FOUR OUTLETS DESCRIBED THE SAME COERCIVE PACKAGE — A MULTI-DAY BOMBING CAMPAIGN AGAINST POWER PLANTS, REFINERIES, TEHRAN'S ELECTRICITY GRID AND DUAL-USE BRIDGES, EXPLICITLY AIMED AT SURRENDER — AND NONE NAMED A LANDING FORCE, AN EMBARKATION, A MEU TASKING OR KHARG ISLAND. THE OBJECTIVE THE MARCH-ERA KHARG SEIZURE OPTION WAS MEANT TO SERVE IS NOW BEING PURSUED BY AIR. (2) KHARG WAS NOT NAMED AS A TARGET AND HAS NEVER BEEN SEIZED. (3) THE AMPHIBIOUS PICTURE IS UNCHANGED FOR A TENTH DAY: USS BOXER (LHD-4) WITH COMSTOCK, PORTLAND AND THE 11TH MEU IN THE ARABIAN SEA, STILL THE SOLE DEPLOYED ARG FLEET-WIDE; NO RELIEF ARG ANNOUNCED; USS TRIPOLI HOME IN SASEBO. (4) IRAN'S OWN ESCALATION THIS CYCLE WAS ONE-WAY DRONES AGAINST GULF AIR BASES — THE AIR RUNG. (5) THE DRAFT RUNG REMAINS DOWN: THE WITHDRAWN SELECTIVE SERVICE RULE HAS NOT BEEN RE-PROPOSED. EVERY EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO FOR A 156TH CONSECUTIVE DAY.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Ground Invasion Tracker",
   "tags": [
    "Ground Invasion Tracker",
    "no_ground_troops",
    "Air Campaign Not Ground",
    "Energy Infrastructure Targets",
    "Kharg Not Named",
    "Kharg Never Seized",
    "Boxer ARG Unchanged",
    "11th MEU",
    "Sole Deployed ARG",
    "No Relief ARG",
    "USS Tripoli In Sasebo",
    "~50,000 Troops",
    "82nd Airborne HQ",
    "Draft Rule Still Withdrawn",
    "No Draft",
    "156 Days No Landing",
    "Disconfirmed"
   ],
   "source": "The Wall Street Journal via The Times of Israel liveblog and Bloomberg, July 31, 2026; CBS News, 'U.S., Israel preparing to bombard energy-related targets in Iran, sources say,' July 31, 2026; CNN live blog, July 31, 2026; Axios, July 31, 2026; USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, July 27, 2026 (most recent edition); CNN Politics, 'Iran building up defenses of Kharg Island to protect against potential US ground attack, sources say,' March 25, 2026; Al Jazeera, \"Pentagon readies 'for weeks of US ground operations' in Iran,\" March 29, 2026; CBS News, 'U.S. expected to deploy troops from 82nd Airborne to Middle East for Iran war,' March 2026; Selective Service System rule withdrawal, July 23, 2026; NDAA FY2026 automatic-registration provision (statutory start December 19, 2026); CNBC and CNN Politics on automatic draft registration, April 9, 2026; Middle East Monitor and IranWire on Iranian drone attacks, July 31, 2026.",
   "summary": "Day 156 holds at no_ground_troops, and it is the most informative cycle on the ground question since the Pentagon's March options reporting — not because anything moved on the ground rung, but because the alternative to it was described in full.\n\nTHE COERCIVE PLAN IS AN AIR PLAN. Four outlets working the same story on July 31 described a multi-day campaign intended to force Iran to accept American terms. The WSJ put the objective as surrender. CBS named the target classes: power plants, refineries, electricity infrastructure across Tehran, and bridges of dual military-civilian purpose. Axios described strikes on energy targets within days. CNN described fresh strikes as soon as this weekend. In none of the four does a ground element appear. No landing, no raid, no embarkation, no MEU tasking, no airborne insertion, no Kharg Island. This matters because the Kharg-seizure option reported since March 2026 — two Marine Expeditionary Units, roughly 1,000-2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne, an amphibious landing against a mined shoreline — existed to supply exactly the leverage this air campaign is now reported to be seeking. When a state chooses between two instruments for one objective and the reported choice is the air instrument, that is evidence about the ground rung even though nothing on the ground rung moved.\n\nTHE CAVEAT THE PROJECT OWES ITSELF. Reported plans are not orders, the authorisation status is itself disputed, and an energy campaign that fails to produce capitulation is precisely the circumstance in which a ground option would be revisited. Destroying Iran's refining and export infrastructure by air and seizing its export terminal by force are not mutually exclusive; the first has historically been argued as a precursor to the second. The tracker records the absence of a ground component in the reported plan as a datum, not as foreclosure.\n\nEVERYTHING ELSE IS UNCHANGED. Kharg was not named as a target and has never been seized. The Boxer Amphibious Ready Group — USS Boxer (LHD-4), USS Comstock (LSD-45), USS Portland (LPD-27) and the 11th Marine Expeditionary Unit — remains in the Arabian Sea and remains the sole deployed ARG fleet-wide; the most recent USNI Fleet and Marine Tracker is the July 27 edition and no relief ARG has been announced. USS Tripoli is home in Sasebo. Troop strength in the region is unchanged at roughly 50,000. Iran's own escalation this cycle was one-way attack drones against US facilities at Gulf air bases — the air rung, not the ground one. The Selective Service's withdrawn automatic-registration rule has not been re-proposed and no explanation has been offered; the December 19, 2026 statutory deadline is unchanged; automatic registration is not a draft, and no draft has been called or planned. Every execution indicator stood at zero for a 156th consecutive day: no US troops in Iran, no landing, no Kharg seizure, no new ARG or MEU order, no draft.",
   "details": [
    "THE REPORTED CAPITULATION PLAN CONTAINS NO GROUND COMPONENT (July 31, 2026): The Wall Street Journal (multi-day bombing aimed at surrender), CBS News (power plants, refineries, Tehran electricity infrastructure, dual-use bridges), Axios (energy targets within days) and CNN (fresh strikes as soon as this weekend) each described the coercive package. None named a ground force, landing, raid, embarkation, MEU tasking, airborne insertion or Kharg Island operation. (The Wall Street Journal via The Times of Israel; CBS News; Axios; CNN, July 31, 2026.)",
    "THE MARCH-ERA GROUND OPTION SERVED THE SAME OBJECTIVE (context, March 2026): The Pentagon's reported ground options — weeks of limited operations comprising Special Operations and conventional raids on Kharg Island and coastal weapons sites, with two Marine Expeditionary Units and roughly 1,000-2,000 soldiers of the 82nd Airborne — were framed as leverage to coerce Iran into reopening the Strait of Hormuz. The air campaign now reported seeks the same coercive end. (CNN Politics, March 25, 2026; Al Jazeera, March 29, 2026; CBS News, March 2026; Stars and Stripes, March 24-25, 2026.)",
    "KHARG ISLAND: NOT NAMED, NOT STRUCK THIS CYCLE, NEVER SEIZED (July 31, 2026): Kharg did not appear among the reported target classes for the planned campaign and was not struck in the July 29-30 wave. Iran's fortification of the island — additional personnel, air defences, and anti-personnel and anti-armour mines laid around the island and on the shoreline where an amphibious landing would stage — stands as last reported. No US or allied ground force has landed on the island at any point in the war.",
    "AMPHIBIOUS PICTURE UNCHANGED FOR A TENTH DAY (July 31, 2026): USS Boxer (LHD-4) remains in the Arabian Sea with USS Comstock (LSD-45), USS Portland (LPD-27) and the 11th Marine Expeditionary Unit, still the sole deployed Amphibious Ready Group fleet-wide. The most recent USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker remains the July 27 edition; no relief ARG has been announced and USS Tripoli remains home-ported in Sasebo. No new ARG, MEU or ground formation was ordered, tasked or repositioned this cycle. (USNI News Fleet and Marine Tracker, July 27, 2026.)",
    "IRAN'S ESCALATION THIS CYCLE WAS ON THE AIR RUNG (July 31, 2026): Iran's army and the IRGC claimed one-way attack drone strikes on US facilities at Sheikh Isa Air Base in Bahrain, Ahmad al-Jaber and Ali al-Salem in Kuwait, and Al Azraq in Jordan. No Iranian ground action, and no US ground response, was reported. (Middle East Monitor; IranWire; CNBC, July 31, 2026.)",
    "DRAFT RUNG REMAINS DOWN (July 31, 2026): The Selective Service System's proposed automatic draft-registration rules, withdrawn on July 23, 2026 after nearly four months at the White House, have not been re-proposed and no explanation has been given. The statutory mandate under the December 2025 NDAA is unchanged — automatic registration must begin December 19, 2026 — and the agency has separately been reported to be procuring a draft mobilisation simulator. Automatic registration is not a draft; no draft has been called and none is planned. (Selective Service System; CNBC, April 9, 2026; CNN Politics, April 9, 2026.)",
    "TROOP STRENGTH UNCHANGED (July 31, 2026): Approximately 50,000 US personnel remain in the Middle East, roughly 10,000 above the normal baseline, with no new deployment order announced this cycle."
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Predictions of a US GROUND seizure of the Strait of Hormuz or Kharg Island remain DISCONFIRMED at Day 156, and the disconfirmation strengthened on evidence rather than on the mere passage of another day. The relevant test for a prediction of ground invasion is not only whether troops have landed but whether the state pursuing the objective has selected the ground instrument. On July 31 the reported plan for forcing Iranian capitulation was described across four outlets in target-class detail, and it is an air campaign against energy and civil infrastructure. The ground option that has existed on paper since March, built around two MEUs and elements of the 82nd Airborne and aimed at the same coercive end, was not selected and was not mentioned. This is a datum against the ground-invasion predictions, not merely an absence of one for them. It does not foreclose the possibility: an energy campaign that fails to force terms is exactly the scenario in which the Kharg option returns, and suppression of coastal defences plus destruction of export infrastructure would shape the ground for it. The tracker holds at no_ground_troops with every execution indicator at zero for a 156th consecutive day."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-08-01",
   "headline": "DAY 156 GULF STATES — RIYADH ASSEMBLES 43 NATIONS FOR A MARITIME DEFENCE COALITION THAT WASHINGTON COULD NOT RAISE FOR HORMUZ: SAUDI ARABIA'S DEFENCE MINISTRY CONVENED MILITARY REPRESENTATIVES OF 43 COUNTRIES IN RIYADH ON JULY 30 TO STAND UP AN ALLIANCE FOR THE RED SEA, BAB AL-MANDEB AND GULF OF ADEN, HEADQUARTERED IN THE KINGDOM, WITH A JOINT STATEMENT FROM THIRTEEN BACKERS INCLUDING KUWAIT, BAHRAIN, QATAR, PAKISTAN, TURKEY, EGYPT, JORDAN, YEMEN, BANGLADESH, NIGERIA, SUDAN, DJIBOUTI AND SOMALIA — WHILE BRITAIN AND FRANCE STILL REFUSE TO LEAD HEGSETH'S HORMUZ COALITION. KUWAIT AND BAHRAIN ABSORBED IRANIAN DRONE ATTACKS ON AHMAD AL-JABER, ALI AL-SALEM AND SHEIKH ISA. BAGHDAD DENIED TRUMP'S CLAIM THAT THE JULY 28 US-SAUDI STRIKES WERE COORDINATED WITH IRAQ, ITS NATIONAL SECURITY COUNCIL CALLING THEM 'A FLAGRANT VIOLATION OF IRAQ'S SOVEREIGNTY,' AND SUSPENDED PM ALI AL-ZAIDI'S PLANNED VISIT TO SAUDI ARABIA. EGYPT REJECTED REPORTING THAT IT BLAMES IRAN FOR DAMIETTA.",
