  {
   "date": "2026-08-01",
   "headline": "DAY 156 RUSSIA-UKRAINE — A RUSSIAN CRUISE MISSILE DETONATES ON NATO SOIL: A PROJECTILE ASSESSED BY EXPERTS AS A KH-101 CROSSED INTO POLISH AIRSPACE DURING RUSSIA'S OVERNIGHT BARRAGE AND EXPLODED IN A FIELD NEAR TARNAWA-KOLONIA, OUTSIDE LUBLIN, LEAVING A TEN-METRE CRATER; NATO SCRAMBLED FIGHTERS, 'ACTIVATED A WIDE RANGE OF AIR DEFENCES' AND SAID IT WOULD 'DEFEND TERRITORY,' AND WARSAW BLAMED MOSCOW. THE SAME BARRAGE — 70-PLUS MISSILES AND ABOUT 280 DRONES AGAINST KYIV AND LVIV — KILLED AT LEAST EIGHT AND BY LATER COUNTS TEN, INCLUDING THREE CHILDREN. UKRAINE ANSWERED ON JULY 31 WITH LONG-RANGE STRIKES ON REFINERIES AND LOGISTICS HUBS IN VOLGOGRAD, TATARSTAN AND KRASNODAR, ZELENSKY HAVING PROMISED TO INTENSIFY STRIKES ON RUSSIAN TERRITORY. THE LINE BARELY MOVED: 226 COMBAT CLASHES ON JULY 30, HEAVIEST AT KOSTIANTYNIVKA AND POKROVSK, WITH DEEPSTATE PUTTING RUSSIA'S FOUR-WEEK NET GAIN AT TEN SQUARE MILES AND THE ECONOMIST AT ZERO OVER THIRTY DAYS.",
   "theatre": "Russia-Ukraine War",
   "tag": "Russia-Ukraine",
   "tags": [
    "Russia-Ukraine",
    "Kh-101 In Poland",
