  {
   "date": "2026-08-01",
   "headline": "DAY 156 MULTI-THEATRE — VENEZUELA'S US-BACKED TRANSITION TALKS OPEN TODAY WITHOUT MARÍA CORINA MACHADO, WITH JORGE RODRÍGUEZ — BROTHER OF INTERIM PRESIDENT DELCY RODRÍGUEZ — LEADING THE GOVERNMENT DELEGATION AND DINORAH FIGUERA THE OPPOSITION SIDE; MACHADO WILL NOT ATTEND BUT DOES NOT OPPOSE THE TALKS. ISRAEL DEMOLISHED A MULTI-LEVEL HEZBOLLAH TUNNEL COMPLEX BENEATH THE BEAUFORT RIDGE IN SOUTHERN LEBANON WITH 700 TONNES OF EXPLOSIVES, FOUR DAYS BEFORE US-BROKERED ISRAEL-LEBANON TALKS CONVENE IN ROME ON AUGUST 4-6. HORMUZ TRANSITS HIT A TWO-WEEK HIGH OF 28 AS LNG TRAFFIC RESUMED AFTER A FORTNIGHT'S GAP, WITH BAB EL-MANDEB CROSSINGS AT 39 AND VLCCs MASSING AT EGYPT'S SIDI KERIR. CHINA'S JULY CRUDE IMPORTS ARE SET TO REBOUND FROM A DECADE LOW WHILE BEIJING URGES BOTH SIDES BACK TO THE MOU. NORTH KOREA'S NAVAL BUILD-OUT CONTINUES WITHOUT A NEW PROVOCATION.",
