   "source": "France 24, 'Venezuela transition talks set to kick off without Machado,' July 31, 2026; The Manila Times, 'Venezuela prepares for transition talks,' August 1, 2026; Latin America Reports, 'Maria Corina Machado rules out participation in talks with Venezuela government,' July 2026; Ground News on Rubio's announcement of an early-August transition start; Cubaheadlines, 'Trial Date Set for Nicolás Maduro in the United States' (Judge Alvin Hellerstein, trial June 1, 2027); Haaretz live blog, 'IDF Destroys Iran-funded Hezbollah Tunnel Network in Lebanon,' July 30-31, 2026; SyriacPress, 'IDF blows up underground Hezbollah tunnel network near historic Beaufort Castle in southern Lebanon,' July 31, 2026; ANI/The Tribune, 'IDF claims to dismantle key Hezbollah tunnel network beneath Beaufort Ridge,' July 31, 2026; Asianet Newsable, 'Israel dismantles key Hezbollah tunnel network ahead of Lebanon talks,' July 31, 2026; S&P Global via webindia123, 'Hormuz vessel transits hit two-week high as LNG tanker traffic resumes,' July 31, 2026; Bloomberg via Yahoo Finance, \"China's Crude Imports in July Poised to Rebound From Decade Low,\" July 2026; Newsweek, 'China Responds to Iran and US Resuming Strikes'; Chinese Foreign Ministry (Mao Ning); USTR Section 301 forced-labour tariff notice, effective July 24, 2026; Zero Carbon Analytics and CNBC on Hormuz-dependent economies; AEI, 'Korean Peninsula Update, July 28, 2026.'",
   "summary": "VENEZUELA. The US-backed political transition talks open on Saturday, August 1, in the first formal negotiation since Nicolás Maduro's removal in January. National Assembly chief Jorge Rodríguez — brother of interim president Delcy Rodríguez — heads the government delegation; Dinorah Figuera, who leads the opposition bloc that won the 2015 parliamentary majority, heads the other. The stated agenda is a roadmap for political transition covering institutional reforms, electoral conditions and guarantees for political participation. María Corina Machado, the Nobel laureate and the opposition's dominant figure, has ruled out participating while stating she does not oppose the talks proceeding — an absence that has left her base sceptical of the process before it begins. Maduro and Cilia Flores remain scheduled for trial before Judge Alvin Hellerstein in Manhattan on June 1, 2027.\n\nLEBANON. The Israel Defense Forces said on Friday, July 31, that it had dismantled a multi-level Hezbollah tunnel complex beneath the Beaufort Ridge in southern Lebanon, using 700 tonnes of explosives to demolish a network built over two decades that served as the central command post of Hezbollah's Bader Unit and sat about six kilometres from Metula and the Galilee Panhandle. The IDF said the network was planned and funded by Iran. The operation came four days before the next round of US-brokered Israel-Lebanon talks, scheduled for Rome on August 4-6, where technical teams are expected to focus on implementing the framework agreement.\n\nTHE CHOKEPOINTS. S&P Global recorded 28 Hormuz transits on July 29, the highest since July 14, as LNG tanker traffic resumed after a two-week gap; Iran-linked vessels fell to 60% of movements from a 68% second-half-of-July average. Bab el-Mandeb crossings rose to 39, and very large crude carriers increasingly gathered at Egypt's Sidi Kerir terminal, complicating voyage logistics. Both chokepoints are now contested simultaneously, and the Damietta strike of July 29 established that the import end of the chain is also a target — a fact of direct consequence for Japan, South Korea, India, Pakistan and Bangladesh, whose Gulf LNG dependence runs from 53% of imports for India to 99% for Pakistan.\n\nCHINA. Beijing's position is unchanged: the Foreign Ministry has urged both sides to settle disputes through negotiation, implement the memorandum of understanding and avoid resorting to force, and its material support for Iran has remained diplomatic. China's July crude imports are poised to rebound from a decade low. The Section 301 forced-labour tariff of 12.5% on Chinese goods, effective July 24, remains the operative new trade measure, raising the overall tariff burden by about 2.5 points. Iranian crude continues to reach China through Kharg Island, at recent flows of roughly 1.25 million barrels per day, with more than 200 million barrels reported stored on tankers near Chinese waters.\n\nKOREAN PENINSULA. No new provocation this cycle. Kim Jong Un's naval build-out continues, with the destroyer Kang Kon to be commissioned by September and a 10,000-tonne guided-missile cruiser in development, alongside deepening Russian support following Foreign Minister Choe Son Hui's June 18 Moscow meetings with Putin and Lavrov.",
   "details": [
    "VENEZUELA'S TRANSITION TALKS OPEN AUGUST 1 (July 31 - August 1, 2026): US-backed political transition talks begin Saturday, August 1. National Assembly chief Jorge Rodriguez, brother of interim president Delcy Rodriguez, heads the government delegation; opposition figure Dinorah Figuera, who leads the bloc that won the 2015 parliamentary majority, heads the opposition side. The talks aim to establish a roadmap for political transition covering institutional reforms, electoral conditions and guarantees for political participation. (France 24; The Manila Times; Ground News, July 31 - August 1, 2026.)",
    "MACHADO WILL NOT ATTEND BUT DOES NOT OPPOSE THE TALKS (July 2026): Nobel Peace Prize-winning opposition leader Maria Corina Machado has ruled out participating in the White House-backed negotiations while stating she does not oppose them going ahead. Her absence has left her base sceptical of the process. (Latin America Reports; France 24, July 2026.)",
    "MADURO TRIAL REMAINS SET FOR JUNE 1, 2027 (unchanged): Federal Judge Alvin Hellerstein has scheduled the trial of Nicolas Maduro and Cilia Flores in Manhattan federal court for June 1, 2027 on narcotics-trafficking charges. (Cubaheadlines.)",
    "ISRAEL DEMOLISHES A HEZBOLLAH TUNNEL COMPLEX BENEATH BEAUFORT RIDGE (July 31, 2026): The IDF said it dismantled several key underground tunnels beneath the Beaufort Ridge in southern Lebanon during limited activity in the security zone, using 700 tonnes of explosives to demolish a multi-level network constructed over two decades. The IDF described it as the central command centre of Hezbollah's Bader Unit, from which commanders directed fire toward Israeli troops and civilians, located about six kilometres from Metula and the Galilee Panhandle, and said it was planned and funded by Iran. (Haaretz; SyriacPress; ANI/The Tribune; Social News XYZ, July 31, 2026.)",
    "US-BROKERED ISRAEL-LEBANON TALKS SET FOR ROME, AUGUST 4-6 (July 31, 2026): The next round of US-brokered Israel-Lebanon talks is scheduled for Rome from August 4 to August 6, with technical teams expected to focus on implementing the framework agreement. (Asianet Newsable; Haaretz, July 31, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ TRANSITS REACH A TWO-WEEK HIGH AS LNG TRAFFIC RESUMES (July 29-31, 2026): Vessel transits through the Strait of Hormuz rose to 28 on July 29, the highest since July 14, driven by resumed LNG tanker traffic after a two-week gap along with several dark transits. Iran-linked vessels made up 60% of movements, down from a 68% average in the second half of July. Red Sea activity also rose, with Bab el-Mandeb crossings up to 39, while VLCCs increasingly gathered at Egypt's Sidi Kerir terminal. (S&P Global via webindia123, July 31, 2026.)",
    "THE IMPORT END OF THE GAS CHAIN REMAINS A DEMONSTRATED TARGET (July 29-31, 2026): The July 29 drone attack on the FSRU Energos Winter and the LNG carrier Gaslog Salem at Egypt's Damietta port established that receiving terminals, not only export chokepoints, are exposed. Qatar and the UAE account for 99% of Pakistan's LNG imports, 72% of Bangladesh's and 53% of India's; South Korea and Japan hold roughly 3.5 million and 4.4 million tonnes of LNG in reserve, on the order of two to four weeks of stable demand. (Zero Carbon Analytics; CNBC; Seatrade Maritime, March-July 2026.)",
    "CHINA HOLDS ITS DIPLOMATIC LINE AS CRUDE IMPORTS REBOUND (July 2026): China's Foreign Ministry has urged both sides to settle disputes through negotiations, carry out the MoU and avoid resorting to force, with Beijing's support for Iran limited to diplomatic statements. China's July crude imports are poised to rebound from a decade low. Roughly 40% of China's oil imports transit the Strait of Hormuz; Iranian crude accounted for 11.6% of China's seaborne imports so far in 2026, with recent flows averaging about 1.252 million barrels per day from Kharg Island and more than 200 million barrels reported stored on tankers near China. (Newsweek; Chinese Foreign Ministry; Bloomberg via Yahoo Finance; Kpler, July 2026.)",
    "THE SECTION 301 FORCED-LABOUR TARIFF REMAINS THE OPERATIVE NEW MEASURE (effective July 24, 2026): The United States Trade Representative's 12.5% Section 301 tariff on Chinese goods, imposed for failure to prohibit and enforce against imports produced with forced labour, took effect July 24 and raises the overall tariff on Chinese goods by about 2.5 percentage points. (USTR; China Briefing.)",
    "NORTH KOREA: NAVAL BUILD-OUT CONTINUES, NO NEW PROVOCATION (July 2026): Kim Jong Un has called for testing of the destroyer Kang Kon to be completed in time for commissioning in September and has turned attention to a 10,000-tonne guided-missile cruiser, twice the size of the Choe Hyon class, to enhance the navy's nuclear deterrence. Foreign Minister Choe Son Hui met Putin and Lavrov in Moscow on June 18 amid continued North Korean support for Russia's war in Ukraine and Russian support for North Korean nuclearisation. (AEI, 'Korean Peninsula Update, July 28, 2026.')"
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Predictions of a negotiated Venezuelan transition under US supervision are moving toward PARTIAL CONFIRMATION in form while remaining untested in substance: talks convene on schedule, led on the government side by the interim president's brother and boycotted by the opposition's most popular figure, which is consistent both with a genuine transition and with a managed continuity dressed as one. Predictions that the Lebanon track would collapse back into open war remain DISCONFIRMED: Israel conducted a demolition operation inside the security zone and both parties are still scheduled to meet in Rome on August 4-6. Predictions of permanent closure of the Strait of Hormuz remain DISCONFIRMED in the absolute form — LNG traffic resumed after a fortnight and transits reached a two-week high — while predictions of sustained degradation remain CONFIRMED at roughly a tenth of pre-crisis throughput. Predictions of Chinese material intervention on Iran's behalf remain UNCONFIRMED: Beijing's position is still diplomatic, and the reported MANPADS transfer remains denied by both China and Pakistan and unverified. Predictions of a Korean-peninsula crisis opening as a second front remain DISCONFIRMED for a 156th day."
  },
  {
   "date": "2026-07-31",
   "headline": "DAY 155 — THE UNITED STATES GOES BACK TO BOMBING IRAN ITSELF: CENTCOM COMPLETES A 'HEAVY WAVE' OF STRIKES ON 'DOZENS' OF IRGC TARGETS OVER ROUGHLY TWO HOURS — THE FIRST STRIKE ON IRANIAN SOIL SINCE JULY 24 AND, PER A US OFFICIAL, 'ABOUT TWICE THE SIZE OF THE PREVIOUS' BOMBARDMENT. THE TARGET SET IS THE COASTLINE: 'COASTAL SURVEILLANCE AND DEFENSE SITES' AND 'MARITIME CAPABILITIES' AT BANDAR ABBAS, QESHM, KISH, ABU MUSA, BUSHEHR, KAZERUN, FARASHBAND, ABADAN AND AHVAZ — BUT NOT KHARG. IRNA: THREE KILLED ON QESHM, REPORTED AS A COUPLE AND THEIR TWO-YEAR-OLD CHILD. THE IRGC VOWS 'THE AGGRESSOR WILL BE PUNISHED TODAY,' WARNS STATES AIDING THE US OF A 'HARSH RESPONSE,' AND CLAIMS 'FULL CONTROL' OF THE STRAIT. IT ALSO CLAIMS THREE F-35s DESTROYED AT AL AZRAQ; CENTCOM DENIES THE AIRCRAFT AND IS SILENT ON THE CASUALTIES. THE WAR WIDENS TWICE: AN IRANIAN STRIKE KILLS A WORKER AT A CHINESE COMPANY'S BUILDING IN KUWAIT, AND AN UNCLAIMED DRONE HITS TWO LNG VESSELS AT EGYPT'S DAMIETTA — THE FIRST ATTACK ON EGYPTIAN SOIL OF THE WAR, AND ON AN IMPORT TERMINAL. SAUDI DEFENCE MINISTER PRINCE KHALID CARRIES A DE-ESCALATION MESSAGE TO THE WHITE HOUSE ONE DAY AFTER FLYING STRIKES IN IRAQ. BRENT EASES BELOW $90 AFTER A 7.9% SURGE; DIESEL SETS ANOTHER WAR HIGH AT $5.339. STILL AIR AND MARITIME ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO RELIEF ARG, NO DRAFT. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED.",
