  {
   "date": "2026-07-31",
   "headline": "DAY 155 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops, AND FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WEEK ONE INDICATOR POINTS THE OTHER WAY. THE RESUMED STRIKES ON IRANIAN TERRITORY CONCENTRATED ON THE LITTORAL: CENTCOM NAMED 'COASTAL SURVEILLANCE AND DEFENSE SITES' AND 'MARITIME CAPABILITIES,' AND THE STRIKE MAP RUNS BANDAR ABBAS-QESHM-KISH-ABU MUSA-BUSHEHR-ABADAN-AHVAZ — THE SAME SUPPRESSION A LIMITED COASTAL RAID WOULD REQUIRE, AND EQUALLY THE WHOLE OBJECTIVE OF A BLOCKADING NAVY. RECORDED AS AN AMBIGUOUS SHAPING SIGNAL, NOT AS INTENT. EVERYTHING ELSE IS UNCHANGED: KHARG WAS NOT STRUCK AND HAS NEVER BEEN SEIZED; NO LANDING; NO NEW ARG, MEU OR GROUND FORMATION ORDERED; BOXER ARG (BOXER, COMSTOCK, PORTLAND, 11TH MEU) STILL THE SOLE DEPLOYED ARG FLEET-WIDE WITH TRIPOLI HOME IN SASEBO AND NO RELIEF NINE DAYS ON; ~50,000 PERSONNEL; THE DRAFT RULE STILL WITHDRAWN SINCE JULY 23. EVERY STATED US ESCALATION OPTION REMAINS AERIAL. RIYADH SPENT THE CYCLE ARGUING FOR DE-ESCALATION IN THE OVAL OFFICE; BRITAIN AND FRANCE STILL REFUSE TO LEAD THE NAVAL COALITION. NEW: US TROOPS IN JORDAN TOLD PHONES MAY BE CONFISCATED OVER OPSEC.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
   "tag": "Ground Invasion Tracker",
   "tags": [
    "Ground Invasion Tracker",
    "no_ground_troops",
    "Ambiguous Shaping Signal",
    "Coastal Target Set",
    "Coastal Surveillance And Defense Sites",
    "Maritime Capabilities",
