  {
   "date": "2026-07-29",
   "headline": "DAY 153 — IRAN BREAKS THE PAUSE: THE IRGC FIRES BALLISTIC MISSILES AT US FORCES IN AN 'ATTEMPTED SURPRISE ATTACK' AT 5:45 P.M. ET AND CENTCOM SAYS ALL WERE INTERCEPTED — THE FIRST KINETIC ACT AFTER FOUR QUIET DAYS, AND IT CAME FROM TEHRAN, NOT WASHINGTON. HOURS EARLIER TRUMP HOSTED NETANYAHU AT THE WHITE HOUSE — THEIR FIRST MEETING SINCE THE WAR BEGAN — AFTER PUBLICLY SLAPPING DOWN HIS PICKAXE MOUNTAIN INTELLIGENCE: 'I DON'T NEED BIBI TO TELL ME THAT... HE WANTS ME TO STAY INVOLVED.' AFTERWARDS: 'WE TOOK OUT THEIR NUCLEAR SITES AND WE'LL HAVE TO TAKE OUT PICKAXE,' AND 'IF THEY DON'T MAKE A DEAL THEN I GO BACK AND I FINISH THE JOB.' ON THE STRAIT: 'WE CONTROL THE STRAIT. OUR NAVY IS INCREDIBLE. NOT ONE SHIP HAS GOTTEN TO IRAN DURING ANY BLOCKADE.' OMAN'S GULF-BACKED HORMUZ PLAN OFFERS VOLUNTARY FEES, NOT IRANIAN TOLLS; GHARIBABADI SAYS IRAN WILL TAKE 'ANY ACTION' TO KEEP CONTROL. BRENT SLIPS A THIRD SESSION TO ~$86.6. THE STRANDED-SHIP BACKLOG EASES FOR THE FIRST TIME (426→405). STILL AIR/MARITIME ONLY — NO LANDING, NO KHARG SEIZURE, NO RELIEF ARG, NO DRAFT. PREDICTED US GROUND SEIZURE REMAINS DISCONFIRMED.",
