   "summary": "The Ukraine theatre stayed in high-tempo attrition with the negotiation track frozen. On July 25, Ukrainian attacks in the partly Russian-occupied Zaporizhzhia region killed 12 people and a Russian drone strike in Sumy region killed three, for 15 dead across both sides' strikes. The preceding 24-hour period (July 24) logged 192 combat engagements, 24 of them in the Pokrovsk direction, with Russia launching two missile strikes comprising five missiles, 56 airstrikes delivering 186 guided bombs, 5,746 one-way attack drones and 2,297 shelling attacks; three Iskander-M/S-400 ballistic missiles were fired at the Bucha district of Kyiv Oblast, one intercepted and two impacting. ISW's July 22 assessment recorded confirmed Russian ground advances near Kryva Luka and Hlushkivka in the Lyman/Kupiansk sector and near Novodanilovka in the Orikhiv direction, while characterising overall Russian momentum as decelerating relative to 2024-25. Diplomatically nothing moved: Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said on July 22 that Putin's June 2024 maximalist terms — full Ukrainian withdrawal from the parts of Luhansk, Donetsk, Zaporizhzhia and Kherson oblasts Kyiv still holds, and abandonment of NATO accession — remain the basis for ending the war, and senior Russian officials reiterated unwillingness to negotiate directly with Kyiv. Russia continues to hold roughly 20% of Ukraine with no confirmed net change, and no US or NATO ground troops are committed.",
   "details": [
    "JULY 25 CASUALTIES: Ukrainian attacks in the partly Russian-occupied Zaporizhzhia region killed 12; a Russian drone strike in Sumy region killed three — 15 across both. (AP via The Washington Times, July 25, 2026.)",
    "JULY 24 TEMPO: 192 combat engagements in 24 hours, 24 of them in the Pokrovsk direction; Russia fired five missiles in two missile strikes, flew 56 airstrikes delivering 186 guided bombs, launched 5,746 one-way attack drones and conducted 2,297 shelling attacks. (Ukrainian General Staff via GlobalSecurity, July 24, 2026.)",
    "BALLISTIC STRIKE ON KYIV OBLAST: Three Iskander-M/S-400 ballistic missiles were fired at the Bucha district — one intercepted, two struck. (GlobalSecurity, July 24, 2026.)",
    "GROUND MOVEMENT: ISW confirmed Russian advances near Kryva Luka and Hlushkivka (Lyman/Kupiansk sector) and near Novodanilovka (Orikhiv direction), while assessing that the marked advances of 2024 and parts of 2025 have decelerated. Russia holds ~20% of Ukraine with no confirmed net change; Kostiantynivka remains contested. (ISW/Critical Threats, July 22, 2026.)",
    "NEGOTIATIONS FROZEN: Peskov said July 22 that Putin's June 2024 speech setting maximalist aims — Ukrainian withdrawal from Ukrainian-held areas of Luhansk, Donetsk, Zaporizhzhia and Kherson oblasts and abandonment of NATO accession — remains the Kremlin's precondition for talks; Russia is unwilling to return any occupied territory and Putin remains committed to seizing the remainder of Donetsk Oblast. Senior Russian officials reiterated refusal to negotiate directly with Kyiv. (ISW/Critical Threats, July 22, 2026.)",
    "NO US GROUND INVOLVEMENT: No US or NATO combat troops are committed to Ukraine; the theatre remains a materiel-and-intelligence commitment. (ISW; Russia Matters, July 2026.)"
