  {
   "date": "2026-07-26",
   "headline": "MULTI-THEATRE ROUNDUP — US-CHINA/TAIWAN: Taiwan and the EU were the ONLY two of the ~60 economies hit by the July 24 Section 301 tariff wave to receive 10% NOT stacked on existing MFN duties — the most favourable treatment in the package, which Taipei assesses could advantage Taiwanese traditional manufacturers over Japanese and Chinese rivals; China at 12.5% signalled it would look past the levies before Xi's US trip. DPRK: Kim Jong Un logged 92 public activities in H1 2026, 30 of them military — his highest first-half military count since 2012 — with Kang Kon destroyer weapons tests July 3 and September commissioning targeted. LATIN AMERICA: Maduro/Flores trial set for June 1, 2027; Cuba's grid suffered another total collapse (~10 million without power, tens of thousands of surgeries cancelled, pot-banging protests in Havana). HORMUZ FALLOUT: ~80% of crude and 90% of LNG transiting Hormuz is Asia-bound; India, Japan and Pakistan stocks at 10-year lows; the IEA warns the global economy is in peril if the crisis persists.",
   "theatre": "Multi-Theatre",
   "tag": "Multi-Theatre Roundup",
