   ],
   "source": "Taipei Times, 'USTR notices a 10% tariff on Taiwan under Section 301,' July 25, 2026; Bloomberg, 'China Set to Look Past New Trump Tariffs Before Xi's US Trip,' July 24, 2026; South China Morning Post, July 24, 2026; AEI, 'Korean Peninsula Update, July 14, 2026'; Fox News, 'Cuba suffers nationwide blackout as electrical grid collapses,' July 2026; ABC News/US News, 'US judge sets June 2027 trial date for Venezuela's Maduro,' July 22, 2026; East Asia Forum, 'Asia bears the brunt of the Hormuz crisis'; Gulf International Forum, 'Hormuz Disruptions and Asia's Energy Resilience'; EnergyConnects, 'IEA Boss Warns Global Economy in Peril If Hormuz Crisis Persists,' July 2026; The New York Times via Ynet/JPost/ANI, 'US assesses Mojtaba Khamenei more interested in nuclear weapons than predecessor,' July 25, 2026.",
   "summary": "Outside the Gulf, four tracked theatres logged incremental movement. US-China/Taiwan: following the July 24 entry into force of Section 301 forced-labour tariffs of 10-12.5% on about 60 economies, the Taipei Times reported July 25 that Taiwan and the EU were the only two partners assigned a 10% rate that was NOT added to their existing MFN duties — the most favourable treatment in the package — which Taipei assesses could improve the competitiveness of Taiwanese traditional manufacturers against Japanese and Chinese rivals facing higher stacked burdens; China, at 12.5% on top of existing Section 301 and 232 duties (combined around 35% above MFN on most goods and well over 100% on some strategic products), signalled it would look past the levies ahead of Xi's planned US visit while reciprocal-cut talks worth roughly $30B a side continue. DPRK: AEI's Korean Peninsula tracking shows Kim Jong Un made 92 public appearances in the first half of 2026, 30 of them military-related — his highest first-half military count since taking power in 2012 — with July 3 weapons tests aboard the destroyer Kang Kon including evaluation of 'strategic' cruise missile launch capability, commissioning targeted for September, and a 10,000-ton guided-missile cruiser in development; watch the July 27 armistice anniversary. Latin America: a US judge set the Maduro/Cilia Flores trial for June 1, 2027, with Delcy Rodríguez continuing as acting president in Caracas, while Cuba suffered another total grid collapse leaving roughly 10 million without power, halting public transport, cancelling tens of thousands of surgeries and triggering scattered pot-banging protests in Havana — the island is producing only about 40% of the oil it consumes after the US blockade and the cutoff of Venezuelan crude. Hormuz fallout: about 80% of the crude and products and 90% of the LNG transiting the Strait is Asia-bound; Japan and South Korea normally route 93% and 70.7% of their oil imports through it, while Pakistan and Bangladesh are the most exposed on gas, with Qatar and the UAE supplying 99% and 72% of their LNG respectively; India faces LPG shortfalls and stocks in India, Japan and Pakistan have hit 10-year lows, with the IEA's executive director warning the global economy is in peril if the crisis persists.",
   "details": [
    "TAIWAN'S FAVOURABLE TARIFF TREATMENT (July 25, 2026): Taiwan and the EU were the only two of the ~60 economies to receive a 10% Section 301 rate not added to existing MFN duties; Taipei assesses the lighter burden could advantage Taiwanese traditional manufacturers over Japanese and Chinese competitors. (Taipei Times, July 25, 2026.)",
    "CHINA'S RESPONSE (July 24-25, 2026): China faces 12.5% on top of existing Section 301/232 duties — roughly 35% above MFN on most goods, well over 100% on some strategic products — but Bloomberg assessed the new level 'might irk Beijing without provoking retaliation' as China looks past it ahead of Xi's planned US trip; teams continue accelerating a reciprocal-cut framework valued near $30B a side. (Bloomberg; SCMP, July 24, 2026.)",
    "DPRK ACTIVITY PROFILE (H1 2026): Kim Jong Un made 92 public activities January-June 2026, 30 of them military-related — the highest first-half military count since 2012. July 3 saw multiple weapons tests for the guided-missile destroyer Kang Kon including 'strategic' cruise missile launch capability, with Kim directing testing be completed for a September commissioning; a 10,000-ton guided-missile cruiser, twice the Choe Hyon class, is in development. Watch the July 27 armistice anniversary. (AEI Korean Peninsula Update, July 7 and 14, 2026.)",
    "MADURO TRIAL AND VENEZUELA (July 22, 2026): A US judge set trial for ousted president Nicolás Maduro and Cilia Flores for June 1, 2027 on narcoterrorism, cocaine-importation and firearms conspiracy charges; both plead not guilty. Delcy Rodríguez continues as acting president. (ABC News; US News; GlobalSecurity, July 22-23, 2026.)",
    "CUBA GRID (July 2026): Another total collapse of the national grid left roughly 10 million without power, largely halted public transport, cancelled tens of thousands of surgeries and drew scattered protests in Havana with residents banging pots and shouting 'turn on the lights.' Cuba produces only about 40% of the oil it consumes; the crisis deepened after the US operation that captured Maduro halted Venezuelan oil exports. Outlets differ on the running count of 2026 total outages. (Fox News; CBS News; Al Jazeera, July 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ FALLOUT IN ASIA (July 2026): ~80% of crude and products and ~90% of LNG transiting Hormuz is Asia-bound. Japan and South Korea normally source 93% and 70.7% of oil imports through the Strait; Pakistan and Bangladesh are most exposed on gas (Qatar and the UAE supply 99% and 72% of their LNG). India faces LPG supply disruption; stocks in India, Japan and Pakistan are at 10-year lows. The IEA's executive director warned the global economy is in peril if the crisis persists. (East Asia Forum; Gulf International Forum; EnergyConnects, 2026.)"
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "US-China: the July 24 tariff wave rebuilds a broad protectionist wall, but Taiwan's most-favoured treatment within it, China's muted response, and live reciprocal-cut talks ahead of an Xi visit read as managed friction rather than rupture — cutting against corpus predictions of imminent decoupling or a Taiwan-linked confrontation. Status untested. DPRK: sustained military-modernisation tempo without a July launch keeps provocation-cycle predictions partially confirmed. Latin America: the Maduro prosecution and Rodríguez caretaker government keep US-intervention predictions partially confirmed. Hormuz fallout: the Asia-first distribution of chokepoint pain is consistent with corpus claims about Asian energy dependence, and untested as to the predicted political realignments."
