   "summary": "On Day 148 the US ran a 12TH consecutive night of strikes on Iran while the war's price signal broke a psychological ceiling and its maritime front widened again. Oil topped $100 a barrel for the first time since May: Brent crude gained about 4.6% to $98.44 and US WTI rose about 3.8% to $90.14 on Thursday, putting Brent on course for a monthly gain of roughly 35.3% — one of the three biggest monthly jumps in a decade. The trigger was a qualitative Houthi escalation: after declaring a Bab el-Mandeb blockade earlier in the week, the Iran-aligned Houthis actually ATTACKED vessels carrying Saudi crude in the Red Sea, converting a threatened second chokepoint into an active one and, with Hormuz already functionally shut, leaving oil (in CNN's framing) with 'no way out.' President Trump refused to negotiate a new ceasefire, saying Iran 'need[s] more of the same,' told Axios that Iran has not 'received enough pain yet,' and said he was weighing a 'massive attack' — while warning that the US would hold Iran responsible for Houthi strikes and threatening 'major military punishment.' UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres warned the war 'is getting out of control... teetering on the edge of the unimaginable,' with 'the region being pulled into an ever-widening circle of confrontation,' and urged an end to attacks on civilian infrastructure and a return to diplomacy. The US toll rose again: CENTCOM reported another service member killed — in northern Iraq during the controlled detonation of a downed Iranian drone — said it had located unidentified remains in Jordan tied to an earlier attack that left two dead and one missing, and put the number of troops injured since July 7 at nearly 100 (mostly minor). Despite the vertical escalation in rhetoric, price, and the maritime fight, every ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops entered Iran, no Kharg landing or seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, and no draft; ~50,000 US personnel unchanged and the weighed 'massive attack' framed as an air/standoff option. The corpus-predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg remains disconfirmed.",
