   "source": "Al Jazeera, 'US attacks Iran for 10th consecutive night,' July 21, 2026; Al Jazeera Iran-war live blog, 'Trump claims Iran desperate to talk, threatens heavy attacks,' July 21, 2026; The Times of Israel, 'Trump claims US will strike Iran's Pickaxe Mountain \"probably pretty soon\",' July 21, 2026; NPR/Ideastream, 'Amid U.S.-Iran war, Houthis declare a blockade of another key strait: Bab el-Mandeb,' July 21, 2026; CNBC, 'Iran's Houthi allies declare maritime embargo against Saudi Arabia,' July 20, 2026; The Washington Post, 'A new threat by Yemen's Houthis could widen the Iran war,' July 21, 2026; The New Arab / US News (Reuters), 'Mediators propose 10-day Iran-US ceasefire to revive interim deal,' July 20, 2026; Axios, 'Iran mediators push new ceasefire as Trump eyes all-out war,' July 21, 2026; TradingEconomics / Fortune (Brent), July 21, 2026; Al Mayadeen, 'US defers Maduro trial hearing to July 22,' 2026; CENTCOM public releases.",
   "summary": "On Day 146 the US-Iran war widened along three new axes without crossing to a ground landing. FIRST, President Trump publicly threatened to strike Iran's 'Pickaxe Mountain' (Kuh-e Kolang Gazla) — a deeply buried enrichment complex ~220 km south of Tehran and ~2 km from Natanz, built to survive bombing — saying 'we'll be hitting that area probably pretty soon, and there's not a thing they can do about it,' and that the US would target 'any site where they've been thinking about nuclear.' Israeli intelligence assesses Iran moved thousands of centrifuges and possibly some 60%-enriched uranium there after the 2025 fighting. Iran's top military command warned that an attack on the site would widen the war and trigger broader strikes on US regional allies. SECOND, Iran-aligned Yemeni Houthis declared a blockade of the Bab el-Mandeb strait — opening a SECOND maritime chokepoint — in stated retaliation for Saudi strikes on Sanaa's airport; two tankers that had just loaded Saudi crude at the Red Sea port of Yanbu for China and India made U-turns toward the Suez Canal. Bab el-Mandeb had become Saudi Arabia's principal export 'relief valve' after Hormuz went functionally shut, so the threat compounds the oil-supply squeeze. THIRD, mediators — Qatar and Pakistan, with Egyptian and Omani officials — formally floated a 10-DAY US-Iran ceasefire to revive the suspended June MOU: an immediate halt to hostilities, a return to pre-July-9 positions, full restoration of Hormuz shipping, and a proposed 'middle corridor' between Omani and Iranian waters for safe transit. Iran's Foreign Ministry (spokesman Esmaeil Baghaei) confirmed it had received the proposals; Reuters/JPost reported Iran had also quietly submitted its own 10-day ceasefire idea while under strikes. A source familiar with White House deliberations said Washington could keep striking for several more days before seriously weighing the offer, and Trump claimed Iran is 'desperate' to talk while vowing Tehran 'will pay' for the US service members killed. Militarily, the US completed its 10TH consecutive night of strikes (Iranian media cited Sirik, Bandar Abbas, Qeshm Island, Shiraz and Isfahan; CENTCOM said it hit 'command centers, maritime capabilities, missile and drone launch sites, and air defense systems'), and analysts flagged an anticipated 11TH night — with the transmission grid, Pickaxe Mountain or Kharg Island as the watched escalation targets. Iran sustained Gulf retaliation (fresh fires at a Kuwaiti desalination-and-power complex; strikes on Bahrain and Jordan; IRGC claims of hitting HIMARS systems, radars and air-defenses) and struck more shipping (two Greek-owned tankers Monday; a tanker abandoned off Oman's Limah coast; IRGC claims of 'massive fires' on additional tankers). Brent settled ~$91/bbl (its highest in over a month). Senate Minority Leader Chuck Schumer called for ending the conflict. Across all three new fronts the instruments stayed AIR, MARITIME and NUCLEAR-STRIKE THREAT — no US troops entered Iran, no Kharg landing or seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, and no draft; ~50,000 US personnel unchanged. The corpus-predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg remains disconfirmed.",
   "details": [
    "PICKAXE MOUNTAIN THREATENED, NOT YET STRUCK (July 21, 2026): Trump said the US would hit Iran's underground 'Pickaxe Mountain' enrichment site 'probably pretty soon, and there's not a thing they can do about it,' extending the target set from military/energy/nuclear-adjacent sites to a core nuclear-enrichment facility. Iran's military command warned it would widen the war. This is a declared AIR-strike threat against a buried site — not a ground operation. (The Times of Israel; ABC News, July 21, 2026.)",
    "HOUTHIS OPEN A SECOND CHOKEPOINT (July 20-21, 2026): The Houthis declared a Bab el-Mandeb blockade in retaliation for Saudi strikes on Sanaa airport; two Saudi crude tankers loaded at Yanbu for China/India reversed toward Suez. With Hormuz already functionally shut, a Bab el-Mandeb disruption threatens Saudi Arabia's Red Sea 'relief-valve' exports and pressures oil higher. (CNBC; NPR; The Washington Post; Honolulu Star-Advertiser, July 20-21, 2026.)",
    "10-DAY CEASEFIRE ON THE TABLE (July 20-21, 2026): Qatar and Pakistan, with Egyptian/Omani officials, proposed a 10-day US-Iran halt: suspend hostilities, revert to pre-July-9 positions, fully restore Hormuz shipping, and open a 'middle corridor' between Omani and Iranian waters. Iran confirmed receiving the proposals and reportedly submitted a parallel 10-day idea; the White House signaled it could keep striking for several more days first. (The New Arab; US News/Reuters; JPost; Axios, July 20-21, 2026.)",
    "10TH NIGHT DONE, 11TH ANTICIPATED (July 20-21, 2026): CENTCOM ran a 10th consecutive night (Sirik, Bandar Abbas, Qeshm Island, Shiraz, Isfahan) 'to further degrade Iranian military capabilities used to attack commercial shipping in the Strait of Hormuz'; analysts watched for an 11th night potentially extending to Iran's transmission grid, Pickaxe Mountain or Kharg. (Al Jazeera; PBS; CBS News, July 21, 2026.)",
    "GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED (July 21-22, 2026): No US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 US personnel unchanged. Reuters reporting that the strike waves also destroy capabilities the US would want gone before 'more complex operations' describes preparatory targeting, not an executed ground move. Brent ~$91/bbl. (Al Jazeera; TradingEconomics, July 21, 2026.)"
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "The corpus-predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg remains disconfirmed. Day 146 widened the war on three new axes — a nuclear-enrichment-site strike THREAT (Pickaxe Mountain), a second-chokepoint blockade by Iran's Houthi allies (Bab el-Mandeb), and a 10-day ceasefire proposal — yet every one of them stayed in the AIR/MARITIME/DIPLOMATIC register; no landing, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. Trump's Pickaxe threat and the standing Kharg threat remain declared intent, not execution (CONTESTED-UNRESOLVED — open-question: kharg-seizure-total-control-threat-june-2026).",
