  {
   "date": "2026-07-21",
   "headline": "DAY 145 — THE AIR WAR REACHES A NINTH AND TENTH STRAIGHT NIGHT AND STRIKES A SECOND NUCLEAR-ADJACENT SITE: US PROJECTILES HIT MULTIPLE LOCATIONS IN BUSHEHR (HOME TO IRAN'S ONLY CIVILIAN NUCLEAR PLANT). IRAN IMMOBILIZES A SECOND OIL TANKER AT HORMUZ AND SAYS IT INTERCEPTED FOUR VESSELS OVER THE WEEKEND; KUWAIT'S POWER-AND-WATER PLANT BURNS A THIRD DAY (CUMULATIVE 11 KILLED, 187 WOUNDED IN KUWAIT), BAHRAIN TAKES FRESH STRIKES (3 KILLED, 51 WOUNDED). BRENT PUSHES ABOVE $90; ONLY ~8 SHIPS CROSS HORMUZ. TRUMP: 'WE'RE GOING TO HIT THEM VERY HARD TONIGHT... AND TOMORROW' AND WON'T RULE OUT TAKING KHARG — BUT THE INSTRUMENT STAYS AIR/MARITIME, NOT A LANDING.",
   "theatre": "Iran / Strait of Hormuz",
