    "EIGHTH 'PUNISHMENT' NIGHT HITS A NUCLEAR PLANT, WIDENS INTO KHUZESTAN (July 18-19, 2026): CENTCOM's latest wave (beginning ~6pm ET Saturday, ~5.5 hours) was framed as punishment for the Jordan deaths and to 'further degrade Iran's ability to threaten commercial shipping.' It hit Sirik (Hormozgan), Qeshm Island and Shadegan (Khuzestan) and — a first for the war — an under-construction NUCLEAR power plant at Darkhovin; the IAEA confirmed no nuclear material was present and no radiological risk. (Al Jazeera; The National; CENTCOM, July 19, 2026.)",
