   "summary": "The Russia-Ukraine front held to its established pattern through July 19-20: Russian assault pressure stayed concentrated around Kostiantynivka and north/west of Pokrovsk in Donetsk Oblast, with no confirmed Russian territorial gains despite Moscow's July 3 claim to have seized Kostiantynivka outright. CNN (July 16) reported the capture claim is false and 'exposes the slow pace of Russia's bloody advance,' contradicted by videos, Ukrainian troop testimony and independent frontline mapping; Ukraine's 19th Army Corps commander Yuriy Madyar said his forces were pushing Russian infiltrators back out at a loss ratio of roughly 53 Russians to 3 Ukrainians. Zelensky again urged Putin to meet him in the town if it were truly under Moscow's control. Polling continues to show openness to a deal (~60% of Russians favor negotiations; ~66% of Ukrainians want the government to seek an end soon), but talks stay stalled. Russia still occupies ~20% of Ukraine. No US ground-deployment surge accompanied the theatre — consistent with the corpus pattern in which the war stresses US bandwidth without triggering a US ground commitment.",
