   "source": "NPR, 'The U.S. and Iran blow past red lines as they lurch back toward all-out war,' July 18, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'US launches seventh straight night of strikes on Iran,' July 17, 2026; Euronews, 'US forces strike Iran for seventh consecutive night,' July 18, 2026; Haaretz live blog, 'U.S. to send refueling aircraft to Israel amid Iran escalation fears,' July 18, 2026; The Times of Israel, 'US sending dozens of refueling aircraft to Israel ahead of potential attack on Iran,' July 17, 2026; Ynet; Israel Hayom, 'US to send dozens of aerial refueling tankers to Israel,' July 17, 2026; The War Zone (TWZ), 'Will USAF Tankers Getting The Boot From Israel's Biggest Airport Impact Combat Capabilities?'; CENTCOM public release, 'U.S. Forces Complete Another Round of Strikes Against Iran'; Mehr News; Wikipedia '2026 Iran war' and 'Timeline of the 2026 Iran war,' July 18, 2026.",
   "summary": "On Day 143 the US-Iran contest deepened on the AIR rung: the US ran an EIGHTH consecutive night of strikes and, for the first time, widened the campaign geographically into CENTRAL Iran and shifted MEANS — employing MANNED FIGHTER JETS (previously the campaign leaned on standoff cruise missiles and drones), reportedly pushing ~650 km inland to Yazd, where Al Jazeera reported five explosions and Iran's Mehr agency said the strikes fell 'outside the city limits' with no casualties there. CENTCOM described hitting 'multiple sites throughout central and southern Iran, including through the use of jet fighters,' beyond the coastal/Hormuz belt of the first seven nights, alongside surveillance sites, military-logistics and underground-weapons-storage and maritime targets. Iranian media reported at least 3 killed and 8 wounded across Hormozgan and additional deaths in bridge strikes near Bandar Khamir; the disabled Curacao-flagged tanker M/T Belma was struck AGAIN by two US missiles at Kharg Island (per Bushehr's deputy governor). Crucially, the US notified Israel it is SURGING DOZENS MORE AERIAL-REFUELING TANKERS there (the Pentagon already operates ~30 from Ben Gurion and a similar number from Ramon; ~10 more arriving Friday-Saturday, to be based at air-force fields after Ben Gurion congestion forced civilian-flight concerns) as President Trump WEIGHS A BROADER CAMPAIGN against Iran than the strikes conducted so far — a buildup to enable a LARGER AIR effort, not an amphibious/ground order. IRGC adviser Mohsen Rezaei (to Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei) repeated that if US attacks continue 'another two or three days' Iran will move 'from the phase of retaliation to the offensive phase,' warning 'no political border will be safe' — an ultimatum window analysts placed at ~July 19-20. Oil stayed ELEVATED at multi-week highs (Brent last reliably near ~$88 on the July 17 close, up ~14% on the week) with Hormuz functionally shut; a far higher ~$113/bbl figure circulated via a single unverified aggregator and could NOT be corroborated by mainstream market reporting (CNBC/Bloomberg/Al Jazeera). Talks stayed collapsed. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 US personnel unchanged. The deepening is a widening and intensification of the AIR/MARITIME campaign (jets, tankers, a re-strike on a tanker at Kharg) — NOT the corpus-predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg, which stays disconfirmed.",
