    "REFUELING-TANKER SURGE TO ISRAEL / 'BROADER CAMPAIGN' WEIGHED (July 17-18, 2026): The US told Israel it will send DOZENS MORE aerial-refueling tankers as Washington prepares for a possible EXPANSION of operations; the Pentagon already runs ~30 tankers from Ben Gurion and a similar number from Ramon, with ~10 more arriving Friday-Saturday to be based at air-force fields (Ben Gurion congestion threatened civilian flights). Reporting said Trump is weighing a broader campaign than the strikes so far. This is AIR-campaign enablement — not an amphibious/ground order. (Times of Israel; Ynet; Israel Hayom; Haaretz; TWZ, July 17-18, 2026.)",
    "BELMA RE-STRUCK AT KHARG; MARITIME INTERDICTION CONTINUES (July 17-18, 2026): The disabled tanker M/T Belma (first hit July 15 by a Hellfire into its smokestack) was struck AGAIN by two US missiles at Kharg Island per Bushehr's deputy governor — a maritime interdiction action against a vessel, NOT a landing on or seizure of the island. (Wikipedia '2026 Kharg Island attack'; NPR, July 2026.)",
    "IRGC 'FULL-SCALE OFFENSIVE' ULTIMATUM NEARS EXPIRY (July 18, 2026): Mohsen Rezaei warned Iran would move 'from the phase of retaliation to the offensive phase' if US attacks continue 'another two or three days,' vowing 'no political border will be safe' — an ultimatum window analysts placed at ~July 19-20. (Iranian state TV/IRIB via Al Jazeera; Haaretz, July 18, 2026.)",
    "OIL FIGURE CAUTION (July 18-19, 2026): Brent stayed elevated at multi-week highs (last reliable print ~$88 on the July 17 close, +~14% on the week), with Hormuz functionally shut. A ~$113/bbl figure circulating via a single unverified aggregator could not be corroborated by CNBC/Bloomberg/Al Jazeera and is NOT adopted here. (CNBC; Al Jazeera; TradingEconomics, July 15-18, 2026.)"
