   "prediction_impact": "Day 142 extends the sharpest test of the corpus's imminent-US-ground-seizure-of-Hormuz/Kharg thesis, and the verdict holds. A seventh night of US strikes leveled southern Iranian infrastructure (bridges, an airport, rail, power) and Iran widened its retaliation onto Kuwaiti utilities and US-backed Kurds in Iraq, yet the instruments on all sides stayed AIR, MISSILE and MARITIME — no US landing, Kharg assault, new amphibious order, or draft. Oil surging to ~$88 and Hormuz falling below 5% of pre-war transits show a chokepoint being strangled by blockade, air power and sanctions snapback, not seized by troops. Even an IRGC 'full-scale offensive operations' warning is framed as escalation within the air/missile register. The predicted mechanism — US ground forces seizing Hormuz/Kharg — remains disconfirmed even as US coercive control of the Strait deepens.",
