    "EXECUTION INDICATORS ALL ZERO (July 17-18, 2026): Despite a seventh straight night of strikes leveling southern Iranian infrastructure and Iran's widened retaliation onto Kuwaiti utilities and US-backed Kurds in Iraq, there were no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new amphibious-ready-group/MEU order, and no draft. ~50,000 US personnel in the CENTCOM AOR remained unchanged. (NPR; CNN; ABC News, July 17, 2026.)",
    "MARINES USED FOR BOARDINGS, NOT A LANDING (July 16-17, 2026): US Marines BOARDED the commercial vessel M/T Wen Yao to enforce the naval blockade, and a US fighter jet earlier disabled the Curacao-flagged tanker M/T Belma (a Hellfire missile into its smokestack) as it transited toward Kharg Island — visit-board-search-and-seizure and interdiction actions at sea, NOT an amphibious landing or seizure of Iranian territory. Reporting continued to note a Kharg ground takeover 'would require a significant number of ground troops' and that seizure plans stay 'continuously shelved' as too risky. (The Hill; NPR; CBS News; Task & Purpose, July 2026.)",
    "AMPHIBIOUS/MARINE POSTURE UNCHANGED (July 17-18, 2026): No landing, forcible-entry staging, or ground order accompanied the seventh night of strikes. The USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~2,200 Marines) and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~2,200-3,500 sailors/Marines) — the units repeatedly named as the toolkit for a Kharg operation, alongside ~1,000-1,200 82nd Airborne paratroopers — remained in the Arabian Sea/Indian Ocean in routine/contingency posture. Task & Purpose reiterated a Kharg seizure would need at least ~1,200 troops. (19FortyFive; Stars and Stripes; Task & Purpose, 2026.)",
    "NO DRAFT / MOBILIZATION SIGNAL (July 17-18, 2026): No Selective Service activation, stop-loss, Guard/Reserve call-up, or conscription language accompanied the escalation — even after an IRGC commander warned of 'full-scale offensive operations.' The only standing item remains the pre-existing FY2026 plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by December 2026 — not a draft activation. (Poynter; ABC News, 2026.)"
