   "source": "CNN, 'US expands strikes into northern Iran and disables ship trying to run blockade,' July 16, 2026; NPR, 'The U.S. fires a new wave of strikes on Iran and hits a tanker trying to skirt its blockade,' July 15, 2026; CBS News, 'U.S. launches another night of strikes as battle continues over Strait of Hormuz,' July 15-16, 2026; Britannica, '2026 Iran war' (Trump Fox News 'Guardian Angel of the Strait' remark; FM Araghchi 'GUARDIAN...FOREVER' retort); Bloomberg 'Latest Oil Market News for July 16'; CNBC; Al Jazeera; Kpler; en.wikipedia.org, '2026 Strait of Hormuz crisis,' July 15-16, 2026.",
   "summary": "On Day 141 the US-Iran contest over the Strait of Hormuz ran into a SIXTH consecutive day of exchanged fire, and Washington both WIDENED the campaign geographically and tightened the blockade — while the ground rung stayed empty. US CENTCOM EXPANDED its strikes into NORTHERN Iran (beyond the southern coastal/Hormuz belt it had concentrated on), hitting command centers and missile sites, as Iran again targeted US military bases in Gulf countries. Under the re-imposed blockade the US said it DISABLED an UNLADEN (empty) oil tanker that was HEADED FOR KHARG ISLAND and trying to avoid/skirt the blockade — a Kharg-ADJACENT maritime INTERDICTION, not a landing on the island. Trump told Fox News the US was 'going to keep the Strait, and we'll probably run it... We'll become the guardian of the Strait. Maybe we'll call it the \"Guardian Angel of the Strait.\" And we should be reimbursed for that' — reviving the 'guardian'/reimbursement framing days after reversing his 20% Hormuz 'toll.' Iran's FM Abbas Araghchi retorted that safe passage warranting compensation was fair but that 'Iran has always been the GUARDIAN of the Strait and will remain so FOREVER.' Oil held its elevated range without a fresh spike — Brent stayed below $85 (having settled ~$84.95 on July 15) and WTI above $80 — as Hormuz traffic ground back to, or below, the pre-MOU pace (only ~21 transits recorded Tuesday; the running toll reached ~56 confirmed shipping incidents and 17 seafarer deaths). The interim deal stayed in tatters with no progress toward a final settlement. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged. The US is asserting control of the Strait via blockade, air power and maritime interdiction (now reaching Kharg-BOUND shipping) — still NOT a ground landing; the predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed.",
   "details": [
    "SIXTH STRAIGHT DAY; US STRIKES EXPAND INTO NORTHERN IRAN (July 16, 2026): The US and Iran traded fire for a sixth consecutive day, with US strikes targeting Iranian command centers and missile sites — reporting noting the US EXPANDED its strike map into NORTHERN Iran, beyond the southern coastal/Hormuz belt struck in earlier rounds — as Iran targeted US military bases in Gulf countries. CENTCOM framed the campaign as degrading Iran's ability to attack commercial shipping in the Strait. It stayed on the air/naval rung; no ground forces entered Iran. (CNN; CBS News, July 16, 2026.)",
    "US DISABLES UNLADEN TANKER HEADED FOR KHARG ISLAND UNDER THE BLOCKADE (July 15-16, 2026): The US military said it disabled an unladen (empty) oil tanker that was headed for a port in Iran and trying to avoid the US blockade; CENTCOM said the vessel was steaming toward Kharg Island. This is Kharg-ADJACENT maritime INTERDICTION — the instrument the US has used throughout — not a landing on or seizure of the island. (NPR, July 15, 2026; CBS News; en.wikipedia.org, '2026 Strait of Hormuz crisis.')",
    "TRUMP: 'GUARDIAN ANGEL OF THE STRAIT'; ARAGHCHI: IRAN 'THE GUARDIAN... FOREVER' (mid-July 2026): Trump told Fox News the US was 'going to keep the Strait, and we'll probably run it. We'll become the guardian of the Strait. Maybe we'll call it the \"Guardian Angel of the Strait.\" And we should be reimbursed for that' — reasserting the 'guardian'/reimbursement framing days after he reversed his 20% Hormuz 'toll.' Iran's FM Abbas Araghchi replied that compensation for safe passage was fair but that 'Iran has always been the GUARDIAN of the Strait and will remain so FOREVER.' A rhetorical sovereignty contest over who governs the chokepoint, not a ground move. (Britannica, '2026 Iran war,' July 2026.)",
    "OIL HOLDS BELOW $85; HORMUZ TRAFFIC GRINDS BACK TO PRE-MOU PACE (July 15-16, 2026): Brent held its one-month-high range without a fresh spike — settling ~$84.95/bbl (+22c) on July 15 and closing below $85 — while WTI traded above $80 after adding more than 11% over three sessions. Analysts said Hormuz traffic was 'grinding to a halt,' back to or below the pre-MOU pace, keeping prices elevated. Still >15% above the late-February pre-war level, but far below the ~$126 April wartime peak and the $130+ a sustained US GROUND commitment would imply. (Bloomberg; CNBC; Al Jazeera, July 15-16, 2026.)",
    "SHIPPING TOLL REACHES ~56 INCIDENTS / 17 SEAFARER DEATHS; ~21 HORMUZ TRANSITS (July 14-16, 2026): Kpler recorded ~21 ships transiting the Strait of Hormuz on Tuesday — primarily crude, LPG, methanol and iron ore carriers — as three further attacks off Oman were verified, bringing the running war tally to ~56 confirmed shipping incidents and 17 seafarer fatalities. (Kpler via CBS News/NPR, July 15-16, 2026.)",
    "GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED (July 16-17, 2026): The sixth day of strikes, the widening into northern Iran, and the Kharg-bound tanker interdiction added NO US ground forces: no landing, port seizure, Kharg assault, new ARG/MEU order, or draft; ~50,000 US personnel in the CENTCOM AOR unchanged. The predicted US ground seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed. (CBS News; Stars and Stripes; Task & Purpose, July 2026.)"
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Day 141 extends the sharpest test of the corpus's imminent-US-ground-seizure-of-Hormuz/Kharg thesis, and the verdict holds: the US widened its air campaign into northern Iran and, under the re-imposed blockade, DISABLED a tanker HEADED FOR KHARG ISLAND — the closest the interdiction campaign has come to the island — yet still WITHOUT a ground landing, Kharg assault, new amphibious order, or draft. Stopping Kharg-BOUND shipping from the sea is a way to strangle the island's export function WITHOUT putting Marines ashore; combined with Trump's 'Guardian Angel of the Strait' framing, the US is asserting coercive control of the chokepoint through blockade, air power and maritime interdiction, not troops. The predicted mechanism — US ground forces seizing Hormuz/Kharg — remains disconfirmed even as US coercive control of the Strait deepens.",
