   "summary": "Status holds no_ground_troops on Day 140. The US intensified its coercion of the chokepoint — a fifth consecutive round of air strikes, the blockade's first interdictions (two commercial vessels 'redirected' within ~17 hours), and a US COMBAT FIRST: three 'Corsair' one-way attack sea drones striking the Bandar Abbas naval base. But every one of those instruments is stand-off, naval or unmanned — none is a ground landing. No US troops entered Iran; no Kharg landing or port seizure; no new amphibious-ready-group / MEU order; no draft, Selective Service activation or mobilization. ~50,000 US personnel in the CENTCOM AOR unchanged; the standing USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU stayed in routine/contingency posture. Kharg takeover plans remain 'continuously shelved' as too risky. The corpus-predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg stays disconfirmed — the introduction of attack sea drones is an escalation of maritime MEANS that, if anything, substitutes for a landing rather than presaging one.",
   "details": [
    "STATUS: no_ground_troops (Day 140, July 15, 2026). The most active US coercion of the chokepoint yet ran entirely on the air, naval and unmanned-maritime rungs — a fifth night of strikes, blockade interdictions, and a sea-drone strike on Bandar Abbas — with zero ground-execution indicators.",
