    "US RE-IMPOSES NAVAL BLOCKADE (July 14, 2026): US forces launched strikes against Iranian targets shortly before the US resumed its naval blockade of Iranian ports in and around the Strait of Hormuz at 4pm ET Tuesday; CENTCOM said 'more than 20 US Navy warships and hundreds of military aircraft' were operating in the region. The restart ends the ~27-day period in which the blockade had been lifted (since the June 17 MOU). It is a return of the US MARITIME-interdiction instrument, not a ground operation. (NPR; CBS News; CNBC, July 13-14, 2026.)",
    "TRUMP'S 20% TOLL — ANNOUNCED, THEN REVERSED (July 13-14, 2026): Trump said the US would charge a 20% toll/reimbursement on cargo passing through Hormuz in exchange for US protection, casting the US as the Strait's 'guardian' and saying beneficiary states (Saudi Arabia, UAE, Qatar, Bahrain, Kuwait) should compensate the US. He reversed the fee the same day — 'I don't think anybody should be able to charge a fee' — and pivoted to Gulf-state investment deals instead. (Al Jazeera; CBS News, July 14, 2026.)",
    "FOURTH NIGHT OF US STRIKES (July 14, 2026): US CENTCOM conducted a fourth consecutive night of strikes (begun ~4:45pm ET Monday and continuing Tuesday) to 'continue degrading Iranian capabilities used to attack commercial shipping,' hitting military targets across Iran including Bushehr, Chah Bahar, Jask, Konarak, Abu Musa and Bandar Abbas. (NPR; CBS News; CNN, July 13-14, 2026.)",
    "IRAN'S TANKER ATTACKS AND CASUALTIES (July 14, 2026): Early July 14 Iran attacked three tankers — the chemical tanker Stolt Magnesium (projectile NE of Qalhat) and the UAE-owned oil tankers Mombasa B and Al Bahyah (cruise missiles); the IRGC said it targeted 'offending supertankers' entering a 'mined route.' One Indian national was killed aboard Mombasa B; eight others (six Indians, two Ukrainians) were injured; three crew aboard Al Bahyah were declared missing. The GFS Galaxy's missing crewman (from Pune, India) was confirmed dead July 14, his body recovered by the Omani Navy. Iran also fired missiles/drones at US assets in Kuwait and Bahrain (Kuwait intercepted 33 drones, five cruise missiles, one ballistic missile). (en.wikipedia.org, '2026 Strait of Hormuz crisis,' accessed July 15, 2026; CBS News, July 14, 2026.)",
    "OIL — BRENT ABOVE $85, HIGHEST SINCE JUNE 15 (July 14, 2026): Brent's September contract reached ~$85.92/bbl as of 08:00 GMT July 14 (rising ~3.8% on the day after a ~9.6% gain the prior session) and traded above $86 — its highest since June 15, up ~19% from late-February pre-conflict levels; the week's gain topped 10%. The US Department of Energy said 8.5 million barrels passed through the Strait the previous day 'with military assistance.' Still war-risk repricing far below the $130+ a sustained US ground commitment would imply. (Al Jazeera, 'Oil hits 1-month high...,' July 14, 2026; TradingEconomics; CNBC, July 13-14, 2026.)",
