   "summary": "On Day 139 the US mounted its most active coercion of the chokepoint of the war, and it stayed maritime/air. On July 14 the US restarted its naval blockade of Iranian ports (CENTCOM: 20+ US Navy warships and hundreds of military aircraft operating in the region), ran a fourth consecutive night of strikes (Bushehr, Chah Bahar, Jask, Konarak, Abu Musa, Bandar Abbas), and Trump announced then reversed a 20% Hormuz 'toll,' casting the US as the Strait's 'guardian.' Iran hit three more tankers and salvoed Kuwait and Bahrain. Brent surged above $85 (highest since June 15). Yet every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; ~50,000 personnel unchanged; the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU held routine/contingency posture; Kharg takeover plans stay 'continuously shelved' as too risky. The predicted US GROUND seizure of Hormuz/Kharg remains disconfirmed — the war re-escalated toward US control of the Strait, but the mechanism is a naval blockade and air strikes, not a landing.",
