   "summary": "Across the non-Iran theatres July 13-14 was a continuation, not a break. RUSSIA-UKRAINE: peace talks stayed stalled with the Kremlin holding its precondition that Ukraine withdraw from all of Donbas before any resumption; Kostiantynivka stayed contested (Ukraine's 19th Army Corps reported pushing Russian infiltrators back at a lopsided loss ratio), and The Economist estimated Ukraine had netted ~16 sq km over the prior 30 days — no US ground surge. LATIN AMERICA: Cuba suffered its second full island-wide blackout in a week (its fourth of 2026), the grid crippled by a ~2,000 MW shortfall and fuel reserves down to ~40% of need amid the US fuel blockade and the end of Venezuelan oil shipments; Venezuela's constitutional crisis stayed unresolved under acting President Delcy Rodríguez, and the Maduro/Flores SDNY hearing stayed set for July 22. US-CHINA: the China-Russia 'Joint Sea-2026' naval exercise (July 6-13, near Qingdao) wound down after a July 6 PLA SLBM test in the South Pacific; the Trump-Xi tariff truce held. DPRK: no new July launch, with activity expected around the July 27 armistice anniversary. HORMUZ-DEPENDENT ASIA stayed under fuel-supply stress — Japan and South Korea drawing on strategic stockpiles, South Asia (Pakistan, Bangladesh, India) most exposed on LNG and LPG.",
