    "LATIN AMERICA — CUBA (July 6-13, 2026): Cuba suffered its second full nationwide blackout in a week — its fourth of 2026 — with a ~2,000 MW shortfall and the island producing only ~40% of the fuel it needs, the grid crippled by the US fuel blockade and the end of Venezuelan oil shipments after Maduro's January fall. (Al Jazeera; CBS News; Media Selangor, July 6-13, 2026.)",
