    "KHARG SEIZURE STILL SHELVED AS TOO RISKY (July 8-11, 2026): Plans to capture Kharg Island 'have been drawn up for months but continuously shelved because the operation was considered too risky,' and a takeover 'would require a significant number of ground troops'; the July 8 Kharg action was an air strike that spared the oil terminals, and CFR characterized the episode as Trump having 'walked back' the threat. No landing, port-seizure order, or Kharg amphibious tasking was reported. (Al Jazeera; NBC News; CFR, July 8-9, 2026.)",
    "FORCE POSTURE UNCHANGED (July 11-12, 2026): ~50,000 US personnel in the CENTCOM AOR and ~24 warships (carriers Abraham Lincoln and George H.W. Bush, 15 destroyers) per Stars and Stripes (July 1). The USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (2,200 Camp Pendleton Marines aboard Boxer and USS Portland; arrived ~June 30) and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~3,500 troops) remained in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture. No new July deployment, ARG/MEU landing order, or forcible-entry staging was reported. (Stars and Stripes, July 1; Times of San Diego; The Hill, June 30-July 5, 2026.)",
