   "summary": "The ground-invasion indicators stayed at zero through Day 135 even as the seizure RHETORIC hit its wartime peak. Trump's Truth Social post that the US 'will be taking Kharg Island, and other oil infrastructure points, and assume total control of their Oil and Gas Markets' is the most explicit oil-seizure threat of the war, and reporting flagged that seizing Kharg 'would all but assuredly require boots on the ground.' But the July 8 Kharg action was an AIR strike that deliberately spared oil terminals, and by July 10-11 US officials said Washington was 'deliberately striking and then pausing… to let diplomacy work' and 'letting diplomacy take the lead.' No landing or port seizure was ordered or executed, no new ARG/MEU landing order or draft followed, ~50,000 US personnel were unchanged, and the blockade stayed lifted (Day 23). The standing USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU remained in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture. The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg ground seizure stays disconfirmed and inverted — Kharg was struck only from the air, and it is Iran, not the US, that has used force at the chokepoint.",
   "details": [
