  {
   "date": "2026-07-10",
   "headline": "DAY 134 — BREACH-RETALIATION CYCLE GOES TWO-SIDED AND REGIONAL: IRAN RETALIATES ACROSS THE GULF (KUWAIT, QATAR, BAHRAIN AND JORDAN) FOR THE US STRIKES, THE US RUNS A SECOND-DAY WAVE OF ~90 TARGETS, AND TRUMP SAYS 'WE ATTACKED KHARG ISLAND' AND 'MAYBE WE'LL TAKE OVER KHARG ISLAND' — YET BY JULY 10 PAKISTAN AND QATAR ARE MAKING FRESH CONTACTS TO HALT THE STRIKES, IRAN HAS REPORTEDLY ASKED TO REOPEN A DEAL, AND THE EXCHANGE STILL HAS NOT LEFT THE AIR/MISSILE AND MARITIME RUNGS. On July 9 Iran's IRGC launched one-way attack drones and ballistic/cruise missiles at four US-partner states — a Patriot interceptor site in Kuwait, an early-warning system in Qatar, fuel tanks in Bahrain, and a US command-and-control node plus the Al-Azraq air base in Jordan (10 ballistic missiles) — the first multi-Gulf-state Iranian retaliation since June 28-29. Kuwait reported one person injured (stable) and intercepts of 3 ballistic missiles, 1 cruise missile and 10 drones with damage at several sites; Jordan shot down 8 missiles (debris fell, no casualties); Bahrain intercepted several. The US answered with a second straight day of strikes (~90 targets: missile/drone storage and coastal logistics), and at least 14 people were killed and dozens wounded in Iran. Trump said US forces had hit military facilities on Kharg Island 'last night' while deliberately sparing its oil infrastructure, claimed to have 'knocked out 28 boats,' and revived the seizure threat — 'maybe we'll take over Kharg Island… there's not a thing they can do about it' — while conceding doubt over whether the US had 'the stomach' for boots on the ground. CRITICALLY, THE KHARG ACTION WAS AN AIR STRIKE, NOT A LANDING: no US troops entered Iran, no Kharg assault or port seizure was ordered or executed, no new ARG/MEU order issued, and no draft; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 22). Brent, after settling +5.2% at $78.02 on July 8, eased back toward $77 on July 9. By July 10 Pakistan and Qatar were in fresh contact with Washington and Tehran to stop the strikes and restore the Islamabad MOU — which Pakistan said it still expected to hold — and Trump said Iran had called seeking a new deal, though he was unsure it was 'worthy.' Talks are paused, not terminated. Iran warned via PressTV it would close Hormuz and respond with overwhelming force to fresh attacks.",
   "summary": "The July 7 kinetic reopening broadened on July 9 from a US-Iran exchange into a regional one, but it widened horizontally (more targets, more states) rather than escalating vertically (up the rung to ground operations). Iran retaliated for the US strikes by hitting four US-partner states — Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain and Jordan — with drones and ballistic/cruise missiles, its first multi-Gulf-state salvo since June 28-29; regional air defenses intercepted most incoming fire, with Kuwait reporting a single stable injury and Jordan downing 8 missiles with only debris damage. The US ran a second straight day of strikes (~90 targets in missile/drone storage and coastal logistics), killing at least 14 in Iran, and President Trump said US forces had struck military sites on Kharg Island 'last night' while deliberately sparing its oil terminals, revived the takeover threat ('maybe we'll take over Kharg Island'), and simultaneously questioned whether the US had 'the stomach' for a ground deployment. Every US ground-execution indicator nonetheless stayed at zero: no troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure, no new amphibious/Marine order, no draft; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 22). Oil eased off the July 8 spike, with Brent slipping back toward $77 on July 9. By July 10 Pakistan and Qatar were making fresh contacts to halt the strikes and salvage the Islamabad MOU — which Pakistan publicly expected to survive — and Trump said Tehran had contacted the US seeking a new deal. The framework is rhetorically repudiated by the US president and materially breached, yet the blockade is still lifted, the MOU is not formally cancelled, and talks are paused rather than terminated. The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg ground seizure remains disconfirmed and inverted — even with Kharg struck from the air and a renewed takeover threat, it is Iran, not the US, using force at the chokepoint, and the US answered from the air.",
   "details": [
    "IRAN RETALIATES ACROSS THE GULF — KUWAIT, QATAR, BAHRAIN, JORDAN (July 9, 2026): Iran's IRGC launched one-way attack drones and ballistic/cruise missiles at a Patriot interceptor system in Kuwait, an early-warning system in Qatar, fuel tanks in Bahrain, and a US 'command-and-control center in West Asia' plus the Al-Azraq air base in Jordan (10 ballistic missiles), in retaliation for the US strikes — the first multi-Gulf-state Iranian retaliation since June 28-29. Kuwait's Defense Ministry said at least one person was injured (stable) and that 3 ballistic missiles, 1 cruise missile and 10 drones were intercepted, with damage caused at several sites during interception; Jordan intercepted and shot down 8 missiles (only debris fell, no casualties or property damage); Bahrain said it 'intercepted and destroyed several' Iranian aerial attacks. (NPR; The National; Al Jazeera; IranWire; RFE/RL, July 9, 2026.)",
    "US RUNS SECOND-DAY WAVE, ~90 TARGETS; ~14 IRANIANS KILLED (July 9, 2026): The US struck about 90 Iranian targets — missile and drone storage plus logistics sites along Iran's coastline — a second straight day of strikes 'to further degrade [Iran's] ability to threaten freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz.' At least 14 people were killed and dozens wounded in Iran following the second wave. (NBC News; Al Jazeera; CNN, July 9, 2026.)",
    "TRUMP: 'WE ATTACKED KHARG ISLAND'… 'MAYBE WE'LL TAKE OVER' (July 8-9, 2026): Trump said US forces hit military facilities on Kharg Island 'last night' while deliberately avoiding its oil infrastructure, claimed the US had 'knocked out 28 boats' (of 60+ IRGC small boats struck), and revived the seizure threat — 'maybe we'll take over Kharg Island, and we may take over Kharg Island… there's not a thing they can do about it' — his most explicit takeover rhetoric since June 11. He simultaneously questioned whether the US had 'the stomach' for boots on the ground. The action on Kharg was an AIR strike, not a ground assault or landing; no US targeting posture for a Kharg seizure was reported. (Al Jazeera; Washington Examiner, July 8, 2026.)",
    "MEDIATORS MOVE TO HALT STRIKES; IRAN SEEKS NEW DEAL (July 9-10, 2026): Pakistan and Qatar urged both sides to uphold the Islamabad MOU and, per Pakistani sources, made fresh contacts on July 10 to stop further strikes and return the parties to negotiations; Pakistan said it remained confident the MOU would hold. Trump said Iran had contacted the US seeking a new deal after the strikes resumed, though he was unsure Iran was 'worthy of making a deal.' Talks are paused, not terminated. (Al Jazeera; Pakistan Today; CNN, July 9-10, 2026.)",
    "OIL EASES OFF THE SPIKE (July 9, 2026): After Brent settled +5.2% at $78.02/bbl on July 8 (WTI +4.4% to $73.52) on the ceasefire-'over' declaration and 'additional strikes,' Brent fell back toward $77/bbl on July 9, snapping a two-day rally even as the second-day strikes landed. War-risk repricing, still far below the early-2026 wartime peaks above $110 and the $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. (Al Jazeera, 'Oil surges as US strikes Iran'; TradingEconomics, Brent crude, July 8-9, 2026.)",
    "GROUND RUNG STILL ZERO AT WIDER SCOPE (July 9-10, 2026): Despite the two-sided regional exchange and the renewed Kharg takeover threat, there were no US troops in Iran, no Kharg landing or port seizure ordered or executed, no new ARG/MEU landing order, and no draft; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 22). The exchange widened horizontally (four partner states hit, ~90 targets struck) rather than climbing to the ground rung. Iran warned via PressTV it would close Hormuz and respond with overwhelming force to fresh attacks. (NBC News; Al Jazeera, July 9-10, 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "Al Jazeera, 'US, Iran launch more attacks as mediators urge warring sides to uphold MoU,' July 9, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Trump says US may take over Kharg Island: Here's what you need to know,' July 8, 2026; NPR, 'Tehran targets Bahrain and Kuwait after U.S. strikes,' July 8, 2026; The National, 'Iran attacks Bahrain, Kuwait, Qatar and Jordan after US strikes,' July 9, 2026; IranWire, 'Iran Claims Missile, Drone Strikes On US Bases In Kuwait And Bahrain,' July 9, 2026; RFE/RL, 'Iran Targets Base Housing US Forces In Jordan,' July 9, 2026; NBC News, 'U.S., Iran exchange intense new attacks after Trump says ceasefire is over,' July 9, 2026; CNN, 'Live updates: US-Iran ceasefire crumbles as fresh strikes rock Middle East,' July 9, 2026; Pakistan Today, 'Mediators make fresh contacts with US, Iran to halt further military strikes,' July 10, 2026; Washington Examiner, 'Trump says US attacked Kharg Island and could take it over,' July 8, 2026; TradingEconomics/CNBC, Brent crude, July 8-9, 2026.",
