   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 134: STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops EVEN AS THE KHARG-SEIZURE QUESTION RE-ESCALATES. On July 8-9 President Trump said US forces 'attacked Kharg Island' and that 'maybe we'll take over Kharg Island… there's not a thing they can do about it' — his most explicit seizure rhetoric since June 11 — and Iran's retaliation widened the war regionally to Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain and Jordan. YET THE KHARG ACTION WAS AN AIR STRIKE, NOT A LANDING: oil terminals were deliberately spared, no amphibious/Marine landing or port-seizure order was issued, ~50,000 US personnel in-theatre are unchanged, the USS Boxer / 11th MEU and USS Tripoli / 31st MEU stayed in routine/contingency posture, and no draft signal appeared; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 22). Trump himself questioned whether the US had 'the stomach' for boots on the ground. The exchange widened HORIZONTALLY (four partner states hit, ~90 targets struck) rather than climbing VERTICALLY to the ground rung.",
   "summary": "The ground-invasion indicators are tracked separately because the imminent-US-ground-invasion / Kharg-seizure thesis is the corpus's most load-bearing prediction. July 8-9 produced the strongest surface signals in a month — an explicit presidential 'we attacked Kharg Island / maybe we'll take over Kharg Island' and a Kharg air strike — but the execution again stayed off the ground rung. No US troops entered Iran; no Kharg landing, port seizure, or forcible-entry staging was ordered or executed; no new amphibious/Marine order issued; oil infrastructure was deliberately spared; and no draft or mobilization signal appeared. In-theatre strength is broadly unchanged at ~50,000 US personnel and ~24 warships (carriers Abraham Lincoln and George H.W. Bush; 15 destroyers), with the Boxer and Tripoli ARGs in the Arabian Sea in routine posture. Trump's 'do we have the stomach for it' aside is itself a marker of the rhetoric-vs-execution gap. Iran's cross-Gulf retaliation (Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain, Jordan) shows the conflict widening in geography, not climbing in kind. Assessment: no_ground_troops holds; the predicted US ground seizure of Kharg/Hormuz remains disconfirmed and inverted.",
   "details": [
    "KHARG STRUCK FROM THE AIR, NOT SEIZED (July 8-9, 2026): Trump said US forces hit military facilities on Kharg Island 'last night' while deliberately sparing its oil infrastructure and claimed to have 'knocked out 28 boats.' No ground assault, amphibious landing, or port-seizure order accompanied the strike; no US assault posture against Kharg was reported. (Al Jazeera; Washington Examiner, July 8, 2026.)",
    "TAKEOVER RHETORIC REVIVED BUT HEDGED (July 8, 2026): 'Maybe we'll take over Kharg Island, and we may take over Kharg Island… there's not a thing they can do about it' — the most explicit seizure threat since June 11 — paired in the same remarks with Trump questioning whether the US had 'the stomach' for boots on the ground. Rhetoric, not a ground order. (Al Jazeera, 'Trump says US may take over Kharg Island,' July 8, 2026.)",
    "STANDING POSTURE UNCHANGED (July 9-10, 2026): ~50,000 US personnel and ~24 warships in the CENTCOM AOR (Stars and Stripes, July 1) — carriers USS Abraham Lincoln and USS George H.W. Bush and 15 destroyers — with USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture. The two days of strikes and Iran's four-state retaliation added no ground forces and triggered no new amphibious/Marine order. (Stars and Stripes, July 1, 2026; NBC News; Al Jazeera, July 9, 2026.)",
    "WAR WIDENS HORIZONTALLY, NOT VERTICALLY (July 9, 2026): Iran retaliated against Kuwait, Qatar, Bahrain and Jordan (mostly intercepted; one stable injury in Kuwait, debris-only damage in Jordan), and the US ran a ~90-target second-day wave — a broader, more regional exchange that still did not climb to a US ground operation. No draft, conscription, or domestic mobilization signal appeared. (NPR; The National; RFE/RL, July 9, 2026.)"
