   "date": "2026-07-09",
   "headline": "DAY 133 — CEASEFIRE DECLARED 'OVER' BY TRUMP, THEN WALKED BACK THE SAME DAY / US BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 21 — KINETIC CYCLE INTENSIFIED BUT STAYED AIR/MARITIME. ON JULY 8 US CENTCOM ANNOUNCED IT HAD 'STARTED CONDUCTING ADDITIONAL STRIKES AGAINST IRAN TO FURTHER DEGRADE THEIR ABILITY TO THREATEN FREEDOM OF NAVIGATION IN THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ' — A SECOND WAVE ON TOP OF THE JULY 7 PACKAGE, WITH REPORTING PUTTING THE CAMPAIGN AT 80+ TARGETS AND MORE THAN 60 IRGC SMALL BOATS STRUCK ALONGSIDE AIR-DEFENSE, COMMAND-AND-CONTROL, COASTAL-RADAR, SURVEILLANCE AND ANTI-SHIP-MISSILE SITES; EXPLOSIONS AND ACTIVATED AIR DEFENSES WERE REPORTED IN TWO LOCATIONS IN SOUTHERN IRAN. SPEAKING AT THE NATO ANKARA SUMMIT, TRUMP DECLARED THE CEASEFIRE/MOU 'OVER' ('A WASTE OF TIME'; IRAN 'VICIOUS, VIOLENT'; 'EVERY TIME THEY HIT US, WE HIT THEM 20') AND THREATENED TO BOMB AND BLOCKADE IRAN AGAIN — THEN, LATER THE SAME DAY, WALKED IT BACK: 'I DON'T THINK IT'S GOING TO START AGAIN,' SAYING THE EXCHANGE WOULD NOT LEAD TO LONG-TERM MILITARY ACTION. BRENT JUMPED 5.2% TO SETTLE AT $78.02/BBL (OFF SESSION HIGHS AFTER THE WALK-BACK). CRITICALLY, EVEN AT THE WAR'S SHARPEST RHETORICAL PEAK SINCE THE MOU, THE EXECUTION STAYED AIR AND MARITIME — NO US GROUND TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; THE BLOCKADE STAYS LIFTED (DAY 21). ON JULY 9 KHAMENEI WAS BURIED AT THE IMAM REZA SHRINE IN MASHHAD, HIS BIRTHPLACE, CLOSING THE SIX-DAY STATE FUNERAL; NEW SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI (NAMED MARCH 8-9) STILL HAD NOT APPEARED PUBLICLY.",
   "summary": "The breach-retaliation cycle that reopened July 7 intensified on July 8 without changing rungs. US CENTCOM said it had begun 'additional strikes against Iran to further degrade their ability to threaten freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz' — a second retaliatory wave layered on the July 7 package. Aggregating the reporting, the campaign hit 80+ targets, including more than 60 IRGC small boats used to harass shipping, plus air defenses, command-and-control, coastal-radar and surveillance sites, anti-ship-missile capabilities, and underground drone/missile storage; explosions and activated air defenses were reported at two locations in southern Iran. From the NATO summit in Ankara, President Trump declared the ceasefire and the Islamabad MOU 'over' — calling the agreement 'a waste of time,' Iran 'vicious, violent,' and warning 'every time they hit us, we hit them 20' with a threat to bomb and blockade Iran again — the sharpest US escalation rhetoric since the MOU. Hours later he walked it back, saying 'I don't think it's going to start again' and that the exchange would not lead to long-term military action; oil eased off its highs on the reversal, with Brent settling +5.2% at $78.02/bbl and WTI up in step. Despite the peak rhetoric, every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops entered Iran, no Kharg assault or port seizure was ordered or executed, no new amphibious/Marine landing order issued, and no draft or mobilization signal appeared. The US answer to Iranian maritime coercion remained an air/stand-off strike package plus the July 7 oil-waiver revocation — the structural inverse of a Kharg landing — and the naval blockade stayed lifted (Day 21). Separately, the six-day state funeral for slain Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei closed on July 9 with burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad, his birthplace and Iran's holiest city, after rites in Tehran, Qom, Najaf and Karbala. New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, designated in early March, still had not appeared publicly, keeping the who-governs-Iran question live.",
   "details": [
    "US CENTCOM LAUNCHES 'ADDITIONAL STRIKES' (July 8, 2026): CENTCOM announced its forces 'have started conducting additional strikes against Iran to further degrade their ability to threaten freedom of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz.' Aggregated reporting put the two-day campaign at 80+ targets and more than 60 IRGC small boats struck, plus air-defense, C2, coastal-radar, surveillance and anti-ship-missile sites and underground drone/missile storage; Iranian media reported activated air defenses and explosions at two locations in southern Iran. The wave was air/stand-off — no ground operation, Kharg assault, or troop movement was reported. (Al Jazeera live; NBC News; PBS NewsHour, July 8, 2026.)",
    "TRUMP DECLARES CEASEFIRE 'OVER' AT NATO SUMMIT (July 8, 2026): From the NATO Ankara summit Trump said he considered the truce and the MOU 'over' and 'a waste of time,' called Iran 'vicious, violent,' warned 'every time they hit us, we hit them 20,' and threatened to bomb and blockade Iran again — the sharpest US escalation rhetoric since the mid-June MOU. (Britannica '2026 Iran war'; CNN NATO summit live; NBC News, July 8, 2026.)",
    "SAME-DAY WALK-BACK (July 8, 2026): Later the same day Trump said the exchange of fire would not lead to long-term military action — 'I don't think it's going to start again' — cooling war-restart fears. The MOU is now rhetorically repudiated by the US president yet no formal cancellation, ground order, or mobilization followed. (Britannica; CNBC; NBC News, July 8, 2026.)",
    "OIL SETTLES $78 THEN EASES (July 8, 2026): Brent jumped 5.2% to settle at $78.02/bbl and WTI rose in step as fresh strikes and the ceasefire-'over' remark raised export-disruption fears; prices eased off session highs after Trump's walk-back. Still a war-risk repricing far below the early-2026 wartime peaks above $110 and the $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. (CNBC, 'Oil jumps as U.S. strikes on Iran,' July 8, 2026.)",
    "GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED AT PEAK RHETORIC (July 8-9, 2026): Even with the ceasefire declared 'over' and the largest strike wave of the post-MOU period, there were no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU landing order, and no draft; the blockade stayed lifted (Day 21). The response to Iranian maritime coercion was air/stand-off plus the oil-waiver revocation — not a ground move. (NBC News; PBS NewsHour, July 8, 2026.)",
    "KHAMENEI BURIED IN MASHHAD (July 9, 2026): Khamenei's remains, after farewell rites in Tehran (July 3-5), processions in Tehran and Qom (July 6-7) and rites at Najaf and Karbala in Iraq (July 8), were returned to Iran and buried at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad — his birthplace and Iran's holiest city — on July 9, closing the six-day state funeral. New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei (designated early March) still had not appeared publicly. (Wikipedia, 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei'; ABC News; RFE/RL, July 8-9, 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "Al Jazeera live, 'US forces carry out additional strikes on Iran,' July 8, 2026; NBC News, 'Live updates: U.S. military begins new strikes on Iran,' July 8, 2026; PBS NewsHour, 'U.S. launches new strikes on Iran after attacks on tankers in Strait of Hormuz,' July 7-8, 2026; CNBC, 'Oil jumps as U.S. strikes on Iran risk fragile Mideast truce' (Brent settled $78.02, +5.2%), July 8, 2026; The Washington Post, 'U.S. and Iran launch fresh strikes after attacks on commercial ships,' July 7-8, 2026; Britannica, '2026 Iran war' (Trump: truce 'over' July 7, walk-back July 8); Wikipedia, '2026 Iran war' / 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei' (burial Mashhad July 9); RFE/RL, July 8-9, 2026; NATO, '2026 Ankara Summit' overview and Russia Matters 'War Report Card, July 8, 2026'; USTR Section 301 hearing July 7, 2026.",
