  {
   "date": "2026-07-09",
   "headline": "DAY 133 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops AT THE WAR'S SHARPEST RHETORICAL PEAK. ON JULY 8 TRUMP DECLARED THE CEASEFIRE/MOU 'OVER' AND THREATENED TO BOMB AND BLOCKADE IRAN AGAIN, AND US CENTCOM RAN ITS LARGEST POST-MOU STRIKE WAVE ('ADDITIONAL STRIKES'; 80+ TARGETS, 60+ IRGC SMALL BOATS, AIR-DEFENSE/C2/RADAR/ANTI-SHIP-MISSILE SITES) — BUT THE EXECUTION STAYED AIR AND MARITIME. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR REMAINED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 21), AND THE PRESIDENT WALKED THE 'OVER' REMARK BACK THE SAME DAY ('I DON'T THINK IT'S GOING TO START AGAIN'). STANDING POSTURE UNCHANGED (STARS AND STRIPES, JULY 1): ~50,000 US TROOPS AND ~24 WARSHIPS (CARRIERS ABRAHAM LINCOLN AND GEORGE H.W. BUSH, 15 DESTROYERS), WITH USS BOXER ARG / 11TH MEU AND USS TRIPOLI ARG / 31ST MEU IN THE ARABIAN SEA IN ROUTINE/CONTINGENCY POSTURE — NO LANDING ORDERED OR EXECUTED. THE INVERSION HOLDS: IRAN, NOT THE US, IS USING FORCE AT THE CHOKEPOINT, AND THE US ANSWERED FROM THE AIR. BRENT'S MOVE TO $78/BBL IS WAR-RISK REPRICING, STILL FAR BELOW GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "The ground-invasion track held at no_ground_troops even as the war reached its sharpest rhetorical peak since the MOU. On July 8 Trump declared the ceasefire and the Islamabad MOU 'over,' threatened renewed bombing and blockade, and CENTCOM announced 'additional strikes' — a second retaliatory wave that, aggregated, hit 80+ targets and more than 60 IRGC small boats along with air-defense, command-and-control, coastal-radar, surveillance and anti-ship-missile sites. None of it crossed to the ground rung: no US troops entered Iran, no Kharg assault was ordered or executed, no new amphibious/Marine landing order was issued, and no draft or mobilization signal appeared. The president then walked the 'over' remark back the same day. The standing footprint was unchanged from the spring buildup — ~50,000 troops, two carriers, 15 destroyers, and two amphibious ready groups (Boxer/11th MEU and Tripoli/31st MEU) in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture — and the blockade stayed lifted (Day 21). The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg seizure stays disconfirmed-and-inverted: it is Iran using force at the chokepoint and the US answering from the air, with Brent's move to $78/bbl a war-risk repricing well below the $130+ a ground commitment would imply.",
   "details": [
    "NO GROUND EXECUTION AT PEAK RHETORIC (July 8-9): The ceasefire-'over' declaration and the largest post-MOU strike wave produced no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU landing order, and no draft. The response was an air/stand-off package, not a ground operation, and the 'over' remark was walked back the same day. (NBC News; PBS NewsHour; Britannica, July 8, 2026.)",
    "STRIKE PROFILE WAS AIR/MARITIME (July 8): The 'additional strikes' aggregated to 80+ targets and 60+ IRGC small boats plus air-defense, C2, coastal-radar, surveillance and anti-ship-missile sites and underground drone/missile storage — a maritime-domain deterrent package, the inverse of a Kharg landing. (Al Jazeera live; NBC News, July 8, 2026.)",
    "STANDING POSTURE UNCHANGED (Stars and Stripes, July 1 baseline): ~50,000 US troops and ~24 warships (carriers Abraham Lincoln and George H.W. Bush, 15 destroyers); USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (in-theatre since June 30) and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture; reported 82nd Airborne elements are part of the standing spring buildup, not a new July order.",
    "NO DRAFT SIGNAL: The peak rhetoric and second strike wave produced no mobilization order, Guard/Reserve call-up, brigade-scale activation, or conscription language. The only standing item remains the pre-existing FY2026 NDAA administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration by December 2026 — not a draft activation. (CNBC; Newsweek, 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "Al Jazeera live, 'US forces carry out additional strikes on Iran,' July 8, 2026; NBC News, 'Live updates: U.S. military begins new strikes on Iran,' July 8, 2026; PBS NewsHour, 'U.S. launches new strikes on Iran after attacks on tankers in Strait of Hormuz,' July 7-8, 2026; CNBC, 'Oil jumps as U.S. strikes on Iran risk fragile Mideast truce' (Brent settled $78.02, +5.2%), July 8, 2026; The Washington Post, 'U.S. and Iran launch fresh strikes after attacks on commercial ships,' July 7-8, 2026; Britannica, '2026 Iran war' (Trump: truce 'over' July 7, walk-back July 8); Wikipedia, '2026 Iran war' / 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei' (burial Mashhad July 9); RFE/RL, July 8-9, 2026; NATO, '2026 Ankara Summit' overview and Russia Matters 'War Report Card, July 8, 2026'; USTR Section 301 hearing July 7, 2026.",
