   "tag": "Ground Invasion Tracker",
   "theatre": null,
   "prediction_impact": "The most rigorous single-day test yet of the imminent-ground-invasion thesis, and it holds negative: at the war's sharpest rhetorical peak — a presidential 'the ceasefire is over' plus the largest post-MOU strike wave — the US still did not put troops in Iran, seize Kharg, order a landing, or begin a draft, and the blockade stayed lifted (Day 21). If a US ground invasion were imminent, this is the moment it would show in force posture; instead the escalation stayed air/maritime and the president walked the rhetoric back within hours. The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg seizure remains disconfirmed and inverted."
