  {
   "date": "2026-07-08",
   "headline": "DAY 132 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops DESPITE THE KINETIC CYCLE RESUMING. THE FIVE-DAY OFF-THE-KINETIC STREAK BROKE ON JULY 7 (IRAN ATTACKED THREE TANKERS NEAR HORMUZ; US CENTCOM ANSWERED WITH ITS LARGEST 'POWERFUL STRIKES' PACKAGE AND OFAC REVOKED IRAN'S OIL WAIVER), BUT THE EXCHANGE STAYED ON THE AIR/MISSILE AND MARITIME RUNGS. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR REMAINED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 20). THE US RESPONSE TO IRANIAN MARITIME COERCION WAS AN AIR-STRIKE PACKAGE ON AIR-DEFENSE, COASTAL, MISSILE, DRONE AND PORT SITES NEAR BANDAR ABBAS/QESHM/SIRIK — THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF A KHARG LANDING. NO NEW TROOP MOVEMENTS, GROUND-OPERATION AUTHORIZATIONS, PENTAGON GROUND STATEMENTS OR DRAFT SIGNALS ACCOMPANIED THE STRIKES. STANDING IN-THEATRE POSTURE UNCHANGED (STARS AND STRIPES, JULY 1): ~50,000 US TROOPS AND ~24 WARSHIPS (CARRIERS ABRAHAM LINCOLN AND GEORGE H.W. BUSH, 15 DESTROYERS), WITH USS BOXER ARG / 11TH MEU (IN-THEATRE SINCE JUNE 30) AND USS TRIPOLI ARG / 31ST MEU IN THE ARABIAN SEA IN ROUTINE/CONTINGENCY POSTURE — NO LANDING ORDERED OR EXECUTED. IT IS IRAN, NOT THE US, USING FORCE TO ASSERT CONTROL OVER HORMUZ TRANSIT — THE INVERSE OF THE PREDICTED US SEIZURE. BRENT'S SPIKE TO ~$76/BBL IS WAR-RISK REPRICING, STILL FAR BELOW GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "The ground-invasion track held at no_ground_troops even as the war's kinetic register reopened on July 7. Iran's IRGC attacked three tankers near the Strait of Hormuz, US CENTCOM launched what it called its largest retaliatory strike package to date, and the Treasury revoked Iran's oil-sales waiver — but the entire exchange stayed on the air/missile and maritime rungs. No US ground troops entered Iran, no Kharg assault was ordered or executed, no new amphibious/Marine landing order was issued, and no draft or mobilization signal appeared. The US answer to Iranian maritime coercion was an air-strike package against air-defense, coastal-surveillance, SAM, anti-ship cruise-missile, drone-launch and port targets near Bandar Abbas, Qeshm Island, Bandar Khamir and Sirik — the structural inverse of a landing to seize Iran's oil-export hub. The standing footprint was unchanged from the spring buildup: ~50,000 troops, two carriers, 15 destroyers, and two amphibious ready groups (Boxer/11th MEU and Tripoli/31st MEU) in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture; reported 82nd Airborne elements in-region remain part of that standing posture, not a new July order. The blockade stayed lifted (Day 20). The predicted US Hormuz/Kharg seizure stays disconfirmed-and-inverted: it is Iran using force to assert transit control, and Brent's spike to ~$76/bbl is war-risk repricing well below the $130+ a ground commitment would imply.",
   "details": [
    "NO GROUND EXECUTION DESPITE ESCALATION (July 7-8): The resumed breach-retaliation cycle produced no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU landing order, and no draft. The US response was an air/stand-off strike package, not a ground operation. (CBS News; NBC News; CNBC, July 7, 2026.)",
    "CENTCOM STRIKE PROFILE WAS AIR/MARITIME (July 7): Targets were air defenses, coastal-surveillance/radar, SAM, anti-ship cruise-missile, drone-launch and port sites near Bandar Abbas, Qeshm Island, Bandar Khamir and Sirik — a maritime-domain deterrent package, the inverse of a Kharg landing. (NBC News; The Hill, July 7, 2026.)",
    "STANDING POSTURE UNCHANGED (Stars and Stripes, July 1 baseline): ~50,000 US troops and ~24 warships (carriers Abraham Lincoln and George H.W. Bush, 15 destroyers); USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (in-theatre since June 30) and USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture; reported 82nd Airborne elements are part of the standing spring buildup, not a new July order.",
    "INVERSION SHARPENS: Iran, not the US, used force to assert control over Hormuz transit ('designated routes'), and the US answered from the air and with an oil-waiver revocation — the opposite of the predicted US seizure of Kharg/Iranian oil. (Al Jazeera; CBS News, July 7, 2026.)"
