  {
   "date": "2026-07-07",
   "headline": "DAY 131 — CEASEFIRE DAY 91 / US BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 19 — FUNERAL RITES MOVE TO QOM: AFTER THE JULY 6 TEHRAN PROCESSION (TENS OF MILLIONS), THE CORTEGE FOR SLAIN SUPREME LEADER AYATOLLAH ALI KHAMENEI REACHED QOM ON JULY 7 FOR PRAYERS AT THE JAMKARAN MOSQUE AND FATIMA MASOUMEH SHRINE, AHEAD OF NAJAF/KARBALA (JULY 8) AND BURIAL AT THE IMAM REZA SHRINE IN MASHHAD (JULY 9). NEW SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI (NAMED MARCH 9) STILL HAD NOT APPEARED PUBLICLY — REPORTING NOW ATTRIBUTES HIS ABSENCE BOTH TO AN ISRAELI ASSASSINATION THREAT AND TO INJURIES FROM THE FEB 28 STRIKE (US OFFICIALS EARLIER SAID HE WAS 'WOUNDED AND LIKELY DISFIGURED'), KEEPING THE WHO-RUNS-IRAN QUESTION LIVE. US-IRAN TALKS REMAINED PAUSED FOR THE FUNERAL WEEK (TO RESUME 'AT THE EARLIEST POSSIBLE TIME' PER QATAR). BRENT HELD NEAR ITS PRE-WAR ~$72/BBL; HORMUZ FLOWS ABOVE 10M BPD; NO NEW STRIKES OR SHIPPING INCIDENTS REPORTED. THE GROUND RUNG STAYED UNCHANGED AND DE-ESCALATORY — NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 19).",
   "summary": "The Iran war ran a fifth straight day off the kinetic register, on the ceremonial and diplomatic track. Following the July 6 main Tehran procession — which Tehran's mayor had projected at up to 20 million and which unfolded as one of the largest gatherings in the city's history — the funeral cortege for Ayatollah Ali Khamenei moved on July 7 to Qom, with prayers at the Jamkaran mosque and the Fatima Masoumeh shrine. The rites are due to reach Najaf and Karbala in Iraq on July 8 (an official reception with Iraq's prime minister at the Imam Ali shrine) and conclude with burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad — Khamenei's birthplace — on July 9. The newly named Supreme Leader, Mojtaba Khamenei (designated March 9), had still not appeared publicly; reporting now ties his months-long absence both to an Israeli threat to assassinate Iran's new leader and to injuries sustained in the Feb 28 decapitation strike (US officials in March had said he was 'wounded and likely disfigured,' and later reports described severe facial and leg injuries) — leaving the succession/who-runs-Iran question open. US-Iran talks stayed paused for the funeral week; Qatar said the earlier Doha round made 'positive progress' with no breakthrough and that further discussions would be scheduled 'at the earliest possible time' after the rites. Oil markets held Brent near the pre-war ~$72/bbl, with Saudi exports ~90% of the pre-war baseline, UAE exports above 3.9M bpd, and total Hormuz flows above 10M bpd. The Hormuz-governance dispute stayed unresolved — Iran maintaining mid-August 'service fees' the US rejects, and the UK and France backing an Oman-led freedom-of-navigation effort. The ground-invasion rung stayed unchanged and de-escalatory: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; the naval blockade stays lifted (Day 19). No new strikes or shipping incidents were reported.",
   "details": [
    "FUNERAL RITES MOVE TO QOM (July 7, 2026): After the July 6 main Tehran procession (Imam Hossein Square to Azadi Square, projected up to 20 million mourners), the cortege for Ayatollah Ali Khamenei reached Qom on July 7 for prayers at the Jamkaran mosque and the Fatima Masoumeh shrine. The six-day schedule continues to Najaf and Karbala, Iraq (July 8, Imam Ali shrine, reception with Iraq's PM) and burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad on July 9. (CNN/Al Jazeera funeral coverage, July 3-6, 2026; Wikipedia, 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei,' July 2026.)",
    "SUCCESSION QUESTION STAYS LIVE — NEW SUPREME LEADER STILL ABSENT (July 6-7, 2026): New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, named to succeed his father on March 9, had still not appeared publicly. Reporting attributed his absence both to security concerns after an Israeli threat to assassinate Iran's new leader and to injuries from the Feb 28 opening strike — Defense Secretary Hegseth said in March he was 'wounded and likely disfigured,' and later reports described severe facial and leg injuries (possible loss of a leg). Three of Khamenei's other sons had prayed at the coffin on July 5; the designated successor did not appear. (CNBC; TIME; US News; The Tribune, July 5, 2026.)",
    "US-IRAN TALKS REMAIN PAUSED FOR FUNERAL WEEK (July 6-7, 2026): The indirect US-Iran track, mediated by Qatar and Pakistan, stayed paused for the funeral; Qatar said the earlier Doha round made 'positive progress' with no breakthrough and that further discussions would be scheduled 'at the earliest possible time' after the rites. Core disputes remained open — the US rejects any Iranian-led Hormuz toll mechanism, no frozen funds have moved, and the IAEA-access dispute over the US-bombed Fordow/Natanz/Isfahan sites is unresolved (Speaker Ghalibaf again denied access to the bombed sites). (Al Jazeera; CBS News; CNN, July 1-6, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ / OIL — DISPUTE UNRESOLVED, PRICES NEAR PRE-WAR (July 6-7, 2026): Iran maintained it would charge transit 'service fees' once the 60-day toll-free window ends around mid-August (with 'special treatment' for 'friendly' nations), a mechanism the US rejects, while the UK and France pledged to help Oman keep navigation free. Brent held near the pre-war ~$72/bbl after OPEC+ agreed July 5 to raise August output by 188,000 bpd; Saudi crude exports ran ~90% of the pre-war baseline, UAE exports topped 3.9M bpd, and total Hormuz flows stayed above 10M bpd. No new strikes or shipping incidents were reported July 6-7. (TradingEconomics/CNBC; RFE/RL; CBS News, July 1-6, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ-AFFECTED ECONOMIES (early July 2026): The war's supply shock kept straining import-dependent economies even as flows recovered: Slovenia became the first EU country to impose fuel rationing (50L/day private), Bangladesh rationed fuel and shortened university terms, India managed an LPG squeeze (spring arrivals down 40%+) while lifting record discounted Russian crude, and Japan and South Korea — ranked most exposed by petrochemical dependence — kept up non-Gulf sourcing (Seoul's energy minister said it faced no supply problem for over a year). (Zero Carbon Analytics; Oxford Energy; Reuters, July 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "CNN/Al Jazeera funeral coverage, July 3-6, 2026; Wikipedia, 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei,' July 2026; CNBC; TIME; US News, 'Iran's new supreme leader absent from funeral,' July 5, 2026; CBS News live, July 4-6, 2026; TradingEconomics, Brent crude, July 3, 2026; RFE/RL, Hormuz service-fees dispute, July 2026; Zero Carbon Analytics / Oxford Energy, Hormuz-affected economies, July 2026.",
