   "headline": "DAY 131 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. JULY 6-7 RAN OFF THE KINETIC TRACK — THE QOM LEG OF KHAMENEI'S SIX-DAY STATE FUNERAL AND A US-IRAN NEGOTIATION STILL PAUSED FOR THE FUNERAL WEEK. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 19). NO NEW TROOP MOVEMENTS, GROUND-OPERATION AUTHORIZATIONS, PENTAGON GROUND STATEMENTS OR DRAFT SIGNALS. STANDING IN-THEATRE POSTURE (STARS AND STRIPES, JULY 1): ~50,000 US TROOPS AND ~24 WARSHIPS (CARRIERS ABRAHAM LINCOLN AND GEORGE H.W. BUSH, 15 DESTROYERS), WITH USS BOXER ARG / 11TH MEU (IN-THEATRE SINCE JUNE 30) AND USS TRIPOLI ARG / 31ST MEU IN THE ARABIAN SEA IN ROUTINE/CONTINGENCY POSTURE — NO LANDING ORDERED OR EXECUTED. IRAN, NOT THE US, IS ASSERTING COERCIVE CONTROL OVER THE REOPENING STRAIT (MID-AUGUST FEES) — THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF THE PREDICTED US SEIZURE. BRENT NEAR PRE-WAR ~$72/BBL — THE INVERSE OF GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "On July 7 (Day 131) the ground-invasion track stayed at no_ground_troops and off the kinetic register entirely. July 6-7 ran on ceremony and diplomacy — the Qom leg of Khamenei's six-day state funeral (after the July 6 main Tehran procession) and a US-Iran negotiation still paused for the funeral week. No new troop movements, ground-operation authorizations, Pentagon ground statements, draft signals, strikes or shipping incidents were reported. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft — and the naval blockade stayed lifted (Day 19). The standing in-theatre footprint (Stars and Stripes, July 1) is ~50,000 troops and ~24 warships (carriers Abraham Lincoln and George H.W. Bush, 15 destroyers), with the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~2,200-4,000 Marines, in-theatre since June 30) and the USS Tripoli (LHA-7) ARG / 31st MEU (~2,000-3,500 Marines) in the Arabian Sea in routine/contingency posture — no landing ordered or executed. Reported 82nd Airborne elements and a division command in the region remain part of the standing spring buildup, not a new July order. Iran, not the US, is asserting coercive control over the reopening Strait (mid-August 'service fees') — the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure — and Brent near pre-war ~$72/bbl is the inverse of ground-commitment pricing.",
   "details": [
    "GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATORS ALL ZERO (July 6-7, 2026): No US troops in Iran; no Kharg ground assault or port-seizure order; no third ARG or new MEU surge ordered; no Selective Service or draft activation; blockade still lifted (Day 19). The period's US activity was diplomatic (funeral-week talks pause) and the day's dominant event was ceremonial (the Qom leg of Khamenei's funeral). (CBS News live; CNN, July 4-6, 2026.)",
    "STANDING POSTURE UNCHANGED (per Stars and Stripes, July 1, 2026): ~50,000 US troops and at least 24 warships in the CENTCOM AOR — carriers USS Abraham Lincoln and USS George H.W. Bush and 15 destroyers — with the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~2,200-4,000 Marines; USS Portland, USS Comstock; in-theatre since June 30) and the USS Tripoli (LHA-7) ARG / 31st MEU (~2,000-3,500 Marines) in the Arabian Sea. Reported 82nd Airborne elements and a division-level command in-region are part of the standing spring 2026 buildup (the largest since the 2003 Iraq invasion), not a new July movement. All in routine/contingency posture; no forcible-entry staging, no landing ordered or executed. (Stars and Stripes, 'Another amphibious assault ship joins US naval buildup amid Iran talks,' July 1, 2026.)",
    "KHARG ISLAND — SEIZURE PATHWAY REMAINS SUPERSEDED (July 6-7, 2026): No US targeting of or assault posture against Kharg was reported; the only Kharg-related reporting was oil-export tracking (Iranian loadings resuming from Kharg's Azarpad Jetty since the June 17 MOU). Kharg is still described as an option the administration has weighed, but no new Kharg action occurred and the reopening is proceeding by negotiation; Iran continued fortifying the island's defenses (a defensive, not offensive, indicator). (United Against Nuclear Iran, June 22, 2026; CNN, 'Iran building up defenses of Kharg Island,' March 25, 2026.)",
    "NO DRAFT SIGNAL (July 6-7, 2026): The funeral and the funeral-week talks pause produced no mobilization order, Guard/Reserve call-up, brigade-scale activation or conscription language. The only standing item is the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by December 2026 (an FY2026 NDAA change predating the war) — not a draft activation; reinstatement would require an act of Congress, and fact-checkers continue to rate reinstatement claims false. (CNBC; Newsweek, 2026.)"
   ],
