   "headline": "RUSSIA-UKRAINE — JULY 6-7: UKRAINE STRIKES OMSK — RUSSIA'S LARGEST REFINERY, ~2,500-3,000 KM AWAY, THE DEEPEST STRIKE OF THE WAR (ALSO YAROSLAVL/SLAVNEFT-YANOS AND UST-LUGA). RUSSIA ANSWERED WITH A MASS OVERNIGHT BARRAGE ON KYIV (351 DRONES + 68 MISSILES) THAT KILLED ~22 AND INJURED ~90 NATIONWIDE. TRUMP HELD A ~90-MIN CALL WITH PUTIN ('BUSINESSLIKE AND VERY CONSTRUCTIVE') AND SPOKE WITH ZELENSKY AHEAD OF THE NATO SUMMIT IN ANKARA (JULY 7-8), WHERE HE IS SET TO MEET ZELENSKY AND GERMANY IS FINANCING TWO PATRIOT SYSTEMS. KOSTIANTYNIVKA STAYS CONTESTED — RUSSIA PROPOSED A LOCAL CEASEFIRE (UKRAINE REJECTED IT), AND ISW PUTS RUSSIAN PRESENCE AT ~37% OF THE CITY (~4.3% OF LYMAN), CALLING PUTIN'S 96% CLAIM 'GREATLY EXAGGERATED.' RUSSIA HOLDS ~20% WITH NO CONFIRMED NET CHANGE. NO US GROUND-DEPLOYMENT SURGE.",
   "summary": "The Russia-Ukraine war stayed on its established July track — a deep-strike energy war, mass Russian barrages on cities, contested Donbas ground claims, and stalled diplomacy — while high-level contacts picked up ahead of a NATO summit. On July 6 Ukrainian long-range drones struck the Omsk refinery in Siberia — Russia's largest, some 2,500-3,000 km from Ukraine — described as the deepest strike into Russia of the full-scale war and, per Ukraine's General Staff, the last of Russia's eleven largest gasoline-producing refineries to be hit; the same wave hit the Slavneft-Yanos refinery at Yaroslavl and Novatek's Ust-Luga Baltic complex. Overnight into July 6 Russia launched a mass barrage — about 351 drones and 68 missiles, mainly at Kyiv (all 29 ballistic missiles reportedly striking targets) — that Zelensky said killed about 22 and injured roughly 90 nationwide (15 killed and 58 injured in Kyiv city, plus 8 killed in Kyiv region), framed by Moscow as retaliation for Ukraine's refinery campaign. Over the weekend Trump held a roughly 90-minute call with Putin (the Kremlin called it 'businesslike and very constructive') and separately spoke with Zelensky, who said 'there is a real prospect to put an end to this war' and agreed to continue talks at the NATO summit in Ankara (July 7-8), where Trump was set to meet him; Germany signalled it would finance two Patriot systems for Ukraine amid a PAC-3 interceptor shortage worsened by Middle East demand. On the ground, Kostiantynivka stayed contested — Russia proposed a local ceasefire (paired with a body handover) that Ukraine rejected, and ISW put Russian presence at about 37% of the city and 4.3% of Lyman, calling Putin's claim of 96% control 'greatly exaggerated.' Russia holds about 20% of Ukraine with no confirmed net change, and there was no US ground-deployment surge.",
   "details": [
    "OMSK — DEEPEST STRIKE OF THE WAR (July 6, 2026): Ukrainian long-range drones struck the Omsk refinery, Russia's largest (~8.4M t/yr ELOU-AVT-11 unit), some 2,500-3,000 km from Ukraine — described as the deepest strike into Russia of the full-scale war and, per Ukraine's Special Operations Forces, the last of Russia's eleven biggest gasoline-producing refineries to be targeted. The same wave hit the Slavneft-Yanos refinery at Yaroslavl (~700 km) and Novatek's Ust-Luga Baltic complex. Ukraine has struck Russian refineries nearly 200 times in H1 2026. (United24; Moscow Times; Ukrainska Pravda; Euronews, July 6, 2026.)",
    "RUSSIA'S MASS BARRAGE ON KYIV (overnight into July 6, 2026): Russia launched ~351 drones and 68 missiles, concentrated on Kyiv (all 29 ballistic missiles reportedly hit their targets); Zelensky's evening address cited ~22 killed and ~90 injured nationwide, with 15 killed and 58 injured in Kyiv city and 8 killed in Kyiv region. Podilskyi district was hit hardest; residential high-rises were struck. Moscow framed it as retaliation for Ukraine's long-range strikes. (NPR; NBC News; CNN; Ukrinform, July 6, 2026.)",
    "TRUMP-PUTIN AND TRUMP-ZELENSKY CALLS; NATO SUMMIT IN ANKARA (July 4-7, 2026): Trump held a ~90-minute call with Putin (Kremlin: 'businesslike and very constructive'; Trump offered to help find a solution) and separately spoke with Zelensky, who said there was 'a real prospect to put an end to this war' and agreed to continue talks at the NATO summit of 32 heads of state in Ankara (July 7-8), where Trump was scheduled to meet him. The core impasse held — Russia insists on full control of Donbas; Ukraine rejects it. (NBC News; CNBC; NPR; The Hill, July 4-6, 2026.)",
    "PATRIOTS / AIR DEFENSE (July 6-7, 2026): Under Trump's arrangement (US supplies systems, NATO nations pay), Germany signalled willingness to finance two Patriot systems for Ukraine, with a 100-interceptor coalition schedule and a Germany-Ukraine barter deal pending into the summit; German Defense Minister Pistorius said Germany had no remaining launcher capacity. A PAC-3 MSE interceptor shortage — worsened by Middle East demand (Israel, Saudi, UAE, Qatar) — constrains supply as Ukraine leans on Patriots for ballistic intercepts. (TWZ; Defence Ukraine; NPR, July 6-7, 2026.)",
    "KOSTIANTYNIVKA STAYS CONTESTED (July 4-6, 2026): Russia proposed a local ceasefire in Kostiantynivka paired with a handover of bodies; Russia said Ukraine rejected it. ISW mapping put Russian presence at ~37% of the city and only ~4.3% of Lyman, calling Putin's claim of 96% control of Kostiantynivka 'greatly exaggerated' and characterizing gains as small-group infiltration (~50 m/day) rather than consolidated control. Russia holds ~20% of Ukraine with no confirmed net change. (Ukrainska Pravda; Al Jazeera; ISW/Russia Matters; Euromaidan Press, July 4-5, 2026.)"
   ],
