   "prediction_impact": "The Russia-Ukraine theatre stays untested against Predictive History's framing: the war is a mutual deep-strike/attrition contest (Ukraine's deepest-ever strike on Omsk; Russia's mass barrage on Kyiv; Kostiantynivka control disputed with only ~37% Russian presence), diplomacy is stirring but stalled on Russia's maximalist Donbas terms even amid Trump-Putin/Zelensky calls and the Ankara NATO summit, and there is no US ground-deployment surge — the US role stays materiel (Patriots via NATO financing), not manpower. The contested Kostiantynivka claim is tracked as an open question (kostiantynivka-control-contested-july-2026).",
   "alternate_readings": [
