   "headline": "OTHER THEATRES — JULY 6-7: (CUBA) AN ISLAND-WIDE BLACKOUT TOOK THE ENTIRE NATIONAL GRID OFFLINE JULY 6 AS THE US OIL BLOCKADE AND THE CUTOFF OF VENEZUELAN CRUDE DEEPEN THE ENERGY CRISIS (20-22 HR DAILY CUTS). (VENEZUELA) ACTING PRESIDENT DELCY RODRÍGUEZ ALLEGED DESTABILIZATION ATTEMPTS DURING THE POST-EARTHQUAKE EMERGENCY AND FACES A DISPUTE THAT HER 180-DAY INTERIM MANDATE HAS LAPSED; MADURO'S SDNY HEARING STAYS SET FOR JULY 22. (US-CHINA) USTR HELD JULY 7 HEARINGS ON PROPOSED SECTION 301 FORCED-LABOR TARIFFS (60-COUNTRY PROBE, JULY 6 COMMENT DEADLINE); THE SECTION 122 10% TARIFF EXPIRES ~JULY 24. (DPRK) NO NEW TEST AFTER THE JULY 4 KANG KON EVENT. NO US GROUND-FORCE MOVES TIED TO ANY OF THESE.",
   "summary": "Secondary theatres moved incrementally. In Cuba, an island-wide blackout took the entire national grid offline on July 6, deepening an energy emergency driven by the US de facto oil blockade and the cutoff of Venezuelan crude after the US intervention, with some areas seeing 20-22 hours of daily power cuts. In Venezuela, acting President Delcy Rodríguez alleged on July 6 that opponents tried to 'destabilize' the country during the late-June earthquake emergency (twin M7.2/M7.5 quakes in the Yaracuy/La Guaira area killed 2,295+; she announced a $200M 'Venezuela Reborn Fund'), and faces a live dispute that her 180-day interim mandate has now exceeded the constitutional limit; Nicolás Maduro and Cilia Flores's next SDNY hearing remains set for July 22, and Colombia's formal transition to Trump-endorsed president-elect Abelardo de la Espriella (handover Aug 7) continued. On US-China trade, USTR held July 7 hearings on proposed Section 301 forced-labor tariffs covering a ~60-country probe (public-comment deadline July 6), with the base Section 122 10% tariff set to expire around July 24 and the administration intending to replace it for China with Section 301 measures. On the Korean Peninsula, there was no new missile test after Kim Jong Un's July 4 weapons trials aboard the new destroyer Kang Kon. None of these involved US ground-force movements.",
   "details": [
    "CUBA — ISLAND-WIDE BLACKOUT (July 6, 2026): The entire Cuban national grid went offline in an island-wide blackout, deepening an energy crisis driven by the US de facto oil blockade and the loss of Venezuelan crude after the US intervention; some areas were enduring 20-22 hours of daily power cuts. (Bloomberg; Washington Post; Washington Times, July 6, 2026.)",
    "VENEZUELA — RODRÍGUEZ ALLEGES DESTABILIZATION; MANDATE DISPUTE (July 5-6, 2026): Acting President Delcy Rodríguez alleged on July 6 that opponents attempted to 'destabilize' the country during the late-June earthquake emergency, after a July 5 Independence Day address warning against 'any kind of conspiracy, either internal or external'; she faces disputes that her interim mandate exceeds the constitution's 180-day limit. Context: twin June quakes (M7.2, M7.5) killed at least 2,295; she announced a $200M 'Venezuela Reborn Fund.' Maduro and Flores's next SDNY hearing remains set for July 22, 2026. (UPI; Al Jazeera; Foreign Policy, July 1-6, 2026.)",
    "COLOMBIA (July 2026): The formal transition between Petro's government and Trump-endorsed president-elect Abelardo de la Espriella (who won the June 21 runoff ~49.66% to Iván Cepeda's ~48.70%) proceeded, with the handover of power set for Aug 7. (ColombiaOne; Al Jazeera; Atlantic Council, July 2, 2026.)",
    "US-CHINA TRADE (July 6-7, 2026): USTR held July 7 hearings on proposed Section 301 forced-labor actions covering a ~60-country investigation, following a July 6 public-comment deadline; the base Section 122 10% tariff (in effect pending appeal after a May 7 Court of International Trade ruling) is set to expire around July 24, and the administration intends to replace it for China (and Thailand, Vietnam, India) with Section 301 tariffs. No new Taiwan military event was reported. (USTR; Skadden; Global Trade Alert; Tax Foundation, July 2026.)",
