   "date": "2026-07-06",
   "headline": "DAY 130 — CEASEFIRE DAY 90 / US BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 18 — MAIN FUNERAL DAY IN TEHRAN: THE CENTRAL PROCESSION FOR SLAIN SUPREME LEADER AYATOLLAH ALI KHAMENEI STEPPED OFF AT 6 A.M. LOCAL ON A ~10 KM ROUTE FROM IMAM HOSSEIN SQUARE TO AZADI SQUARE, WITH TEHRAN'S MAYOR PROJECTING UP TO 20 MILLION MOURNERS — POTENTIALLY THE LARGEST GATHERING IN THE CITY'S HISTORY. THE RITES CONTINUE TO QOM (JAMKARAN, JULY 7), NAJAF (JULY 8, IRAQI PM RECEPTION AT THE IMAM ALI SHRINE) AND BURIAL AT THE IMAM REZA SHRINE IN MASHHAD (JULY 9). NEW SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI (NAMED MARCH 9) STILL HAD NOT APPEARED PUBLICLY, KEEPING THE SUCCESSION / WHO-RUNS-IRAN QUESTION LIVE. US-IRAN TALKS REMAINED PAUSED FOR THE FUNERAL WEEK (TO RESUME 'AT THE EARLIEST POSSIBLE TIME' AFTER, PER QATAR). ON HORMUZ, IRAN'S AMBASSADOR TO CHINA REAFFIRMED TRANSIT 'SERVICE FEES' ONCE THE 60-DAY PAUSE ENDS (MID-AUGUST), WITH 'SPECIAL TREATMENT' FOR FRIENDLY NATIONS — AN IDEA THE US REJECTS — WHILE IRAN WARNED AGAINST ANY 'MILITARY DISPLAY OF EXTRA-REGIONAL POWERS' AND THE UK/FRANCE BACKED OMAN ON FREE NAVIGATION. OPEC+ AGREED JULY 5 TO RAISE AUGUST OUTPUT BY 188,000 BPD; OIL MARKETS REOPENED JULY 6 AFTER THE US HOLIDAY WEEKEND WITH BRENT NEAR ITS PRE-WAR ~$72/BBL (SAUDI EXPORTS ~90% OF PRE-WAR, UAE >3.9M BPD, TOTAL HORMUZ FLOWS >10M BPD). THE GROUND RUNG STAYED UNCHANGED AND DE-ESCALATORY ON THE US SIDE — NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 18). ISRAEL RENEWED A THREAT TO KILL IRAN'S NEW SUPREME LEADER. NO NEW STRIKES OR SHIPPING INCIDENTS REPORTED JULY 5-6.",
   "summary": "The Iran war again ran on the ceremonial and diplomatic register, not the ground one, as July 6 brought the central and largest day of Ayatollah Ali Khamenei's six-day state funeral. The main Tehran procession stepped off at 6 a.m. local along a roughly 10-kilometre route from Imam Hossein Square to Azadi Square; Tehran's mayor said attendance could reach 20 million, which would make it the largest gathering in the city's history and the largest state funeral in Iran's, exceeding Khomeini's 1989 rites. The cortege is due to reach Qom (Jamkaran) on July 7, Najaf in Iraq on July 8 (an official reception with Iraq's prime minister at the Imam Ali shrine), and burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad — Khamenei's birthplace — on July 9. The newly named Supreme Leader, Mojtaba Khamenei (designated March 9), had still not appeared publicly, leaving the succession/who-runs-Iran question open. US-Iran talks stayed paused for the funeral week, with Qatar saying the indirect track made 'positive progress' and further discussions would be scheduled 'at the earliest possible time' afterward. On the Strait, Iran's ambassador to China reaffirmed that transit 'service fees' would apply once the 60-day toll-free window ends around mid-August, promising 'special treatment' for 'friendly' nations — a mechanism the US rejects — while Iran warned against any 'military display of extra-regional powers' in the Strait and the UK and France pledged to help Oman keep navigation free. On energy, OPEC+ agreed on July 5 to raise August output by 188,000 bpd; US oil markets reopened July 6 after the Independence Day weekend with Brent near its pre-war ~$72/bbl, Saudi crude exports back to ~90% of the pre-war baseline, UAE exports above 3.9M bpd, and total Hormuz flows back above 10M bpd. The ground-invasion rung stayed unchanged and de-escalatory on the US side — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; the naval blockade stays lifted (Day 18). Israel renewed a threat to kill Iran's new supreme leader. No new strikes or shipping incidents were reported on July 5-6.",
   "details": [
    "MAIN FUNERAL DAY — TEHRAN PROCESSION IMAM HOSSEIN SQ. TO AZADI SQ. (July 6, 2026): The central procession began at 6 a.m. local along a ~10 km route from Imam Hossein Square to Azadi Square, the largest-crowd day of the six-day rites; Tehran's mayor projected up to 20 million mourners, potentially the largest gathering in the city's history. The schedule runs to Qom (Jamkaran mosque, prayers July 7), Najaf, Iraq (July 8, Imam Ali shrine, reception with Iraq's PM and senior officials), and burial at the Imam Reza shrine in Mashhad on July 9. (CNN live, July 5-6, 2026; CNBC, 'Khamenei funeral procession route,' July 4, 2026; Wikipedia, 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei,' July 2026.)",
    "SUCCESSION QUESTION STAYS LIVE — NEW SUPREME LEADER STILL ABSENT (July 5-6, 2026): New Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei, named to succeed his father on March 9, had still not appeared publicly and his whereabouts remained unreported as Tehran prepared for the largest day of the funeral, sustaining open questions over his health and who is actually running Iran (three of Khamenei's sons attended earlier rites; the successor did not). (CNN, 'New supreme leader yet to appear as Tehran prepares for largest day of Khamenei's funeral,' July 5, 2026.)",
    "US-IRAN TALKS REMAIN PAUSED FOR FUNERAL WEEK (July 5-6, 2026): The indirect US-Iran track, mediated by Qatar and Pakistan, stayed paused for the funeral; Qatar said the earlier Doha round made 'positive progress' with no breakthrough and that further discussions would be scheduled 'at the earliest possible time' after the rites. Core disputes remained open — the US rejects any Iranian-led Hormuz toll mechanism, no frozen funds have moved, and the IAEA-access dispute over the bombed Fordow/Natanz/Isfahan sites is unresolved. (CNN, July 2, 2026; CBS News live, July 4-5, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ — IRAN REAFFIRMS MID-AUGUST FEES, WARNS 'EXTRA-REGIONAL POWERS'; UK/FRANCE BACK OMAN (July 5-6, 2026): Iran's ambassador to China said transit 'service fees' would be charged once the 60-day toll-free window ends (mid-August), with 'special treatment' for 'friendly' countries — a mechanism the US rejects — and Iran warned against any 'military display of extra-regional powers' in the Strait. The UK and France pledged to work with Oman to keep 'safe transit for ships of all nations,' with reports of a possible Franco-British-led multinational freedom-of-navigation mission and Oman cooperating. Israel renewed a public threat to kill Iran's new supreme leader. (CBS News live, July 4-5, 2026; PBS NewsHour, July 4, 2026.)",
    "OPEC+ RAISES AUGUST OUTPUT; OIL MARKETS REOPEN NEAR PRE-WAR LEVELS (July 5-6, 2026): OPEC+ producers agreed on July 5 to raise August production by 188,000 bpd, extending the group's supply unwind. US commodity markets reopened July 6 after the Independence Day weekend with Brent near its pre-war ~$72/bbl (last print Fri July 3 ~$71.30-72.49), as Saudi crude exports rebounded to ~90% of the pre-war baseline, UAE exports topped 3.9M bpd, and total Hormuz flows climbed back above 10M bpd — de-escalation pricing far below the early-2026 wartime peaks above $110 and the $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. (CBS News, OPEC+ update, July 5, 2026; TradingEconomics/CNBC, Brent crude, July 3, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ-AFFECTED ECONOMIES (early July 2026): The IEA chief again called the war's supply shock the 'greatest global energy security challenge in history.' South Korea's energy minister said Seoul would face no supply problem for over a year; Japan and South Korea kept up non-Gulf sourcing and cooperation. Pakistan and Bangladesh remained among the worst-hit (Pakistan urged cricket fans to watch matches from home to conserve fuel); India managed an LPG/gas squeeze while lifting record volumes of discounted Russian crude. European benchmark gas (TTF) stayed elevated on the gradual normalization. (IEA; Al Jazeera; Reuters, July 1-3, 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "CNN live, 'New supreme leader yet to appear as Tehran prepares for largest day of Khamenei's funeral,' July 5, 2026; CBS News live, 'Tehran enters second day of massive funeral for slain supreme leader,' July 4-5, 2026; PBS NewsHour, 'Iran begins dayslong funeral for the late Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei, killed in war,' July 4, 2026; CNBC, 'Khamenei funeral procession route,' July 4, 2026; CBS News, OPEC+ August output update, July 5, 2026; TradingEconomics, Brent crude, July 3, 2026; Wikipedia, 'State funeral of Ali Khamenei' and '2026 Strait of Hormuz crisis,' July 2026; IEA, 'The Middle East and Global Energy Markets,' July 2026.",
