   "prediction_impact": "July 6 keeps Predictive History's imminent-US-ground-invasion and Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis disconfirmed-and-inverted and extends the off-the-kinetic-track register into a fourth straight day: the war's dominant event was the central day of a six-day state funeral, with talks paused and every US ground-execution indicator at zero — no landing, Kharg assault, ARG/MEU surge, or draft — and the blockade still lifted (Day 18). The structural inversion holds: the chokepoint is being reopened and governed by negotiation and coercive Iranian claims (mid-August 'service fees,' a warning against 'extra-regional powers'), not a US seizure, and oil near pre-war ~$72/bbl with OPEC+ adding barrels is the inverse of ground-commitment pricing. Two open questions stay live — deal durability (iran-us-deal-reached-june-2026), since talks are only paused and no frozen funds have moved, and Hormuz governance (iran-hormuz-administration-tolls-dispute-june-2026), now with a mid-August toll deadline the US rejects and a possible Franco-British freedom-of-navigation mission forming. The succession question (iran-succession-mojtaba-khamenei-2026) remains open with the new Supreme Leader still absent, bearing on regime cohesion and on who can deliver any deal, not on US ground posture. Any renewed collapse would return the war to the air/missile/maritime register, not vindicate a ground invasion.",
   "alternate_readings": [
    {
     "reading": "Mojtaba Khamenei's continued public absence on the central day of his father's funeral admits the same two readings noted July 5. One treats it as wartime security prudence and Shia mourning protocol — keeping the principal out of a predictable, crowd-dense target set after the Feb 28 decapitation strike and Israel's renewed threat to kill Iran's new leader, with real authority exercised through the SNSC and IRGC as designed. The other treats the months-long non-appearance since his March 9 designation as evidence of a genuine leadership vacuum or incapacity — that Mojtaba may be gravely unwell, sidelined, or a figurehead and that the security establishment is effectively running Iran, which would bear on who can actually deliver on any US-Iran deal.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Both readings rest on the same on-record facts: Mojtaba was named successor March 9; he has not appeared publicly since; his whereabouts stayed unreported through the funeral's largest day (CNN, July 5); and Israel renewed a threat against Iran's new leader. Which reading is correct depends on non-public information about his health, location, and decision-making role, none of it determinable from open sources today.",
     "public_assertion_by": [
      "CNN (July 5, 2026): the new supreme leader has yet to appear as Tehran prepares for the largest day of the funeral, sustaining questions over his health and who is running Iran.",
      "Iran-watchers and analysts: cite the non-appearance as a marker of possible IRGC ascendancy or a contested succession.",
      "Iranian state framing (implicit): treats the leadership as intact and the mass funeral as a demonstration of national cohesion and continuity."
     ],
     "why_unresolvable": "Resolution requires non-public knowledge of Mojtaba Khamenei's health, physical location, and real authority; open sources currently show only his continued public absence, consistent with both prudent concealment and genuine incapacity.",
     "open_question_ref": "iran-succession-mojtaba-khamenei-2026"
    }
   ]
