   "prediction_impact": "The ground-invasion tracker stays at no_ground_troops for a 130th day and inverts the predicted US Hormuz/Kharg seizure: on the day of Iran's largest-ever funeral procession, with US-Iran talks paused, there was no landing, Kharg assault, ARG/MEU surge, or draft, and the blockade stayed lifted (Day 18). The standing ~50,000-troop, two-carrier, two-ARG footprint is a deterrent/contingency posture, not an execution buildup. Iran's coercive claims over the reopening Strait (mid-August fees, an 'extra-regional powers' warning) are the structural inverse of a US seizure, and oil near pre-war ~$72/bbl with OPEC+ adding barrels is the inverse of ground-commitment pricing (kharg-seizure-total-control-threat-june-2026)."
