   "prediction_impact": "July 4-5 keeps Predictive History's imminent-US-ground-invasion and Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis disconfirmed-and-inverted, and deepens the off-the-kinetic-track register: the war's dominant events were a six-day state funeral and a paused negotiation, with no US landing, Kharg assault, ARG/MEU surge, or draft, and the blockade still lifted (Day 17). The structural inversion holds — the chokepoint is being reopened and governed by negotiation and coercive Iranian claims (mid-August 'service fees,' a 'serious warning' to France/UK), not a US seizure. Two open questions stay live: deal durability (iran-us-deal-reached-june-2026) — talks are only paused for the funeral, no frozen funds have moved, and the toll and IAEA-inspection disputes are unresolved — and Hormuz governance (iran-hormuz-administration-tolls-dispute-june-2026), now with a mid-August toll deadline the US rejects and a possible Franco-British freedom-of-navigation mission forming. A new succession question (iran-succession-mojtaba-khamenei-2026) emerged as the new Supreme Leader's whereabouts stayed unknown, bearing on regime cohesion, not on US ground posture. Any renewed collapse would return the war to the air/missile/maritime register, not vindicate a ground invasion.",
