     "reading": "The unexplained public absence of the new Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei during his father's massive state funeral reads two ways from the same facts. One reading treats it as deliberate security prudence and Shia mourning protocol — a wartime leadership keeping its principal out of a predictable, crowd-dense target set after the Feb 28 decapitation strike, with real authority exercised through the Supreme National Security Council and the IRGC as designed. The other reading treats the months-long non-appearance since his March 9 designation as evidence of a genuine leadership vacuum or incapacity — that Mojtaba may be gravely unwell, sidelined, or a figurehead, and that the IRGC and security establishment are effectively running Iran, which would bear on who can actually deliver on any US-Iran deal.",
     "evidentiary_status": "Both readings rest on the same on-record facts: Mojtaba Khamenei was named successor March 9; he has not appeared publicly since; his whereabouts were unknown as the funeral opened (CNN, July 4); and it was unclear whether he would attend. Which reading is correct depends on non-public information about his health, location, and actual decision-making role — none of it determinable from open sources today.",
