  {
   "date": "2026-07-05",
   "headline": "DAY 129 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. JULY 4-5 RAN OFF THE KINETIC TRACK ENTIRELY — A SIX-DAY KHAMENEI STATE FUNERAL AND A US-IRAN NEGOTIATION PAUSED FOR THE FUNERAL WEEK. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 17). NO NEW TROOP MOVEMENTS, GROUND-OPERATION AUTHORIZATIONS, PENTAGON GROUND STATEMENTS OR DRAFT SIGNALS WERE REPORTED. STANDING IN-THEATRE POSTURE (PER STARS AND STRIPES, JULY 1): ~50,000 US TROOPS AND ~24 WARSHIPS (CARRIERS ABRAHAM LINCOLN AND GEORGE H.W. BUSH, 15 DESTROYERS), WITH THE USS BOXER ARG / 11TH MEU (ARRIVED IN-THEATRE JUNE 30) AND THE USS TRIPOLI ARG / 31ST MEU IN THE ARABIAN SEA — ALL IN ROUTINE/CONTINGENCY POSTURE, NO LANDING ORDERED OR EXECUTED. IRAN, NOT THE US, IS ASSERTING COERCIVE CONTROL OVER THE REOPENING STRAIT (MID-AUGUST FEES, A 'SERIOUS WARNING' TO FRANCE/UK) — THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF THE PREDICTED US SEIZURE. OIL NEAR PRE-WAR LEVELS (BRENT ~$72/BBL, JULY 3) — THE INVERSE OF GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "The ground-invasion tracker holds at no_ground_troops for July 4-5 (Days 128-129). The period's developments were ceremonial and diplomatic — the six-day Khamenei state funeral and a US-Iran round paused for the funeral week — with no ground move on either side. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops on Iranian soil, no assault on or landing toward Kharg Island (the seizure pathway that dominated March-June planning coverage remains superseded, not executed), no new amphibious ready group or Marine Expeditionary Unit order, no Guard/Reserve call-up, and no Selective Service or conscription move. The naval blockade lifted June 18 stays lifted (Day 17). The standing in-theatre posture, per Stars and Stripes (July 1), is ~50,000 US troops and at least 24 warships — including the carriers USS Abraham Lincoln and USS George H.W. Bush and 15 destroyers — with the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~2,500 Marines; arrived in-theatre June 30) and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~2,000 Marines) in the Arabian Sea; that amphibious presence remains in routine/contingency posture, with no landing, forcible-entry staging, or ground order. Kharg Island remains an option Trump is described as weighing to pressure Iran over the Strait, but no new Kharg action occurred July 4-5. On the draft, no formal plans exist; the only standing item is the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by December 2026 (an FY2026 NDAA change predating the war, not a draft activation). Oil near pre-war levels (Brent ~$72/bbl) is the inverse of the sustained $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. Iran, not the US, is asserting coercive control over the reopening Strait (mid-August 'service fees,' a 'serious warning' to France/UK) — the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure.",
   "details": [
    "NO GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR ON JULY 4-5 (2026): The Khamenei funeral and the paused talks produced no US mobilization order, no brigade-scale activation, no new ARG/MEU surge, no landing toward Iran or Kharg, and no conscription language. No new troop movements, ground-operation authorizations or Pentagon ground statements were reported. The blockade stays lifted (Day 17). (CBS News; NPR; Stars and Stripes, July 1-4, 2026.)",
    "STANDING NAVAL/AMPHIBIOUS POSTURE (per Stars and Stripes, July 1, 2026): ~50,000 US troops and at least 24 warships in the region, including the carriers USS Abraham Lincoln and USS George H.W. Bush and 15 destroyers; the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~2,500 Marines) arrived in-theatre June 30 and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~2,000 Marines) is in the Arabian Sea (USS Portland and USS Comstock also with the 11th MEU). All remain in routine/contingency posture — no landing, no forcible-entry staging, no ground assault ordered or executed. (Stars and Stripes, 'Another amphibious assault ship joins US naval buildup amid Iran talks,' July 1, 2026.)",
    "KHARG-SEIZURE PATHWAY REMAINS SUPERSEDED (July 4-5, 2026): No US ground troops are on Kharg Island and no assault has been ordered or executed; the seizure option that dominated March-June planning coverage stays off the table as the chokepoint is routed through negotiation, an Iran-Oman corridor claim, and coercive Iranian route enforcement. Kharg is still described as an option Trump is weighing to pressure Iran over the Strait, but no new Kharg action occurred July 4-5. (CNBC; Middle East Eye, July 2026.)",
