   "prediction_impact": "Day 129 keeps Predictive History's predicted US ground invasion / Kharg-and-Hormuz seizure disconfirmed-and-inverted. The war spent July 4-5 off the kinetic track (a state funeral plus a paused negotiation); every US ground-execution indicator is at zero, the blockade stays lifted (Day 17), and oil sits near pre-war levels — the inverse of ground-commitment pricing. The standing ~50,000-troop, multi-carrier, two-ARG posture is a deterrent/contingency footprint, not an execution buildup: no landing, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft. The active risk is deal durability in the diplomatic/air/maritime register, not a forming ground invasion.",
