   "prediction_impact": "The Russia-Ukraine theatre continues to stress US strategic bandwidth (the July 4 Patriot/precision-artillery pause and the Zelensky-Trump call both underline competing demands on US air-defense stocks during the Iran drawdown) but triggered no US ground-deployment surge and no NATO troop commitment on July 4-5 — consistent with the corpus pattern that this theatre is a resource/attention strain, not a US ground-force trigger. The contested Kostiantynivka capture claim is logged as an alternate-reading dispute (see iran-adjacent open-questions register); it bears on Donbas control, not on any tracked US ground-invasion prediction.",
