   "date": "2026-07-05",
   "headline": "LATIN AMERICA — JULY 4: ACTING PRESIDENT DELCY RODRÍGUEZ'S 180-DAY INTERIM MANDATE FORMALLY EXPIRED (SHE WAS SWORN IN JAN 5 AFTER MADURO'S US CAPTURE), WITH NO GOVERNMENT STATEMENT ON NEXT STEPS — THE PARTY-CONTROLLED NATIONAL ASSEMBLY COULD EXTEND THE MANDATE 90 DAYS OR DECLARE THE POST VACANT AND TRIGGER A SNAP ELECTION, AS OPPOSITION LEADER MARÍA CORINA MACHADO PRESSES TO RETURN. THE EXPIRY LANDS AMID A POST-QUAKE CRISIS: TWIN JUNE 24 LA GUAIRA EARTHQUAKES KILLED 2,295+, THE US MOBILIZED ~2,000 PERSONNEL AND PLEDGED $100M IN AID, AND RODRÍGUEZ HAS FACED MOUNTING CRITICISM OF THE RESPONSE. MADURO'S SDNY NARCOTERRORISM TRIAL WAS DELAYED FROM JUNE 30 TO JULY 22. CUBA: NO NEW JULY 4-5 DEVELOPMENT.",
   "summary": "In Venezuela, acting President Delcy Rodríguez's 180-day interim mandate — she was sworn in January 5, 2026 after Nicolás Maduro's US capture — formally expired on July 4, with no immediate government statement on what follows. The National Assembly, controlled by her party, could extend the mandate for 90 days or declare the presidency vacant and trigger a snap election; opposition leader María Corina Machado is pressing to return. The expiry lands amid an acute post-earthquake crisis: twin June 24 quakes in La Guaira killed at least 2,295, the US mobilized roughly 2,000 personnel and pledged $100M in aid, and Rodríguez has faced mounting criticism over the response (she issued the government's first public defense of it on July 3). Separately, the SDNY narcoterrorism trial of Maduro and his wife Cilia Flores — both of whom pleaded not guilty in January — was again delayed, from June 30 to July 22, with no trial date set. No new July 4-5 development surfaced in Cuba (the ongoing US fuel blockade and grid crisis continue, last major reporting mid-May) or in Colombia beyond World Cup coverage. This theatre remains a Western-Hemisphere political/humanitarian story with no direct bearing on the Iran ground-invasion track.",
   "details": [
    "RODRÍGUEZ INTERIM MANDATE EXPIRES (July 4, 2026): Acting President Delcy Rodríguez's 180-day mandate formally expired; no government statement on next steps. The party-controlled National Assembly could extend it 90 days or declare the post vacant and call a snap election; María Corina Machado is pressing to return. (AP via ABC News; MercoPress, July 3-4, 2026.)",
    "POST-QUAKE CRISIS BACKDROP (June 24-July 3, 2026): Twin La Guaira earthquakes June 24 killed 2,295+; the US mobilized ~2,000 personnel and pledged $100M in aid, and the top US diplomat in Caracas expressed 'a great deal of confidence' in her administration; Rodríguez issued the government's first public defense of the quake response July 3. (Washington Post; Foreign Policy, July 3, 2026.)",
    "MADURO TRIAL DELAYED TO JULY 22 (procedural): The SDNY narcoterrorism trial of Maduro and Cilia Flores was pushed from June 30 to July 22, 2026; both pleaded not guilty in January; no trial date set. (Latin Times, June-July 2026.)",
    "CUBA / COLOMBIA — NO NEW JULY 4-5 POLITICAL NEWS: No discrete July 4-5 development surfaced in Cuba (US fuel blockade and grid crisis ongoing; latest major reporting mid-May) or Colombia (only World Cup coverage). (Regional reporting, July 4, 2026.)"
   ],
