  {
   "date": "2026-07-04",
   "headline": "DAY 128 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. THE WAR SPENT JULY 1-4 OFF THE KINETIC TRACK ENTIRELY — A PAUSED US-IRAN NEGOTIATION (THE JULY 1-2 DOHA ROUND CONCLUDED WITH 'POSITIVE PROGRESS' BUT NO BREAKTHROUGH; NEXT ROUND POSTPONED FOR A WEEK UNTIL AFTER THE FUNERAL) AND THE OPENING OF A SIX-DAY STATE FUNERAL FOR KHAMENEI (JULY 4-9, 15-20 MILLION MOURNERS EXPECTED). EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 16), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED. THE ONLY US MILITARY EVENT WAS A NON-COMBAT MISHAP — A NAVY HELICOPTER'S EMERGENCY WATER LANDING IN THE ARABIAN SEA (ONE CREW MEMBER MISSING) — NOT A GROUND OR AMPHIBIOUS MOVE. OIL AT A FOUR-MONTH LOW (BRENT ~$71.5/BBL) — THE INVERSE OF GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "The ground-invasion tracker holds at no_ground_troops for July 1-4 (Days 125-128). The period's developments were diplomatic and ceremonial: the July 1-2 US-Iran Doha round concluded with 'positive progress' but no breakthrough and only implementation mechanics (a frozen-asset goods-purchase channel, a violations-deconfliction line, a Hormuz-passage focus), after which the US agreed to halt talks for a week until Khamenei's six-day state funeral (July 4-9) concludes. None of this is a ground move. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops on Iranian soil, no assault on or landing toward Kharg Island (the seizure pathway that dominated March-June planning coverage remains superseded, not executed), no new amphibious ready group or Marine Expeditionary Unit order, no Guard/Reserve call-up, and no Selective Service or conscription move. The naval blockade lifted June 18 stays lifted (Day 16) and the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU stays disaggregated — amphibious mass removed from a forcible-entry posture. The standing in-theatre amphibious/Marine elements (USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU; 11th MEU; the ~2,000-strong 82nd Airborne forward HQ) remain in routine/contingency posture, not an execution buildup. The single US military event of the week — a Navy helicopter's emergency water landing in the Arabian Sea, one crew member missing — is a non-combat mishap, not a ground or amphibious operation. Oil at a four-month low (Brent ~$71.5/bbl) is the inverse of the sustained $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. Iran, not the US, is asserting coercive control over the reopening Strait (Tehran-designated tanker routes, a mid-August toll deadline) — the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure.",
   "details": [
    "NO GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR ON JULY 1-4 (2026): The Doha round and the Khamenei funeral produced no US mobilization order, no brigade-scale activation, no new ARG/MEU surge, no landing toward Iran or Kharg, and no conscription language. The US move was to pause negotiations for a week; the blockade stays lifted (Day 16) and the USS Boxer ARG stays disaggregated. (CNN; Al Jazeera; Fox News Digital, July 1-3, 2026.)",
    "KHARG-SEIZURE PATHWAY REMAINS SUPERSEDED (July 1-4, 2026): No US ground troops are on Kharg Island and no assault has been ordered or executed; the seizure option that dominated March-June planning coverage stays off the table as the chokepoint is routed through negotiation (US-Iran comms channel; Iran-Oman corridor claim; toll dispute). Iran is enforcing its own designated Hormuz routes by warning of a 'forceful response' — an Iranian coercive move, the inverse of a US landing. (The Bridge Chronicle; Gulf News, July 2-3, 2026.)",
    "AMPHIBIOUS/MARINE POSTURE UNCHANGED (July 1-4, 2026): The USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~4,000-5,000 Marines) remains disaggregated; the USS Tripoli (LHA-7) ARG / 31st MEU stays forward-deployed in routine posture. No third ARG, no new MEU surge, no forcible-entry staging. The week's only US military event was a Navy helicopter's emergency water landing in the Arabian Sea (one crew member missing) — a non-combat mishap. (CBS News, July 3, 2026.)",
    "NO DRAFT SIGNAL (July 1-4, 2026): No Selective Service activation, Guard/Reserve call-up or conscription language accompanied the Doha round or the funeral; the only standing item remains the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration. (CBS News; Fox News Digital, July 3, 2026.)"
