   "prediction_impact": "Directly tracks the imminent-US-ground-invasion / Hormuz-and-Kharg-seizure thesis, which stays disconfirmed-and-inverted. Across July 1-4 the US instrument was diplomacy (a paused Doha round) against the backdrop of a six-day Iranian state funeral; there was no landing, no Kharg assault, no ARG/MEU surge and no draft, the blockade stayed lifted (Day 16), and oil sat at a four-month low — the inverse of ground-commitment pricing. The seizure pathway is superseded by negotiation, and it is Iran (Tehran-designated tanker routes, a mid-August toll deadline) rather than the US that is asserting coercive control over the reopening Strait.",
