  {
   "date": "2026-07-03",
   "headline": "DAY 127 — CEASEFIRE DAY 87 / US BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 15 — THE US AGREED TO HALT US-IRAN TALKS FOR A WEEK AS IRAN OPENED A SIX-DAY STATE FUNERAL FOR SLAIN SUPREME LEADER KHAMENEI. HIS COFFIN WAS PLACED ON DISPLAY AT TEHRAN'S GRAND MOSALLA JULY 3 AHEAD OF THE JULY 4 START; OFFICIALS EXPECT 15-20 MILLION MOURNERS OVER SIX DAYS (TEHRAN → QOM → NAJAF/KARBALA → MASHHAD, BURIAL JULY 9), THE LARGEST STATE FUNERAL IN IRANIAN HISTORY, WITH ~30 FOREIGN DELEGATIONS. IRAN'S JOINT MILITARY COMMAND WARNED ALL TANKERS TO USE ITS APPROVED HORMUZ ROUTES OR FACE A 'FORCEFUL RESPONSE,' AND TEHRAN WARNED OF 'HARSH RETALIATION' AGAINST THE US AS NSA WALTZ DISPARAGED THE LATE LEADER. HORMUZ TRAFFIC RECOVERED TO 258 VESSELS LAST WEEK (FROM 138); BRENT SLID TO A FOUR-MONTH LOW ~$71.5/BBL. A US NAVY HELICOPTER MADE A NON-COMBAT EMERGENCY WATER LANDING IN THE ARABIAN SEA (ONE CREW MISSING). GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED — NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 15), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED.",
   "summary": "With the Doha round concluded, July 3 was defined by the pause and the funeral. Mediators Qatar and Pakistan said the next US-Iran round would resume 'at the earliest possible time' after Khamenei's funeral, and the US agreed to halt talks for roughly a week. Iran placed Ayatollah Ali Khamenei's coffin on display at Tehran's Grand Mosalla ahead of a six-day funeral opening July 4 — lying in state July 4-5, a Tehran procession July 6, Qom July 7, Najaf and Karbala in Iraq July 8, and burial in Mashhad July 9 — expecting 15-20 million mourners and delegations from about 30 countries, including Russia (Medvedev as Putin's 'special emissary') and China. Iran hardened its Hormuz posture: its joint military command warned tankers to use Tehran-designated routes or face a 'forceful response,' and Tehran warned of 'harsh retaliation' against the US as national security adviser Mike Waltz disparaged the late leader. Hormuz traffic kept recovering (258 vessels the prior week, up from 138), and Brent slid to a four-month low near $71.5/bbl. A US Navy helicopter made an emergency water landing in the Arabian Sea with one crew member missing — a non-combat mishap. The ground rung was unchanged and de-escalatory on the US side: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; the blockade stays lifted (Day 15) and the USS Boxer ARG stays disaggregated.",
