    "US HALTS TALKS FOR A WEEK (July 3, 2026): Qatar and Pakistan said the next negotiation round would resume 'at the earliest possible time' after the funeral; the US agreed to pause talks for about a week, with no fixed resumption date. (Fox News Digital; CBS News, July 3, 2026.)",
    "KHAMENEI LIES IN STATE; FUNERAL OPENS JULY 4 (July 3, 2026): Khamenei's coffin went on display at Tehran's Grand Mosalla ahead of a six-day funeral (Tehran July 4-6, Qom July 7, Najaf/Karbala July 8, Mashhad burial July 9), expected to draw 15-20 million mourners — the largest state funeral in Iranian history — with ~30 foreign delegations including Russia (Medvedev) and China. (Al Jazeera; TIME; CBS News, July 3, 2026.)",
    "IRAN HARDENS HORMUZ POSTURE AND RHETORIC (July 3, 2026): Iran's joint military command warned all oil tankers to use its approved Hormuz routes or face a 'forceful response'; Tehran warned of 'harsh retaliation' against the US as the funeral opened, while US NSA Mike Waltz publicly disparaged the late leader. (Gulf News; Fox News Digital, July 3, 2026.)",
    "OIL AT FOUR-MONTH LOW; NON-COMBAT NAVY MISHAP (July 2-3, 2026): Brent slid to about $71.54/bbl (-0.36%), a four-month low, on easing tensions and the gradual Hormuz reopening; a US Navy helicopter made an emergency water landing in the Arabian Sea with one crew member missing (non-combat). Hormuz traffic recovered to 258 vessels the prior week (from 138). (TradingEconomics/CNBC; Gulf News; CBS News, July 2-3, 2026.)"
