   "headline": "DAY 125 — CEASEFIRE DAY 85 / US BLOCKADE LIFTED DAY 13 — THE DOHA MEETING CONVENED, RESOLVING THE JUNE 30 UNCERTAINTY OVER WHETHER IT WOULD HAPPEN. VP VANCE SAID THE INDIRECT US-IRAN TALKS (MEDIATED BY QATAR AND PAKISTAN; WITKOFF AND KUSHNER PRESENT) WERE 'GOING WELL,' WITH FOCUS ON HORMUZ MARITIME TRAFFIC AND UNFREEZING IRANIAN FUNDS. IRAN KEPT ASSERTING HORMUZ SOVEREIGNTY AND ITS PLANNED MID-AUGUST TOLLS; OIL HELD NEAR A FOUR-MONTH LOW. GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED AND DE-ESCALATORY ON THE US SIDE — NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 13), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED.",
   "summary": "The Doha meeting Trump had announced convened, resolving the June 30 uncertainty — Iran's deputy FM Gharibabadi had publicly denied any technical talks were scheduled — over whether it would happen. The talks were held indirectly, mediated by Qatar and Pakistan, with US envoy Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner present on the US side; VP JD Vance said they were 'going well.' The agenda centered on Hormuz maritime traffic and unfreezing Iranian funds under the June 17 MOU. Iran continued to assert sovereignty over the Strait and its intention to impose transit tolls after the toll-free window (now cited as mid-August), while the US maintained Hormuz is an international waterway on which no country may charge fees. Oil held near a four-month low. The ground rung was unchanged and de-escalatory on the US side: the day's activity was diplomatic, not a ground move — no US troops in Iran, no Kharg assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft; the blockade stays lifted (Day 13) and the USS Boxer ARG stays disaggregated.",
   "details": [
    "DOHA MEETING CONVENES; VANCE SAYS TALKS 'GOING WELL' (July 1, 2026): The indirect US-Iran meeting announced by Trump convened in Doha, mediated by Qatar and Pakistan, with Witkoff and Kushner present; VP Vance said the talks were 'going well.' Convening resolved the June 30 uncertainty created by Iran's public denial that technical talks were scheduled. (CNN; Al Jazeera, July 1, 2026.)",
    "AGENDA: HORMUZ TRAFFIC AND FROZEN FUNDS (July 1, 2026): The talks focused on restoring Strait of Hormuz maritime traffic and unfreezing Iranian funds — the two critical issues under the interim agreement. (Al Jazeera; The National, July 1-2, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ SOVEREIGNTY DISPUTE CARRIES IN (July 1, 2026): Iran reiterated its claim to administer the Strait and its plan to charge transit tolls once the MOU's toll-free window expires (cited as mid-August), while the US held that Hormuz is an international waterway on which no tolls may be charged. Oil held near a four-month low. (The Bridge Chronicle; Gulf News, July 1-2, 2026.)"
