   "prediction_impact": "Day 123 keeps the ground-invasion execution thesis disconfirmed-and-inverted while marking the cycle's most serious escalation yet. The breakthrough event — Iran striking US bases in Kuwait and Bahrain — is exactly the kind of vertical escalation that could, in principle, precede a ground phase; instead it confirms the opposite dynamic, with both sides escalating within the air/missile/maritime register and neither moving ground forces. The blockade stays lifted, the Boxer ARG stays disaggregated, and there is no draft, no Kharg assault, and no new amphibious surge. Deal-durability risk is now high, but a collapse would resume the air/missile war, not initiate the predicted invasion.",
