   "headline": "DAY 122 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. THE BREACH-RETALIATION CYCLE REPEATED A SECOND STRAIGHT DAY (JUNE 27: IRANIAN DRONE HIT THE M/T KIKU TANKER → A SECOND, LARGER US AIRSTRIKE ON IRANIAN AIR-DEFENSE, DRONE STORAGE, CRUISE MISSILES, RADARS AND MINELAYER CAPABILITIES) — STILL AN AIR/NAVAL-REGISTER RESPONSE, NOT A GROUND OPERATION. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT; BLOCKADE LIFTED (DAY 10), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED. OIL STAYED BELOW $73 — THE INVERSE OF GROUND-COMMITMENT PRICING.",
   "summary": "JUNE 28 (Day 122): The ground-invasion EXECUTION track produced no new indicator even as the conflict's breach-retaliation cycle repeated for a second straight day. After an Iranian one-way attack drone hit the Panama-flagged tanker M/T Kiku on June 27 (~2M barrels of Qatari crude; bridge damaged, crew safe), US Central Command launched a second, larger round of airstrikes on Iran — air-defense and SAM systems, drone storage, cruise missiles, targeting radars and minelayer capabilities ('a larger strike than last night,' per a senior US official). As on June 26, the US instrument was air power from existing in-theatre assets, not a ground operation, and it is the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure of the Strait: Iran (not the US) is using force to assert coercive control over Hormuz — firing on a second tanker, threatening a 'broader response,' menacing Bahrain's airspace — while the US keeps the chokepoint open (JMIC widened the transit route), the blockade lifted (Day 10), and the USS Boxer ARG disaggregated. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg Island assault, no new ARG/MEU order, no draft. Oil stayed below $73/bbl. The live risk is deal durability — whether the day-on-day breach-retaliation cycle keeps repeating — in the air/missile/maritime register, not a forming ground invasion. (CNBC; Fox News Digital; Al Jazeera; ABC News, June 27, 2026.)",
   "details": [
    "US RESPONSE WAS AGAIN AIR, NOT GROUND (June 27): The second US strike package in two days hit Iranian air-defense/SAM systems, drone storage, cruise missiles, targeting radars and minelayer capabilities — the same air/naval instrument used June 2-3, June 6 and June 26 — with no ground component, no Kharg assault, and no amphibious/Marine move. (CNBC; ABC News, June 27, 2026.)",
    "EVERY GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR AT ZERO (June 28): No US troops in Iran; no Kharg Island ground assault; no third ARG or new MEU surge; no Guard/Reserve call-up; no draft. The naval blockade stays lifted (Day 10) and the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU stays disaggregated.",
    "STRUCTURAL INVERSION HARDENS (June 28): Iran is the actor using force on the Strait — a second tanker struck, an IRGC Navy threat of 'a broader response,' a drone over Bahrain — while the US keeps Hormuz open (JMIC widened the route), the blockade lifted, and Gulf exports climbing to ~75% of pre-war. That is the opposite of a forcible US seizure of Hormuz and Kharg.",
    "MARKETS PRICE DE-ESCALATION, NOT MOBILIZATION (June 26-27): Brent below $73/bbl (lowest since Feb 27; >10% weekly drop) through the two-day exchange — the inverse of the sustained $130+ a US ground commitment would imply.",
    "NO DRAFT SIGNAL (June 28): The second US airstrike produced no mobilization order, no Guard/Reserve call-up and no conscription language. The only standing item remains the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by end-2026 — not a draft activation; fact-checkers continue to rate reinstatement claims false."
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "The repeating breach-retaliation cycle raises air/maritime risk but leaves the ground-invasion thesis disconfirmed-and-inverted: both US responses were airstrikes, the blockade stays lifted, the Strait stays open, and Iran (not the US) is the one using force to control Hormuz. Ground-invasion execution probability remains LOW.",
   "source": "CNBC, June 27, 2026; Fox News Digital live blog, June 27, 2026; ABC News live updates, June 27, 2026; Al Jazeera live blog, June 27, 2026."
  },
