   "headline": "DAY 121 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. THE FIRST US KINETIC STRIKES ON IRAN SINCE THE MOU (JUNE 26) WERE AIRSTRIKES ON MISSILE/DRONE STORAGE, COASTAL RADAR AND QESHM ISLAND — AN AIR/NAVAL-REGISTER RESPONSE TO IRAN'S JUNE 25 DRONE ATTACK ON THE M/V EVER LOVELY, NOT A GROUND OPERATION. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT, BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 9), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED. OIL EASED TO ~$74/BBL DESPITE THE STRIKES — FAR BELOW THE SUSTAINED $130+ A GROUND COMMITMENT WOULD IMPLY.",
   "summary": "JUNE 27 (Day 121): The ground-invasion EXECUTION track produced no new indicator even as the conflict turned two-sided kinetic for the first time since the June 17 MOU. After Iran's IRGC fired four one-way attack drones at Hormuz shipping June 25 (one hitting the M/V Ever Lovely), US Central Command retaliated June 26 with AIRSTRIKES on Iranian missile and drone storage facilities, coastal radar sites and Qeshm Island — an air/naval-register self-defense package of the same kind used in the early-June flare-ups (June 2-3, June 6), not a ground move. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg Island assault, no new amphibious ready group or Marine Expeditionary Unit order, no National Guard call-up, no Selective Service/draft language. The US naval blockade has been lifted for a ninth day and the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~4,000-5,000 Marines) remains disaggregated. Oil eased to ~$74/bbl despite the strikes — the inverse of ground-commitment pricing. Assessment: ground-invasion execution probability remains LOW; the escalation is in the air/maritime register, with deal-durability — not a forming ground invasion — the live risk. (NBC News; CBS News; CNBC, June 26, 2026.)",
   "details": [
    "TROOP MOVEMENTS: No new ground deployment ordered. US strength in the CENTCOM area of responsibility is broadly unchanged (~50,000); the day's US military action was airstrikes from existing in-theatre air/naval assets, not a ground move.",
    "KHARG ISLAND: Seizure pathway remains superseded. The June 26 US strikes targeted missile/drone storage, coastal radar and Qeshm Island — not a Kharg ground assault or port seizure. Iran's turning-back of tankers and fee threats are coercive maritime moves, the inverse of a US seizure of the export hub.",
    "AMPHIBIOUS / MARINES: USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU stays disaggregated (amphibious mass removed). No new ARG/MEU surge, no forcible-entry concentration, no USS Tripoli/Bataan movement toward Iran reported.",
    "DRAFT / CONSCRIPTION: No Selective Service or draft signal. The retaliatory airstrikes produced no mobilization, Guard activation, or conscription language; the only standing item remains the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by end-2026 (CNBC, Apr 9, 2026) — not a draft activation.",
    "MARKET CONFIRMATION: Oil eased to ~$74/bbl (Brent -1 to -2% on June 26) despite the first US strikes on Iran since the MOU — still ~2% above pre-conflict levels and far below the sustained $130+ a US ground commitment would require; an air-register flare-up, not war-scare repricing."
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Day 121 keeps Predictive History's predicted US ground invasion / Kharg-and-Hormuz seizure disconfirmed-and-inverted: the first US strikes on Iran since the deal were airstrikes on missile/drone storage and radar, not a landing. The blockade stays lifted, amphibious mass is disaggregated, and every US ground-execution indicator is at zero. The active risk is deal durability in the air/maritime register, not a forming ground invasion.",
