   "headline": "DAY 120 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. THE CYCLE'S ESCALATION WAS MARITIME, NOT GROUND: IRAN FIRED ON A CARGO VESSEL NEAR OMAN (JUNE 25) AND THE IRGC NAVY THREATENED VIOLATORS OF ITS DESIGNATED ROUTES — AN IRANIAN MARITIME MOVE, NOT A US GROUND OPERATION. EVERY US GROUND-EXECUTION INDICATOR STAYED AT ZERO: NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT, BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED (DAY 8), USS BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED. THE SENATE WALKED BACK ITS WAR-POWERS REBUKE (50-47, JUNE 24) — REMOVING A LEGISLATIVE CONSTRAINT BUT ORDERING NO FORCE MOVEMENT. OIL REVERSED HIGHER (BRENT $75.26, WTI $71.92) ON RENEWED RISK, STILL FAR BELOW THE SUSTAINED $130+ A GROUND COMMITMENT WOULD IMPLY.",
   "summary": "JUNE 26 (Day 120): The ground-invasion EXECUTION track produced no new indicator even as the maritime track re-escalated. Iran fired on a cargo vessel near Oman on June 25 and the IRGC Navy warned that ships must use Tehran-designated routes or 'face action,' prompting the UN IMO to pause its Hormuz shepherding program — but this is an Iranian maritime/coercive move, not a US ground operation, and it is the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure of the Strait. Every US ground-execution indicator stayed at zero: no US troops in Iran, no Kharg Island assault, no new amphibious ready group or Marine Expeditionary Unit order, no National Guard call-up, no Selective Service/draft language. The US naval blockade has been lifted for an eighth day and the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~4,000-5,000 Marines) remains disaggregated. The Senate walked back its June 23 war-powers rebuke of Trump (a procedural motion failed 50-47 on June 24), removing a near-term legislative constraint on the president's war powers but ordering no force movement. Oil reversed higher on the strike (Brent $75.26, WTI $71.92) yet stayed far below the sustained $130+ a US ground commitment would imply. Assessment: ground-invasion execution probability remains LOW and stable; the cycle's escalation was maritime, not ground. (CNBC; NBC News; CNN, June 24-25, 2026.)",
