   "headline": "DAY 119 GROUND-INVASION TRACKER — STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops. NO NEW GROUND INDICATOR ON JUNE 25. THE DAY'S MOVEMENT WAS DIPLOMATIC (RUBIO'S GULF TOUR; THE HORMUZ-TOLLS AND IAEA-INSPECTIONS DISPUTES) AND THE US POSTURE STAYED DE-ESCALATORY — BLOCKADE LIFTED (DAY 7), HORMUZ REOPENING BY NEGOTIATED MINE-CLEARING, NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO NEW ARG/MEU ORDER, NO DRAFT. THE USS BOXER ARG / 11TH MEU REMAINS DISAGGREGATED (AMPHIBIOUS MASS REMOVED). OIL AT A WAR-PERIOD LOW (BRENT <$74) CONFIRMS DEAL/DE-ESCALATION PRICING, NOT THE SUSTAINED $130+ A GROUND COMMITMENT WOULD IMPLY.",
