   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 117 (June 23): STATUS UNCHANGED AT 'NO_GROUND_TROOPS' AND STILL DE-ESCALATORY ON THE US SIDE. THE JUNE 22 BÜRGENSTOCK ROUND PRODUCED A 'ROADMAP TO A FINAL DEAL WITHIN 60 DAYS,' A LEBANON DECONFLICTION CELL, AND A HORMUZ COMMUNICATIONS CHANNEL — ALL DIPLOMATIC/DE-ESCALATORY MECHANISMS, NOT GROUND MOVES. THE NAVAL BLOCKADE REMAINS LIFTED AND THE USS BOXER ARG STAYS DISAGGREGATED. STILL ~50,000 US TROOPS IN THE CENTCOM AOR; NO NEW DEPLOYMENT; NO KHARG ASSAULT; NO THIRD ARG / NEW MEU; NO DRAFT. THE ONLY ESCALATION LEVER AIRED REMAINS AIR-POWER, NOT GROUND.",
   "summary": "JUNE 23 (Day 117): No change to the ground-invasion picture on the US side, which stayed de-escalatory as the first technical round at Bürgenstock concluded with a 'roadmap toward a final deal within 60 days.' Every concrete output was diplomatic, not a ground move: a Lebanon deconfliction cell (US/Iran/Lebanon, mediator-facilitated), a communications channel to keep the Strait of Hormuz open, and a reaffirmed sanctions/reconstruction package. The US naval blockade remains lifted and the USS Boxer amphibious ready group / 11th MEU stays disaggregated — removing, not adding, amphibious mass. There are still ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM area of responsibility with no new deployment ordered; the USS Tripoli (LHA-7) ARG / 31st MEU remains forward-deployed in a routine posture (its blockade-enforcement role wound down); no Kharg assault has been ordered or executed; no third ARG or new MEU has been ordered; and there is no draft signal. The 82nd Airborne forward headquarters remains a fading standing forcible-entry contingency, not an execution order. The only escalation lever aired stayed air-power (Trump's weekend 'hit Iran very hard again'), not ground.",
   "details": [
    "TROOP LEVEL: Still ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM AOR (official figure, holding since March 2026); no net change and no new ground deployment ordered around the June 22 Bürgenstock round, which produced diplomatic mechanisms, not force movement. (CNBC; NPR, June 22, 2026.)",
    "ROADMAP / DECONFLICTION CELL ARE DIPLOMATIC, NOT GROUND (June 22): The first technical round yielded a 'roadmap to a final deal within 60 days,' a US/Iran/Lebanon deconfliction cell (mediator-facilitated) to enforce the Lebanon ceasefire, and a Hormuz communications channel to keep the strait open. None involves US ground forces; the deconfliction cell is a communications/enforcement body, not a deployment. (CNBC; Iran International, June 22, 2026.)",
    "BLOCKADE STILL LIFTED / BOXER ARG DISAGGREGATED: The US naval blockade remains lifted and the Hormuz contest is being managed by communications channel rather than seizure; the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU (~4,000-5,000 Marines) stays disaggregated, a continuing drawdown signal that removes amphibious mass. (The War Zone; CBS News, June 20-22, 2026.)",
    "KHARG ISLAND: The seizure pathway remains superseded and now further marginalized by the 60-day roadmap and the Hormuz communications channel. No US ground troops are on Kharg and no assault has been ordered or executed. (Al Jazeera; War on the Rocks 'The Folly of Seizing Kharg Island,' April 2026, as standing context.)",
    "MARINE / AMPHIBIOUS — POSTURE TRENDING TO ROTATION/DRAWDOWN: No new amphibious or Marine deployment ordered. The USS Tripoli (LHA-7) ARG / 31st MEU remains forward-deployed in a routine posture (not invasion staging), its enforcement role wound down; the USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU stays disaggregated; the USS Abraham Lincoln carrier strike group was earlier flagged as likely first to rotate out. No third ARG, no new MEU surge, no landing toward Iran or Kharg. (The War Zone; armyrecognition.com, June 2026.)",
    "DRAFT / MOBILIZATION: No draft or conscription signal. The Bürgenstock round and the continued Lebanon fighting produced no Selective Service action, no expanded Guard/Reserve call-up language, and no brigade-scale activation. The previously legislated automatic Selective Service registration (effective Dec 2026) is unrelated to the war. (CNN Politics; CNBC, April 9, 2026, as standing context.)",
    "ASSESSMENT: Ground-invasion execution probability is LOW and stable at Day 117. The day's developments cut further against a ground war — a negotiated roadmap, a Lebanon deconfliction cell, and a Hormuz communications channel all route the conflict toward settlement and away from force. The live risks (Lebanon ceasefire enforcement, deal durability over 60 days) bear on whether the war ends cleanly, not on any forming US ground invasion."
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Reinforces the disconfirmation and tightens its boundary further. The ground-invasion thesis required US troops moving toward Iran, a Kharg seizure, an amphibious buildup, or a draft; the June 22-23 window delivered the opposite — a 60-day roadmap to a final deal, a Lebanon deconfliction cell, a Hormuz communications channel, the blockade still lifted, and the USS Boxer ARG still disaggregated. A chokepoint kept open by a communications channel is the structural inverse of the predicted US seizure of Hormuz and Kharg by ground force; the only escalation aired remained air-power.",
   "source": "CNBC, 'U.S., Iran agree on roadmap for final deal...,' June 22, 2026; Iran International, 'Lebanon deconfliction cell emerges...,' June 22, 2026; NPR, June 21-22, 2026; The War Zone (USS Boxer ARG disaggregation; naval posture), June 2026; CBS News live blog, June 20-22, 2026; CNN Politics / CNBC (Selective Service), April 9, 2026; War on the Rocks (Kharg), April 2026."
