   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 114 (June 20): STATUS UNCHANGED AT 'NO_GROUND_TROOPS' AND STILL DE-ESCALATORY. THE DAY'S DEVELOPMENTS — THE POSTPONEMENT OF THE IN-PERSON SWISS TALKS AND A LEBANON FLARE-UP THAT WAS QUICKLY CAPPED BY A TRUMP-BROKERED ISRAEL-HEZBOLLAH CEASEFIRE RENEWAL — ARE A DIPLOMATIC WOBBLE AND A KINETIC AIR/NAVAL RISK, NEITHER A MOVE TOWARD US GROUND FORCES. STILL ~50,000 US TROOPS IN THE CENTCOM AOR; NO NEW DEPLOYMENT ORDERED; THE NAVAL BLOCKADE STAYS LIFTED (CENTCOM: ENFORCEMENT 'CEASED'); NO KHARG ASSAULT ORDERED OR EXECUTED; NO THIRD ARG / NEW MEU; NO DRAFT SIGNAL. THE ONLY ESCALATION LEVERS AIRED REMAIN AIR-POWER (TRUMP'S 'RESTART THE BOMBING' THREAT) AND DIPLOMATIC (VANCE'S 'NO TOLLS OR NO DEAL'), NOT GROUND.",
   "summary": "JUNE 20 (Day 114): No change to the ground-invasion picture, which stayed decisively de-escalatory. The two notable developments cut against, not toward, a ground war: (1) the in-person follow-on talks in Switzerland were postponed (Vance trip canceled), a diplomatic stumble that triggered no military mobilization; and (2) a Lebanon flare-up (≥16 killed in Lebanon overnight, four IDF dead) briefly threatened the deal but was capped when Trump brokered a renewed Israel-Hezbollah ceasefire — defusing the war's main resumption tripwire. There remain ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM area of responsibility with no new deployment ordered; the naval blockade stays physically lifted (CENTCOM: 'all U.S. military blockade enforcement efforts have ceased') and Hormuz keeps reopening by negotiated mine-clearing; no Kharg assault has been ordered or executed; no third amphibious ready group or new Marine Expeditionary Unit has been ordered; and there is no draft/conscription signal. The 82nd Airborne forward headquarters remains a fading standing forcible-entry contingency, not an execution order. The only US escalation levers on the table are air-power (Trump's standing threat to 'restart the bombing campaign' if Iran breaks the deal) and diplomacy (Vance's 'no tolls or no deal') — neither a ground move.",
   "details": [
    "TROOP LEVEL: Still ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM AOR (official figure, holding since March 2026); no net change and no new ground deployment ordered on June 20. The postponement of the Swiss talks produced no re-mobilization, and the Lebanon flare-up was resolved diplomatically (ceasefire renewal), not by US ground action. (CBS News; CENTCOM, June 18-19, 2026.)",
    "KHARG ISLAND: The seizure pathway remains superseded. With the blockade lifted and Hormuz reopening by negotiated mine-clearing, the chokepoint/oil-export question continues to run through a negotiated reopening rather than a Kharg landing; no US ground troops are on Kharg and no assault has been ordered or executed. (CBS News; CNBC, June 18-19, 2026.)",
    "MARINE / AMPHIBIOUS: No new amphibious or Marine deployment ordered; the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~2,200 Marines) remains on station but with the blockade lifted its enforcement mission is winding down toward the deal's force-withdrawal clause rather than building toward a landing. No third ARG or additional MEU ordered.",
    "DRAFT / MOBILIZATION: No draft or conscription signal. The Swiss-talks postponement and the Lebanon flare-up produced no Selective Service action, no expanded Guard/Reserve call-up language, and no brigade-scale activation; the House's June 3 war-powers resolution (215-208) remains the dominant counter-mobilization domestic signal, now joined by GOP Sen. Wicker's complaint that the deal 'negotiates away' war gains — pressure to concede, not to escalate. The only standing item is the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by end-2026 (not a draft activation); fact-checkers (PolitiFact, Poynter) continue to rate reinstatement claims false.",
    "ASSESSMENT: Ground-invasion execution probability is LOW and stable at Day 114. Friday's developments are a diplomatic wobble (talks postponed) and a contained kinetic risk (Lebanon flare-up, then ceasefire renewal), both inside the air/naval/diplomatic register; none is a ground-force indicator. The disconfirmation holds, with durability — not existence — the open question."
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Reinforces the disconfirmation. The ground-invasion thesis required US troops moving toward Iran, a Kharg seizure, an amphibious buildup, or a draft; June 20 delivered the opposite on every axis — troop level flat, blockade lifted, Kharg pathway superseded, no new MEU, no draft — while the day's risks (a stalled negotiation and a Lebanon flare-up) were handled by postponement and a brokered ceasefire, not by mobilization. Even the worst live failure mode (a collapse of the postponed talks) points to resumed bombing, not a ground push.",
