   "theatre": null,
   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 113 (JUNE 19): STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops AND THE POSTURE TURNED EVEN MORE DECISIVELY DE-ESCALATORY AS THE DEAL WAS CONSUMMATED. THE MOU WAS SIGNED ELECTRONICALLY (TRUMP AND PEZESHKIAN) AND TOOK IMMEDIATE EFFECT; US CENTRAL COMMAND ANNOUNCED THE NAVAL BLOCKADE OF IRANIAN PORTS HAS BEEN LIFTED (MILITARY VESSELS REMAIN ONLY TO MONITOR COMPLIANCE); AND HORMUZ BEGAN REOPENING BY NEGOTIATED MINE-CLEARING — TANKERS TRANSITING AGAIN FOR THE FIRST TIME IN ~110 DAYS VIA THE NORTHERN (IRANIAN) AND SOUTHERN (OMANI) ROUTES WHILE ~80 MINES ON THE CENTRAL CHANNEL ARE CLEARED. THIS IS THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF THE PREDICTED HORMUZ/KHARG SEIZURE: BLOCKADE LIFTED, US FORCES TO WITHDRAW, CHOKEPOINT REOPENED BY NEGOTIATION. NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT, NO THIRD ARG / NEW MEU, NO DRAFT; ~50,000 US TROOPS REMAIN IN THE CENTCOM AOR WITH NO NET CHANGE. THE LONE US ESCALATION LEVERS ARE AIR-POWER (TRUMP: 'RESTART THE BOMBING CAMPAIGN' IF IRAN BREAKS IT) AND DIPLOMATIC (VANCE: 'NO TOLLS OR NO DEAL') — NEITHER A GROUND OPERATION.",
   "summary": "JUNE 19 (Day 113): The ground-invasion rung stayed at no_ground_troops and the consummation of the deal pushed the posture to its most de-escalatory point of the war. The MOU was signed electronically by Trump and Pezeshkian and took immediate effect; US Central Command announced the naval blockade of Iranian ports has been lifted 'in accordance with the president's direction,' with military vessels remaining only to monitor compliance; and the Strait of Hormuz began reopening by negotiated mine-clearing, with commercial tankers transiting for the first time in roughly 110 days via the northern (Iranian) and southern (Omani) routes while an estimated 80 mines on the central channel await clearance. Every one of these is the structural inverse of a ground buildup. No US ground troops are in Iran, no Kharg assault has been ordered or executed, no third ARG or new MEU has been ordered, and there is no draft signal; ~50,000 US troops remain in the CENTCOM area of responsibility with no net change, three carrier strike groups and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU on station, and the 82nd Airborne forward HQ now a fading standing contingency as the blockade-lift and force-withdrawal clauses take effect. The only US escalation levers still on the table are air-power (Trump's G7 warning to 'restart the bombing campaign' if Iran breaks the deal) and diplomatic (Vance's 'no tolls or no deal' on Hormuz) — neither a ground operation. The live caveats — the still-mined central route, the toll/fee dispute, and the unresolved Lebanon track — bear on whether the reopening normalizes and the ceasefire holds, not on any forming US ground invasion.",
   "details": [
    "STATUS: no_ground_troops (unchanged, Day 113). The deal is now consummated — signed electronically, immediately effective, blockade lifted by CENTCOM — and its terms point toward a US drawdown, not a buildup. (CBS News; Al Jazeera, June 17-18, 2026.)",
    "BLOCKADE PHYSICALLY LIFTED: US Central Command announced the naval blockade of Iranian ports has been lifted, with military vessels remaining only to monitor compliance — ending the April 13 maritime-interdiction campaign rather than escalating it. (CBS News live updates, June 18, 2026.)",
    "HORMUZ REOPENS BY MINE-CLEARING, NOT SEIZURE: Tankers began transiting again (~18 vessels June 17-18 per Windward; first transit in 110 days per Lloyd's List) on the northern (Iranian) and southern (Omani) routes; the central channel stays closed pending clearance of ~80 mines — a maritime-clearance operation, not a Kharg ground assault. No US ground troops landed on Kharg and no assault was ordered or executed; the 82nd Airborne forward HQ remains a fading standing contingency, not an order. (Windward via CBS/CNBC; Lloyd's List, June 18, 2026.)",
    "THE ESCALATION LEVERS ARE AIR AND DIPLOMATIC, NOT GROUND: Trump's G7 warning to 'restart the bombing campaign' if Iran breaks the deal is an air/naval threat; Vance's 'no tolls or no deal' on Hormuz is a diplomatic lever against Iran's 'charge fees for services' signal. Neither is a ground operation, order, or staging. (NBC News; CBS News, June 17-18, 2026.)",
    "FORCE LEVELS / DRAFT: ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM AOR, no net change; three carrier strike groups and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU on station; no third ARG or new MEU ordered. No Selective Service action, no expanded Guard/Reserve call-up, no BCT-scale activation; the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by end-2026 (CNBC, Apr 9, 2026) is not a draft activation. The House's June 3 war-powers resolution (215-208) and Thursday's congressional briefing keep the domestic debate in a constrain-the-executive register. (June 18-19, 2026.)"
   ],
   "source": "CBS News live updates, 'U.S.-Iran deal signing gets more ships moving in Strait of Hormuz,' June 18, 2026; Al Jazeera, 'Iran, US presidents sign deal to extend ceasefire, reopen Strait of Hormuz,' June 17, 2026; CNBC, 'Strait of Hormuz reopening may take weeks,' June 18, 2026; NBC News live blog, June 17, 2026; CNBC, 'Trump administration to begin automatic Selective Service registration,' Apr 9, 2026 (context); U.S. House war-powers resolution, June 3, 2026 (context).",
   "prediction_impact": "Day 113 holds the ground-invasion rung at no_ground_troops for a 113th consecutive day and now upgrades the reading from de-escalatory to a near-consummated disconfirmation: a signed, immediately-effective MOU; a physically lifted US naval blockade; and a Hormuz reopening by mine-clearing are the codified inverse of the predicted Hormuz/Kharg seizure. The fact that the only remaining US escalation levers are air-power and diplomacy — not a ground push — further cuts against Predictive History's imminent-US-ground-invasion framing. The rung is not yet an airtight, durable falsification (the central route is still mined, the toll/fee dispute is open, and the Lebanon tripwire is live), but every documented June 19 indicator points away from a US ground invasion and toward an eventual drawdown.",
