   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 112 (JUNE 18): STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops; THE DEAL SURVIVED THE CLOSE OF THE G7 AND THE POSTURE STAYED DECISIVELY DE-ESCALATORY. TRUMP CLOSED THE SUMMIT DEFENDING 'THE TRUMP DEAL' AND PUT ONLY ONE ESCALATION THREAT ON THE TABLE — TO 'RESTART THE BOMBING CAMPAIGN' IF IRAN BREAKS IT, AN AIR-POWER THREAT, NOT A GROUND OPERATION. THE FRIDAY JUNE 19 SWISS SIGNING (BÜRGENSTOCK/LUZERN) STILL LIFTS THE NAVAL BLOCKADE WITHIN 30 DAYS, WITHDRAWS US FORCES FROM AROUND IRAN, AND REOPENS HORMUZ BY NEGOTIATED INTERNATIONAL MINE-CLEARING — THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF THE PREDICTED HORMUZ/KHARG SEIZURE. NO US TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG ASSAULT ORDERED OR EXECUTED, NO THIRD ARG / NEW MEU ORDERED, NO DRAFT SIGNAL; ~50,000 US TROOPS REMAIN IN THE CENTCOM AOR WITH NO NET CHANGE.",
   "summary": "JUNE 18 (Day 112): The ground-invasion rung stayed at no_ground_troops and the close of the G7 held the posture toward de-escalation. Trump wrapped the summit defending the 14-point 'Trump deal' and warning that the US 'may restart its bombing campaign' if Iran does not abide — an air-power contingency, explicitly not a ground operation. The in-person signing remained set for Friday June 19 in Switzerland (Bürgenstock/Luzern), and the deal's codified terms still lift the US naval blockade within 30 days, withdraw US forces from around Iran, and reopen Hormuz by negotiated international mine-clearing rather than by a Kharg seizure. No US ground troops are in Iran, no Kharg assault has been ordered or executed, no third ARG or new MEU has been ordered, and there is no draft signal. ~50,000 US troops remain in the CENTCOM area of responsibility (no net change), with three carrier strike groups and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU (~2,200 Marines) on station; the 82nd Airborne forward HQ remains a standing forcible-entry contingency, not an execution order, and a fading one as the blockade-lift and withdrawal clauses move toward effect. The only Hormuz-related theatre activity is the planned multinational mine-clearing mission that opens after Friday's signing — a maritime-clearance task, not a ground deployment.",
