    "STATUS: no_ground_troops (unchanged, Day 112). The June 14 war-ending MOU survived the close of the G7; its terms point toward a US drawdown, not a buildup. (G7 coverage, June 17, 2026.)",
    "THE ESCALATION THREAT IS AIR, NOT GROUND: Trump's G7 closing warning to 'restart the bombing campaign' if Iran breaks the deal is an air/naval-power threat. No ground operation was threatened, ordered, or staged. (WGME/Sinclair; NBC News, June 17, 2026.)",
    "KHARG / FORCIBLE-ENTRY: No US ground troops on Kharg, no assault ordered or executed; the chokepoint/oil-export question is routed through a negotiated Hormuz reopening and international mine-clearing. The 82nd Airborne forward HQ remains a standing contingency, not an order. (Derived from deal terms, June 2026.)",
    "FORCE LEVELS / DRAFT: ~50,000 US troops in the CENTCOM AOR, no net change; three carrier strike groups and the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU on station; no third ARG or new MEU ordered. No Selective Service action, no expanded Guard/Reserve call-up, no BCT-scale activation; the pre-existing administrative plan for automatic Selective Service registration of men 18-26 by end-2026 (CNBC, Apr 9, 2026) is not a draft activation. The House's June 3 war-powers resolution (215-208) remains the dominant counter-mobilization domestic signal. (June 17-18, 2026.)"
