     "reading": "On Lebanon, the same unreleased MOU is read two ways: Iran (FM Araghchi) asserts it requires Israel to withdraw from the southern-Lebanon territory it occupied during the war — without which 'the war has not fully come to an end' — while a US official asserts 'the deal did not call for an Israeli withdrawal,' and Netanyahu says Israel will stay 'as long as necessary' in 'security zones.' One reading makes an Israeli pullback a binding condition of the deal; the other treats Israel's Lebanon presence as outside the US-Iran MOU entirely.",
