   "theatre": null,
   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 111 (JUNE 16-17): STATUS HOLDS no_ground_troops; THE DEAL HELD THROUGH THE G7 AND THE POSTURE STAYED DECISIVELY DE-ESCALATORY. AT THE G7, TRUMP TOUTED THE MOU, SAID THE US 'WILL NOT INVEST MONEY' IN IRAN, AND A US OFFICIAL SAID THE TEXT DROPS 'WITHIN 24 TO 48 HOURS'; THE FRIDAY JUNE 19 SWISS SIGNING (BÜRGENSTOCK/LUZERN) STILL LIFTS THE NAVAL BLOCKADE WITHIN 30 DAYS, WITHDRAWS US FORCES FROM AROUND IRAN, AND REOPENS HORMUZ BY NEGOTIATION — THE STRUCTURAL INVERSE OF A GROUND BUILDUP. NO US GROUND TROOPS IN IRAN, NO KHARG GROUND ASSAULT, NO THIRD ARG / NEW MEU ORDER, NO BCT-SCALE GUARD ACTIVATION, NO DRAFT. HORMUZ STAYS CLOSED (~12-15 SHIPS/DAY) PENDING A 40-50-DAY US/UK/FRANCE/GERMANY MINE-CLEARING MISSION THAT OPENS ONLY AFTER FRIDAY — A MARITIME-CLEARANCE, NOT A GROUND, OPERATION. CAVEAT: THE NEW IRAN-vs-US DISPUTE OVER WHETHER THE DEAL REQUIRES AN ISRAELI WITHDRAWAL FROM SOUTHERN LEBANON, PLUS NETANYAHU'S 'AS LONG AS NECESSARY' STANCE, KEEPS A KINETIC-RESUMPTION TRIPWIRE LIVE — BUT NONE OF IT IS A US GROUND MOVE.",
   "summary": "JUNE 16-17 (Day 111): The ground-invasion rung stayed at no_ground_troops and the day's developments held the posture toward de-escalation. The June 14 war-ending MOU held through the opening of the G7 summit: Trump touted it to allies, said the US 'will not invest money' in Iran, and a senior US official said the full text would be released 'within 24 to 48 hours'; the in-person signing remained set for Friday June 19 in Switzerland (the Swiss foreign ministry named the Bürgenstock resort near Luzern). The deal's codified terms — lifting the US naval blockade within 30 days, withdrawing US forces from around Iran, and reopening the Strait of Hormuz by negotiation with international mine-clearing — remain structurally the inverse of a ground buildup and a continued contradiction of Predictive History's predicted seizure of Hormuz / Kharg Island and occupation of Iranian oil infrastructure. No US ground troops entered Iran; no Kharg ground assault was ordered or executed; no third ARG and no new MEU were ordered; no BCT-scale Guard activation and no Selective Service/draft action occurred. The only theatre 'movement' was diplomatic: the Strait of Hormuz stays effectively closed (~12-15 ships/day vs 120-140 pre-war) pending a mine-removal mission — by an international naval force (US, UK, France, Germany) using drone boats and minesweepers — that opens only after Friday's signing and that insurers/shippers estimate at 40-50 days; this is a maritime-clearance operation, not a movement of ground combat power, armor, or troops toward Iran. Standing capability is unchanged but continues to point toward an eventual drawdown: ~50,000 troops in CENTCOM; three carrier strike groups plus the USS Tripoli ARG / 31st MEU that had enforced the now-to-be-lifted blockade; USS Boxer ARG / 11th MEU still under INDOPACOM; the 82nd Airborne forward HQ (Maj Gen Tegtmeier) remains a standing Kharg forcible-entry CONTINGENCY, not an execution order, and a fading one as the blockade-lift and force-withdrawal clauses move toward effect. The day's one new caveat keeps a tripwire live rather than a buildup: Iran (FM Araghchi) now says the deal requires an Israeli withdrawal from southern Lebanon while a US official denies it, and Netanyahu vows to stay 'as long as necessary' — a dispute that could trigger an Iranian resumption, but is not a US ground movement.",
   "details": [
    "DEAL HELD THROUGH THE G7 — A DRAWDOWN VECTOR, NOT A BUILDUP (June 16, 2026): At the G7 summit Trump touted the MOU ('the oil is plummeting down and the stock market is shooting up like a rocket'), said the US 'will not invest money' in Iran, and a US official said the text drops 'within 24 to 48 hours'; the Friday June 19 Swiss signing (Bürgenstock/Luzern) still lifts the naval blockade within 30 days, withdraws US forces from around Iran, and reopens Hormuz by negotiation — the structural inverse of a ground buildup. (CNBC; PBS NewsHour, June 16, 2026.)",
    "NO US GROUND MOVE; THE ONLY THEATRE MOVEMENT IS DIPLOMATIC/CLEARANCE (June 16-17, 2026): No US ground troops entered Iran, no Kharg ground assault was ordered or executed, no third ARG and no new MEU were ordered, no BCT-scale Guard activation and no Selective Service/draft action occurred. The Strait of Hormuz stays closed (~12-15 ships/day) pending a mine-removal mission that opens only after Friday — a maritime-clearance operation by an international naval force (US, UK, France, Germany), NOT a movement of ground combat power, assault shipping, armor, fuel/ammo prepositioning, or troops toward Iran.",
    "BLOCKADE NOT YET PHYSICALLY LIFTED — 30-DAY WINDOW, MINE-CLEARING 40-50 DAYS (June 16, 2026): The MOU specifies a complete lifting of the blockade 'within 30 days' and the strait opens for mine removal only after Friday's signing; security and shipping firms estimate 40-50 days before insurers/shippers transit in volume. The US thus retains its maritime instrument in the interim, but the codified direction is drawdown, not reinforcement. (Jerusalem Post; Globe and Mail; Claims Journal, June 16, 2026.)",
    "LEBANON-WITHDRAWAL DISPUTE KEEPS A TRIPWIRE LIVE — NOT A US GROUND MOVE (June 16, 2026): Iran's FM Araghchi said the deal requires an Israeli withdrawal from southern Lebanon ('the war has not fully come to an end' without it), a US official said it 'did not call for an Israeli withdrawal,' and Netanyahu vowed to stay 'as long as necessary' in 'security zones'; Trump said he was 'not happy' with Israel's handling of Hezbollah. This is a deal-interpretation dispute and an Iranian resumption-risk tripwire, NOT US ground troops in Iran. (PBS NewsHour; NBC News, June 16, 2026.)"
   ],
   "prediction_impact": "Day 111 holds the ground-invasion rung at no_ground_troops for a 111th consecutive day and sustains the de-escalatory reading: a deal that held through the G7, with the text-release window tightening to 24-48 hours and the blockade-lift/force-withdrawal clauses intact, is the codified inverse of the predicted seizure-and-occupation pathway. EXECUTION has not moved on the ground; the live caveats (unreleased text, 30-day blockade-lift window, 40-50-day mine-clearing, and the new Lebanon-withdrawal dispute) bear on whether the war ends cleanly, not on whether a US ground invasion is forming — none of them is a troop movement, Kharg assault, amphibious order, or draft action.",
