   "headline": "GROUND INVASION TRACKER — DAY 99 (June 4-5): STATUS HELD 'NO_GROUND_TROOPS.' The June 4 Israel-Lebanon CONDITIONAL CEASEFIRE FRAMEWORK is deescalatory at the ground rung — it points toward a halt to the Lebanon front Iran named as its condition for resuming US talks, even though Hezbollah rejected it and strikes continued. The day's escalation signal — Araghchi's warning that an Israeli attack on Beirut would trigger a 'full-scale resumption' of the US-Iran conflict — is CONDITIONAL and specified in a MISSILE/AIR register, not a US-ground trigger. NO US ground troops in Iran; NO Kharg ground assault; NO new ground-deployment order; NO third ARG; NO new MEU order; NO BCT-scale Guard activation; NO Selective Service/draft action. USS Boxer ARG still INDOPACOM; USS Gerald R. Ford home at Norfolk; USS Abraham Lincoln + USS George H.W. Bush CSGs + USS Tripoli ARG in the Arabian Sea enforcing the blockade. Oil ~$98 Brent = risk/escalation pricing, not ground-commitment pricing.",
