   "headline": "Day 93 — CEASEFIRE DAY 53 / BLOCKADE DAY 48 / PROJECT FREEDOM PAUSED. MAY 29-30: TRUMP'S 'FINAL DETERMINATION' SITUATION ROOM MEETING ENDS WITH NO DECISION — TRUMP CONVENED A ~2-HOUR WHITE HOUSE SITUATION ROOM MEETING FRI MAY 29 TO MAKE A 'FINAL DETERMINATION' ON THE TENTATIVE 60-DAY MOU AND ENDED IT WITHOUT ANNOUNCING ONE; SENIOR ADMIN OFFICIAL (NYT): AGREEMENT 'STILL CLOSE' BUT NEEDS FURTHER DEBATE INCL. THE UNFREEZING OF IRANIAN FUNDS — TRUMP (TRUTH SOCIAL) RESTATED DEMANDS: IRAN 'MUST AGREE' TO NEVER HAVE A NUCLEAR WEAPON; HORMUZ 'IMMEDIATELY OPEN, NO TOLLS, FOR UNRESTRICTED SHIPPING TRAFFIC'; REMOVE REMAINING MINES — IRAN FARS: TRUMP POST 'RAISED ISSUES THAT CONTRADICT THE PROVISIONS OF THE AGREEMENT'S TEXT'; TASNIM: 'FINAL TEXT... NOT YET COMPLETED OR APPROVED'; MOU 'IN FINAL STAGES OF APPROVAL IN IRAN, NO FINAL DECISION YET' — VANCE: SIGNING 'TBD'; STILL NEGOTIATING 'A COUPLE OF LANGUAGE POINTS'; PROGRESS 'GOOD' — MOJTABA KHAMENEI OUT OF PUBLIC VIEW SINCE FEB 28; APPROVAL UNCLEAR — OIL FALLS AGAIN: BRENT -1.77% TO ~$92.05/BBL, WTI -1.73% TO ~$87.36/BBL (FRI MAY 29 CLOSE); BRENT -19% IN MAY = WORST MONTH SINCE MARCH 2020, ~20% OFF 2026 PEAK — LOW-GRADE KINETIC SKIRMISHING PERSISTS IN AIR/MARITIME REGISTER: US DOWNED IRANIAN OWA DRONES NEAR HORMUZ + STRUCK BANDAR ABBAS GROUND-CONTROL STATION (FURTHER LAUNCH PREVENTED); IRAN STATE TV CLAIMED A US AIRCRAFT DOWNED NEAR BUSHEHR (JAM GOV TANGESTANI) — CENTCOM DENIED ('NO US AIRCRAFT WERE SHOT DOWN. ALL US AIR ASSETS ARE ACCOUNTED FOR'); STRIKES REPORTED ON QESHM/ABU MUSA/BANDAR ABBAS/LAVAN REFINERY/ASALUYEH — RUSSIA-UKRAINE: 189 COMBAT CLASHES MAY 28 (POKROVSK + HULIAIPOLE HEAVIEST); SOUFAN CENTER FLAGS POSSIBLE TURNING POINT BUT UKRAINE NEEDS US/EUROPEAN SUPPORT; SECOND DIRECT ROUND ~JUNE 2 — DPRK: KIM SUPERVISES CRUISE + ANTI-SHIP MISSILE TESTS FROM DESTROYER CHOE HYON; BACKS CHINA 'MULTIPOLAR WORLD' WITH WANG YI — USS BOXER ARG STILL INDOPACOM; USS GERALD R. FORD HOME; LINCOLN + BUSH CSGs + TRIPOLI ARG ARABIAN SEA — HORMUZ TRAFFIC NEAR-ZERO — NO NEW GROUND-DEPLOYMENT ORDER, NO THIRD ARG, NO DRAFT; THE MOU STILL ROUTES HORMUZ THROUGH A NEGOTIATED REOPENING, NOT A GROUND SEIZURE; THE NAMED DEAL-FAILURE ALTERNATIVE STAYS AIR/STRIKE-PACKAGE (CONTESTED-UNRESOLVED — open-questions: nyt-intense-preparations-iran-resumption-may-2026)",
