   "headline": "Day 90 — CEASEFIRE DAY 50 / BLOCKADE DAY 45 / PROJECT FREEDOM PAUSED. MAY 26-27: FIRST KINETIC US-IRAN EXCHANGE SINCE PROJECT FREEDOM PAUSE — CENTCOM ANNOUNCES 'SELF-DEFENSE STRIKES' EARLY TUESDAY MAY 26 ON 2 IRGC MINE-LAYING BOATS IN THE STRAIT OF HORMUZ AND A SAM SITE NEAR BANDAR ABBAS THAT WAS REPORTEDLY TARGETING US AIRCRAFT; IRANIAN STATE TV / FARS REPORTS 4 KILLED IN BANDAR ABBAS — CENTCOM: STRIKES WERE 'IN RESPONSE TO 24 HOURS OF MISSILE, DRONE AND SMALL BOAT LAUNCHES' BY IRGC NEAR HORMUZ; INSISTS CEASEFIRE 'REMAINS IN PLACE' — IRGC CALLS STRIKES A 'FLAGRANT VIOLATION' OF THE APR 7-8 CEASEFIRE; SAYS 'RIGHT TO RECIPROCAL RESPONSE IS LEGITIMATE AND CERTAIN'; ARMY SPOKESPERSON SHEKARCHI WARNS ANY NEW ATTACK WILL GENERATE A 'FAR MORE SEVERE' RESPONSE 'BEYOND THE REGION'; SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI WARNS US BASES IN REGION 'NO LONGER SAFE' — TRUMP DOWNPLAYS STRIKES AS 'JUST A LOVE TAP' (TO ABC NEWS), INSISTS CEASEFIRE INTACT; CNN POLITICS: 'WHEN IRAN THUMBS ITS NOSE AT THE CEASEFIRE, THE TRUMP ADMINISTRATION SHRUGS' — DOHA TRACK: IRANIAN DELEGATION ARRIVES IN QATAR — FM ARAGHCHI + PARLIAMENT SPEAKER (CHIEF NEGOTIATOR) QALIBAF + CENTRAL BANK GOVERNOR HEMMATI MEET QATARI MEDIATORS ON SHEIKH TAMIM'S INSTRUCTIONS; TALKS 'GENERALLY POSITIVE'; KEY ITEMS DISCUSSED: ~$24B FROZEN IRANIAN ASSETS + NUCLEAR STOCKPILE — FOX NEWS (CITING SENIOR US OFFICIALS, MON MAY 26): DEAL '95% THERE' — TRUMP (MAY 27): BOTH SIDES 'CLOSE TO FINALIZING' AGREEMENT INVOLVING 'STRONG INSPECTIONS' — ARAGHCHI (MAY 27): UNSURE WHETHER DEAL IS IMMINENT; FM SPOX BAGHAEI: 'TO SAY THIS MEANS AN AGREEMENT IS ABOUT TO BE SIGNED — NO ONE CAN MAKE SUCH A CLAIM' — KHAMENEI ADVISER ALI SHAMKHANI DISMISSES TRUMP'S DESIRED CONTROL OVER IRANIAN NUCLEAR PROGRAM AS 'FANTASY' — PEZESHKIAN: IRAN 'READY TO REASSURE THE WORLD' NOT SEEKING NUCLEAR WEAPONS; WILL NOT COMPROMISE ON 'HONOR AND DIGNITY' — US OFFICIALS: SUPREME LEADER MOJTABA KHAMENEI HAS 'ENDORSED THE BROAD TEMPLATE OF THE DEAL' — AUSTRIA'S DOMESTIC INTELLIGENCE SERVICE (MAY 26): IRAN PURSUING ADVANCED NUCLEAR WEAPONS PROGRAM WITH BMs CAPABLE OF DELIVERING NUCLEAR WARHEADS LONG-RANGE; IRAN REJECTS AS 'FALSE AND BASELESS' — IRAN'S INTERNET BLACKOUT PARTIALLY LIFTED AFTER 87 DAYS (NORMALIZATION SIGNAL) — OIL: BRENT +3%+ TO $99.58/BBL ON RETALIATION VOW; WTI -~3% TO $93.89/BBL (MIXED) — NOTE: KINETIC EXCHANGE + IRGC 'FLAGRANT VIOLATION' / 'BEYOND THE REGION' THREAT + KHAMENEI 'BASES NO LONGER SAFE' WARNING + AUSTRIAN INTEL WAFT MARGINALLY RE-ELEVATE NEAR-TERM RE-ESCALATION RISK; BUT BOTH SIDES MOVE IMMEDIATELY TO PRESERVE CEASEFIRE FRAMING (TRUMP 'LOVE TAP'; CENTCOM 'CEASEFIRE REMAINS IN PLACE'; IRAN ARAGHCHI/QALIBAF/HEMMATI IN DOHA; '95% THERE' US OFFICIALS) — GROUND RUNG UNCHANGED: NO NEW TROOP MOVEMENTS, USS BOXER ARG STILL UNDER INDOPACOM, USS GERALD R. FORD HOME AT NORFOLK, NO THIRD ARG, NO DRAFT; THE US RESPONSE TO IRAN'S 24-HOUR PROVOCATION CHAIN WAS A DISCRETE AIR/MARITIME 'SELF-DEFENSE' STRIKE PACKAGE — NOT A GROUND ORDER (CONTESTED-UNRESOLVED — open-questions: nyt-intense-preparations-iran-resumption-may-2026)",
