   "headline": "Day 89 — CEASEFIRE DAY 49 / BLOCKADE DAY 44 / PROJECT FREEDOM PAUSED. MAY 25-26: TRUMP TIES THE IRAN DEAL TO A WIDENED ABRAHAM ACCORDS — ON TRUTH SOCIAL (MON MAY 25) HE 'MANDATORILY' REQUESTS THAT ALL COUNTRIES SIGN THE ABRAHAM ACCORDS AND SAYS EGYPT, JORDAN, PAKISTAN, QATAR AND SAUDI ARABIA SHOULD ESTABLISH FULL DIPLOMATIC RELATIONS WITH ISRAEL ('IF IRAN SIGNS ITS AGREEMENT WITH ME... IT WOULD BE AN HONOR TO HAVE THEM ALSO BE PART OF THIS UNPARALLELED WORLD COALITION'); SAYS NEGOTIATIONS 'PROCEEDING NICELY' BUT GIVES NO SIGN A DEAL IS IMMINENT — THE EMERGING 60-DAY MOU DRAWS SHARP PRO-ISRAEL CRITICISM: TED CRUZ (A REGIME 'RECEIVING BILLIONS' WHILE ABLE TO 'ENRICH URANIUM & DEVELOP NUCLEAR WEAPONS' = 'A DISASTROUS MISTAKE'), ROGER WICKER (60-DAY CEASEFIRE 'A DISASTER'), MIKE POMPEO ('NOT REMOTELY AMERICA FIRST,' LIKENS IT TO THE 2015 JCPOA), WHILE LINDSEY GRAHAM REVERSES FROM 'NIGHTMARE' TO 'SIMPLY BRILLIANT' AND MARK LEVIN PRAISES THE NORMALIZATION AS 'A TRULY MASSIVE ACCOMPLISHMENT' — RUBIO (MAY 25): A DEAL 'COULD MATERIALIZE TODAY,' CONFIDENT ON HORMUZ REOPENING BUT WILLING TO PURSUE 'ALTERNATIVES' IF DIPLOMACY FAILS — IRAN FM SPOX: 'WE HAVE REACHED A CONCLUSION ON A LARGE PORTION OF THE ISSUES' BUT 'AN AGREEMENT IS NOT IMMINENT,' ACCUSES WASHINGTON OF 'SHIFTING POSITIONS' — STICKING POINTS PERSIST: HORMUZ MANAGEMENT (IRAN INSISTS 'UNDER IRANIAN MANAGEMENT'), TIMING OF ~$25B FROZEN-ASSET RELEASE (IRAN WANTS IT BEFORE A NUCLEAR AGREEMENT), AND WHETHER THE DEAL ENDS THE LEBANON WAR (NETANYAHU WANTS TO RETAIN THE RIGHT TO CONTINUE) — TRUMP HOLDS 'TIME IS ON OUR SIDE' / 'NOT TO RUSH'; BLOCKADE 'IN FULL FORCE AND EFFECT UNTIL... SIGNED' — PAKISTAN ARMY CHIEF ASIM MUNIR + PM MET CHINESE LEADERS IN BEIJING ON THE IRAN FILE (CHINA DRAWN INTO MEDIATION) — OIL: MARKETS CLOSED MON MAY 25 (US MEMORIAL DAY + UK BANK HOLIDAY); BRENT ~$105 LAST (FRI) PRINT, -~6% ON WEEK — CARRIERS: USS BOXER ARG STILL UNDER INDOPACOM; USS GERALD R. FORD HOME AT NORFOLK; LINCOLN + BUSH CSGs ARABIAN SEA — GROUND RUNG: NO NEW TROOP MOVEMENTS, NO THIRD ARG, NO DRAFT; NPR: 'NO MAJOR MILITARY POSTURE CHANGES REPORTED FOR MAY 25'; NAMED DEAL-FAILURE ALTERNATIVE REMAINS AN AIR STRIKE / 'ALTERNATIVES,' NOT A GROUND ORDER — RUSSIA-UKRAINE: 1,000-FOR-1,000 POW SWAP CONTINUES, SECOND DIRECT ROUND ~JUNE 2 — CUBA: HAVANA BLACKOUT PROTESTS PERSIST, DIAZ-CANEL JOINS PROTESTERS DENOUNCING US — VENEZUELA: MADURO/FLORES NEXT NYC COURT DATE JUNE 30 — NORTH KOREA: NO NEW BM TEST; CHOE HYON DESTROYER HANDOVER MID-JUNE — US-CHINA: POST-SUMMIT STABILIZATION; $30B+ TARIFF-REDUCTION FRAMEWORK; TAIWAN TENSION PERSISTS",
